body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "1371506001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eNASHVILLE − Country music star Miranda Lambert, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/people/2017/09/05/miranda-lamberts-crusade-save-houstons-dogs-hurricane-harvey/634513001/\"\u003ea well-known advocate for shelter dogs and animal welfare\u003c/a\u003e, confirmed she is mourning the loss of two of her cherished rescue dogs.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn two\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/p/C77A8EfuBqM/?hl\u003den\u0026img_index\u003d1\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e recent, separate\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/p/C75EYgHO2wt/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eInstagram posts\u003c/a\u003e, the 40-year-old singer, who lives with her husband on farm about an hour south of Nashville, revealed in that she’d lost Delta Dawn and Louise, \u0026#34;the best and most loyal friends I have ever had.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I’m so heartbroken to have lost them,\u0026#34; the awarded-winning \u0026#34;Bluebird\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;Mama\u0026#39;s Broken Heart\u0026#34; singer wrote in her first social media post. \u0026#34;To love this big you have to hurt just as big. They are worth it.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMiranda Lambert\u0026#39;s dog Delta Dawn\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn the post, Lambert wrote she spent 16 years traveling the world with her Chihuahua and pug mix, Delta Dawn, before the dog\u0026#39;s April 22 death. The post includes photos and videos of her late dog who she said she found at an Oklahoma \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.sonicdrivein.com/menu/?gad_source\u003d1\u0026gclid\u003dCjwKCAjwjqWzBhAqEiwAQmtgTzzyzUMJQaqzzqB24SpGAxyc68SpemcwlkBfC4NHioW4CkxieF_GMRoCBwkQAvD_BwE\"\u003eSonic Drive-In\u003c/a\u003e in 2009. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“She was homeless and hungry but still full of personality. I opened my car door and she jumped in,” she \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/p/C75EYgHO2wt/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewrote\u003c/a\u003e. “Little did I know when I was trying to just get a cherry limeade, I would meet one of the most amazing dogs I would ever know.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74070188007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eBilly Ray Cyrus files for divorce: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2024/06/11/billy-ray-cyrus-divorce-firerose/74062238007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eThe country music star married Firerose 8 months ago\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMiranda Lambert\u0026#39;s dog Louise\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn the second post created over the weekend, Lambert paid tribute to her late dog Louise, who she wrote went by the pet names Lou Lou , boo boo, Lou bell, Lunas, and fluff cloud.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Yesterday we said goodbye to the fluffiest most protective gal pal I could ever ask for,\u0026#34; wrote Lambert, who rescued Louise and her sister Thelma in 2016.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74070213007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“The first day I ever brought them to the farm in TN they were right at home,” Lambert wrote. \u0026#34;I have mini horses, chickens and goats and I needed them for protection for the critters. And boy did they do the job. I had 7 years with Thelma who we lost last July and 8 years with this beauty. My Lou Lou polar bear. She loved it when I sang her ‘special songs’ to her.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBoth dogs, according to Lambert, passed away within the past six weeks.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "71811658007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMaranda Lambert\u0026#39;s MuttNation non profit\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn addition to being an empowering female country artist, Lambert and her mother Bev Lambert founded the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://muttnation.com/#:~:text\u003dMuttNation%20is%20shining%20a%20spotlight,Learn%20More\"\u003eMuttNation Foundation \u003c/a\u003ein 2009.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAccording to its website, the nonprofit has raised more than $9 million since inception and aims to promote shelter pet adoption and spaying and neutering pets.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "105299378"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The goal is to ensure as many dogs as possible would have a safe place to call home,\u0026#34; she previously told the USA TODAY Network.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe non-profit also works with transport partners to assist and relocate animals during natural disasters.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eNatalie Neysa Alund is a senior reporter for USA TODAY. Reach her at nalund@usatoday.com and follow her on X @nataliealund. \u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "1371506001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eNASHVILLE − Country music star Miranda Lambert, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/people/2017/09/05/miranda-lamberts-crusade-save-houstons-dogs-hurricane-harvey/634513001/\"\u003ea well-known advocate for shelter dogs and animal welfare\u003c/a\u003e, confirmed she is mourning the loss of two of her cherished rescue dogs.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn two\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/p/C77A8EfuBqM/?hl\u003den\u0026img_index\u003d1\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e recent, separate\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/p/C75EYgHO2wt/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eInstagram posts\u003c/a\u003e, the 40-year-old singer, who lives with her husband on farm about an hour south of Nashville, revealed in that she’d lost Delta Dawn and Louise, \u0026#34;the best and most loyal friends I have ever had.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I’m so heartbroken to have lost them,\u0026#34; the awarded-winning \u0026#34;Bluebird\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;Mama\u0026#39;s Broken Heart\u0026#34; singer wrote in her first social media post. \u0026#34;To love this big you have to hurt just as big. They are worth it.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMiranda Lambert\u0026#39;s dog Delta Dawn\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn the post, Lambert wrote she spent 16 years traveling the world with her Chihuahua and pug mix, Delta Dawn, before the dog\u0026#39;s April 22 death. The post includes photos and videos of her late dog who she said she found at an Oklahoma \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.sonicdrivein.com/menu/?gad_source\u003d1\u0026gclid\u003dCjwKCAjwjqWzBhAqEiwAQmtgTzzyzUMJQaqzzqB24SpGAxyc68SpemcwlkBfC4NHioW4CkxieF_GMRoCBwkQAvD_BwE\"\u003eSonic Drive-In\u003c/a\u003e in 2009. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“She was homeless and hungry but still full of personality. I opened my car door and she jumped in,” she \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/p/C75EYgHO2wt/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewrote\u003c/a\u003e. “Little did I know when I was trying to just get a cherry limeade, I would meet one of the most amazing dogs I would ever know.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74070188007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eBilly Ray Cyrus files for divorce: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2024/06/11/billy-ray-cyrus-divorce-firerose/74062238007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eThe country music star married Firerose 8 months ago\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMiranda Lambert\u0026#39;s dog Louise\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn the second post created over the weekend, Lambert paid tribute to her late dog Louise, who she wrote went by the pet names Lou Lou , boo boo, Lou bell, Lunas, and fluff cloud.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Yesterday we said goodbye to the fluffiest most protective gal pal I could ever ask for,\u0026#34; wrote Lambert, who rescued Louise and her sister Thelma in 2016.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74070213007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“The first day I ever brought them to the farm in TN they were right at home,” Lambert wrote. \u0026#34;I have mini horses, chickens and goats and I needed them for protection for the critters. And boy did they do the job. I had 7 years with Thelma who we lost last July and 8 years with this beauty. My Lou Lou polar bear. She loved it when I sang her ‘special songs’ to her.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBoth dogs, according to Lambert, passed away within the past six weeks.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "71811658007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMaranda Lambert\u0026#39;s MuttNation non profit\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn addition to being an empowering female country artist, Lambert and her mother Bev Lambert founded the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://muttnation.com/#:~:text\u003dMuttNation%20is%20shining%20a%20spotlight,Learn%20More\"\u003eMuttNation Foundation \u003c/a\u003ein 2009.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAccording to its website, the nonprofit has raised more than $9 million since inception and aims to promote shelter pet adoption and spaying and neutering pets.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "105299378"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The goal is to ensure as many dogs as possible would have a safe place to call home,\u0026#34; she previously told the USA TODAY Network.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe non-profit also works with transport partners to assist and relocate animals during natural disasters.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eNatalie Neysa Alund is a senior reporter for USA TODAY. Reach her at nalund@usatoday.com and follow her on X @nataliealund. \u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

