  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "2141358001"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“@g_eazy you have my number,” Rexha reportedly wrote under the image in her Story. “Why don’t you text me and ask me yourself you stuck up ungrateful loser.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eShe continued, \u0026#34;You’re lucky people are liking you again. Cause I could go in on all the ... things you’ve done and how you treated me after giving you your only real hit. Btw the answer is no. Hope you good.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eHours after deleting the post, Rexha \u003ca href\u003d\"https://x.com/BebeRexha/status/1801397654468825395\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003etook to X\u003c/a\u003e — formerly Twitter — to double down on the statement, writing, \u0026#34;Someone from my team had me take down my Instagram story. I decided to remove it because it felt very negative and toxic.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eShe added, \u0026#34;Sometimes trauma can lead us to react that way, and that period of my life was traumatizing. I am writing this because I regret taking it down and I want to say that I still stand by what I said.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74093668007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eG-Eazy, who\u0026#39;s been busy promoting his latest \u003ca href\u003d\"https://youtu.be/-pnXVff2bPk?si\u003d3_vwbX-ChblYzdkI\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003emusic video\u003c/a\u003e, upcoming album \u0026#34;Freak Show\u0026#34; and world tour, has not responded on social media. USA TODAY has reached out to reps for Rexha and G-Eazy for comment.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe two artists were not just one-time collaborators; they also performed together on the track \u0026#34;F.F.F.\u0026#34; off her 2017 EP, \u0026#34;All Your Fault: Pt. 1.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe nascent feud comes as \u0026#34;Me, Myself \u0026amp; I\u0026#34; – which was featured on G-Eazy\u0026#39;s 2015 album \u0026#34;When It’s Dark Out\u0026#34; – is seeing a resurgence nearly a decade after its release, thanks to TikTok. The track made its debut on Billboard\u0026#39;s \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.billboard.com/charts/tiktok-billboard-top-50/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eTikTok Top 50\u003c/a\u003e chart this week at No. 31.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAt the 2016 MTV VMAs, G-Eazy and Britney Spears \u003ca href\u003d\"https://youtu.be/mGDeAWDNaZo?si\u003dtxaDdb9gvJevzwlE\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eperformed their song\u003c/a\u003e “Make Me,\u0026#34; which transitioned into a mashup with \u0026#34;Me, Myself \u0026amp; I.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "2141341001"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eRexha made headlines earlier this month for allegedly \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/06/03/bebe-rexha-removes-fans-concert-throwing-objects/73965932007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003erequesting the removal\u003c/a\u003e of several fans who\u0026#39;d thrown objects on stage while she was performing. The incident happened a year after she was \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2023/06/19/bebe-rexha-assault-man-charged-throwsphone-at-star-onstage/70335320007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eseriously injured in a concert\u003c/a\u003e when a fan threw a phone at her.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFootage of the performance shared on social media showed Rexha scolding a fan who allegedly threw an object toward her. \u0026#34;If you want to hit me in the face, I had them press charges to the other guy. I would love to become richer,\u0026#34; Rexha told the crowd in a clip shared by TikTok user \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.tiktok.com/@donavanrose/video/7375800775072582954\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e@donavanrose\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026#34;But I\u0026#39;m not inviting that, please. It\u0026#39;s a joke.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eNicolas Malvagna of New Jersey \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2023/06/19/bebe-rexha-assault-man-charged-throwsphone-at-star-onstage/70335320007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewas charged\u003c/a\u003e with harassment and assault in 2023 for allegedly intentionally throwing a phone that struck Rexha\u0026#39;s face during her set at New York\u0026#39;s Pier 17. In photos she posted on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/p/CtrQQLDuoV3/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eInstagram\u003c/a\u003e after the event, she \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2023/06/19/bebe-rexha-assault-man-charged-throwsphone-at-star-onstage/70335320007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eappeared to have a black eye\u003c/a\u003e and a cut to her eyebrow.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;(I\u0026#39;m) good,\u0026#34; Rexha captioned the pictures.\u003c/p\u003e"
