    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eUSA TODAY has reached out to representatives for the F/V Northwestern and Discovery for comment. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.tmz.com/2024/06/14/deadliest-catch-star-nick-mavar-dead-dies-medical-emergency/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eTMZ\u003c/a\u003e was first to report the news.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMavar appeared on 16 seasons of \u0026#34;Deadliest Catch,\u0026#34; which started airing on Discovery Channel in 2005. Fifteen years after making his debut in Season 2, Mavar\u0026#39;s final appearance on the Emmy-nominated show was in Season 17, which aired in 2021.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Deadliest Catch,\u0026#34; now in its 20th season, follows crab fisherman off the coast of Alaska as they continuously defy death during expeditions in the Bering Sea. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72087830007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn December 2022, Mavar — who served under Captain Sig Hansen — sued his employer F/V Northwestern, alleging he was \u0026#34;seriously and permanently injured\u0026#34; when he suffered a ruptured appendix while on board the ship \u0026#34;following a time period of repeated reports of pain and discomfort.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMavar claimed his employer was negligent in failing to obtain timely medical care that would have prevented the rupture. A \u0026#34;cancerous tumor\u0026#34; was later found to be growing inside his appendix, he claimed. A trial date is scheduled for April 2025, according to King County Superior Court records.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSeveral months after Mavar\u0026#39;s filing, the F/V Northwestern sued \u0026#34;Deadliest Catch\u0026#39;s\u0026#34; production company for failing to provide appropriate medical care while requiring the vessel\u0026#39;s adherence to COVID-19 protocols.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe production company, in a June 2023 filing, asked the court to dismiss the case and denied \u0026#34;any and all liability, and denies that it acted negligently or contributed to any injury Mavar may have suffered that is or becomes the subject of this action.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe case is ongoing, though the judge ruled to suspend proceedings pending the resolution Mavar\u0026#39;s case in Washington.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

