body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhat did R\u0026amp;B superstar Chris Brown do when he found himself with a Saturday night to spend in Peoria, Illinois?\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;He went bowling,\u0026#34; said Vince Pollard, bowling general manager at Peoria\u0026#39;s Landmark Lanes, who said the incident left him \u0026#34;stunned\u0026#34;. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;He\u0026#39;s actually not too bad,\u0026#34; Pollard said. \u0026#34;But what a night for us.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.pjstar.com/story/entertainment/local/2024/06/02/chris-brown-goes-bowling-in-peoria-ahead-of-two-shows-in-illinois/73948335007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.pjstar.com/story/entertainment/local/2024/06/02/chris-brown-goes-bowling-in-peoria-ahead-of-two-shows-in-illinois/73948335007/\"\u003eBrown had been in Peoria on covert practice sessions\u003c/a\u003e for his 11:11 tour, which is scheduled for Detroit Wednesday before appearances in Chicago this weekend. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBrown chose the Peoria Civic Center for these rehearsal sessions, something other artists have done secretly in Peoria over the years when they want a venue in which they can shake out their songs and setups ahead of performing elsewhere.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73948312007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSo Saturday night in Peoria, Brown\u0026#39;s tour bus pulled up and an entourage of about 50 joined him on the lanes at Landmark, which was once a destination venue for the PBA Tour.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I got a phone call from his manager, asking if we were busy,\u0026#34; Pollard said. \u0026#34;He said, \u0026#39;Chris Brown would like to know if he can come bowl there at 10 p.m.?\u0026#39;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I said, \u0026#39;\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eThe\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e Chris Brown? That Chris Brown? Well, yes.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;We got a security team together and created a VIP section for him. They stayed to about midnight.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73948288007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBrown was joined by his dancers from the show, traveling staff, private security and some friends. They set up over eight lanes while Pollard cranked up the facility\u0026#39;s jukebox, including some of Brown\u0026#39;s songs, of course.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The dancers danced on the lanes,\u0026#34; Pollard said. \u0026#34;And Brown danced a little bit, too. It was impressive, after those guys danced for 10 hours on a stage at the Civic Center, and now they were doing it at a bowling alley for fun.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eHow\u0026#39;d Chris Brown roll?\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73948296007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003ePollard is no stranger to the local bowling season, a longtime competitor in Peoria\u0026#39;s Tournament of Champions and a man who is part of three generations of bowlers who\u0026#39;ve rolled 300 games.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHis impressions? \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Chris Brown used a house ball,\u0026#34; Pollard said. \u0026#34;Just picked one out and rolled a 112, 89, 117 and 135. I\u0026#39;d say he was among the top 5 in his entourage.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhen the group was done, Pollard contacted Peoria police and asked them to assist with crowd control, as about 100 people had gathered outside in Landmark\u0026#39;s parking lot, waiting for superstar.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;He\u0026#39;s easily the most famous person I\u0026#39;ve ever met in my life,\u0026#34; Pollard said.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eDave Eminian is the Journal Star sports columnist, and covers Bradley men\u0026#39;s basketball, the Rivermen and Chiefs. He writes the Cleve In The Eve sports column for pjstar.com. He can be reached at 686-3206 or deminian@pjstar.com. Follow him on X.com @icetimecleve.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
