body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "71952122007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eLast September, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/09/30/sphere-las-vegas-u2-opening-night-review/71008238007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eU2 changed the concert experience\u003c/a\u003e as we knew it.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn a stage designed as a turntable, the illustrious rockers \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dNmuGrNWUebg\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ebroke into “Zoo Station”\u003c/a\u003e and the concrete walls towering over them trembled and broke apart.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOr at least it looked that way thanks to a massive 160,000-square-foot wraparound LED screen. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs a static backdrop hissed, Bono roared, “I’m ready. Ready for what’s next.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt was an apt proclamation for the first concert at Las Vegas’ new toy, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.thesphere.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethe Sphere\u003c/a\u003e, an imposing domed venue on the Strip that promises to be the next frontier in live entertainment through design and technology. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSince September, Phish and Grateful Dead have had turns at the Sphere, and The Eagles today announced their run will start Sept. 20. This prompted us to ask if the $2.3 billion venue is really the \u0026#34;quantum leap forward\u0026#34; as \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/04/24/u-2-las-vegas-sphere-concerts-date-and-tickets/11714827002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eThe Edge described it to USA TODAY\u003c/a\u003e before that first show, or another Vegas landmark where you can take a spectacular photo? \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter seeing all three bands at the Sphere and talking with fans and stakeholders, we can say it turns the mundane into magical. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhat is inside the Las Vegas Sphere?\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73883552007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn the Vegas skyline, the Sphere is the rotund counter to its towering neighbors The Venetian and Wynn Las Vegas. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt\u0026#39;s the size of two city blocks and is taller than a football field is long. The Sphere has the seating capacity of an arena with all of the jaw-dropping wonder of a \u0026#34;Star Wars\u0026#34; ride at a Disney theme park, felt from the moment fans enter the futuristic atrium.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBuilt over four years, the Sphere is a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/04/24/u-2-las-vegas-sphere-concerts-date-and-tickets/11714827002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003euniquely fashioned venu\u003c/a\u003ee with immersive sound from 167,000 individual speakers installed behind a 160,000-square-foot (about 3.5 acres) LED screen with stunning 16k resolution.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe encompassing visuals are dizzying in the best way, whether they\u0026#39;re the Elvis-inspired video \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003ddgWko2HISog\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ecreating a swooping feeling\u003c/a\u003e of movement during U2\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Even Better Than the Real Thing,\u0026#34; \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003d0zhxUilKArQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethe \u0026#34;scaffolding\u0026#34; that parted \u003c/a\u003eat the start of Dead \u0026amp; Company\u0026#39;s “Mississippi Half-Step Uptown Toodeloo” to display a quaint row of Haight-Ashbury houses then a hovering image of Earth\u0026#39;s atmosphere or Phish\u0026#39;s \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dAe5UWYj8g3A\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eamber-lit floating fabric pods\u003c/a\u003e during \u0026#34;Leaves.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73420323007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dA-1ICkrXu-Y\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u0026#34;beamforming\u0026#34; sound technology\u003c/a\u003e in the venue allows sound to be controlled and targeted directly to certain sections, which Phish employed to head trippy effect. The absence of sound bleed from inside the dome into the concourse is another extraordinary element. Take a step out of the seating area and hear nothing but ambient background. Step back into the venue and feel an aural bear hug.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhy the Sphere is special for musicians: \u0026#39;It\u0026#39;s not just plug and play\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/02/17/bob-weir-keeps-moving-beyond-grateful-dead-mayer-wolf-bros-sammy-hagar-dead-and-company/6789714001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDead \u0026amp; Company frontman Bob Weir\u003c/a\u003e told USA TODAY in an email, the Sphere unlocks creative boundaries to \u0026#34;take storytelling in live performance to the level of opera – maybe even beyond. U2 and Phish got the ball rolling. Now it’s our turn.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBecause it can take up to a year to create specialized content to accompany live productions, the Sphere is utilizing the residency model – ideally at least eight shows – as its blueprint. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eJoin our Watch Party!  \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://profile.usatoday.com/newsletters/watch-party/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSign up to receive USA TODAY\u0026#39;s movie and TV recommendations right in your inbox\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe U2 extravaganza, which found the veteran hitmakers performing all of their 1991 album, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dvTxrgXWToZA\u0026list\u003dPL1s1DNmtn8DjDlkxBdOglc4ZMMv_fO-fQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“Achtung Baby,”\u003c/a\u003e along with a set of hits, extended from a rollout of five shows to 40. By its March 2 finale, about 800,000 fans experienced its marvel. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“It’s definitely not a touring venue. It’s not just plug and play,” said  Josephine Vaccarello, executive vice president, live, for MSG Entertainment, who oversees concert bookings for the Sphere. “We need an act that has the fan base and the following, the artist that has the creative vision for what we can do with these creative tools and the journey they want to take their fans on.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDead \u0026amp; Company, which has \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.thesphere.com/shows/dead-and-company\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003edates through Aug. 10\u003c/a\u003e, demonstrated the nimbleness of the Sphere\u0026#39;s technology during its May 25 show when a camera atop the venue\u0026#39;s roof captured a photo of the full moon. The image was quickly uploaded during the concert and appeared, along with a close-up of Weir, during “Black Peter.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73884941007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Live concerts have always been the ultimate expression for music, and part of the joy of creating shows is making the most of what’s available in order to build a world with and around the music,\u0026#34; \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2021/07/14/john-mayer-sob-rock-inspired-80-s-music/7954506002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eJohn Mayer, Dead \u0026amp; Company guitarist and singer,\u003c/a\u003e said in an email to USA TODAY. \u0026#34;Having the Sphere as this giant new set of tools is a spectacular opportunity for musicians to tell a deeper, more immersive story. I’m honored to be one of the first explorers of this new frontier.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eThe Sphere offers an experience that\u0026#39;s \u0026#39;completely different\u0026#39; for fans\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eU2 fan Alejandro Familiar attended three of the band\u0026#39;s shows, twice among the general admission throng on the floor and once from the steep 400-level.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Las Vegas resident is a devotee of the Irish rockers, whom he\u0026#39;s seen at least seven times in stadiums, which made the 20,000 concert capacity at the Sphere a relatively intimate experience – and one that enthralled him.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003d0NrsRRg8zOw\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003etechnology is crazy\u003c/a\u003e, the sound is completely different than anything I\u0026#39;ve experienced in every other venue. It\u0026#39;s just a whole immersive experience. (The band) can make you feel like you\u0026#39;re in space, at a beach, they can transport you anywhere,\u0026#34; he said. \u0026#34;You\u0026#39;re used to going to a venue and looking at the band and maybe the guitars on stage for a minute, but there\u0026#39;s no other place to look. Now, the band is what you pay the least attention to because of everything around you, but I don\u0026#39;t think that\u0026#39;s a bad thing.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFamiliar surmised that some U2 fans – like himself – went to multiple shows so they could focus on different elements of the concert each time, as well as from various vantage points. (Be aware that the visuals can be \u003ca href\u003d\"https://10best.usatoday.com/interests/travel-tips/sphere-las-vegas-tips/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eobstructed by an overhang\u003c/a\u003e above the 100-level from about rows 24-37. Tickets are categorized as limited view.)\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;It was a different experience sitting up top, like being in a huge movie theater. The band looks small from there and the stage looks \u003cem\u003ereally\u003c/em\u003e small, but the sound and visuals, that\u0026#39;s what makes it,\u0026#34; he said. \u0026#34;And you can be listening to a song and then they\u0026#39;ll blast (images of) giant Bonos and the band on the screen and you go, \u0026#39;Ah, OK, there they are.\u0026#39;\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/05/29/beatles-love-las-vegas-cirque-du-soleil-ending-2024/73797612007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eThe Beatles\u0026#39; \u0026#39;Love\u0026#39; closes July 6. Why Ringo Starr says \u0026#39;it’s worth seeing\u0026#39; while you can\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSphere challenges: \u0026#39;We\u0026#39;ll continue to learn\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJennifer Koester, president and chief operating officer of Sphere, said nearly a million guests traveled through the venue \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.sphereentertainmentco.com/sphere-entertainment-co-reports-fiscal-2024-third-quarter-results/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eby the fiscal third quarter\u003c/a\u003e that ended March 31. Yet some skeptics remain.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFor those who wonder just what the big deal is about a venue \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cnn.com/2024/04/20/entertainment/phish-concerts-sphere-anastasio-cec/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewith groovy technology\u003c/a\u003e, extremely vertical seating and pristine sound, it’s difficult to verbalize how transformative it is to feel, see and hear a show at the Sphere.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut as Vaccarello summarized, “Seeing it on videos is not the same as experiencing it in person. Once people experience it, they fall in love because it touches all of the senses.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73884854007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAlong with the indisputable wonders of the Sphere, though, some operational hiccups left some guests with a frustrated impression.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAt several U2 concerts and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/videos/entertainment/music/2024/04/22/phish-las-vegas-sphere-shows/73415374007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eduring Phish’s opening show\u003c/a\u003e, the ingress was poorly managed, leaving fans crammed on the pedestrian bridge from inside the Venetian to the Sphere’s entry for 45 to 90 minutes. The first night of Dead \u0026amp; Company, the men’s bathroom lines snaked into the atrium. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThese “pain points” as Koester calls them, were addressed by directing fans to other entry areas outside the venue for U2, opening doors earlier for Phish the second night of their residency and reversing one of the women’s restrooms – not quite as busy at a Dead show – to accommodate men.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe venue has also worked to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.thesphere.com/plan-your-visit/transportation-and-parking\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eoffer reasonable parking options\u003c/a\u003e. Several hundred spaces are available on site at the Sphere, with concert parking starting around $50 (it\u0026#39;s $18 for the ongoing Sphere Experience with Darren Aronofsky’s \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.thesphere.com/shows/the-sphere-experience\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ebreathtaking “Postcard From Earth” film\u003c/a\u003e). The self-park garages at the adjoining \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.venetianlasvegas.com/resort/explore-the-venetian/map.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eVenetian and Palazzo\u003c/a\u003e are a minimum of $23 (event rates can vary), though casino visitors holding a certain level of player\u0026#39;s club card can park for free. The rideshare scene is typical of any major event, with significant congestion at peak entry and exit times. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAll are the types of aggravating customer experiences management hopes to eradicate.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“Those are all adjustments,” Koester said. “And we’ll continue to learn.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhat will the Sphere be in five years?\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOnly live event ticket buyers will experience the sensory engulfment found inside of the Sphere. But anyone can gape at the continually glistening digital exosphere, whether they are a photo-snapping tourist or one of the many airplane passengers   scrambling for their phones on the descent to capture the newest landmark. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Sphere\u0026#39;s exosphere has shown \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/p/CxN2m_LxUsy/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eplayful emojis\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/videos/travel/2023/12/17/months-after-its-grand-opening-the-vegas-sphere-is-still-turning-heads/71952122007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eglaring eyeballs\u003c/a\u003e, logos of its musical inhabitants, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://twitter.com/VitalVegas/status/1768002232375718056\"\u003eadorable memes\u003c/a\u003e, advertising and, coming July 4, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://investor.sphereentertainmentco.com/press-releases/news-details/2024/SPHERE-LAUNCHES-SPHERE-XO-STUDENT-DESIGN-CHALLENGE-A-FIRST-OF-ITS-KIND-PARTNERSHIP-WITH-THE-LAS-VEGAS-COMMUNITY-MARKING-THE-FIRST-TIME-MEMBERS-OF-THE-GENERAL-PUBLIC-WILL-SEE-THEIR-ART-FEATURED-ON-THE-EXOSPHERE/default.aspx\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003estudent art\u003c/a\u003e. Only the truly apathetic can\u0026#39;t be impressed.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Sphere will also soon \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.reviewjournal.com/business/tourism/now-hear-this-sphere-exosphere-audio-is-coming-3048728/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eemit sound from its skeleton\u003c/a\u003e, an addition that has piqued the curiosity of some and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.fox5vegas.com/2024/05/27/las-vegas-strip-restaurants-react-sphere-possibly-adding-sound/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003epre-irritated others.\u003c/a\u003e The feeling among Sphere brass is that Las Vegas is already a cauldron of sound, so what\u0026#39;s a little more?\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut as eye-catching as the exosphere is, the future of the venue is all about what happens inside the dome.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe initial trio of Sphere bands leaned toward a middle-aged demographic, and the fourth,\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/09/08/the-eagles-final-tour-long-goodbye-opening-night-new-york/70788342007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e the Eagles\u003c/a\u003e, will park at the venue for eight shows beginning Sept. 20. Tickets are on sale at 1 p.m. ET June 21 via ticketmaster.com. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut there are plans to diversify the offerings and announce a few more performers, as well as other age-spanning multimedia events this year.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“We’re talking to a huge variety of artists. We’re just scratching the surface,” said Vaccarello.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73380522007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOne future ambition is being able to “flip” the venue within a single day; perhaps have a showing \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.thesphere.com/shows/the-sphere-experience\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ePostcard From Earth”\u003c/a\u003e – which plays most days there isn’t a concert at the venue – during the day and hold a live event that night.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/nhl/2024/05/07/nhl-draft-2024-sphere-las-vegas/73607999007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eThe staging of the NHL Draft\u003c/a\u003e June 28-29 will mark the first live broadcast from the Sphere. Even corporate activity has emerged, with Hewlett Packard Enterprise scheduled to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.sphereentertainmentco.com/sphere-announces-first-keynote-event-with-hewlett-packard-enterprise-next-generation-venue-poised-to-redefine-brand-storytelling-and-keynote-category/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ehold its keynote address \u003c/a\u003eat the venue June 18.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/05/31/bon-jovi-interview-forever-album-tour/73811993007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eJon Bon Jovi says \u0026#39;Forever\u0026#39; pays homage to The Beatles, his wife and the working class\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eKoester knows that for the Sphere to thrive, constant movement is paramount.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“I go back to the premise upon which this was built, that this is a venue that is a disruptor,” she said. “The hope is that I can sit here in five years and say, we’re still ahead of everyone else and are continuing to evolve and push the boundaries with technology. I wake up every day thinking about that.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eDoes the Sphere live up to the hype?\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe future of the Sphere is unquestionably intriguing. But its nine months of existence, it has proven to be a game changer for live experiences Its bewitching presence has convinced most cynics that this flashy attraction on the Strip is more than a colorful orb with impressive sound and visual technology.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“Everyone is pushing the boundaries of the capabilities of that venue,” said Koester. “I was at U2 opening night – I’ve been going to see them since I was 13 – and it ruined me for every other concert.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "71952122007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eLast September, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/09/30/sphere-las-vegas-u2-opening-night-review/71008238007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eU2 changed the concert experience\u003c/a\u003e as we knew it.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn a stage designed as a turntable, the illustrious rockers \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dNmuGrNWUebg\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ebroke into “Zoo Station”\u003c/a\u003e and the concrete walls towering over them trembled and broke apart.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOr at least it looked that way thanks to a massive 160,000-square-foot wraparound LED screen. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs a static backdrop hissed, Bono roared, “I’m ready. Ready for what’s next.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt was an apt proclamation for the first concert at Las Vegas’ new toy, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.thesphere.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethe Sphere\u003c/a\u003e, an imposing domed venue on the Strip that promises to be the next frontier in live entertainment through design and technology. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSince September, Phish and Grateful Dead have had turns at the Sphere, and The Eagles today announced their run will start Sept. 20. This prompted us to ask if the $2.3 billion venue is really the \u0026#34;quantum leap forward\u0026#34; as \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/04/24/u-2-las-vegas-sphere-concerts-date-and-tickets/11714827002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eThe Edge described it to USA TODAY\u003c/a\u003e before that first show, or another Vegas landmark where you can take a spectacular photo? \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter seeing all three bands at the Sphere and talking with fans and stakeholders, we can say it turns the mundane into magical. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhat is inside the Las Vegas Sphere?\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73883552007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn the Vegas skyline, the Sphere is the rotund counter to its towering neighbors The Venetian and Wynn Las Vegas. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt\u0026#39;s the size of two city blocks and is taller than a football field is long. The Sphere has the seating capacity of an arena with all of the jaw-dropping wonder of a \u0026#34;Star Wars\u0026#34; ride at a Disney theme park, felt from the moment fans enter the futuristic atrium.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBuilt over four years, the Sphere is a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/04/24/u-2-las-vegas-sphere-concerts-date-and-tickets/11714827002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003euniquely fashioned venu\u003c/a\u003ee with immersive sound from 167,000 individual speakers installed behind a 160,000-square-foot (about 3.5 acres) LED screen with stunning 16k resolution.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe encompassing visuals are dizzying in the best way, whether they\u0026#39;re the Elvis-inspired video \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003ddgWko2HISog\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ecreating a swooping feeling\u003c/a\u003e of movement during U2\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Even Better Than the Real Thing,\u0026#34; \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003d0zhxUilKArQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethe \u0026#34;scaffolding\u0026#34; that parted \u003c/a\u003eat the start of Dead \u0026amp; Company\u0026#39;s “Mississippi Half-Step Uptown Toodeloo” to display a quaint row of Haight-Ashbury houses then a hovering image of Earth\u0026#39;s atmosphere or Phish\u0026#39;s \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dAe5UWYj8g3A\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eamber-lit floating fabric pods\u003c/a\u003e during \u0026#34;Leaves.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73420323007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dA-1ICkrXu-Y\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u0026#34;beamforming\u0026#34; sound technology\u003c/a\u003e in the venue allows sound to be controlled and targeted directly to certain sections, which Phish employed to head trippy effect. The absence of sound bleed from inside the dome into the concourse is another extraordinary element. Take a step out of the seating area and hear nothing but ambient background. Step back into the venue and feel an aural bear hug.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhy the Sphere is special for musicians: \u0026#39;It\u0026#39;s not just plug and play\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/02/17/bob-weir-keeps-moving-beyond-grateful-dead-mayer-wolf-bros-sammy-hagar-dead-and-company/6789714001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDead \u0026amp; Company frontman Bob Weir\u003c/a\u003e told USA TODAY in an email, the Sphere unlocks creative boundaries to \u0026#34;take storytelling in live performance to the level of opera – maybe even beyond. U2 and Phish got the ball rolling. Now it’s our turn.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBecause it can take up to a year to create specialized content to accompany live productions, the Sphere is utilizing the residency model – ideally at least eight shows – as its blueprint. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eJoin our Watch Party!  \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://profile.usatoday.com/newsletters/watch-party/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSign up to receive USA TODAY\u0026#39;s movie and TV recommendations right in your inbox\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe U2 extravaganza, which found the veteran hitmakers performing all of their 1991 album, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dvTxrgXWToZA\u0026list\u003dPL1s1DNmtn8DjDlkxBdOglc4ZMMv_fO-fQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“Achtung Baby,”\u003c/a\u003e along with a set of hits, extended from a rollout of five shows to 40. By its March 2 finale, about 800,000 fans experienced its marvel. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“It’s definitely not a touring venue. It’s not just plug and play,” said  Josephine Vaccarello, executive vice president, live, for MSG Entertainment, who oversees concert bookings for the Sphere. “We need an act that has the fan base and the following, the artist that has the creative vision for what we can do with these creative tools and the journey they want to take their fans on.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDead \u0026amp; Company, which has \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.thesphere.com/shows/dead-and-company\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003edates through Aug. 10\u003c/a\u003e, demonstrated the nimbleness of the Sphere\u0026#39;s technology during its May 25 show when a camera atop the venue\u0026#39;s roof captured a photo of the full moon. The image was quickly uploaded during the concert and appeared, along with a close-up of Weir, during “Black Peter.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73884941007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Live concerts have always been the ultimate expression for music, and part of the joy of creating shows is making the most of what’s available in order to build a world with and around the music,\u0026#34; \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2021/07/14/john-mayer-sob-rock-inspired-80-s-music/7954506002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eJohn Mayer, Dead \u0026amp; Company guitarist and singer,\u003c/a\u003e said in an email to USA TODAY. \u0026#34;Having the Sphere as this giant new set of tools is a spectacular opportunity for musicians to tell a deeper, more immersive story. I’m honored to be one of the first explorers of this new frontier.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eThe Sphere offers an experience that\u0026#39;s \u0026#39;completely different\u0026#39; for fans\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eU2 fan Alejandro Familiar attended three of the band\u0026#39;s shows, twice among the general admission throng on the floor and once from the steep 400-level.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Las Vegas resident is a devotee of the Irish rockers, whom he\u0026#39;s seen at least seven times in stadiums, which made the 20,000 concert capacity at the Sphere a relatively intimate experience – and one that enthralled him.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003d0NrsRRg8zOw\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003etechnology is crazy\u003c/a\u003e, the sound is completely different than anything I\u0026#39;ve experienced in every other venue. It\u0026#39;s just a whole immersive experience. (The band) can make you feel like you\u0026#39;re in space, at a beach, they can transport you anywhere,\u0026#34; he said. \u0026#34;You\u0026#39;re used to going to a venue and looking at the band and maybe the guitars on stage for a minute, but there\u0026#39;s no other place to look. Now, the band is what you pay the least attention to because of everything around you, but I don\u0026#39;t think that\u0026#39;s a bad thing.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFamiliar surmised that some U2 fans – like himself – went to multiple shows so they could focus on different elements of the concert each time, as well as from various vantage points. (Be aware that the visuals can be \u003ca href\u003d\"https://10best.usatoday.com/interests/travel-tips/sphere-las-vegas-tips/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eobstructed by an overhang\u003c/a\u003e above the 100-level from about rows 24-37. Tickets are categorized as limited view.)\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;It was a different experience sitting up top, like being in a huge movie theater. The band looks small from there and the stage looks \u003cem\u003ereally\u003c/em\u003e small, but the sound and visuals, that\u0026#39;s what makes it,\u0026#34; he said. \u0026#34;And you can be listening to a song and then they\u0026#39;ll blast (images of) giant Bonos and the band on the screen and you go, \u0026#39;Ah, OK, there they are.\u0026#39;\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/05/29/beatles-love-las-vegas-cirque-du-soleil-ending-2024/73797612007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eThe Beatles\u0026#39; \u0026#39;Love\u0026#39; closes July 6. Why Ringo Starr says \u0026#39;it’s worth seeing\u0026#39; while you can\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSphere challenges: \u0026#39;We\u0026#39;ll continue to learn\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJennifer Koester, president and chief operating officer of Sphere, said nearly a million guests traveled through the venue \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.sphereentertainmentco.com/sphere-entertainment-co-reports-fiscal-2024-third-quarter-results/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eby the fiscal third quarter\u003c/a\u003e that ended March 31. Yet some skeptics remain.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFor those who wonder just what the big deal is about a venue \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cnn.com/2024/04/20/entertainment/phish-concerts-sphere-anastasio-cec/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewith groovy technology\u003c/a\u003e, extremely vertical seating and pristine sound, it’s difficult to verbalize how transformative it is to feel, see and hear a show at the Sphere.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut as Vaccarello summarized, “Seeing it on videos is not the same as experiencing it in person. Once people experience it, they fall in love because it touches all of the senses.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73884854007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAlong with the indisputable wonders of the Sphere, though, some operational hiccups left some guests with a frustrated impression.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAt several U2 concerts and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/videos/entertainment/music/2024/04/22/phish-las-vegas-sphere-shows/73415374007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eduring Phish’s opening show\u003c/a\u003e, the ingress was poorly managed, leaving fans crammed on the pedestrian bridge from inside the Venetian to the Sphere’s entry for 45 to 90 minutes. The first night of Dead \u0026amp; Company, the men’s bathroom lines snaked into the atrium. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThese “pain points” as Koester calls them, were addressed by directing fans to other entry areas outside the venue for U2, opening doors earlier for Phish the second night of their residency and reversing one of the women’s restrooms – not quite as busy at a Dead show – to accommodate men.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe venue has also worked to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.thesphere.com/plan-your-visit/transportation-and-parking\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eoffer reasonable parking options\u003c/a\u003e. Several hundred spaces are available on site at the Sphere, with concert parking starting around $50 (it\u0026#39;s $18 for the ongoing Sphere Experience with Darren Aronofsky’s \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.thesphere.com/shows/the-sphere-experience\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ebreathtaking “Postcard From Earth” film\u003c/a\u003e). The self-park garages at the adjoining \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.venetianlasvegas.com/resort/explore-the-venetian/map.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eVenetian and Palazzo\u003c/a\u003e are a minimum of $23 (event rates can vary), though casino visitors holding a certain level of player\u0026#39;s club card can park for free. The rideshare scene is typical of any major event, with significant congestion at peak entry and exit times. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAll are the types of aggravating customer experiences management hopes to eradicate.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“Those are all adjustments,” Koester said. “And we’ll continue to learn.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhat will the Sphere be in five years?\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOnly live event ticket buyers will experience the sensory engulfment found inside of the Sphere. But anyone can gape at the continually glistening digital exosphere, whether they are a photo-snapping tourist or one of the many airplane passengers   scrambling for their phones on the descent to capture the newest landmark. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Sphere\u0026#39;s exosphere has shown \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/p/CxN2m_LxUsy/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eplayful emojis\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/videos/travel/2023/12/17/months-after-its-grand-opening-the-vegas-sphere-is-still-turning-heads/71952122007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eglaring eyeballs\u003c/a\u003e, logos of its musical inhabitants, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://twitter.com/VitalVegas/status/1768002232375718056\"\u003eadorable memes\u003c/a\u003e, advertising and, coming July 4, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://investor.sphereentertainmentco.com/press-releases/news-details/2024/SPHERE-LAUNCHES-SPHERE-XO-STUDENT-DESIGN-CHALLENGE-A-FIRST-OF-ITS-KIND-PARTNERSHIP-WITH-THE-LAS-VEGAS-COMMUNITY-MARKING-THE-FIRST-TIME-MEMBERS-OF-THE-GENERAL-PUBLIC-WILL-SEE-THEIR-ART-FEATURED-ON-THE-EXOSPHERE/default.aspx\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003estudent art\u003c/a\u003e. Only the truly apathetic can\u0026#39;t be impressed.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Sphere will also soon \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.reviewjournal.com/business/tourism/now-hear-this-sphere-exosphere-audio-is-coming-3048728/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eemit sound from its skeleton\u003c/a\u003e, an addition that has piqued the curiosity of some and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.fox5vegas.com/2024/05/27/las-vegas-strip-restaurants-react-sphere-possibly-adding-sound/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003epre-irritated others.\u003c/a\u003e The feeling among Sphere brass is that Las Vegas is already a cauldron of sound, so what\u0026#39;s a little more?\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut as eye-catching as the exosphere is, the future of the venue is all about what happens inside the dome.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe initial trio of Sphere bands leaned toward a middle-aged demographic, and the fourth,\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/09/08/the-eagles-final-tour-long-goodbye-opening-night-new-york/70788342007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e the Eagles\u003c/a\u003e, will park at the venue for eight shows beginning Sept. 20. Tickets are on sale at 1 p.m. ET June 21 via ticketmaster.com. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut there are plans to diversify the offerings and announce a few more performers, as well as other age-spanning multimedia events this year.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“We’re talking to a huge variety of artists. We’re just scratching the surface,” said Vaccarello.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73380522007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOne future ambition is being able to “flip” the venue within a single day; perhaps have a showing \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.thesphere.com/shows/the-sphere-experience\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ePostcard From Earth”\u003c/a\u003e – which plays most days there isn’t a concert at the venue – during the day and hold a live event that night.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/nhl/2024/05/07/nhl-draft-2024-sphere-las-vegas/73607999007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eThe staging of the NHL Draft\u003c/a\u003e June 28-29 will mark the first live broadcast from the Sphere. Even corporate activity has emerged, with Hewlett Packard Enterprise scheduled to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.sphereentertainmentco.com/sphere-announces-first-keynote-event-with-hewlett-packard-enterprise-next-generation-venue-poised-to-redefine-brand-storytelling-and-keynote-category/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ehold its keynote address \u003c/a\u003eat the venue June 18.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/05/31/bon-jovi-interview-forever-album-tour/73811993007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eJon Bon Jovi says \u0026#39;Forever\u0026#39; pays homage to The Beatles, his wife and the working class\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eKoester knows that for the Sphere to thrive, constant movement is paramount.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“I go back to the premise upon which this was built, that this is a venue that is a disruptor,” she said. “The hope is that I can sit here in five years and say, we’re still ahead of everyone else and are continuing to evolve and push the boundaries with technology. I wake up every day thinking about that.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eDoes the Sphere live up to the hype?\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe future of the Sphere is unquestionably intriguing. But its nine months of existence, it has proven to be a game changer for live experiences Its bewitching presence has convinced most cynics that this flashy attraction on the Strip is more than a colorful orb with impressive sound and visual technology.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“Everyone is pushing the boundaries of the capabilities of that venue,” said Koester. “I was at U2 opening night – I’ve been going to see them since I was 13 – and it ruined me for every other concert.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

contentBody:
{
  "contentBody": [{
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "71952122007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eLast September, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/09/30/sphere-las-vegas-u2-opening-night-review/71008238007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eU2 changed the concert experience\u003c/a\u003e as we knew it.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn a stage designed as a turntable, the illustrious rockers \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dNmuGrNWUebg\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ebroke into “Zoo Station”\u003c/a\u003e and the concrete walls towering over them trembled and broke apart.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eOr at least it looked that way thanks to a massive 160,000-square-foot wraparound LED screen. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs a static backdrop hissed, Bono roared, “I’m ready. Ready for what’s next.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt was an apt proclamation for the first concert at Las Vegas’ new toy, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.thesphere.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethe Sphere\u003c/a\u003e, an imposing domed venue on the Strip that promises to be the next frontier in live entertainment through design and technology. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eSince September, Phish and Grateful Dead have had turns at the Sphere, and The Eagles today announced their run will start Sept. 20. This prompted us to ask if the $2.3 billion venue is really the \u0026#34;quantum leap forward\u0026#34; as \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/04/24/u-2-las-vegas-sphere-concerts-date-and-tickets/11714827002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eThe Edge described it to USA TODAY\u003c/a\u003e before that first show, or another Vegas landmark where you can take a spectacular photo? \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter seeing all three bands at the Sphere and talking with fans and stakeholders, we can say it turns the mundane into magical. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhat is inside the Las Vegas Sphere?\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73883552007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn the Vegas skyline, the Sphere is the rotund counter to its towering neighbors The Venetian and Wynn Las Vegas. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt\u0026#39;s the size of two city blocks and is taller than a football field is long. The Sphere has the seating capacity of an arena with all of the jaw-dropping wonder of a \u0026#34;Star Wars\u0026#34; ride at a Disney theme park, felt from the moment fans enter the futuristic atrium.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBuilt over four years, the Sphere is a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/04/24/u-2-las-vegas-sphere-concerts-date-and-tickets/11714827002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003euniquely fashioned venu\u003c/a\u003ee with immersive sound from 167,000 individual speakers installed behind a 160,000-square-foot (about 3.5 acres) LED screen with stunning 16k resolution.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe encompassing visuals are dizzying in the best way, whether they\u0026#39;re the Elvis-inspired video \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003ddgWko2HISog\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ecreating a swooping feeling\u003c/a\u003e of movement during U2\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Even Better Than the Real Thing,\u0026#34; \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003d0zhxUilKArQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethe \u0026#34;scaffolding\u0026#34; that parted \u003c/a\u003eat the start of Dead \u0026amp; Company\u0026#39;s “Mississippi Half-Step Uptown Toodeloo” to display a quaint row of Haight-Ashbury houses then a hovering image of Earth\u0026#39;s atmosphere or Phish\u0026#39;s \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dAe5UWYj8g3A\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eamber-lit floating fabric pods\u003c/a\u003e during \u0026#34;Leaves.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73420323007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dA-1ICkrXu-Y\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u0026#34;beamforming\u0026#34; sound technology\u003c/a\u003e in the venue allows sound to be controlled and targeted directly to certain sections, which Phish employed to head trippy effect. The absence of sound bleed from inside the dome into the concourse is another extraordinary element. Take a step out of the seating area and hear nothing but ambient background. Step back into the venue and feel an aural bear hug.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhy the Sphere is special for musicians: \u0026#39;It\u0026#39;s not just plug and play\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/02/17/bob-weir-keeps-moving-beyond-grateful-dead-mayer-wolf-bros-sammy-hagar-dead-and-company/6789714001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDead \u0026amp; Company frontman Bob Weir\u003c/a\u003e told USA TODAY in an email, the Sphere unlocks creative boundaries to \u0026#34;take storytelling in live performance to the level of opera – maybe even beyond. U2 and Phish got the ball rolling. Now it’s our turn.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBecause it can take up to a year to create specialized content to accompany live productions, the Sphere is utilizing the residency model – ideally at least eight shows – as its blueprint. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eJoin our Watch Party!  \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://profile.usatoday.com/newsletters/watch-party/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSign up to receive USA TODAY\u0026#39;s movie and TV recommendations right in your inbox\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe U2 extravaganza, which found the veteran hitmakers performing all of their 1991 album, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dvTxrgXWToZA\u0026list\u003dPL1s1DNmtn8DjDlkxBdOglc4ZMMv_fO-fQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“Achtung Baby,”\u003c/a\u003e along with a set of hits, extended from a rollout of five shows to 40. By its March 2 finale, about 800,000 fans experienced its marvel. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“It’s definitely not a touring venue. It’s not just plug and play,” said  Josephine Vaccarello, executive vice president, live, for MSG Entertainment, who oversees concert bookings for the Sphere. “We need an act that has the fan base and the following, the artist that has the creative vision for what we can do with these creative tools and the journey they want to take their fans on.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eDead \u0026amp; Company, which has \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.thesphere.com/shows/dead-and-company\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003edates through Aug. 10\u003c/a\u003e, demonstrated the nimbleness of the Sphere\u0026#39;s technology during its May 25 show when a camera atop the venue\u0026#39;s roof captured a photo of the full moon. The image was quickly uploaded during the concert and appeared, along with a close-up of Weir, during “Black Peter.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73884941007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Live concerts have always been the ultimate expression for music, and part of the joy of creating shows is making the most of what’s available in order to build a world with and around the music,\u0026#34; \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2021/07/14/john-mayer-sob-rock-inspired-80-s-music/7954506002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eJohn Mayer, Dead \u0026amp; Company guitarist and singer,\u003c/a\u003e said in an email to USA TODAY. \u0026#34;Having the Sphere as this giant new set of tools is a spectacular opportunity for musicians to tell a deeper, more immersive story. I’m honored to be one of the first explorers of this new frontier.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eThe Sphere offers an experience that\u0026#39;s \u0026#39;completely different\u0026#39; for fans\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eU2 fan Alejandro Familiar attended three of the band\u0026#39;s shows, twice among the general admission throng on the floor and once from the steep 400-level.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Las Vegas resident is a devotee of the Irish rockers, whom he\u0026#39;s seen at least seven times in stadiums, which made the 20,000 concert capacity at the Sphere a relatively intimate experience – and one that enthralled him.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003d0NrsRRg8zOw\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003etechnology is crazy\u003c/a\u003e, the sound is completely different than anything I\u0026#39;ve experienced in every other venue. It\u0026#39;s just a whole immersive experience. (The band) can make you feel like you\u0026#39;re in space, at a beach, they can transport you anywhere,\u0026#34; he said. \u0026#34;You\u0026#39;re used to going to a venue and looking at the band and maybe the guitars on stage for a minute, but there\u0026#39;s no other place to look. Now, the band is what you pay the least attention to because of everything around you, but I don\u0026#39;t think that\u0026#39;s a bad thing.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFamiliar surmised that some U2 fans – like himself – went to multiple shows so they could focus on different elements of the concert each time, as well as from various vantage points. (Be aware that the visuals can be \u003ca href\u003d\"https://10best.usatoday.com/interests/travel-tips/sphere-las-vegas-tips/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eobstructed by an overhang\u003c/a\u003e above the 100-level from about rows 24-37. Tickets are categorized as limited view.)\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;It was a different experience sitting up top, like being in a huge movie theater. The band looks small from there and the stage looks \u003cem\u003ereally\u003c/em\u003e small, but the sound and visuals, that\u0026#39;s what makes it,\u0026#34; he said. \u0026#34;And you can be listening to a song and then they\u0026#39;ll blast (images of) giant Bonos and the band on the screen and you go, \u0026#39;Ah, OK, there they are.\u0026#39;\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/05/29/beatles-love-las-vegas-cirque-du-soleil-ending-2024/73797612007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eThe Beatles\u0026#39; \u0026#39;Love\u0026#39; closes July 6. Why Ringo Starr says \u0026#39;it’s worth seeing\u0026#39; while you can\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSphere challenges: \u0026#39;We\u0026#39;ll continue to learn\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eJennifer Koester, president and chief operating officer of Sphere, said nearly a million guests traveled through the venue \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.sphereentertainmentco.com/sphere-entertainment-co-reports-fiscal-2024-third-quarter-results/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eby the fiscal third quarter\u003c/a\u003e that ended March 31. Yet some skeptics remain.  \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFor those who wonder just what the big deal is about a venue \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cnn.com/2024/04/20/entertainment/phish-concerts-sphere-anastasio-cec/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewith groovy technology\u003c/a\u003e, extremely vertical seating and pristine sound, it’s difficult to verbalize how transformative it is to feel, see and hear a show at the Sphere.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut as Vaccarello summarized, “Seeing it on videos is not the same as experiencing it in person. Once people experience it, they fall in love because it touches all of the senses.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73884854007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAlong with the indisputable wonders of the Sphere, though, some operational hiccups left some guests with a frustrated impression.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAt several U2 concerts and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/videos/entertainment/music/2024/04/22/phish-las-vegas-sphere-shows/73415374007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eduring Phish’s opening show\u003c/a\u003e, the ingress was poorly managed, leaving fans crammed on the pedestrian bridge from inside the Venetian to the Sphere’s entry for 45 to 90 minutes. The first night of Dead \u0026amp; Company, the men’s bathroom lines snaked into the atrium. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThese “pain points” as Koester calls them, were addressed by directing fans to other entry areas outside the venue for U2, opening doors earlier for Phish the second night of their residency and reversing one of the women’s restrooms – not quite as busy at a Dead show – to accommodate men.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe venue has also worked to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.thesphere.com/plan-your-visit/transportation-and-parking\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eoffer reasonable parking options\u003c/a\u003e. Several hundred spaces are available on site at the Sphere, with concert parking starting around $50 (it\u0026#39;s $18 for the ongoing Sphere Experience with Darren Aronofsky’s \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.thesphere.com/shows/the-sphere-experience\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ebreathtaking “Postcard From Earth” film\u003c/a\u003e). The self-park garages at the adjoining \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.venetianlasvegas.com/resort/explore-the-venetian/map.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eVenetian and Palazzo\u003c/a\u003e are a minimum of $23 (event rates can vary), though casino visitors holding a certain level of player\u0026#39;s club card can park for free. The rideshare scene is typical of any major event, with significant congestion at peak entry and exit times. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAll are the types of aggravating customer experiences management hopes to eradicate.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“Those are all adjustments,” Koester said. “And we’ll continue to learn.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhat will the Sphere be in five years?\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eOnly live event ticket buyers will experience the sensory engulfment found inside of the Sphere. But anyone can gape at the continually glistening digital exosphere, whether they are a photo-snapping tourist or one of the many airplane passengers   scrambling for their phones on the descent to capture the newest landmark. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Sphere\u0026#39;s exosphere has shown \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/p/CxN2m_LxUsy/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eplayful emojis\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/videos/travel/2023/12/17/months-after-its-grand-opening-the-vegas-sphere-is-still-turning-heads/71952122007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eglaring eyeballs\u003c/a\u003e, logos of its musical inhabitants, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://twitter.com/VitalVegas/status/1768002232375718056\"\u003eadorable memes\u003c/a\u003e, advertising and, coming July 4, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://investor.sphereentertainmentco.com/press-releases/news-details/2024/SPHERE-LAUNCHES-SPHERE-XO-STUDENT-DESIGN-CHALLENGE-A-FIRST-OF-ITS-KIND-PARTNERSHIP-WITH-THE-LAS-VEGAS-COMMUNITY-MARKING-THE-FIRST-TIME-MEMBERS-OF-THE-GENERAL-PUBLIC-WILL-SEE-THEIR-ART-FEATURED-ON-THE-EXOSPHERE/default.aspx\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003estudent art\u003c/a\u003e. Only the truly apathetic can\u0026#39;t be impressed.  \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Sphere will also soon \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.reviewjournal.com/business/tourism/now-hear-this-sphere-exosphere-audio-is-coming-3048728/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eemit sound from its skeleton\u003c/a\u003e, an addition that has piqued the curiosity of some and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.fox5vegas.com/2024/05/27/las-vegas-strip-restaurants-react-sphere-possibly-adding-sound/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003epre-irritated others.\u003c/a\u003e The feeling among Sphere brass is that Las Vegas is already a cauldron of sound, so what\u0026#39;s a little more?\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut as eye-catching as the exosphere is, the future of the venue is all about what happens inside the dome.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe initial trio of Sphere bands leaned toward a middle-aged demographic, and the fourth,\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/09/08/the-eagles-final-tour-long-goodbye-opening-night-new-york/70788342007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e the Eagles\u003c/a\u003e, will park at the venue for eight shows beginning Sept. 20. Tickets are on sale at 1 p.m. ET June 21 via ticketmaster.com. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut there are plans to diversify the offerings and announce a few more performers, as well as other age-spanning multimedia events this year.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“We’re talking to a huge variety of artists. We’re just scratching the surface,” said Vaccarello.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73380522007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eOne future ambition is being able to “flip” the venue within a single day; perhaps have a showing \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.thesphere.com/shows/the-sphere-experience\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ePostcard From Earth”\u003c/a\u003e – which plays most days there isn’t a concert at the venue – during the day and hold a live event that night.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/nhl/2024/05/07/nhl-draft-2024-sphere-las-vegas/73607999007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eThe staging of the NHL Draft\u003c/a\u003e June 28-29 will mark the first live broadcast from the Sphere. Even corporate activity has emerged, with Hewlett Packard Enterprise scheduled to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.sphereentertainmentco.com/sphere-announces-first-keynote-event-with-hewlett-packard-enterprise-next-generation-venue-poised-to-redefine-brand-storytelling-and-keynote-category/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ehold its keynote address \u003c/a\u003eat the venue June 18.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/05/31/bon-jovi-interview-forever-album-tour/73811993007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eJon Bon Jovi says \u0026#39;Forever\u0026#39; pays homage to The Beatles, his wife and the working class\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eKoester knows that for the Sphere to thrive, constant movement is paramount.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“I go back to the premise upon which this was built, that this is a venue that is a disruptor,” she said. “The hope is that I can sit here in five years and say, we’re still ahead of everyone else and are continuing to evolve and push the boundaries with technology. I wake up every day thinking about that.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eDoes the Sphere live up to the hype?\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe future of the Sphere is unquestionably intriguing. But its nine months of existence, it has proven to be a game changer for live experiences Its bewitching presence has convinced most cynics that this flashy attraction on the Strip is more than a colorful orb with impressive sound and visual technology.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“Everyone is pushing the boundaries of the capabilities of that venue,” said Koester. “I was at U2 opening night – I’ve been going to see them since I was 13 – and it ruined me for every other concert.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73539754007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSorry Swifties, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/entertainment/music/taylor-swift/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eTaylor Swift\u003c/a\u003e will not extend her record-breaking, behemoth \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/03/17/a-year-of-the-eras-tour-a-look-back-at-taylor-swifts-unprecedented-show/72972730007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eEras Tour\u003c/a\u003e to 2025.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;This is the very first time I’ve ever acknowledged to myself and admitted that this tour is going to end in December,\u0026#34; the singer said sentimentally during her \u0026#34;All Too Well\u0026#34; speech before the 10-minute song. \u0026#34;I once used to have hobbies,\u0026#34; she joked in her bedazzled red and black jacket\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;You have done so much to be with us,\u0026#34; she continued. \u0026#34;You\u0026#39;ve made plans so far in advance. You planned what you were going to wear. You memorized lyrics. You got yourself here. You figured out parking. You figured out transportation, and I want spend the 100th show just thinking about that and living in that moment and being here with you, and just know I appreciate every single ounce of effort that you put in to be with us when this show reaches triple digits in shows. So thank you!\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eA show that \u0026#39;spans 18 years of music\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn November 2022, Taylor Swift announced her magnum opus \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.facebook.com/TaylorSwift/posts/pfbid0kQmh5p1r1FyXw3PZSXZ4U5TWwDisneyvyxc9EjvrnkxNATiLMxDq4mz6Z82ivonol\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eon social media\u003c/a\u003e, \u0026#34;I’m enchanted to announce my next tour: Taylor Swift | The Eras Tour, a journey through the musical eras of my career (past and present!) The first leg of the tour will be in stadiums across the US, with international dates to be announced as soon as we can!\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe original post only showed 27 concerts over the course of a year. The demand quickly escalated that number to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/03/17/a-year-of-the-eras-tour-a-look-back-at-taylor-swifts-unprecedented-show/72972730007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e66 shows for year one\u003c/a\u003e and 86 for year two in 22 countries (U.S., Mexico, Argentina, Brazil, Japan, Australia, Singapore, France, Sweden, Portugal, Spain, Scotland, England, Wales, Ireland, Netherlands, Switzerland, Italy, Germany, Poland, Austria and Canada).\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWith \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/08/10/taylor-swift-eras-wraps-in-la-with-epic-concert/70559206007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ealbum announcements\u003c/a\u003e, music video reveals, special guests appearances and a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/04/18/taylor-swift-tortured-poets-album-release-updates/73149372007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewhole new \u0026#34;Tortured Poets\u0026#34; set\u003c/a\u003e unveiled in Paris, France, the tour has continued to evolve and impress. Swift has broken attendance records for many stadiums across the world and countries have welcomed the singer in innovative ways. A hidden language of Swift-ese has developed in the form of friendship bracelets, custom concert chants (\u0026#34;1, 2, 3 let\u0026#39;s go b****\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;Where you going Taylor?\u0026#34;) and unforgettable dance moves. Tens of thousands of fans log on to watch livestreams every concert night anticipating Swift\u0026#39;s outfits, possible surprises and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/02/07/taylor-swift-eras-tour-setlist-complete-list-of-surprise-songs/72484807007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ecustom acoustic set\u003c/a\u003e of songs not included in the massive \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.tennessean.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/05/09/taylor-swift-set-list-changes-eras-tour-tortured-poets/73514671007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e46-song set list\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73078313007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/03/17/a-year-of-the-eras-tour-a-look-back-at-taylor-swifts-unprecedented-show/72972730007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eA year of the Eras Tour: A look back at Taylor Swift\u0026#39;s record-breaking show\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/10/12/taylor-swift-eras-tour-movie-premiere/71145770007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSwift\u0026#39;s concert movie\u003c/a\u003e bypassed production studios as the singer worked directly with AMC as a distributor bringing fans dancing and singing in the aisles. The movie is available to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/03/14/taylor-swift-eras-tour-disney-bonus-acoustic-collection/72980833007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewatch on Disney+\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eNo word on if she will release a second movie with the newly scrambled show and additional set.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSwift is only a third of the way through her 51 European stops. In the fall, she will come back to North America, heading to Miami, New Orleans and Indianapolis in October and November and then Canada. Her last show for 2024 is on Dec. 8 in Vancouver, British Columbia.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73627073007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eDon\u0026#39;t miss any Taylor Swift news; sign up for the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://profile.tennessean.com/newsletters/this-swift-beat/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003efree, weekly newsletter This Swift Beat.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/em\u003e \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eFollow Taylor Swift reporter Bryan West on \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/bryanwesttv/\"\u003eInstagram\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.tiktok.com/@bryanwesttv\"\u003eTikTok\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://twitter.com/bryanwesttv\"\u003eX as @BryanWestTV\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73539754007"
    }, {
