body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73483327007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThey claimed the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://summerof.love/usa-today-dont-miss-summer-loves-50th-anniversary/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSummer of Love in 1967\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e2024 is primed to be the Summer of Rock.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eNot because rock songs are topping music charts or surging on streamers. They\u0026#39;re not. It\u0026#39;s because titans of the genre have decided to unleash themselves on the road, giving fans a gluttony of opportunity to revel, whether they prefer hard rock, metal, alternative or punk. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJust look at who is on tour. There are the guitar slingers in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/05/12/def-leppard-joe-elliott-interview-drastic-symphonies-album-official-story-of-def-leppard-book/70191324007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDef Leppard,\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/01/17/green-day-american-idiot-dookie-tour-saviors-album/72151607007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eGreen Day\u003c/a\u003e and Journey; \u003ca href\u003d\"https://nickelback.com/pages/upcoming-dates\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethe resurgent Nickelback\u003c/a\u003e; reunions of Jane’s Addiction \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/10/23/blink-182-tour-2024-dates-cities-tickets/71288854007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eand Blink-182\u003c/a\u003e; a 25-year anniversary for Slipknot; adrenalized hits from \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/01/22/avril-lavigne-concert-tour-simple-plan-all-time-low-dates-tickets/72310932007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eAvril Lavigne\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/videos/entertainment/music/2022/09/28/alanis-morissette-performs-you-oughta-know-taylor-hawkins-tribute/10450243002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eAlanis Morissette\u003c/a\u003e; and, perhaps most surprisingly, the monster return of Creed, who will embark on the biggest tour of their career July 17. Even those sultans of stadium shows, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/04/29/rolling-stones-hackney-diamonds-tour/73489516007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethe Rolling Stones\u003c/a\u003e, continue their age-defying lap around the country through July.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dLQ123T3zD2k\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eNeil Young once sang\u003c/a\u003e, “Rock ‘n’ roll can never die.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis summer, it’s about to thrive.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhen it comes to rock fandom, there\u0026#39;s \u0026#39;a fresh new energy,\u0026#39; says Creed frontman\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMany of the rockers on tour this summer are pulling in fans from two buckets: those who listened during their heyday (people who remember when you went to MTV to watch music videos) and those who are discovering the greats for the first time (young music fans expanding their musical horizons). \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“There is this fresh new energy,” \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.tennessean.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/03/28/scott-stapp-nashville-move-creed-reunion/72843490007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eCreed frontman Scott Stapp\u003c/a\u003e says of a rock revival. “My 17-year-old is tapping into Nirvana and Soundgarden and old Metallica and she’s hearing it for the first time. We’ve carried that theme in how we’ve designed this tour, as though there was never time off. This is the 2024 version of what we did in 2002.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCreed is leading one of the most anticipated tours of the summer. Their Summer of ’99 trek is sold out, according to Live Nation, and will bring openers \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/music/2016/03/04/playlist-whats-3-doors-down-listening/81224642/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e3 Doors Down\u003c/a\u003e and Finger Eleven, with a rotation \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2022/01/20/chris-daughtry-reveals-daughter-cause-death-suggests-resources/6590028001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eof Daughtry\u003c/a\u003e, Switchfoot, Tonic and Big Wreck joining certain dates. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74120737007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt’s the first time in more than a decade that Stapp, guitarist Mark Tremonti, bassist Brian Marshall and drummer Scott Phillips have toured, a scenario that Stapp likens to “that friend you have that you don’t talk to every day, but you pick up where you left off. It feels right.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhile many ticketholders likely lived during the Summer of \u0026#39;99 referenced in their tour name, a slice of them are newer fans driven by the use of Creed\u0026#39;s songs in viral TikTok videos, the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/mlb/playoffs/2023/10/09/texas-rangers-love-creed-in-the-playoffs/71125097007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eTexas Rangers use of \u0026#34;Higher\u0026#34; in its\u003c/a\u003e pre-game soundtrack during its World Series-winning run and even by Grammy-winning R\u0026amp;B/hip-hop artist SZA giving permission to think Creed is cool, saying \u0026#34;I will be a Creed fan forever\u0026#34; in her 2023 “\u003ca href\u003d\"https://variety.com/2023/music/features/sza-hitmaker-of-the-year-sos-grammy-song-leakers-1235810535/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSZA: Variety’s Hitmaker of the Year”\u003c/a\u003e interview. Even Live Nation’s statistics show the key demographic of ticket buyers to the band’s tour at 25-34.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74163692007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEven though Stapp, through\u003ca href\u003d\"https://scottstapp.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e a vibrant solo career\u003c/a\u003e, and Tremonti with the successful rock outfit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://alterbridge.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eAlter Bridge\u003c/a\u003e, have stayed visible, the revival of the band’s popularity has been revelatory.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“It’s not common,” Stapp admits, “unless you can remind me of someone with this resurgence after this amount of time.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eThese rock \u0026#39;n\u0026#39; rollers are \u0026#39;clearly the real deal\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhile there are fewer stadium tours in 2024, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.livenation.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003econcert promoter Live Nation\u003c/a\u003e reports to USA TODAY that sales for shows in arenas, amphitheaters, theaters and clubs are up double digits year-over-year, with more than 100 million tickets sold so far.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“We have a more diverse set of artists on the road than ever before,” said Omar-Al Joulani, president of touring for Live Nation Concerts. “While many rock bands will be touring, there will also be a wide range of artists across various genres.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIndeed, if there is a through line to this season’s rock-heavy itinerary, it’s that while nostalgia inevitably seeps in, most of the bands filling amphitheaters and stadiums have never been too far from public consciousness, whether with new music or enduring affection for their hits.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/06/13/las-vegas-sphere-changed-live-music-experience/73880112007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eThe Sphere in Las Vegas really is a \u0026#39;quantum leap\u0026#39; for live music: Inside the first shows\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn June 13, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/06/23/motley-crue-def-leppard-poison-joan-jett-review-stadium-tour/7701783001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eperennial stadium-fillers Def Leppard\u003c/a\u003e released the stomper \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dMUTI7Ck8VaQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“Just Like 73”\u003c/a\u003e with guitar ace Tom Morello adding his signature wizardry. While the band, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/05/26/def-leppard-new-album-stadium-tour/9932555002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewhich dropped “Diamond Star Halos” \u003c/a\u003ewith the crunchy single “Kick” in 2022, has no shortage of smashes to tear through onstage, the thought of merely trotting out classics is unappealing.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74129906007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“It would be really lame to be out there as a nostalgia act or doing it for the money,” says \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/videos/entertainment/entertainthis/2022/05/26/heres-what-mick-jagger-rolling-stones-taught-def-leppard/9943551002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDef Leppard guitarist Phil Collen\u003c/a\u003e, who noted that “Just Like 73” will be on the new setlist alongside evergreen fist-pumpers \u0026#34;Pour Some Sugar On Me,\u0026#34; \u0026#34;Photograph\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;Armageddon It.\u0026#34; “We got into music because we wanted to be in a band, and for us, (playing live) is very easy because you still really want to do it.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDef Leppard \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/12/07/def-leppard-journey-2024-tour-dates-tickets/71833067007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewill share this summer’s stadium stretch\u003c/a\u003e – which kicks off July 6 – with Journey. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/08/25/steve-miller-santana-grateful-dead-and-the-san-francisco-sounds/70678021007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eThe Steve Miller Band \u003c/a\u003eoccupies a regular opening slot, while Cheap Trick and Heart will dot other dates with their melodic guitar rock.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJourney is never far from a spotlight, with “Faithfully” still landing on prom night playlists and, of course, the self-generating popularity of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003d1k8craCGpgs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“Don’t Stop Believin’,” \u003c/a\u003ewhich will live on as long as new generations discover “The Sopranos.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThough the band released the album “Freedom” in 2022, they plan to hit rewind/repeat on the vintage tape deck this tour.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThanks to the “great chemistry” shared between not just the members of both chart-topping, guitar-forward bands but also their audiences, Schon is anticipating sold-out sing-a-longs across the nation this summer.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/03/17/def-leppard-recruits-alison-krauss-12-th-album-out-may-marc-bolan-t-rex/7068347001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDef Leppard\u003c/a\u003e had a lot of radio success at the same time we did, so history kind of puts us together,” says Journey \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/07/08/neal-schon-interview-journey-album-freedom/7807287001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eguitarist and co-founder Neal Schon\u003c/a\u003e. “We first met them many years back when they were broke, but you immediately admire people in your same rock arena who are clearly the real deal.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eIs rock ‘n’ roll dead? Yes. No. Maybe? But enjoy it this summer \u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMost of the artists sweating for your entertainment this summer are close to, if not in, AARP territory – Lavigne is a relative youngster at 39 – and the debate continues about the current state of rock ‘n’ roll and who might maintain longevity to fill amphitheaters and stadiums in 20 years.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/08/04/wolfgang-van-halen-interview-mammoth-wvh-album-his-parents-and-love-of-cats/70452253007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eMammoth WVH with Wolfgang Van Halen\u003c/a\u003e is the type of rock outfit carrying an old-fashioned torch as they open stadiums with Metallica, play club shows in between and will join Creed for a fall arena run.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72462552007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eGreta Van Fleet spans the globe this summer at a combination of festivals, theaters and arenas and Dorothy, fronted by\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dcg2P3MH5WYs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e singer Dorothy Martin\u003c/a\u003e (who duets with Stapp on his single \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dxTAUdWoASNQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“If These Walls Could Talk”\u003c/a\u003e) is the kind of power-lunged belter who makes you nearly blow a speaker.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCollen thinks that rock is more of an idea – “People love the idea of a rock star,” he says – and artists he considers rock icons, such as Jimi Hendrix, Mick Jagger \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2021/07/03/jim-morrison-quotes-the-doors-frontman-death-anniversary/5297160001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eand Jim Morrison\u003c/a\u003e, have no one in their shadows.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“You’re got getting new versions of that,” Collen says. “I think the image part of rock is dead.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/06/14/songwriters-hall-of-fame-rem-performance-video/74095830007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eR.E.M. performs together for first time in nearly 20 years\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eStapp, meanwhile, points to country music and the cross-pollination of rock and country, as a meaningful migration.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“In a weird way, the country music scene is reinvigorating rock,” he says.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe future of rock might be hazy, but for now, there are plenty of guitar amps ready to be turned to 11.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSo for those who still want to rock, we salute you.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73483327007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThey claimed the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://summerof.love/usa-today-dont-miss-summer-loves-50th-anniversary/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSummer of Love in 1967\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e2024 is primed to be the Summer of Rock.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eNot because rock songs are topping music charts or surging on streamers. They\u0026#39;re not. It\u0026#39;s because titans of the genre have decided to unleash themselves on the road, giving fans a gluttony of opportunity to revel, whether they prefer hard rock, metal, alternative or punk. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJust look at who is on tour. There are the guitar slingers in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/05/12/def-leppard-joe-elliott-interview-drastic-symphonies-album-official-story-of-def-leppard-book/70191324007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDef Leppard,\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/01/17/green-day-american-idiot-dookie-tour-saviors-album/72151607007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eGreen Day\u003c/a\u003e and Journey; \u003ca href\u003d\"https://nickelback.com/pages/upcoming-dates\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethe resurgent Nickelback\u003c/a\u003e; reunions of Jane’s Addiction \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/10/23/blink-182-tour-2024-dates-cities-tickets/71288854007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eand Blink-182\u003c/a\u003e; a 25-year anniversary for Slipknot; adrenalized hits from \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/01/22/avril-lavigne-concert-tour-simple-plan-all-time-low-dates-tickets/72310932007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eAvril Lavigne\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/videos/entertainment/music/2022/09/28/alanis-morissette-performs-you-oughta-know-taylor-hawkins-tribute/10450243002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eAlanis Morissette\u003c/a\u003e; and, perhaps most surprisingly, the monster return of Creed, who will embark on the biggest tour of their career July 17. Even those sultans of stadium shows, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/04/29/rolling-stones-hackney-diamonds-tour/73489516007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethe Rolling Stones\u003c/a\u003e, continue their age-defying lap around the country through July.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dLQ123T3zD2k\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eNeil Young once sang\u003c/a\u003e, “Rock ‘n’ roll can never die.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis summer, it’s about to thrive.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhen it comes to rock fandom, there\u0026#39;s \u0026#39;a fresh new energy,\u0026#39; says Creed frontman\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMany of the rockers on tour this summer are pulling in fans from two buckets: those who listened during their heyday (people who remember when you went to MTV to watch music videos) and those who are discovering the greats for the first time (young music fans expanding their musical horizons). \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“There is this fresh new energy,” \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.tennessean.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/03/28/scott-stapp-nashville-move-creed-reunion/72843490007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eCreed frontman Scott Stapp\u003c/a\u003e says of a rock revival. “My 17-year-old is tapping into Nirvana and Soundgarden and old Metallica and she’s hearing it for the first time. We’ve carried that theme in how we’ve designed this tour, as though there was never time off. This is the 2024 version of what we did in 2002.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCreed is leading one of the most anticipated tours of the summer. Their Summer of ’99 trek is sold out, according to Live Nation, and will bring openers \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/music/2016/03/04/playlist-whats-3-doors-down-listening/81224642/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e3 Doors Down\u003c/a\u003e and Finger Eleven, with a rotation \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2022/01/20/chris-daughtry-reveals-daughter-cause-death-suggests-resources/6590028001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eof Daughtry\u003c/a\u003e, Switchfoot, Tonic and Big Wreck joining certain dates. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74120737007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt’s the first time in more than a decade that Stapp, guitarist Mark Tremonti, bassist Brian Marshall and drummer Scott Phillips have toured, a scenario that Stapp likens to “that friend you have that you don’t talk to every day, but you pick up where you left off. It feels right.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhile many ticketholders likely lived during the Summer of \u0026#39;99 referenced in their tour name, a slice of them are newer fans driven by the use of Creed\u0026#39;s songs in viral TikTok videos, the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/mlb/playoffs/2023/10/09/texas-rangers-love-creed-in-the-playoffs/71125097007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eTexas Rangers use of \u0026#34;Higher\u0026#34; in its\u003c/a\u003e pre-game soundtrack during its World Series-winning run and even by Grammy-winning R\u0026amp;B/hip-hop artist SZA giving permission to think Creed is cool, saying \u0026#34;I will be a Creed fan forever\u0026#34; in her 2023 “\u003ca href\u003d\"https://variety.com/2023/music/features/sza-hitmaker-of-the-year-sos-grammy-song-leakers-1235810535/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSZA: Variety’s Hitmaker of the Year”\u003c/a\u003e interview. Even Live Nation’s statistics show the key demographic of ticket buyers to the band’s tour at 25-34.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74163692007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEven though Stapp, through\u003ca href\u003d\"https://scottstapp.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e a vibrant solo career\u003c/a\u003e, and Tremonti with the successful rock outfit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://alterbridge.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eAlter Bridge\u003c/a\u003e, have stayed visible, the revival of the band’s popularity has been revelatory.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“It’s not common,” Stapp admits, “unless you can remind me of someone with this resurgence after this amount of time.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eThese rock \u0026#39;n\u0026#39; rollers are \u0026#39;clearly the real deal\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhile there are fewer stadium tours in 2024, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.livenation.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003econcert promoter Live Nation\u003c/a\u003e reports to USA TODAY that sales for shows in arenas, amphitheaters, theaters and clubs are up double digits year-over-year, with more than 100 million tickets sold so far.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“We have a more diverse set of artists on the road than ever before,” said Omar-Al Joulani, president of touring for Live Nation Concerts. “While many rock bands will be touring, there will also be a wide range of artists across various genres.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIndeed, if there is a through line to this season’s rock-heavy itinerary, it’s that while nostalgia inevitably seeps in, most of the bands filling amphitheaters and stadiums have never been too far from public consciousness, whether with new music or enduring affection for their hits.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/06/13/las-vegas-sphere-changed-live-music-experience/73880112007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eThe Sphere in Las Vegas really is a \u0026#39;quantum leap\u0026#39; for live music: Inside the first shows\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn June 13, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/06/23/motley-crue-def-leppard-poison-joan-jett-review-stadium-tour/7701783001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eperennial stadium-fillers Def Leppard\u003c/a\u003e released the stomper \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dMUTI7Ck8VaQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“Just Like 73”\u003c/a\u003e with guitar ace Tom Morello adding his signature wizardry. While the band, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/05/26/def-leppard-new-album-stadium-tour/9932555002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewhich dropped “Diamond Star Halos” \u003c/a\u003ewith the crunchy single “Kick” in 2022, has no shortage of smashes to tear through onstage, the thought of merely trotting out classics is unappealing.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74129906007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“It would be really lame to be out there as a nostalgia act or doing it for the money,” says \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/videos/entertainment/entertainthis/2022/05/26/heres-what-mick-jagger-rolling-stones-taught-def-leppard/9943551002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDef Leppard guitarist Phil Collen\u003c/a\u003e, who noted that “Just Like 73” will be on the new setlist alongside evergreen fist-pumpers \u0026#34;Pour Some Sugar On Me,\u0026#34; \u0026#34;Photograph\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;Armageddon It.\u0026#34; “We got into music because we wanted to be in a band, and for us, (playing live) is very easy because you still really want to do it.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDef Leppard \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/12/07/def-leppard-journey-2024-tour-dates-tickets/71833067007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewill share this summer’s stadium stretch\u003c/a\u003e – which kicks off July 6 – with Journey. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/08/25/steve-miller-santana-grateful-dead-and-the-san-francisco-sounds/70678021007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eThe Steve Miller Band \u003c/a\u003eoccupies a regular opening slot, while Cheap Trick and Heart will dot other dates with their melodic guitar rock.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJourney is never far from a spotlight, with “Faithfully” still landing on prom night playlists and, of course, the self-generating popularity of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003d1k8craCGpgs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“Don’t Stop Believin’,” \u003c/a\u003ewhich will live on as long as new generations discover “The Sopranos.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThough the band released the album “Freedom” in 2022, they plan to hit rewind/repeat on the vintage tape deck this tour.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThanks to the “great chemistry” shared between not just the members of both chart-topping, guitar-forward bands but also their audiences, Schon is anticipating sold-out sing-a-longs across the nation this summer.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/03/17/def-leppard-recruits-alison-krauss-12-th-album-out-may-marc-bolan-t-rex/7068347001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDef Leppard\u003c/a\u003e had a lot of radio success at the same time we did, so history kind of puts us together,” says Journey \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/07/08/neal-schon-interview-journey-album-freedom/7807287001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eguitarist and co-founder Neal Schon\u003c/a\u003e. “We first met them many years back when they were broke, but you immediately admire people in your same rock arena who are clearly the real deal.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eIs rock ‘n’ roll dead? Yes. No. Maybe? But enjoy it this summer \u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMost of the artists sweating for your entertainment this summer are close to, if not in, AARP territory – Lavigne is a relative youngster at 39 – and the debate continues about the current state of rock ‘n’ roll and who might maintain longevity to fill amphitheaters and stadiums in 20 years.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/08/04/wolfgang-van-halen-interview-mammoth-wvh-album-his-parents-and-love-of-cats/70452253007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eMammoth WVH with Wolfgang Van Halen\u003c/a\u003e is the type of rock outfit carrying an old-fashioned torch as they open stadiums with Metallica, play club shows in between and will join Creed for a fall arena run.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72462552007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eGreta Van Fleet spans the globe this summer at a combination of festivals, theaters and arenas and Dorothy, fronted by\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dcg2P3MH5WYs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e singer Dorothy Martin\u003c/a\u003e (who duets with Stapp on his single \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dxTAUdWoASNQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“If These Walls Could Talk”\u003c/a\u003e) is the kind of power-lunged belter who makes you nearly blow a speaker.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCollen thinks that rock is more of an idea – “People love the idea of a rock star,” he says – and artists he considers rock icons, such as Jimi Hendrix, Mick Jagger \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2021/07/03/jim-morrison-quotes-the-doors-frontman-death-anniversary/5297160001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eand Jim Morrison\u003c/a\u003e, have no one in their shadows.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“You’re got getting new versions of that,” Collen says. “I think the image part of rock is dead.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/06/14/songwriters-hall-of-fame-rem-performance-video/74095830007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eR.E.M. performs together for first time in nearly 20 years\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eStapp, meanwhile, points to country music and the cross-pollination of rock and country, as a meaningful migration.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“In a weird way, the country music scene is reinvigorating rock,” he says.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe future of rock might be hazy, but for now, there are plenty of guitar amps ready to be turned to 11.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSo for those who still want to rock, we salute you.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

contentBody:
{
  "contentBody": [{
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73483327007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThey claimed the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://summerof.love/usa-today-dont-miss-summer-loves-50th-anniversary/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSummer of Love in 1967\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e2024 is primed to be the Summer of Rock.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eNot because rock songs are topping music charts or surging on streamers. They\u0026#39;re not. It\u0026#39;s because titans of the genre have decided to unleash themselves on the road, giving fans a gluttony of opportunity to revel, whether they prefer hard rock, metal, alternative or punk. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eJust look at who is on tour. There are the guitar slingers in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/05/12/def-leppard-joe-elliott-interview-drastic-symphonies-album-official-story-of-def-leppard-book/70191324007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDef Leppard,\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/01/17/green-day-american-idiot-dookie-tour-saviors-album/72151607007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eGreen Day\u003c/a\u003e and Journey; \u003ca href\u003d\"https://nickelback.com/pages/upcoming-dates\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethe resurgent Nickelback\u003c/a\u003e; reunions of Jane’s Addiction \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/10/23/blink-182-tour-2024-dates-cities-tickets/71288854007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eand Blink-182\u003c/a\u003e; a 25-year anniversary for Slipknot; adrenalized hits from \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/01/22/avril-lavigne-concert-tour-simple-plan-all-time-low-dates-tickets/72310932007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eAvril Lavigne\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/videos/entertainment/music/2022/09/28/alanis-morissette-performs-you-oughta-know-taylor-hawkins-tribute/10450243002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eAlanis Morissette\u003c/a\u003e; and, perhaps most surprisingly, the monster return of Creed, who will embark on the biggest tour of their career July 17. Even those sultans of stadium shows, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/04/29/rolling-stones-hackney-diamonds-tour/73489516007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethe Rolling Stones\u003c/a\u003e, continue their age-defying lap around the country through July.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dLQ123T3zD2k\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eNeil Young once sang\u003c/a\u003e, “Rock ‘n’ roll can never die.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis summer, it’s about to thrive.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhen it comes to rock fandom, there\u0026#39;s \u0026#39;a fresh new energy,\u0026#39; says Creed frontman\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eMany of the rockers on tour this summer are pulling in fans from two buckets: those who listened during their heyday (people who remember when you went to MTV to watch music videos) and those who are discovering the greats for the first time (young music fans expanding their musical horizons). \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“There is this fresh new energy,” \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.tennessean.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/03/28/scott-stapp-nashville-move-creed-reunion/72843490007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eCreed frontman Scott Stapp\u003c/a\u003e says of a rock revival. “My 17-year-old is tapping into Nirvana and Soundgarden and old Metallica and she’s hearing it for the first time. We’ve carried that theme in how we’ve designed this tour, as though there was never time off. This is the 2024 version of what we did in 2002.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eCreed is leading one of the most anticipated tours of the summer. Their Summer of ’99 trek is sold out, according to Live Nation, and will bring openers \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/music/2016/03/04/playlist-whats-3-doors-down-listening/81224642/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e3 Doors Down\u003c/a\u003e and Finger Eleven, with a rotation \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2022/01/20/chris-daughtry-reveals-daughter-cause-death-suggests-resources/6590028001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eof Daughtry\u003c/a\u003e, Switchfoot, Tonic and Big Wreck joining certain dates. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74120737007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt’s the first time in more than a decade that Stapp, guitarist Mark Tremonti, bassist Brian Marshall and drummer Scott Phillips have toured, a scenario that Stapp likens to “that friend you have that you don’t talk to every day, but you pick up where you left off. It feels right.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhile many ticketholders likely lived during the Summer of \u0026#39;99 referenced in their tour name, a slice of them are newer fans driven by the use of Creed\u0026#39;s songs in viral TikTok videos, the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/mlb/playoffs/2023/10/09/texas-rangers-love-creed-in-the-playoffs/71125097007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eTexas Rangers use of \u0026#34;Higher\u0026#34; in its\u003c/a\u003e pre-game soundtrack during its World Series-winning run and even by Grammy-winning R\u0026amp;B/hip-hop artist SZA giving permission to think Creed is cool, saying \u0026#34;I will be a Creed fan forever\u0026#34; in her 2023 “\u003ca href\u003d\"https://variety.com/2023/music/features/sza-hitmaker-of-the-year-sos-grammy-song-leakers-1235810535/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSZA: Variety’s Hitmaker of the Year”\u003c/a\u003e interview. Even Live Nation’s statistics show the key demographic of ticket buyers to the band’s tour at 25-34.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74163692007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eEven though Stapp, through\u003ca href\u003d\"https://scottstapp.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e a vibrant solo career\u003c/a\u003e, and Tremonti with the successful rock outfit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://alterbridge.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eAlter Bridge\u003c/a\u003e, have stayed visible, the revival of the band’s popularity has been revelatory.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“It’s not common,” Stapp admits, “unless you can remind me of someone with this resurgence after this amount of time.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eThese rock \u0026#39;n\u0026#39; rollers are \u0026#39;clearly the real deal\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhile there are fewer stadium tours in 2024, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.livenation.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003econcert promoter Live Nation\u003c/a\u003e reports to USA TODAY that sales for shows in arenas, amphitheaters, theaters and clubs are up double digits year-over-year, with more than 100 million tickets sold so far.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“We have a more diverse set of artists on the road than ever before,” said Omar-Al Joulani, president of touring for Live Nation Concerts. “While many rock bands will be touring, there will also be a wide range of artists across various genres.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIndeed, if there is a through line to this season’s rock-heavy itinerary, it’s that while nostalgia inevitably seeps in, most of the bands filling amphitheaters and stadiums have never been too far from public consciousness, whether with new music or enduring affection for their hits.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/06/13/las-vegas-sphere-changed-live-music-experience/73880112007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eThe Sphere in Las Vegas really is a \u0026#39;quantum leap\u0026#39; for live music: Inside the first shows\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn June 13, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/06/23/motley-crue-def-leppard-poison-joan-jett-review-stadium-tour/7701783001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eperennial stadium-fillers Def Leppard\u003c/a\u003e released the stomper \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dMUTI7Ck8VaQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“Just Like 73”\u003c/a\u003e with guitar ace Tom Morello adding his signature wizardry. While the band, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/05/26/def-leppard-new-album-stadium-tour/9932555002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewhich dropped “Diamond Star Halos” \u003c/a\u003ewith the crunchy single “Kick” in 2022, has no shortage of smashes to tear through onstage, the thought of merely trotting out classics is unappealing.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74129906007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“It would be really lame to be out there as a nostalgia act or doing it for the money,” says \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/videos/entertainment/entertainthis/2022/05/26/heres-what-mick-jagger-rolling-stones-taught-def-leppard/9943551002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDef Leppard guitarist Phil Collen\u003c/a\u003e, who noted that “Just Like 73” will be on the new setlist alongside evergreen fist-pumpers \u0026#34;Pour Some Sugar On Me,\u0026#34; \u0026#34;Photograph\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;Armageddon It.\u0026#34; “We got into music because we wanted to be in a band, and for us, (playing live) is very easy because you still really want to do it.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eDef Leppard \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/12/07/def-leppard-journey-2024-tour-dates-tickets/71833067007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewill share this summer’s stadium stretch\u003c/a\u003e – which kicks off July 6 – with Journey. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/08/25/steve-miller-santana-grateful-dead-and-the-san-francisco-sounds/70678021007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eThe Steve Miller Band \u003c/a\u003eoccupies a regular opening slot, while Cheap Trick and Heart will dot other dates with their melodic guitar rock.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eJourney is never far from a spotlight, with “Faithfully” still landing on prom night playlists and, of course, the self-generating popularity of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003d1k8craCGpgs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“Don’t Stop Believin’,” \u003c/a\u003ewhich will live on as long as new generations discover “The Sopranos.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThough the band released the album “Freedom” in 2022, they plan to hit rewind/repeat on the vintage tape deck this tour.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThanks to the “great chemistry” shared between not just the members of both chart-topping, guitar-forward bands but also their audiences, Schon is anticipating sold-out sing-a-longs across the nation this summer.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/03/17/def-leppard-recruits-alison-krauss-12-th-album-out-may-marc-bolan-t-rex/7068347001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDef Leppard\u003c/a\u003e had a lot of radio success at the same time we did, so history kind of puts us together,” says Journey \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/07/08/neal-schon-interview-journey-album-freedom/7807287001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eguitarist and co-founder Neal Schon\u003c/a\u003e. “We first met them many years back when they were broke, but you immediately admire people in your same rock arena who are clearly the real deal.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eIs rock ‘n’ roll dead? Yes. No. Maybe? But enjoy it this summer \u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eMost of the artists sweating for your entertainment this summer are close to, if not in, AARP territory – Lavigne is a relative youngster at 39 – and the debate continues about the current state of rock ‘n’ roll and who might maintain longevity to fill amphitheaters and stadiums in 20 years.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/08/04/wolfgang-van-halen-interview-mammoth-wvh-album-his-parents-and-love-of-cats/70452253007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eMammoth WVH with Wolfgang Van Halen\u003c/a\u003e is the type of rock outfit carrying an old-fashioned torch as they open stadiums with Metallica, play club shows in between and will join Creed for a fall arena run.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "72462552007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eGreta Van Fleet spans the globe this summer at a combination of festivals, theaters and arenas and Dorothy, fronted by\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dcg2P3MH5WYs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e singer Dorothy Martin\u003c/a\u003e (who duets with Stapp on his single \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dxTAUdWoASNQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“If These Walls Could Talk”\u003c/a\u003e) is the kind of power-lunged belter who makes you nearly blow a speaker.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eCollen thinks that rock is more of an idea – “People love the idea of a rock star,” he says – and artists he considers rock icons, such as Jimi Hendrix, Mick Jagger \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2021/07/03/jim-morrison-quotes-the-doors-frontman-death-anniversary/5297160001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eand Jim Morrison\u003c/a\u003e, have no one in their shadows.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“You’re got getting new versions of that,” Collen says. “I think the image part of rock is dead.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/06/14/songwriters-hall-of-fame-rem-performance-video/74095830007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eR.E.M. performs together for first time in nearly 20 years\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eStapp, meanwhile, points to country music and the cross-pollination of rock and country, as a meaningful migration.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“In a weird way, the country music scene is reinvigorating rock,” he says.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe future of rock might be hazy, but for now, there are plenty of guitar amps ready to be turned to 11.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eSo for those who still want to rock, we salute you.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73483327007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThey claimed the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://summerof.love/usa-today-dont-miss-summer-loves-50th-anniversary/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSummer of Love in 1967\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e2024 is primed to be the Summer of Rock.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eNot because rock songs are topping music charts or surging on streamers. They\u0026#39;re not. It\u0026#39;s because titans of the genre have decided to unleash themselves on the road, giving fans a gluttony of opportunity to revel, whether they prefer hard rock, metal, alternative or punk. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJust look at who is on tour. There are the guitar slingers in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/05/12/def-leppard-joe-elliott-interview-drastic-symphonies-album-official-story-of-def-leppard-book/70191324007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDef Leppard,\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/01/17/green-day-american-idiot-dookie-tour-saviors-album/72151607007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eGreen Day\u003c/a\u003e and Journey; \u003ca href\u003d\"https://nickelback.com/pages/upcoming-dates\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethe resurgent Nickelback\u003c/a\u003e; reunions of Jane’s Addiction \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/10/23/blink-182-tour-2024-dates-cities-tickets/71288854007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eand Blink-182\u003c/a\u003e; a 25-year anniversary for Slipknot; adrenalized hits from \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/01/22/avril-lavigne-concert-tour-simple-plan-all-time-low-dates-tickets/72310932007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eAvril Lavigne\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/videos/entertainment/music/2022/09/28/alanis-morissette-performs-you-oughta-know-taylor-hawkins-tribute/10450243002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eAlanis Morissette\u003c/a\u003e; and, perhaps most surprisingly, the monster return of Creed, who will embark on the biggest tour of their career July 17. Even those sultans of stadium shows, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/04/29/rolling-stones-hackney-diamonds-tour/73489516007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethe Rolling Stones\u003c/a\u003e, continue their age-defying lap around the country through July.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dLQ123T3zD2k\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eNeil Young once sang\u003c/a\u003e, “Rock ‘n’ roll can never die.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis summer, it’s about to thrive.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhen it comes to rock fandom, there\u0026#39;s \u0026#39;a fresh new energy,\u0026#39; says Creed frontman\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMany of the rockers on tour this summer are pulling in fans from two buckets: those who listened during their heyday (people who remember when you went to MTV to watch music videos) and those who are discovering the greats for the first time (young music fans expanding their musical horizons). \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“There is this fresh new energy,” \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.tennessean.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/03/28/scott-stapp-nashville-move-creed-reunion/72843490007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eCreed frontman Scott Stapp\u003c/a\u003e says. “My 17-year-old is tapping into Nirvana and Soundgarden and old Metallica, and she’s hearing it for the first time. We’ve carried that theme in how we’ve designed this tour, as though there was never time off. This is the 2024 version of what we did in 2002.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCreed is leading one of the most anticipated tours of the summer. Their Summer of ’99 trek is sold out, according to Live Nation, and will bring openers \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/music/2016/03/04/playlist-whats-3-doors-down-listening/81224642/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e3 Doors Down\u003c/a\u003e and Finger Eleven, with a rotation \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2022/01/20/chris-daughtry-reveals-daughter-cause-death-suggests-resources/6590028001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eof Daughtry\u003c/a\u003e, Switchfoot, Tonic and Big Wreck joining certain dates. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74120737007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt’s the first time in more than a decade that Stapp, guitarist Mark Tremonti, bassist Brian Marshall and drummer Scott Phillips have toured, a scenario that Stapp likens to “that friend you have that you don’t talk to every day, but you pick up where you left off. It feels right.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThough many ticketholders likely lived during the Summer of \u0026#39;99 referenced in their tour name, a slice of them are newer fans driven by the use of Creed\u0026#39;s songs in viral TikTok videos, the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/mlb/playoffs/2023/10/09/texas-rangers-love-creed-in-the-playoffs/71125097007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eTexas Rangers\u0026#39; use of \u0026#34;Higher\u0026#34; in its\u003c/a\u003e pregame soundtrack during its World Series-winning run, and even by Grammy-winning R\u0026amp;B/hip-hop artist SZA giving permission to think Creed is cool, saying \u0026#34;I will be a Creed fan forever\u0026#34; in her 2023 “\u003ca href\u003d\"https://variety.com/2023/music/features/sza-hitmaker-of-the-year-sos-grammy-song-leakers-1235810535/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSZA: Variety’s Hitmaker of the Year”\u003c/a\u003e interview. Even Live Nation’s statistics show the key demographic of ticket buyers to the band’s tour at 25-34.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74163692007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEven though Stapp, through\u003ca href\u003d\"https://scottstapp.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e a vibrant solo career\u003c/a\u003e, and Tremonti, with the successful rock outfit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://alterbridge.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eAlter Bridge\u003c/a\u003e, have stayed visible, the revival of the band’s popularity has been revelatory.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“It’s not common,” Stapp concedes, “unless you can remind me of someone with this resurgence after this amount of time.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eThese rock \u0026#39;n\u0026#39; rollers are \u0026#39;clearly the real deal\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThough there are fewer stadium tours in 2024, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.livenation.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003econcert promoter Live Nation\u003c/a\u003e reports to USA TODAY that sales for shows in arenas, amphitheaters, theaters and clubs are up double digits year-over-year, with more than 100 million tickets sold so far.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“We have a more diverse set of artists on the road than ever before,” said Omar-Al Joulani, president of touring for Live Nation Concerts. “While many rock bands will be touring, there will also be a wide range of artists across various genres.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74170156007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIndeed, if there is a through line to this season’s rock-heavy itinerary, it’s that while nostalgia inevitably seeps in, most of the bands filling amphitheaters and stadiums have never been too far from public consciousness, whether with new music or enduring affection for their hits.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/06/13/las-vegas-sphere-changed-live-music-experience/73880112007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eThe Sphere in Las Vegas really is a \u0026#39;quantum leap\u0026#39; for live music: Inside the first shows\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn June 13, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/06/23/motley-crue-def-leppard-poison-joan-jett-review-stadium-tour/7701783001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eperennial stadium-fillers Def Leppard\u003c/a\u003e released the stomper \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dMUTI7Ck8VaQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“Just Like 73”\u003c/a\u003e with guitar ace Tom Morello adding his signature wizardry. Though the band, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/05/26/def-leppard-new-album-stadium-tour/9932555002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewhich dropped “Diamond Star Halos” \u003c/a\u003ewith the crunchy single “Kick” in 2022, has no shortage of smashes to tear through onstage, the thought of merely trotting out classics is unappealing.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74129906007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“It would be really lame to be out there as a nostalgia act or doing it for the money,” says \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/videos/entertainment/entertainthis/2022/05/26/heres-what-mick-jagger-rolling-stones-taught-def-leppard/9943551002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDef Leppard guitarist Phil Collen\u003c/a\u003e, who noted that “Just Like 73” will be on the new set list alongside evergreen fist-pumpers \u0026#34;Pour Some Sugar On Me,\u0026#34; \u0026#34;Photograph\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;Armageddon It.\u0026#34; “We got into music because we wanted to be in a band, and for us, (playing live) is very easy because you still really want to do it.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDef Leppard \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/12/07/def-leppard-journey-2024-tour-dates-tickets/71833067007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewill share this summer’s stadium stretch\u003c/a\u003e, which kicks off July 6, with Journey. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/08/25/steve-miller-santana-grateful-dead-and-the-san-francisco-sounds/70678021007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eThe Steve Miller Band \u003c/a\u003eoccupies a regular opening slot, and Cheap Trick and Heart will dot other dates with their melodic guitar rock.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJourney is never far from a spotlight, with “Faithfully” still landing on prom night playlists and, of course, the self-generating popularity of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003d1k8craCGpgs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“Don’t Stop Believin’,” \u003c/a\u003ewhich will live on as long as new generations discover “The Sopranos.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThough the band released the album “Freedom” in 2022, they plan to hit rewind/repeat on the vintage tape deck this tour.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThanks to the “great chemistry” shared between not just the members of both chart-topping, guitar-forward bands but also their audiences, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/07/08/neal-schon-interview-journey-album-freedom/7807287001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eJourney guitarist and co-founder Neal Schon\u003c/a\u003e expects sold-out sing-a-longs across the nation this summer.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/03/17/def-leppard-recruits-alison-krauss-12-th-album-out-may-marc-bolan-t-rex/7068347001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDef Leppard\u003c/a\u003e had a lot of radio success at the same time we did, so history kind of puts us together,” Schon says. “We first met them many years back when they first broke, but you immediately admire people in your same rock arena who are clearly the real deal.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eIs rock ‘n’ roll dead? Yes. No. Maybe? But enjoy it this summer \u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMost of the artists sweating for your entertainment this summer are close to, if not in, AARP territory – Lavigne is a relative youngster at 39 – and the debate continues about the current state of rock ‘n’ roll and who might maintain longevity to fill amphitheaters and stadiums in 20 years.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/08/04/wolfgang-van-halen-interview-mammoth-wvh-album-his-parents-and-love-of-cats/70452253007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eMammoth WVH with Wolfgang Van Halen\u003c/a\u003e is the type of rock outfit carrying an old-fashioned torch as they open stadiums with Metallica, play club shows in between and will join Creed for a fall arena run.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72462552007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eGreta Van Fleet spans the globe this summer at a combination of festivals, theaters and arenas, and Dorothy, fronted by\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dcg2P3MH5WYs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e singer Dorothy Martin\u003c/a\u003e (who duets with Stapp on his single \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dxTAUdWoASNQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“If These Walls Could Talk”\u003c/a\u003e) is the kind of power-lunged belter who makes you nearly blow a speaker.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCollen believes rock is more of an idea – “People love the idea of a rock star,” he says – and artists he considers rock icons, such as Jimi Hendrix, Mick Jagger \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2021/07/03/jim-morrison-quotes-the-doors-frontman-death-anniversary/5297160001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eand Jim Morrison\u003c/a\u003e, have no one in their shadows.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“You’re got getting new versions of that,” Collen says. “I think the image part of rock is dead.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/06/14/songwriters-hall-of-fame-rem-performance-video/74095830007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eR.E.M. performs together for first time in nearly 20 years\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eStapp, meanwhile, points to country music and the cross-pollination of rock and country as a meaningful migration.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“In a weird way, the country music scene is reinvigorating rock,” he says.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe future of rock might be hazy, but for now, there are plenty of guitar amps ready to be turned to 11.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSo for those who still want to rock, we salute you.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73483327007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThey claimed the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://summerof.love/usa-today-dont-miss-summer-loves-50th-anniversary/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSummer of Love in 1967\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e2024 is primed to be the Summer of Rock.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eNot because rock songs are topping music charts or surging on streamers. They\u0026#39;re not. It\u0026#39;s because titans of the genre have decided to unleash themselves on the road, giving fans a gluttony of opportunity to revel, whether they prefer hard rock, metal, alternative or punk. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJust look at who is on tour. There are the guitar slingers in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/05/12/def-leppard-joe-elliott-interview-drastic-symphonies-album-official-story-of-def-leppard-book/70191324007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDef Leppard,\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/01/17/green-day-american-idiot-dookie-tour-saviors-album/72151607007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eGreen Day\u003c/a\u003e and Journey; \u003ca href\u003d\"https://nickelback.com/pages/upcoming-dates\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethe resurgent Nickelback\u003c/a\u003e; reunions of Jane’s Addiction \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/10/23/blink-182-tour-2024-dates-cities-tickets/71288854007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eand Blink-182\u003c/a\u003e; a 25-year anniversary for Slipknot; adrenalized hits from \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/01/22/avril-lavigne-concert-tour-simple-plan-all-time-low-dates-tickets/72310932007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eAvril Lavigne\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/videos/entertainment/music/2022/09/28/alanis-morissette-performs-you-oughta-know-taylor-hawkins-tribute/10450243002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eAlanis Morissette\u003c/a\u003e; and, perhaps most surprisingly, the monster return of Creed, who will embark on the biggest tour of their career July 17. Even those sultans of stadium shows, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/04/29/rolling-stones-hackney-diamonds-tour/73489516007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethe Rolling Stones\u003c/a\u003e, continue their age-defying lap around the country through July.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dLQ123T3zD2k\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eNeil Young once sang\u003c/a\u003e, “Rock ‘n’ roll can never die.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis summer, it’s about to thrive.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhen it comes to rock fandom, there\u0026#39;s \u0026#39;a fresh new energy,\u0026#39; says Creed frontman\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMany of the rockers on tour this summer are pulling in fans from two buckets: those who listened during their heyday (people who remember when you went to MTV to watch music videos) and those who are discovering the greats for the first time (young music fans expanding their musical horizons). \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“There is this fresh new energy,” \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.tennessean.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/03/28/scott-stapp-nashville-move-creed-reunion/72843490007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eCreed frontman Scott Stapp\u003c/a\u003e says. “My 17-year-old is tapping into Nirvana and Soundgarden and old Metallica, and she’s hearing it for the first time. We’ve carried that theme in how we’ve designed this tour, as though there was never time off. This is the 2024 version of what we did in 2002.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCreed is leading one of the most anticipated tours of the summer. Their Summer of ’99 trek is sold out, according to Live Nation, and will bring openers \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/music/2016/03/04/playlist-whats-3-doors-down-listening/81224642/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e3 Doors Down\u003c/a\u003e and Finger Eleven, with a rotation \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2022/01/20/chris-daughtry-reveals-daughter-cause-death-suggests-resources/6590028001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eof Daughtry\u003c/a\u003e, Switchfoot, Tonic and Big Wreck joining certain dates. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74120737007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt’s the first time in more than a decade that Stapp, guitarist Mark Tremonti, bassist Brian Marshall and drummer Scott Phillips have toured, a scenario that Stapp likens to “that friend you have that you don’t talk to every day, but you pick up where you left off. It feels right.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThough many ticketholders likely lived during the Summer of \u0026#39;99 referenced in their tour name, a slice of them are newer fans driven by the use of Creed\u0026#39;s songs in viral TikTok videos, the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/mlb/playoffs/2023/10/09/texas-rangers-love-creed-in-the-playoffs/71125097007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eTexas Rangers\u0026#39; use of \u0026#34;Higher\u0026#34; in its\u003c/a\u003e pregame soundtrack during its World Series-winning run, and even by Grammy-winning R\u0026amp;B/hip-hop artist SZA giving permission to think Creed is cool, saying \u0026#34;I will be a Creed fan forever\u0026#34; in her 2023 “\u003ca href\u003d\"https://variety.com/2023/music/features/sza-hitmaker-of-the-year-sos-grammy-song-leakers-1235810535/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSZA: Variety’s Hitmaker of the Year”\u003c/a\u003e interview. Even Live Nation’s statistics show the key demographic of ticket buyers to the band’s tour at 25-34.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74163692007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEven though Stapp, through\u003ca href\u003d\"https://scottstapp.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e a vibrant solo career\u003c/a\u003e, and Tremonti, with the successful rock outfit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://alterbridge.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eAlter Bridge\u003c/a\u003e, have stayed visible, the revival of the band’s popularity has been revelatory.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“It’s not common,” Stapp concedes, “unless you can remind me of someone with this resurgence after this amount of time.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eThese rock \u0026#39;n\u0026#39; rollers are \u0026#39;clearly the real deal\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThough there are fewer stadium tours in 2024, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.livenation.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003econcert promoter Live Nation\u003c/a\u003e reports to USA TODAY that sales for shows in arenas, amphitheaters, theaters and clubs are up double digits year-over-year, with more than 100 million tickets sold so far.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“We have a more diverse set of artists on the road than ever before,” said Omar-Al Joulani, president of touring for Live Nation Concerts. “While many rock bands will be touring, there will also be a wide range of artists across various genres.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74170156007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIndeed, if there is a through line to this season’s rock-heavy itinerary, it’s that while nostalgia inevitably seeps in, most of the bands filling amphitheaters and stadiums have never been too far from public consciousness, whether with new music or enduring affection for their hits.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/06/13/las-vegas-sphere-changed-live-music-experience/73880112007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eThe Sphere in Las Vegas really is a \u0026#39;quantum leap\u0026#39; for live music: Inside the first shows\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn June 13, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/06/23/motley-crue-def-leppard-poison-joan-jett-review-stadium-tour/7701783001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eperennial stadium-fillers Def Leppard\u003c/a\u003e released the stomper \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dMUTI7Ck8VaQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“Just Like 73”\u003c/a\u003e with guitar ace Tom Morello adding his signature wizardry. Though the band, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/05/26/def-leppard-new-album-stadium-tour/9932555002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewhich dropped “Diamond Star Halos” \u003c/a\u003ewith the crunchy single “Kick” in 2022, has no shortage of smashes to tear through onstage, the thought of merely trotting out classics is unappealing.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74129906007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“It would be really lame to be out there as a nostalgia act or doing it for the money,” says \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/videos/entertainment/entertainthis/2022/05/26/heres-what-mick-jagger-rolling-stones-taught-def-leppard/9943551002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDef Leppard guitarist Phil Collen\u003c/a\u003e, who noted that “Just Like 73” will be on the new set list alongside evergreen fist-pumpers \u0026#34;Pour Some Sugar On Me,\u0026#34; \u0026#34;Photograph\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;Armageddon It.\u0026#34; “We got into music because we wanted to be in a band, and for us, (playing live) is very easy because you still really want to do it.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDef Leppard \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/12/07/def-leppard-journey-2024-tour-dates-tickets/71833067007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewill share this summer’s stadium stretch\u003c/a\u003e, which kicks off July 6, with Journey. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/08/25/steve-miller-santana-grateful-dead-and-the-san-francisco-sounds/70678021007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eThe Steve Miller Band \u003c/a\u003eoccupies a regular opening slot, and Cheap Trick and Heart will dot other dates with their melodic guitar rock.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJourney is never far from a spotlight, with “Faithfully” still landing on prom night playlists and, of course, the self-generating popularity of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003d1k8craCGpgs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“Don’t Stop Believin’,” \u003c/a\u003ewhich will live on as long as new generations discover “The Sopranos.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThough the band released the album “Freedom” in 2022, they plan to hit rewind/repeat on the vintage tape deck this tour.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThanks to the “great chemistry” shared between not just the members of both chart-topping, guitar-forward bands but also their audiences, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/07/08/neal-schon-interview-journey-album-freedom/7807287001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eJourney guitarist and co-founder Neal Schon\u003c/a\u003e expects sold-out sing-a-longs across the nation this summer.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/03/17/def-leppard-recruits-alison-krauss-12-th-album-out-may-marc-bolan-t-rex/7068347001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDef Leppard\u003c/a\u003e had a lot of radio success at the same time we did, so history kind of puts us together,” Schon says. “We first met them many years back when they first broke, but you immediately admire people in your same rock arena who are clearly the real deal.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eIs rock ‘n’ roll dead? Yes. No. Maybe? But enjoy it this summer \u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMost of the artists sweating for your entertainment this summer are close to, if not in, AARP territory – Lavigne is a relative youngster at 39 – and the debate continues about the current state of rock ‘n’ roll and who might maintain longevity to fill amphitheaters and stadiums in 20 years.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/08/04/wolfgang-van-halen-interview-mammoth-wvh-album-his-parents-and-love-of-cats/70452253007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eMammoth WVH with Wolfgang Van Halen\u003c/a\u003e is the type of rock outfit carrying an old-fashioned torch as they open stadiums with Metallica, play club shows in between and will join Creed for a fall arena run.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72462552007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eGreta Van Fleet spans the globe this summer at a combination of festivals, theaters and arenas, and Dorothy, fronted by\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dcg2P3MH5WYs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e singer Dorothy Martin\u003c/a\u003e (who duets with Stapp on his single \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dxTAUdWoASNQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“If These Walls Could Talk”\u003c/a\u003e) is the kind of power-lunged belter who makes you nearly blow a speaker.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCollen believes rock is more of an idea – “People love the idea of a rock star,” he says – and artists he considers rock icons, such as Jimi Hendrix, Mick Jagger \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2021/07/03/jim-morrison-quotes-the-doors-frontman-death-anniversary/5297160001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eand Jim Morrison\u003c/a\u003e, have no one in their shadows.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“You’re got getting new versions of that,” Collen says. “I think the image part of rock is dead.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/06/14/songwriters-hall-of-fame-rem-performance-video/74095830007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eR.E.M. performs together for first time in nearly 20 years\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eStapp, meanwhile, points to country music and the cross-pollination of rock and country as a meaningful migration.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“In a weird way, the country music scene is reinvigorating rock,” he says.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe future of rock might be hazy, but for now, there are plenty of guitar amps ready to be turned to 11.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSo for those who still want to rock, we salute you.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

contentBody:
{
  "contentBody": [{
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73483327007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThey claimed the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://summerof.love/usa-today-dont-miss-summer-loves-50th-anniversary/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSummer of Love in 1967\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e2024 is primed to be the Summer of Rock.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eNot because rock songs are topping music charts or surging on streamers. They\u0026#39;re not. It\u0026#39;s because titans of the genre have decided to unleash themselves on the road, giving fans a gluttony of opportunity to revel, whether they prefer hard rock, metal, alternative or punk. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eJust look at who is on tour. There are the guitar slingers in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/05/12/def-leppard-joe-elliott-interview-drastic-symphonies-album-official-story-of-def-leppard-book/70191324007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDef Leppard,\u003c/a\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/01/17/green-day-american-idiot-dookie-tour-saviors-album/72151607007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eGreen Day\u003c/a\u003e and Journey; \u003ca href\u003d\"https://nickelback.com/pages/upcoming-dates\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethe resurgent Nickelback\u003c/a\u003e; reunions of Jane’s Addiction \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/10/23/blink-182-tour-2024-dates-cities-tickets/71288854007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eand Blink-182\u003c/a\u003e; a 25-year anniversary for Slipknot; adrenalized hits from \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/01/22/avril-lavigne-concert-tour-simple-plan-all-time-low-dates-tickets/72310932007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eAvril Lavigne\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/videos/entertainment/music/2022/09/28/alanis-morissette-performs-you-oughta-know-taylor-hawkins-tribute/10450243002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eAlanis Morissette\u003c/a\u003e; and, perhaps most surprisingly, the monster return of Creed, who will embark on the biggest tour of their career July 17. Even those sultans of stadium shows, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/04/29/rolling-stones-hackney-diamonds-tour/73489516007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethe Rolling Stones\u003c/a\u003e, continue their age-defying lap around the country through July.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dLQ123T3zD2k\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eNeil Young once sang\u003c/a\u003e, “Rock ‘n’ roll can never die.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis summer, it’s about to thrive.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhen it comes to rock fandom, there\u0026#39;s \u0026#39;a fresh new energy,\u0026#39; says Creed frontman\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eMany of the rockers on tour this summer are pulling in fans from two buckets: those who listened during their heyday (people who remember when you went to MTV to watch music videos) and those who are discovering the greats for the first time (young music fans expanding their musical horizons). \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“There is this fresh new energy,” \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.tennessean.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/03/28/scott-stapp-nashville-move-creed-reunion/72843490007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eCreed frontman Scott Stapp\u003c/a\u003e says. “My 17-year-old is tapping into Nirvana and Soundgarden and old Metallica, and she’s hearing it for the first time. We’ve carried that theme in how we’ve designed this tour, as though there was never time off. This is the 2024 version of what we did in 2002.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eCreed is leading one of the most anticipated tours of the summer. Their Summer of ’99 trek is sold out, according to Live Nation, and will bring openers \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/music/2016/03/04/playlist-whats-3-doors-down-listening/81224642/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e3 Doors Down\u003c/a\u003e and Finger Eleven, with a rotation \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2022/01/20/chris-daughtry-reveals-daughter-cause-death-suggests-resources/6590028001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eof Daughtry\u003c/a\u003e, Switchfoot, Tonic and Big Wreck joining certain dates. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74120737007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt’s the first time in more than a decade that Stapp, guitarist Mark Tremonti, bassist Brian Marshall and drummer Scott Phillips have toured, a scenario that Stapp likens to “that friend you have that you don’t talk to every day, but you pick up where you left off. It feels right.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThough many ticketholders likely lived during the Summer of \u0026#39;99 referenced in their tour name, a slice of them are newer fans driven by the use of Creed\u0026#39;s songs in viral TikTok videos, the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/sports/mlb/playoffs/2023/10/09/texas-rangers-love-creed-in-the-playoffs/71125097007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eTexas Rangers\u0026#39; use of \u0026#34;Higher\u0026#34; in its\u003c/a\u003e pregame soundtrack during its World Series-winning run, and even by Grammy-winning R\u0026amp;B/hip-hop artist SZA giving permission to think Creed is cool, saying \u0026#34;I will be a Creed fan forever\u0026#34; in her 2023 “\u003ca href\u003d\"https://variety.com/2023/music/features/sza-hitmaker-of-the-year-sos-grammy-song-leakers-1235810535/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSZA: Variety’s Hitmaker of the Year”\u003c/a\u003e interview. Even Live Nation’s statistics show the key demographic of ticket buyers to the band’s tour at 25-34.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74163692007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eEven though Stapp, through\u003ca href\u003d\"https://scottstapp.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e a vibrant solo career\u003c/a\u003e, and Tremonti, with the successful rock outfit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://alterbridge.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eAlter Bridge\u003c/a\u003e, have stayed visible, the revival of the band’s popularity has been revelatory.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“It’s not common,” Stapp concedes, “unless you can remind me of someone with this resurgence after this amount of time.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eThese rock \u0026#39;n\u0026#39; rollers are \u0026#39;clearly the real deal\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThough there are fewer stadium tours in 2024, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.livenation.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003econcert promoter Live Nation\u003c/a\u003e reports to USA TODAY that sales for shows in arenas, amphitheaters, theaters and clubs are up double digits year-over-year, with more than 100 million tickets sold so far.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“We have a more diverse set of artists on the road than ever before,” said Omar-Al Joulani, president of touring for Live Nation Concerts. “While many rock bands will be touring, there will also be a wide range of artists across various genres.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74170156007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIndeed, if there is a through line to this season’s rock-heavy itinerary, it’s that while nostalgia inevitably seeps in, most of the bands filling amphitheaters and stadiums have never been too far from public consciousness, whether with new music or enduring affection for their hits.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/06/13/las-vegas-sphere-changed-live-music-experience/73880112007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eThe Sphere in Las Vegas really is a \u0026#39;quantum leap\u0026#39; for live music: Inside the first shows\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn June 13, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/06/23/motley-crue-def-leppard-poison-joan-jett-review-stadium-tour/7701783001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eperennial stadium-fillers Def Leppard\u003c/a\u003e released the stomper \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dMUTI7Ck8VaQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“Just Like 73”\u003c/a\u003e with guitar ace Tom Morello adding his signature wizardry. Though the band, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/05/26/def-leppard-new-album-stadium-tour/9932555002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewhich dropped “Diamond Star Halos” \u003c/a\u003ewith the crunchy single “Kick” in 2022, has no shortage of smashes to tear through onstage, the thought of merely trotting out classics is unappealing.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74129906007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“It would be really lame to be out there as a nostalgia act or doing it for the money,” says \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/videos/entertainment/entertainthis/2022/05/26/heres-what-mick-jagger-rolling-stones-taught-def-leppard/9943551002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDef Leppard guitarist Phil Collen\u003c/a\u003e, who noted that “Just Like 73” will be on the new set list alongside evergreen fist-pumpers \u0026#34;Pour Some Sugar On Me,\u0026#34; \u0026#34;Photograph\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;Armageddon It.\u0026#34; “We got into music because we wanted to be in a band, and for us, (playing live) is very easy because you still really want to do it.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eDef Leppard \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/12/07/def-leppard-journey-2024-tour-dates-tickets/71833067007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ewill share this summer’s stadium stretch\u003c/a\u003e, which kicks off July 6, with Journey. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/08/25/steve-miller-santana-grateful-dead-and-the-san-francisco-sounds/70678021007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eThe Steve Miller Band \u003c/a\u003eoccupies a regular opening slot, and Cheap Trick and Heart will dot other dates with their melodic guitar rock.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eJourney is never far from a spotlight, with “Faithfully” still landing on prom night playlists and, of course, the self-generating popularity of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003d1k8craCGpgs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“Don’t Stop Believin’,” \u003c/a\u003ewhich will live on as long as new generations discover “The Sopranos.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThough the band released the album “Freedom” in 2022, they plan to hit rewind/repeat on the vintage tape deck this tour.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThanks to the “great chemistry” shared between not just the members of both chart-topping, guitar-forward bands but also their audiences, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/07/08/neal-schon-interview-journey-album-freedom/7807287001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eJourney guitarist and co-founder Neal Schon\u003c/a\u003e expects sold-out sing-a-longs across the nation this summer.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2022/03/17/def-leppard-recruits-alison-krauss-12-th-album-out-may-marc-bolan-t-rex/7068347001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDef Leppard\u003c/a\u003e had a lot of radio success at the same time we did, so history kind of puts us together,” Schon says. “We first met them many years back when they first broke, but you immediately admire people in your same rock arena who are clearly the real deal.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eIs rock ‘n’ roll dead? Yes. No. Maybe? But enjoy it this summer \u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eMost of the artists sweating for your entertainment this summer are close to, if not in, AARP territory – Lavigne is a relative youngster at 39 – and the debate continues about the current state of rock ‘n’ roll and who might maintain longevity to fill amphitheaters and stadiums in 20 years.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/08/04/wolfgang-van-halen-interview-mammoth-wvh-album-his-parents-and-love-of-cats/70452253007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eMammoth WVH with Wolfgang Van Halen\u003c/a\u003e is the type of rock outfit carrying an old-fashioned torch as they open stadiums with Metallica, play club shows in between and will join Creed for a fall arena run.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "72462552007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eGreta Van Fleet spans the globe this summer at a combination of festivals, theaters and arenas, and Dorothy, fronted by\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dcg2P3MH5WYs\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e singer Dorothy Martin\u003c/a\u003e (who duets with Stapp on his single \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v\u003dxTAUdWoASNQ\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e“If These Walls Could Talk”\u003c/a\u003e) is the kind of power-lunged belter who makes you nearly blow a speaker.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eCollen believes rock is more of an idea – “People love the idea of a rock star,” he says – and artists he considers rock icons, such as Jimi Hendrix, Mick Jagger \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2021/07/03/jim-morrison-quotes-the-doors-frontman-death-anniversary/5297160001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eand Jim Morrison\u003c/a\u003e, have no one in their shadows.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“You’re got getting new versions of that,” Collen says. “I think the image part of rock is dead.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/06/14/songwriters-hall-of-fame-rem-performance-video/74095830007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eR.E.M. performs together for first time in nearly 20 years\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eStapp, meanwhile, points to country music and the cross-pollination of rock and country as a meaningful migration.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“In a weird way, the country music scene is reinvigorating rock,” he says.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe future of rock might be hazy, but for now, there are plenty of guitar amps ready to be turned to 11.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eSo for those who still want to rock, we salute you.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73923806007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhen Napster made its debut in June 1999, few knew its potential impact. The software would let you share music files online for free, but at the time consumers were still buying hundreds of millions of music CDs each year.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eNapster certainly helped sunset the CD. Once you downloaded the software, you could connect with other music lovers and peruse the collection of digital music tracks ripped onto and stored on their computers – and download them for free.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhen music industry executives and attorneys saw how Napster could connect a potentially endless legion of the CD-buying public, they \u0026#34;were shocked beyond belief.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;They had figured that the Compact Disc cash cow would go on forever, and now they saw its sudden demise,\u0026#34; said Ken Pohlmann, professor emeritus at the University of Miami and author of \u0026#34;Principles of Digital Audio,\u0026#34; who is also an electrical engineer and a technical consultant during those discussions. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHalf of the executives were saying, “The world is ending,” while the others said, “Why didn\u0026#39;t we think of that?” said Pohlmann, who is also a columnist for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.soundandvision.com/index.html\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.soundandvision.com/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSound \u0026amp; Vision\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026#34;A few of the smartest executives realized that once Napster was shut down, they could appropriate the online distribution model and make a fortune.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd that\u0026#39;s what happened: Napster was forced to shut down and the record labels and Hollywood began revamping how music, movies and other forms of entertainment would be distributed to consumers.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHere are four ways the original file-sharing site transformed the entertainment industry.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eBruce Springsteen: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/05/27/bruce-springsteen-postpones-concerts-vocal-issues/73868208007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSinger-songwriter and E Street postpone four European concerts amid \u0026#39;vocal issues\u0026#39;\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNapster introduced music lovers to digitally-delivered music\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eConsumers were spending more than $25 billion a year on recorded music when Napster began to become popular. As the software spread, colleges began shutting off access to Napster because it was clogging their networks.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eNapster “mainstreamed an underground hobby,” Joseph Menn, author of \u0026#34;All the Rave: The Rise and Fall of Shawn Fanning\u0026#39;s Napster,\u0026#34; told \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-2001-sep-25-fi-49428-story.html\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-2001-sep-25-fi-49428-story.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eThe Los Angeles Times\u003c/a\u003e in May 2024. \u0026#34;No one is going to go out and buy 100 records, but here the supply of music was infinite. It was always a social lubricant to make a mixtape for someone you wanted to date. Now you could do that at scale.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd the fledgling software company also flipped the business model of recorded music. \u0026#34;It wasn\u0026#39;t necessary to replicate millions of copies – manufacturing, distributing, and retailing each of them,\u0026#34; Pohlmann said. \u0026#34;Instead, one file could be placed online, and simultaneously sold to as many people as wanted to buy it. The benefit for the customer was obvious – the price could be cheaper, and the convenience was incredible.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "71811658007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNapster changed how music is sold\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhile Napster didn\u0026#39;t directly cause each music consumer to change their ways, it signaled a coming change in music sales.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn 1999, when Napster launched, music CD sales accounted for $23.4 billion, or nearly 88% of recorded music revenue, according to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.riaa.com/u-s-sales-database/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.riaa.com/u-s-sales-database/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eRecording Industry Association of America\u003c/a\u003e. Overall, 1999 represented peak recorded music revenues, according to RIAA, of $26.7 billion. CD sales would begin a decline to $537.1 million in 2023. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Napster was the beginning of the end for record stores selling physical media such as LPs, cassettes, and CDs,\u0026#34; Pohlmann said. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73927811007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNapster disrupted how music artists made a living\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMany artists relied on sales of recorded music to keep at their craft and Napster led them to come out against its business model: their music traded freely.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Musicians love the idea of all music being available to all people, but without fair payment, many musicians would have to find other ways to make a living,\u0026#34; said singer Peter Gabriel at the time in a statement through the group Artists Against Piracy.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73914388007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut even then, indie artists sang a different tune. At the time of Napster\u0026#39;s emergence \u0026#34;I made my modest living as a punk rock musician and record label owner,\u0026#39; wrote Jenny Toomey in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.fastcompany.com/91119990/where-the-human-brain-still-has-an-edge-over-ai\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.fastcompany.com/91119990/where-the-human-brain-still-has-an-edge-over-ai\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eFast Company\u003c/a\u003e in March 2024. After playing in bands such as Grenadine and Tsunami, she co-founded the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://www.simplemachines.net/story.html\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"http://www.simplemachines.net/story.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSimple Machines\u003c/a\u003e label. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThen, if a band sold 10,000 copies of an album, it could earn about $50,000 in revenue, Toomey said. \u0026#34;Today, that band’s entire album would have to be streamed a million times for the same financial return,\u0026#34; said Toomey, who finds similarities in the tech industries\u0026#39; current drive to push AI and the digital music transformation of the early 2000s.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;We quickly learned the so-called tech revolution in music was never designed to deliver for us,\u0026#34; Toomey writes. \u0026#34;Instead of enabling artists to live off their work, most musicians’ income from physical media like CDs and records \u003ca href\u003d\"https://url.us.m.mimecastprotect.com/s/7EUnCKr7JZf476ONZInRRa-?domain\u003dnytimes.com\"\u003etanked\u003c/a\u003e, and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://url.us.m.mimecastprotect.com/s/JKBdCL91K8fQB7KrlI1sYco?domain\u003dfastcompany.com\"\u003edigital royalties\u003c/a\u003e paid fractions of pennies on the dollar. Today, I can see this history repeating itself across every sector.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eArtists such as \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/04/20/record-store-day-2024-vinyl-records/73390177007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/04/20/record-store-day-2024-vinyl-records/73390177007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eTaylor Swift\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/04/08/beyonce-cowboy-carter-album-tops-billboard-charts/73245512007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/04/08/beyonce-cowboy-carter-album-tops-billboard-charts/73245512007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eBeyoncé\u003c/a\u003e are not the norm, as artists who not only sell huge amounts of albums and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/10/12/taylor-swift-eras-tour-movie-film-business-economy-sales/71152131007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/10/12/taylor-swift-eras-tour-movie-film-business-economy-sales/71152131007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003esell out stadiums\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003e‘Ayuda por favor’: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/05/30/taylor-swift-tells-workers-to-get-water-to-fans-in-spain/73867526007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eTaylor Swift tells workers multiple times to get water to fans in Spain\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eLive performances have become the key revenue driver for most musical artists – even for smaller acts, which can sell merchandise, even vinyl albums and CDs, at shows. Big name artists always relied heavily on live performances. For instance, U2, the highest-paid musical act of 2017 in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.billboard.com/photos/billboards-2018-money-makers-50-highest-paid-musicians/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.billboard.com/photos/billboards-2018-money-makers-50-highest-paid-musicians/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eBillboard\u0026#39;s annual report\u003c/a\u003e, made $54.4 million that year, with about 95%, or $52 million, from touring, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.businessinsider.com/how-do-musicians-make-money-2018-10\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.businessinsider.com/how-do-musicians-make-money-2018-10\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eBusiness Insider reported\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73884752007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDave Matthews, front man of the Dave Matthews Band, had concerns about the impending digital age of music, but told USA TODAY at the time, \u0026#34;I don\u0026#39;t feel threatened financially by the collapse of the industry,\u0026#34; he said. \u0026#34;The vast majority of my living is made from touring. Nobody\u0026#39;s going to be able to download that.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNapster ushered in the future of streaming music and movies \u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn addition to whetting consumers\u0026#39; appetite for digitally-delivered music, Napster foreshadowed the potential of a \u0026#34;celestial jukebox\u0026#34; or a \u0026#34;jukebox in the sky\u0026#34; being fulfilled by today\u0026#39;s music streaming services.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEven though the original Napster \u0026#34;was an illegal enterprise that was the music industry\u0026#39;s worst nightmare, (the network) was also a stroke of genius that perfectly illustrated the future of their industry,\u0026#34; Pohlmann said. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs home and mobile broadband connections evolved, streaming services such as \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/tech/talkingtech/2018/04/03/spotify-goes-public-what-you-need-know-music-streamer-and-its-ipo/480318002/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/tech/talkingtech/2018/04/03/spotify-goes-public-what-you-need-know-music-streamer-and-its-ipo/480318002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSpotify\u003c/a\u003e arrived on the scene. Next, came streaming video players such as Netflix and video game streaming services such PlayStation Plus and Xbox Game Pass Ultimate. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "1410095"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eToday, most consumers get their music from streaming services. Streaming has helped recorded music revenues climb from lows of $8.6 billion in 2015 and 2016, the RIAA says, to $17.1 billion in 2023. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eConsumers spent $10.1 billion on music streaming subscriptions in 2023 – 59.3% of all recorded music revenue, according to the RIAA.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBoth vinyl albums and CDs have shown some resilience as formats, perhaps because some consumers still appreciate the tactile nature of ownership.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73927852007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eContributing: Edna Gundersen.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eFollow Mike Snider on X and Threads: \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://twitter.com/MikeSnider\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003e@mikesnider\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e \u0026amp;\u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.threads.net/@mikegsnider\"\u003e \u003cem\u003emikegsnider\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat\u0026#39;s everyone talking about?\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://profile.usatoday.com/newsletters/everyones-talking/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSign up for our trending newsletter to get the latest news of the day\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73923806007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhen Napster made its debut in June 1999, few knew its potential impact. The software would let you share music files online for free, but at the time consumers were still buying hundreds of millions of music CDs each year.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eNapster certainly helped sunset the CD. Once you downloaded the software, you could connect with other music lovers and peruse the collection of digital music tracks ripped onto and stored on their computers – and download them for free.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhen music industry executives and attorneys saw how Napster could connect a potentially endless legion of the CD-buying public, they \u0026#34;were shocked beyond belief.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;They had figured that the Compact Disc cash cow would go on forever, and now they saw its sudden demise,\u0026#34; said Ken Pohlmann, professor emeritus at the University of Miami and author of \u0026#34;Principles of Digital Audio,\u0026#34; who is also an electrical engineer and a technical consultant during those discussions. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHalf of the executives were saying, “The world is ending,” while the others said, “Why didn\u0026#39;t we think of that?” said Pohlmann, who is also a columnist for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.soundandvision.com/index.html\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.soundandvision.com/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSound \u0026amp; Vision\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026#34;A few of the smartest executives realized that once Napster was shut down, they could appropriate the online distribution model and make a fortune.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd that\u0026#39;s what happened: Napster was forced to shut down and the record labels and Hollywood began revamping how music, movies and other forms of entertainment would be distributed to consumers.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHere are four ways the original file-sharing site transformed the entertainment industry.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eBruce Springsteen: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/05/27/bruce-springsteen-postpones-concerts-vocal-issues/73868208007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSinger-songwriter and E Street postpone four European concerts amid \u0026#39;vocal issues\u0026#39;\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNapster introduced music lovers to digitally-delivered music\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eConsumers were spending more than $25 billion a year on recorded music when Napster began to become popular. As the software spread, colleges began shutting off access to Napster because it was clogging their networks.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eNapster “mainstreamed an underground hobby,” Joseph Menn, author of \u0026#34;All the Rave: The Rise and Fall of Shawn Fanning\u0026#39;s Napster,\u0026#34; told \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-2001-sep-25-fi-49428-story.html\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-2001-sep-25-fi-49428-story.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eThe Los Angeles Times\u003c/a\u003e in May 2024. \u0026#34;No one is going to go out and buy 100 records, but here the supply of music was infinite. It was always a social lubricant to make a mixtape for someone you wanted to date. Now you could do that at scale.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd the fledgling software company also flipped the business model of recorded music. \u0026#34;It wasn\u0026#39;t necessary to replicate millions of copies – manufacturing, distributing, and retailing each of them,\u0026#34; Pohlmann said. \u0026#34;Instead, one file could be placed online, and simultaneously sold to as many people as wanted to buy it. The benefit for the customer was obvious – the price could be cheaper, and the convenience was incredible.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "71811658007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNapster changed how music is sold\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhile Napster didn\u0026#39;t directly cause each music consumer to change their ways, it signaled a coming change in music sales.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn 1999, when Napster launched, music CD sales accounted for $23.4 billion, or nearly 88% of recorded music revenue, according to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.riaa.com/u-s-sales-database/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.riaa.com/u-s-sales-database/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eRecording Industry Association of America\u003c/a\u003e. Overall, 1999 represented peak recorded music revenues, according to RIAA, of $26.7 billion. CD sales would begin a decline to $537.1 million in 2023. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Napster was the beginning of the end for record stores selling physical media such as LPs, cassettes, and CDs,\u0026#34; Pohlmann said. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73927811007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNapster disrupted how music artists made a living\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMany artists relied on sales of recorded music to keep at their craft and Napster led them to come out against its business model: their music traded freely.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Musicians love the idea of all music being available to all people, but without fair payment, many musicians would have to find other ways to make a living,\u0026#34; said singer Peter Gabriel at the time in a statement through the group Artists Against Piracy.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73914388007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut even then, indie artists sang a different tune. At the time of Napster\u0026#39;s emergence \u0026#34;I made my modest living as a punk rock musician and record label owner,\u0026#39; wrote Jenny Toomey in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.fastcompany.com/91119990/where-the-human-brain-still-has-an-edge-over-ai\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.fastcompany.com/91119990/where-the-human-brain-still-has-an-edge-over-ai\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eFast Company\u003c/a\u003e in March 2024. After playing in bands such as Grenadine and Tsunami, she co-founded the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://www.simplemachines.net/story.html\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"http://www.simplemachines.net/story.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSimple Machines\u003c/a\u003e label. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThen, if a band sold 10,000 copies of an album, it could earn about $50,000 in revenue, Toomey said. \u0026#34;Today, that band’s entire album would have to be streamed a million times for the same financial return,\u0026#34; said Toomey, who finds similarities in the tech industries\u0026#39; current drive to push AI and the digital music transformation of the early 2000s.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;We quickly learned the so-called tech revolution in music was never designed to deliver for us,\u0026#34; Toomey writes. \u0026#34;Instead of enabling artists to live off their work, most musicians’ income from physical media like CDs and records \u003ca href\u003d\"https://url.us.m.mimecastprotect.com/s/7EUnCKr7JZf476ONZInRRa-?domain\u003dnytimes.com\"\u003etanked\u003c/a\u003e, and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://url.us.m.mimecastprotect.com/s/JKBdCL91K8fQB7KrlI1sYco?domain\u003dfastcompany.com\"\u003edigital royalties\u003c/a\u003e paid fractions of pennies on the dollar. Today, I can see this history repeating itself across every sector.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eArtists such as \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/04/20/record-store-day-2024-vinyl-records/73390177007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/04/20/record-store-day-2024-vinyl-records/73390177007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eTaylor Swift\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/04/08/beyonce-cowboy-carter-album-tops-billboard-charts/73245512007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/04/08/beyonce-cowboy-carter-album-tops-billboard-charts/73245512007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eBeyoncé\u003c/a\u003e are not the norm, as artists who not only sell huge amounts of albums and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/10/12/taylor-swift-eras-tour-movie-film-business-economy-sales/71152131007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/10/12/taylor-swift-eras-tour-movie-film-business-economy-sales/71152131007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003esell out stadiums\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003e‘Ayuda por favor’: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/05/30/taylor-swift-tells-workers-to-get-water-to-fans-in-spain/73867526007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eTaylor Swift tells workers multiple times to get water to fans in Spain\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eLive performances have become the key revenue driver for most musical artists – even for smaller acts, which can sell merchandise, even vinyl albums and CDs, at shows. Big name artists always relied heavily on live performances. For instance, U2, the highest-paid musical act of 2017 in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.billboard.com/photos/billboards-2018-money-makers-50-highest-paid-musicians/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.billboard.com/photos/billboards-2018-money-makers-50-highest-paid-musicians/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eBillboard\u0026#39;s annual report\u003c/a\u003e, made $54.4 million that year, with about 95%, or $52 million, from touring, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.businessinsider.com/how-do-musicians-make-money-2018-10\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.businessinsider.com/how-do-musicians-make-money-2018-10\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eBusiness Insider reported\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73884752007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDave Matthews, front man of the Dave Matthews Band, had concerns about the impending digital age of music, but told USA TODAY at the time, \u0026#34;I don\u0026#39;t feel threatened financially by the collapse of the industry,\u0026#34; he said. \u0026#34;The vast majority of my living is made from touring. Nobody\u0026#39;s going to be able to download that.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNapster ushered in the future of streaming music and movies \u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn addition to whetting consumers\u0026#39; appetite for digitally-delivered music, Napster foreshadowed the potential of a \u0026#34;celestial jukebox\u0026#34; or a \u0026#34;jukebox in the sky\u0026#34; being fulfilled by today\u0026#39;s music streaming services.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEven though the original Napster \u0026#34;was an illegal enterprise that was the music industry\u0026#39;s worst nightmare, (the network) was also a stroke of genius that perfectly illustrated the future of their industry,\u0026#34; Pohlmann said. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs home and mobile broadband connections evolved, streaming services such as \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/tech/talkingtech/2018/04/03/spotify-goes-public-what-you-need-know-music-streamer-and-its-ipo/480318002/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/tech/talkingtech/2018/04/03/spotify-goes-public-what-you-need-know-music-streamer-and-its-ipo/480318002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSpotify\u003c/a\u003e arrived on the scene. Next, came streaming video players such as Netflix and video game streaming services such PlayStation Plus and Xbox Game Pass Ultimate. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "1410095"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eToday, most consumers get their music from streaming services. Streaming has helped recorded music revenues climb from lows of $8.6 billion in 2015 and 2016, the RIAA says, to $17.1 billion in 2023. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eConsumers spent $10.1 billion on music streaming subscriptions in 2023 – 59.3% of all recorded music revenue, according to the RIAA.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBoth vinyl albums and CDs have shown some resilience as formats, perhaps because some consumers still appreciate the tactile nature of ownership.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73927852007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eContributing: Edna Gundersen.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eFollow Mike Snider on X and Threads: \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://twitter.com/MikeSnider\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003e@mikesnider\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e \u0026amp;\u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.threads.net/@mikegsnider\"\u003e \u003cem\u003emikegsnider\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat\u0026#39;s everyone talking about?\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://profile.usatoday.com/newsletters/everyones-talking/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSign up for our trending newsletter to get the latest news of the day\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

contentBody:
{
  "contentBody": [{
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73923806007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhen Napster made its debut in June 1999, few knew its potential impact. The software would let you share music files online for free, but at the time consumers were still buying hundreds of millions of music CDs each year.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eNapster certainly helped sunset the CD. Once you downloaded the software, you could connect with other music lovers and peruse the collection of digital music tracks ripped onto and stored on their computers – and download them for free.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhen music industry executives and attorneys saw how Napster could connect a potentially endless legion of the CD-buying public, they \u0026#34;were shocked beyond belief.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;They had figured that the Compact Disc cash cow would go on forever, and now they saw its sudden demise,\u0026#34; said Ken Pohlmann, professor emeritus at the University of Miami and author of \u0026#34;Principles of Digital Audio,\u0026#34; who is also an electrical engineer and a technical consultant during those discussions. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eHalf of the executives were saying, “The world is ending,” while the others said, “Why didn\u0026#39;t we think of that?” said Pohlmann, who is also a columnist for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.soundandvision.com/index.html\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.soundandvision.com/index.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSound \u0026amp; Vision\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026#34;A few of the smartest executives realized that once Napster was shut down, they could appropriate the online distribution model and make a fortune.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd that\u0026#39;s what happened: Napster was forced to shut down and the record labels and Hollywood began revamping how music, movies and other forms of entertainment would be distributed to consumers.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eHere are four ways the original file-sharing site transformed the entertainment industry.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eBruce Springsteen: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/05/27/bruce-springsteen-postpones-concerts-vocal-issues/73868208007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSinger-songwriter and E Street postpone four European concerts amid \u0026#39;vocal issues\u0026#39;\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNapster introduced music lovers to digitally-delivered music\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eConsumers were spending more than $25 billion a year on recorded music when Napster began to become popular. As the software spread, colleges began shutting off access to Napster because it was clogging their networks.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eNapster “mainstreamed an underground hobby,” Joseph Menn, author of \u0026#34;All the Rave: The Rise and Fall of Shawn Fanning\u0026#39;s Napster,\u0026#34; told \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-2001-sep-25-fi-49428-story.html\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.latimes.com/archives/la-xpm-2001-sep-25-fi-49428-story.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eThe Los Angeles Times\u003c/a\u003e in May 2024. \u0026#34;No one is going to go out and buy 100 records, but here the supply of music was infinite. It was always a social lubricant to make a mixtape for someone you wanted to date. Now you could do that at scale.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd the fledgling software company also flipped the business model of recorded music. \u0026#34;It wasn\u0026#39;t necessary to replicate millions of copies – manufacturing, distributing, and retailing each of them,\u0026#34; Pohlmann said. \u0026#34;Instead, one file could be placed online, and simultaneously sold to as many people as wanted to buy it. The benefit for the customer was obvious – the price could be cheaper, and the convenience was incredible.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "71811658007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNapster changed how music is sold\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhile Napster didn\u0026#39;t directly cause each music consumer to change their ways, it signaled a coming change in music sales.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn 1999, when Napster launched, music CD sales accounted for $23.4 billion, or nearly 88% of recorded music revenue, according to the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.riaa.com/u-s-sales-database/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.riaa.com/u-s-sales-database/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eRecording Industry Association of America\u003c/a\u003e. Overall, 1999 represented peak recorded music revenues, according to RIAA, of $26.7 billion. CD sales would begin a decline to $537.1 million in 2023. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Napster was the beginning of the end for record stores selling physical media such as LPs, cassettes, and CDs,\u0026#34; Pohlmann said. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73927811007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNapster disrupted how music artists made a living\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eMany artists relied on sales of recorded music to keep at their craft and Napster led them to come out against its business model: their music traded freely.  \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Musicians love the idea of all music being available to all people, but without fair payment, many musicians would have to find other ways to make a living,\u0026#34; said singer Peter Gabriel at the time in a statement through the group Artists Against Piracy.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73914388007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut even then, indie artists sang a different tune. At the time of Napster\u0026#39;s emergence \u0026#34;I made my modest living as a punk rock musician and record label owner,\u0026#39; wrote Jenny Toomey in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.fastcompany.com/91119990/where-the-human-brain-still-has-an-edge-over-ai\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.fastcompany.com/91119990/where-the-human-brain-still-has-an-edge-over-ai\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eFast Company\u003c/a\u003e in March 2024. After playing in bands such as Grenadine and Tsunami, she co-founded the \u003ca href\u003d\"http://www.simplemachines.net/story.html\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"http://www.simplemachines.net/story.html\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSimple Machines\u003c/a\u003e label. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThen, if a band sold 10,000 copies of an album, it could earn about $50,000 in revenue, Toomey said. \u0026#34;Today, that band’s entire album would have to be streamed a million times for the same financial return,\u0026#34; said Toomey, who finds similarities in the tech industries\u0026#39; current drive to push AI and the digital music transformation of the early 2000s.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;We quickly learned the so-called tech revolution in music was never designed to deliver for us,\u0026#34; Toomey writes. \u0026#34;Instead of enabling artists to live off their work, most musicians’ income from physical media like CDs and records \u003ca href\u003d\"https://url.us.m.mimecastprotect.com/s/7EUnCKr7JZf476ONZInRRa-?domain\u003dnytimes.com\"\u003etanked\u003c/a\u003e, and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://url.us.m.mimecastprotect.com/s/JKBdCL91K8fQB7KrlI1sYco?domain\u003dfastcompany.com\"\u003edigital royalties\u003c/a\u003e paid fractions of pennies on the dollar. Today, I can see this history repeating itself across every sector.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eArtists such as \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/04/20/record-store-day-2024-vinyl-records/73390177007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/04/20/record-store-day-2024-vinyl-records/73390177007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eTaylor Swift\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/04/08/beyonce-cowboy-carter-album-tops-billboard-charts/73245512007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/04/08/beyonce-cowboy-carter-album-tops-billboard-charts/73245512007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eBeyoncé\u003c/a\u003e are not the norm, as artists who not only sell huge amounts of albums and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/10/12/taylor-swift-eras-tour-movie-film-business-economy-sales/71152131007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2023/10/12/taylor-swift-eras-tour-movie-film-business-economy-sales/71152131007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003esell out stadiums\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003e‘Ayuda por favor’: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/music/2024/05/30/taylor-swift-tells-workers-to-get-water-to-fans-in-spain/73867526007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eTaylor Swift tells workers multiple times to get water to fans in Spain\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eLive performances have become the key revenue driver for most musical artists – even for smaller acts, which can sell merchandise, even vinyl albums and CDs, at shows. Big name artists always relied heavily on live performances. For instance, U2, the highest-paid musical act of 2017 in \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.billboard.com/photos/billboards-2018-money-makers-50-highest-paid-musicians/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.billboard.com/photos/billboards-2018-money-makers-50-highest-paid-musicians/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eBillboard\u0026#39;s annual report\u003c/a\u003e, made $54.4 million that year, with about 95%, or $52 million, from touring, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.businessinsider.com/how-do-musicians-make-money-2018-10\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.businessinsider.com/how-do-musicians-make-money-2018-10\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eBusiness Insider reported\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73884752007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eDave Matthews, front man of the Dave Matthews Band, had concerns about the impending digital age of music, but told USA TODAY at the time, \u0026#34;I don\u0026#39;t feel threatened financially by the collapse of the industry,\u0026#34; he said. \u0026#34;The vast majority of my living is made from touring. Nobody\u0026#39;s going to be able to download that.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNapster ushered in the future of streaming music and movies \u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn addition to whetting consumers\u0026#39; appetite for digitally-delivered music, Napster foreshadowed the potential of a \u0026#34;celestial jukebox\u0026#34; or a \u0026#34;jukebox in the sky\u0026#34; being fulfilled by today\u0026#39;s music streaming services.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eEven though the original Napster \u0026#34;was an illegal enterprise that was the music industry\u0026#39;s worst nightmare, (the network) was also a stroke of genius that perfectly illustrated the future of their industry,\u0026#34; Pohlmann said. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs home and mobile broadband connections evolved, streaming services such as \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/tech/talkingtech/2018/04/03/spotify-goes-public-what-you-need-know-music-streamer-and-its-ipo/480318002/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/tech/talkingtech/2018/04/03/spotify-goes-public-what-you-need-know-music-streamer-and-its-ipo/480318002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSpotify\u003c/a\u003e arrived on the scene. Next, came streaming video players such as Netflix and video game streaming services such PlayStation Plus and Xbox Game Pass Ultimate. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "1410095"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eToday, most consumers get their music from streaming services. Streaming has helped recorded music revenues climb from lows of $8.6 billion in 2015 and 2016, the RIAA says, to $17.1 billion in 2023. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eConsumers spent $10.1 billion on music streaming subscriptions in 2023 – 59.3% of all recorded music revenue, according to the RIAA.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBoth vinyl albums and CDs have shown some resilience as formats, perhaps because some consumers still appreciate the tactile nature of ownership.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73927852007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eContributing: Edna Gundersen.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eFollow Mike Snider on X and Threads: \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://twitter.com/MikeSnider\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003e@mikesnider\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e \u0026amp;\u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.threads.net/@mikegsnider\"\u003e \u003cem\u003emikegsnider\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat\u0026#39;s everyone talking about?\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://profile.usatoday.com/newsletters/everyones-talking/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSign up for our trending newsletter to get the latest news of the day\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72402013007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/tv/2024/03/18/oprah-winfrey-weight-loss-drugs-ozempic-abc-special/73023896007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eOprah Winfrey\u003c/a\u003e has made her \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.oprahdaily.com/entertainment/books/a61041337/oprah-book-club-106th-pick/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003elatest book club pick\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn Tuesday, the mogul dubbed \u0026#34;Familiaris\u0026#34; by \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.davidwroblewski.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDavid Wroblewski\u003c/a\u003e, published by Blackstone Publishing and out Tuesday, her latest must-read book.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWinfrey said the \u0026#34;epic novel\u0026#34; goes on a journey that \u0026#34;brilliantly interweaves history, philosophy, adventure, and mysticism to explore the meaning of love, friendship, and living your life\u0026#39;s true purpose.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Familiaris\u0026#34; is the 106th \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/picture-gallery/entertainment/books/2019/09/17/oprahs-book-club-complete-list/2210970001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eOprah\u0026#39;s Book Club\u003c/a\u003e selection and is the follow-up to the Wisconsin-born novelist\u0026#39;s 2008 debut, \u0026#34;The Story of Edgar Sawtelle,\u0026#34; another book club pick.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74137694007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;It\u0026#39;s an honor almost beyond fathoming,\u0026#34; Wroblewski told \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.oprahdaily.com/entertainment/books/a61041337/oprah-book-club-106th-pick/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eOprahDaily.com\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026#34;Oprah has become our advocate in chief for the reading of literature, and the roster of talent and titles she has curated for readers over the years is humbling. I am, to put it mildly, thrilled and grateful.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHe continued: \u0026#34;I\u0026#39;m looking forward to discussing this story, whose characters have been part of my imaginative life for so long.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe 992-page prequel novel to \u0026#34;The Story of Edgar Sawtelle\u0026#34; is also endorsed by one \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2024/06/07/tom-hanks-d-day-anniversary-saving-private-ryan-impact/74010870007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eTom Hanks\u003c/a\u003e, who wrote in a blurb that \u0026#34;Wroblewski has set a storytelling bonfire\u0026#34; and the book \u0026#34;is as expansive and enlightening a saga as has ever been written.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eOprah  \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/books/2023/03/14/oprah-winfrey-book-club-100th-pick-ann-napolitano-hello-beautiful/11469581002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003esays her 100th book club pick \u0026#39;Hello Beautiful\u0026#39; is \u0026#39;one of the best books I\u0026#39;ve read\u0026#39;\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "2210970001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWeekly discussions of the book are set to begin later this month on Oprah\u0026#39;s Book Club \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/p/C8E4my1oy1r/?utm_source\u003dig_web_copy_link\u0026igsh\u003dMzRlODBiNWFlZA\u003d\u003d\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003esocial media pages\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOther recent Oprah\u0026#39;s Book Club selections include \u0026#34;Let Us Descend\u0026#34; by Jesmyn Ward, \u0026#34;Wellness\u0026#34; by Nathan Hill and \u0026#34;The Covenant of Water\u0026#34; by Abraham Verghese.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWinfrey marked her 100th book club milestone with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/books/2023/03/14/oprah-winfrey-book-club-100th-pick-ann-napolitano-hello-beautiful/11469581002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u0026#34;Hello Beautiful\u0026#34; by Ann Napolitano\u003c/a\u003e, a book that paid homage to Louisa May Alcott\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Little Women\u0026#34; and followed a family of four sisters over three decades in a city meaningful to Winfrey, Chicago. She aired her eponymous talk show for 25 seasons in the Windy City.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eContributing: Elise Brisco\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72402013007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/tv/2024/03/18/oprah-winfrey-weight-loss-drugs-ozempic-abc-special/73023896007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eOprah Winfrey\u003c/a\u003e has made her \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.oprahdaily.com/entertainment/books/a61041337/oprah-book-club-106th-pick/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003elatest book club pick\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn Tuesday, the mogul dubbed \u0026#34;Familiaris\u0026#34; by \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.davidwroblewski.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDavid Wroblewski\u003c/a\u003e, published by Blackstone Publishing and out Tuesday, her latest must-read book.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWinfrey said the \u0026#34;epic novel\u0026#34; goes on a journey that \u0026#34;brilliantly interweaves history, philosophy, adventure, and mysticism to explore the meaning of love, friendship, and living your life\u0026#39;s true purpose.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Familiaris\u0026#34; is the 106th \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/picture-gallery/entertainment/books/2019/09/17/oprahs-book-club-complete-list/2210970001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eOprah\u0026#39;s Book Club\u003c/a\u003e selection and is the follow-up to the Wisconsin-born novelist\u0026#39;s 2008 debut, \u0026#34;The Story of Edgar Sawtelle,\u0026#34; another book club pick.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74137694007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;It\u0026#39;s an honor almost beyond fathoming,\u0026#34; Wroblewski told \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.oprahdaily.com/entertainment/books/a61041337/oprah-book-club-106th-pick/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eOprahDaily.com\u003c/a\u003e. \u0026#34;Oprah has become our advocate in chief for the reading of literature, and the roster of talent and titles she has curated for readers over the years is humbling. I am, to put it mildly, thrilled and grateful.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHe continued: \u0026#34;I\u0026#39;m looking forward to discussing this story, whose characters have been part of my imaginative life for so long.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe 992-page prequel novel to \u0026#34;The Story of Edgar Sawtelle\u0026#34; is also endorsed by one \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/celebrities/2024/06/07/tom-hanks-d-day-anniversary-saving-private-ryan-impact/74010870007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eTom Hanks\u003c/a\u003e, who wrote in a blurb that \u0026#34;Wroblewski has set a storytelling bonfire\u0026#34; and the book \u0026#34;is as expansive and enlightening a saga as has ever been written.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eOprah  \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/books/2023/03/14/oprah-winfrey-book-club-100th-pick-ann-napolitano-hello-beautiful/11469581002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003esays her 100th book club pick \u0026#39;Hello Beautiful\u0026#39; is \u0026#39;one of the best books I\u0026#39;ve read\u0026#39;\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "2210970001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWeekly discussions of the book are set to begin later this month on Oprah\u0026#39;s Book Club \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/p/C8E4my1oy1r/?utm_source\u003dig_web_copy_link\u0026igsh\u003dMzRlODBiNWFlZA\u003d\u003d\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003esocial media pages\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOther recent Oprah\u0026#39;s Book Club selections include \u0026#34;Let Us Descend\u0026#34; by Jesmyn Ward, \u0026#34;Wellness\u0026#34; by Nathan Hill and \u0026#34;The Covenant of Water\u0026#34; by Abraham Verghese.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWinfrey marked her 100th book club milestone with \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/books/2023/03/14/oprah-winfrey-book-club-100th-pick-ann-napolitano-hello-beautiful/11469581002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u0026#34;Hello Beautiful\u0026#34; by Ann Napolitano\u003c/a\u003e, a book that paid homage to Louisa May Alcott\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Little Women\u0026#34; and followed a family of four sisters over three decades in a city meaningful to Winfrey, Chicago. She aired her eponymous talk show for 25 seasons in the Windy City.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eContributing: Elise Brisco\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

