    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eLove movies? Live for TV? USA TODAY\u0026#39;s Watch Party newsletter has all the best recommendations, delivered right to your inbox. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://profile.usatoday.com/newsletters/watch-party/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://profile.usatoday.com/newsletters/watch-party/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSign up now\u003c/a\u003e and be one of the cool kids.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhile a pair of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2024/06/04/bad-boys-ride-or-die-movie-review/73953767007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u0026#34;Bad Boys\u0026#34;\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2024/06/12/inside-out-2-movie-review/74028666007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2024/06/12/inside-out-2-movie-review/74028666007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethe \u0026#34;Inside Out\u0026#34; emotions\u003c/a\u003e heat up the summer box office, you can catch a bunch of cool guys at home: \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2024/06/07/hit-man-movie-2024-glen-powell-interview/73953847007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eGlen Powell\u003c/a\u003e, the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2024/06/07/brats-documentary-andrew-mccarthy-rob-lowe/73991738007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eBrat Pack\u003c/a\u003e and Godzilla. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eNetflix, Peacock, Max, Hulu and Paramount+ have packed June with a plethora of streaming options for film lovers of all tastes, from sci-fi thrillers and action films to an animated Japanese superhero saga. There are recent theatrical releases, like \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2024/04/04/monkey-man-movie-review/73164801007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDev Patel\u0026#39;s two-fisted directorial debut\u003c/a\u003e and a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2024/04/04/first-omen-2024-movie/73164430007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eprequel to 1976\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;The Omen,\u0026#34;\u003c/a\u003e but also original flicks such as a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2024/06/06/am-i-ok-2024-movie-streaming-max/73957941007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDakota Johnson movie\u003c/a\u003e that\u0026#39;s perfect for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/books/2024/06/11/lgbtq-books-for-pride-month/74019135007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ePride Month\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eHere are 10 notable new movies you can stream right now:\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Am I OK?\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "9233131002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2024/02/13/madame-web-movie-review/72573482007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2024/02/13/madame-web-movie-review/72573482007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSkip \u0026#34;Madame Web\u0026#34;\u003c/a\u003e and instead see what Dakota Johnson can really do in this entertaining coming-out comedy. Jane (Sonoya Mizuno) announces she\u0026#39;s moving to London, her bestie Lucy (Johnson) reveals she really likes women, but an argument leaves them navigating these new life paths for the first time without the other in a joyous movie about female friendship.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere to watch:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://play.max.com/movie/ac037e4c-0b87-4865-9235-c86b98f806c2\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eMax\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Brats\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73677808007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eHere\u0026#39;s the thing about the Brat Pack: They \u003cem\u003ehated\u003c/em\u003e being called the Brat Pack. In an effort to make peace with the past, director Andrew McCarthy \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2024/06/13/andrew-mccarthy-documentary-brat-pack-reunites/74051735007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2024/06/13/andrew-mccarthy-documentary-brat-pack-reunites/74051735007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ereconnects with pals/actors Rob Lowe, Demi Moore, Ally Sheedy and others\u003c/a\u003e to discuss their \u0026#39;80s movie heyday. The really interesting parts of the documentary dig into the actors\u0026#39; influence on the era and McCarthy\u0026#39;s meetup with the writer who coined the group\u0026#39;s infamous nickname.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere to watch:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.hulu.com/movie/3c92789a-4a02-418b-b896-28f9799be387\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eHulu\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;The First Omen\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73183428007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn the demonically effective \u0026#34;Omen\u0026#34; prequel, Nell Tiger Free stars as a young American novitiate at an Italian orphanage who becomes protective of a teen girl (Nicole Sorace) and gets caught up in a shady Catholic Church conspiracy to birth the antichrist. Come for the nun horror and a jaw-droppingly gonzo finale, stay for the feminist undertones and timely take on religion.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere to watch:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.hulu.com/movie/e03e7f1a-d1e4-486f-9d19-ff11f955e7c1\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eHulu\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73427001007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Godzilla Minus One\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "71817272007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe American \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2024/03/28/godzilla-x-kong-movie-interview/73093626007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eMonsterVerse Godzilla\u003c/a\u003e movies have been pretty decent, but this rousing and thoughtful Japanese post-war epic stomps them all. This year\u0026#39;s Oscar winner for visual effects – for real, the G-man has never looked better – is a terrific human tale about a former kamikaze pilot (Ryunosuke Kamiki) navigating survivor\u0026#39;s guilt who\u0026#39;s recruited for a desperate mission to save Tokyo from the rampaging reptilian icon.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere to watch: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.netflix.com/title/81767635\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eNetflix\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Hit Man\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74040193007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eDirector Richard Linklater\u0026#39;s sexy and enjoyably noir \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2024/06/10/hit-man-movie-fact-check-true-story/74045960007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ecomedy/romance/thriller\u003c/a\u003e allows Hollywood \u0026#34;It\u0026#34; dude Glen Powell to shine in his most wide-ranging role to date. A nerdy philosophy professor (Powell) moonlights as a killer for hire on crime stings and winds up falling for a \u0026#34;client\u0026#34; (Adria Arjona) who\u0026#39;d like him to off her hubby in a sneakily deep tale about identity and finding the way to your best self.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere to watch:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.netflix.com/title/81728840\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eNetflix\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;I.S.S.\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "72242507007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;West Side Story\u0026#34; standout Ariana DeBose doesn\u0026#39;t sing but does get shot into space in this star vehicle. The \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2024/01/17/iss-movie-review/72240940007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003escrappy sci-fi thriller\u003c/a\u003e casts the Oscar winner as an astronaut and newest crew member on the International Space Station. Something bad happens on Earth, causing lots of friction between Americans and Russians onboard in a gripping tale full of screwdrivers, a doomsday scenario and some good ol\u0026#39; Cold War-era tension.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere to watch: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.paramountplus.com/movies/video/A1BHotGrdlQFhfsYLsoeJG1iDZR53na0/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eParamount+\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Monkey Man\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73200082007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2024/04/03/dev-patel-movie-monkey-man/73091817007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDev Patel\u003c/a\u003e\u0026#39;s directorial debut is doubly impressive, crafting a \u0026#34;Rocky\u0026#34;-esque underdog tale that dives into Indian mythology and also proving himself the coolest new action hero on the block. His vengeful main character attacks goons with fireworks, platform shoes and all manner of sharp objects in an effort to take on powerful figures and also avenge the murder of his mom.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere to watch:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.peacocktv.com/watch/asset/movies/monkey-man/1d05f6ac-083f-3542-8597-c602c8ea0346\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ePeacock\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73185236007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Perfect Days\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74040110007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIf your kids show interest in a film with subtitles, this delightfully minimalist Japanese drama is a perfect gateway movie. Hiriyama (Koji Yakusho) is content with his daily life of tooling around Tokyo, cleaning public bathrooms, taking pictures of trees and listening to his beloved classic rock cassettes. It\u0026#39;s the interactions, though, with a slacker co-worker, his runaway niece and others, that unlock the complex personality of a quietly honorable man.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere to watch: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.hulu.com/movie/a68e2d56-eeb8-44f3-baaa-3ddb850bb67b\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eHulu\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Ultraman: Rising\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74040191007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eUltraman has been a pop-culture superhero staple in Japan since the 1960s, akin to our Superman. This new animated adventure is an enjoyable reboot for a new generation of kid fans (and adult newbies). Ken Sato (voiced by Christopher Sean) is a star baseball player who returned to his homeland to take over the Ultraman mantle from his dad, but his life gets extra messy when he becomes the reluctant adoptive father of a baby kaiju.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere to watch:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.netflix.com/title/81007144\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eNetflix\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Under Paris\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74040194007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eOK, \u0026#39;fess up: Who had \u0026#34;best actress nominee stars in a nifty shark movie\u0026#34; on their 2024 movie bingo card? In the bloody and just-campy-enough French thriller, Bérénice Bejo (\u0026#34;The Artist\u0026#34;) plays a scientist who, three years after losing her husband and crew to a finned menace, teams with police when a giant mako shark swims into Paris and turns the catacombs into an all-you-can-eat human buffet on the eve of a triathlon.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhere to watch:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.netflix.com/title/81210788\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eNetflix\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72135520007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eDonald Sutherland,\u003c/a\u003e the versatile Canadian actor whose prolific career in TV shows and movies showed a diverse range, from authority-loathing surgeon \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/opinion/voices/2020/10/30/mash-tv-show-charles-dubin-hawkeye-hope-election-2020-column/6067526002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eHawkeye Pierce\u003c/a\u003e in the \u0026#34;M*A*S*H\u0026#34; movie to authoritarian villain President Snow in \u0026#34;The Hunger Games\u0026#34; franchise, has died. He was 88.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;With a heavy heart, I tell you that my father, Donald Sutherland, has passed away,\u0026#34; his son Kiefer \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/p/C8cgckJJ548/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eposted on social media\u003c/a\u003e Thursday along with a black and white photo of the father-son pair.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHe added: \u0026#34;I personally think one of the most important actors in the history of film. Never daunted by a role, good, bad or ugly. He loved what he did and did what he loved, and one can never ask for more than that. A life well lived.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eShirley Douglas \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2020/04/05/kiefer-sutherland-mother-actress-shirley-douglas-dies-86/2952047001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eKiefer Sutherland pays tribute to \u0026#39;extraordinary\u0026#39; mother dead at 86\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74158626007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eStarring in more than 200 TV and movies, Sutherland beat an indelible and idiosyncratic path during his six-decade career. He was the pot-smoking professor in 1978\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Animal House,\u0026#34; the titular detective John Klute starring alongside then-lover Jane Fonda in the 1971 thriller \u0026#34;Klute,\u0026#34; a pod person in the 1978 horror remake \u0026#34;Invasion of the Body Snatchers,\u0026#34; an 18th-century Venetian explorer in 1976\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Fellini\u0026#39;s Casanova\u0026#34; with director Frederico Fellini, and an embattled father working to save his emotionally troubled upper-middle-class family in \u0026#34;Ordinary People.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“I’ve always had a horizontally organized career,\u0026#34; Sutherland told \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eUSA TODAY\u003c/a\u003e in 2018. \u0026#34;You’ve got a big plate of fruit and cheese, and you can take a piece here and there. You won’t like all of it, but you’ll like some of it.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eDonald Sutherland interview: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"http://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e Playing \u0026#39;cold\u0026#39; billionaire Getty, and a pint-size \u0026#39;Hunger Games\u0026#39; fan\u0026#39;s request\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAn Emmy winner and the patriarch of his own family of actors and entertainment professionals (including son Kiefer Sutherland, star of \u0026#34;24\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;Designated Survivor\u0026#34;), Sutherland is inarguably the greatest Hollywood actor never to earn a single Oscar nomination. He was most egregiously overlooked for his widely praised \u0026#34;Ordinary People\u0026#34; role, which saw screen wife Mary Tyler Moore earn one of six Oscar nominations  — and newcomer Timothy Hutton win one of four Oscars playing Sutherland\u0026#39;s screen son. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJohn Bailey, the cinematographer on \u0026#34;Ordinary People,\u0026#34; helped to correct this wrong as the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences president in 2017, calling Sutherland personally to inform the actor that he would be awarded an honorary Oscar.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Thank you for putting my name on this. This is very important to me, to my family,\u0026#34; Sutherland said from the 2017 \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/movies/2017/11/12/hollywood-bestows-honorary-oscars-governors-awards-amid-sexual-harassment-scandal/856166001/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/movies/2017/11/12/hollywood-bestows-honorary-oscars-governors-awards-amid-sexual-harassment-scandal/856166001/\"\u003eGovernors Awards podium\u003c/a\u003e, looking at his Oscar. \u0026#34;I wish I could say thank you to all the characters I have played, thank them for using their lives to inform my life.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "9233363002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBorn to Dorothy and Frederick Sutherland in the seaport city of Saint John, New Brunswick, the young Sutherland found he was destined for character acting during an eye-opening discussion with his mother.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I went to her, and I said, \u0026#39;Mother, am I good-looking?\u0026#39; And my mother looked at me and went. \u0026#39;Your face has character, Donald.\u0026#39; \u0026#34; Sutherland recalled to\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/60-minutes-the-long-unconventional-career-of-donald-sutherland/\"\u003e \u0026#34;60 Minutes\u0026#34; in 2018.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter studying drama and starring in London stage and TV productions, Sutherland earned the one-line part on \u0026#34;The Dirty Dozen,\u0026#34; portraying goofy felon Vernon Pinkley in an all-star cast that included Lee Marvin, Charles Bronson and Telly Savalas. But when actor Clint Walker declined to do a scene where his character impersonates a general, director Robert Aldrich looked at Sutherland.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "9233265002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;He went, \u0026#39;You with the big ears, you do it.\u0026#39; I don\u0026#39;t think he knew my name. But, you know. It changed my life,\u0026#39; \u0026#34; Sutherland told\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/60-minutes-the-long-unconventional-career-of-donald-sutherland/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e 60 Minutes\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSutherland starred in \u0026#39;The Dirty Dozen\u0026#39; and \u0026#39;Kelly\u0026#39;s Heroes\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSutherland shot into stardom brandishing his own brand of quirky Vietnam War-era contempt in war movie portrayals, starting as convict soldier Vernon Pinkley in \u0026#34;The Dirty Dozen\u0026#34; (1967) and the comical tank driver Sgt. Oddball in the 1970s World War II heist comedy \u0026#34;Kelly\u0026#39;s Heroes.\u0026#34;  He ended the streak as the wise-cracking surgeon in Robert Altman\u0026#39;s 1970 Korean War comedy-drama \u0026#34;M*A*S*H\u0026#34; (Alan Alda portrayed Hawkeye Pierce in the seminal 1970s TV series). \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDuring his starring role as the enigmatic private detective in the neo-noir hit \u0026#34;Klute\u0026#34; (which earned Fonda a best actress Oscar), Sutherland, still married to his second wife \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2020/04/05/kiefer-sutherland-mother-actress-shirley-douglas-dies-86/2952047001/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2020/04/05/kiefer-sutherland-mother-actress-shirley-douglas-dies-86/2952047001/\"\u003eShirley Douglas\u003c/a\u003e (mother of twins Rachel and Kiefer), began his relationship with Fonda. The two hit the road in the 1971 anti-Vietnam War road show for GI\u0026#39;s, the \u0026#34;F.T.A.\u0026#34; (\u0026#34;Free the Army\u0026#34;). But the relationship had crashed and burned by the end of the year.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;It broke my heart. I was eviscerated,\u0026#34; Sutherland told \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.theguardian.com/film/2008/mar/30/television.television\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eThe Guardian \u003c/a\u003ein 2008. \u0026#34;It was a wonderful relationship right up to the point we lived together.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe next year, Sutherland met and married actress Francine Racette. He remained married for the rest of his life and had three sons together: Roeg, Rossif, and Angus Sutherland.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSutherland played villain President Snow in \u0026#39;Hunger Games\u0026#39; \u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe actor had a particular skill for playing villains, a spy in 1981\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Eye of the Needle\u0026#34; a sadistic warden in 1989\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Lock Up\u0026#34; a scheming software CEO in 1994\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Disclosure\u0026#34; opposite Michael Douglas and Demi Moore and the cruel Attila in Bernardo Bertolucci\u0026#39;s Italian epic \u0026#34;1900.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter turning 80, Sutherland took on the role of his most famous villain, President Snow, in \u0026#34;The Hunger Games\u0026#34; — the arch-nemesis to Jennifer Lawrence\u0026#39;s Katniss Everdeen for four box office record-breaking films from 2012-2015.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e \u0026#34;My agent sends me these things because I\u0026#39;m 80 and I still like to know what\u0026#39;s going on,\u0026#34; he told Britain\u0026#39;s \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/film/the-hunger-games-mockingjay-part-2/donald-sutherland-interview/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e\u0026#34;The Telegraph.\u0026#34;\u003c/a\u003e \u0026#34;I hadn\u0026#39;t even heard of the books, but it became patently apparent to me that this was something. It was the first thing I\u0026#39;d read in years that could become a creative political stimulus for young people.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "9207830002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSutherland found a new generation of fans eager to take pictures with him, describing one fan who approached him in an airport. “As we’re waiting for her mother to take the picture, the girl turned and whispered in my ear, ‘Look mean.’ \u0026#34; Sutherland recalled with glee to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\"\u003eUSA Today in 2018\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72087830007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFinally, accepting his Oscar, Sutherland looked over his showbiz family, including Kiefer’s \u0026#34;Veep\u0026#34; actress daughter, Sarah Sutherland, and dedicated the award to his wife Francine: \u0026#34;From whom everything has come, and to whom everything is owed.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHe closed the speech quoting comedian Jack Benny when presented with an honor.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;(Benny) said, as I say to you now, \u0026#39;I don\u0026#39;t deserve this, But I have arthritis, and I don\u0026#39;t deserve that either,\u0026#39;\u0026#34; said Sutherland.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eContributing: Naledi Ushe\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72135520007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eDonald Sutherland,\u003c/a\u003e the versatile Canadian actor whose prolific career in TV shows and movies showed a diverse range, from authority-loathing surgeon \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/opinion/voices/2020/10/30/mash-tv-show-charles-dubin-hawkeye-hope-election-2020-column/6067526002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eHawkeye Pierce\u003c/a\u003e in the \u0026#34;M*A*S*H\u0026#34; movie to authoritarian villain President Snow in \u0026#34;The Hunger Games\u0026#34; franchise, has died. He was 88.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;With a heavy heart, I tell you that my father, Donald Sutherland, has passed away,\u0026#34; his son Kiefer \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/p/C8cgckJJ548/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eposted on social media\u003c/a\u003e Thursday along with a black and white photo of the father-son pair.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHe added: \u0026#34;I personally think one of the most important actors in the history of film. Never daunted by a role, good, bad or ugly. He loved what he did and did what he loved, and one can never ask for more than that. A life well lived.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eShirley Douglas \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2020/04/05/kiefer-sutherland-mother-actress-shirley-douglas-dies-86/2952047001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eKiefer Sutherland pays tribute to \u0026#39;extraordinary\u0026#39; mother dead at 86\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74158626007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eStarring in more than 200 TV and movies, Sutherland beat an indelible and idiosyncratic path during his six-decade career. He was the pot-smoking professor in 1978\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Animal House,\u0026#34; the titular detective John Klute starring alongside then-lover Jane Fonda in the 1971 thriller \u0026#34;Klute,\u0026#34; a pod person in the 1978 horror remake \u0026#34;Invasion of the Body Snatchers,\u0026#34; an 18th-century Venetian explorer in 1976\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Fellini\u0026#39;s Casanova\u0026#34; with director Frederico Fellini, and an embattled father working to save his emotionally troubled upper-middle-class family in \u0026#34;Ordinary People.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“I’ve always had a horizontally organized career,\u0026#34; Sutherland told \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eUSA TODAY\u003c/a\u003e in 2018. \u0026#34;You’ve got a big plate of fruit and cheese, and you can take a piece here and there. You won’t like all of it, but you’ll like some of it.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eDonald Sutherland interview: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"http://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e Playing \u0026#39;cold\u0026#39; billionaire Getty, and a pint-size \u0026#39;Hunger Games\u0026#39; fan\u0026#39;s request\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAn Emmy winner and the patriarch of his own family of actors and entertainment professionals (including son Kiefer Sutherland, star of \u0026#34;24\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;Designated Survivor\u0026#34;), Sutherland is inarguably the greatest Hollywood actor never to earn a single Oscar nomination. He was most egregiously overlooked for his widely praised \u0026#34;Ordinary People\u0026#34; role, which saw screen wife Mary Tyler Moore earn one of six Oscar nominations  — and newcomer Timothy Hutton win one of four Oscars playing Sutherland\u0026#39;s screen son. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJohn Bailey, the cinematographer on \u0026#34;Ordinary People,\u0026#34; helped to correct this wrong as the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences president in 2017, calling Sutherland personally to inform the actor that he would be awarded an honorary Oscar.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Thank you for putting my name on this. This is very important to me, to my family,\u0026#34; Sutherland said from the 2017 \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/movies/2017/11/12/hollywood-bestows-honorary-oscars-governors-awards-amid-sexual-harassment-scandal/856166001/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/movies/2017/11/12/hollywood-bestows-honorary-oscars-governors-awards-amid-sexual-harassment-scandal/856166001/\"\u003eGovernors Awards podium\u003c/a\u003e, looking at his Oscar. \u0026#34;I wish I could say thank you to all the characters I have played, thank them for using their lives to inform my life.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "9233363002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBorn to Dorothy and Frederick Sutherland in the seaport city of Saint John, New Brunswick, the young Sutherland found he was destined for character acting during an eye-opening discussion with his mother.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I went to her, and I said, \u0026#39;Mother, am I good-looking?\u0026#39; And my mother looked at me and went. \u0026#39;Your face has character, Donald.\u0026#39; \u0026#34; Sutherland recalled to\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/60-minutes-the-long-unconventional-career-of-donald-sutherland/\"\u003e \u0026#34;60 Minutes\u0026#34; in 2018.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter studying drama and starring in London stage and TV productions, Sutherland earned the one-line part on \u0026#34;The Dirty Dozen,\u0026#34; portraying goofy felon Vernon Pinkley in an all-star cast that included Lee Marvin, Charles Bronson and Telly Savalas. But when actor Clint Walker declined to do a scene where his character impersonates a general, director Robert Aldrich looked at Sutherland.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "9233265002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;He went, \u0026#39;You with the big ears, you do it.\u0026#39; I don\u0026#39;t think he knew my name. But, you know. It changed my life,\u0026#39; \u0026#34; Sutherland told\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/60-minutes-the-long-unconventional-career-of-donald-sutherland/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e 60 Minutes\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSutherland starred in \u0026#39;The Dirty Dozen\u0026#39; and \u0026#39;Kelly\u0026#39;s Heroes\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSutherland shot into stardom brandishing his own brand of quirky Vietnam War-era contempt in war movie portrayals, starting as convict soldier Vernon Pinkley in \u0026#34;The Dirty Dozen\u0026#34; (1967) and the comical tank driver Sgt. Oddball in the 1970s World War II heist comedy \u0026#34;Kelly\u0026#39;s Heroes.\u0026#34;  He ended the streak as the wise-cracking surgeon in Robert Altman\u0026#39;s 1970 Korean War comedy-drama \u0026#34;M*A*S*H\u0026#34; (Alan Alda portrayed Hawkeye Pierce in the seminal 1970s TV series). \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDuring his starring role as the enigmatic private detective in the neo-noir hit \u0026#34;Klute\u0026#34; (which earned Fonda a best actress Oscar), Sutherland, still married to his second wife \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2020/04/05/kiefer-sutherland-mother-actress-shirley-douglas-dies-86/2952047001/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2020/04/05/kiefer-sutherland-mother-actress-shirley-douglas-dies-86/2952047001/\"\u003eShirley Douglas\u003c/a\u003e (mother of twins Rachel and Kiefer), began his relationship with Fonda. The two hit the road in the 1971 anti-Vietnam War road show for GI\u0026#39;s, the \u0026#34;F.T.A.\u0026#34; (\u0026#34;Free the Army\u0026#34;). But the relationship had crashed and burned by the end of the year.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;It broke my heart. I was eviscerated,\u0026#34; Sutherland told \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.theguardian.com/film/2008/mar/30/television.television\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eThe Guardian \u003c/a\u003ein 2008. \u0026#34;It was a wonderful relationship right up to the point we lived together.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe next year, Sutherland met and married actress Francine Racette. He remained married for the rest of his life and had three sons together: Roeg, Rossif, and Angus Sutherland.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSutherland played villain President Snow in \u0026#39;Hunger Games\u0026#39; \u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe actor had a particular skill for playing villains, a spy in 1981\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Eye of the Needle\u0026#34; a sadistic warden in 1989\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Lock Up\u0026#34; a scheming software CEO in 1994\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Disclosure\u0026#34; opposite Michael Douglas and Demi Moore and the cruel Attila in Bernardo Bertolucci\u0026#39;s Italian epic \u0026#34;1900.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter turning 80, Sutherland took on the role of his most famous villain, President Snow, in \u0026#34;The Hunger Games\u0026#34; — the arch-nemesis to Jennifer Lawrence\u0026#39;s Katniss Everdeen for four box office record-breaking films from 2012-2015.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e \u0026#34;My agent sends me these things because I\u0026#39;m 80 and I still like to know what\u0026#39;s going on,\u0026#34; he told Britain\u0026#39;s \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/film/the-hunger-games-mockingjay-part-2/donald-sutherland-interview/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e\u0026#34;The Telegraph.\u0026#34;\u003c/a\u003e \u0026#34;I hadn\u0026#39;t even heard of the books, but it became patently apparent to me that this was something. It was the first thing I\u0026#39;d read in years that could become a creative political stimulus for young people.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "9207830002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSutherland found a new generation of fans eager to take pictures with him, describing one fan who approached him in an airport. “As we’re waiting for her mother to take the picture, the girl turned and whispered in my ear, ‘Look mean.’ \u0026#34; Sutherland recalled with glee to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\"\u003eUSA Today in 2018\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72087830007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFinally, accepting his Oscar, Sutherland looked over his showbiz family, including Kiefer’s \u0026#34;Veep\u0026#34; actress daughter, Sarah Sutherland, and dedicated the award to his wife Francine: \u0026#34;From whom everything has come, and to whom everything is owed.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHe closed the speech quoting comedian Jack Benny when presented with an honor.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;(Benny) said, as I say to you now, \u0026#39;I don\u0026#39;t deserve this, But I have arthritis, and I don\u0026#39;t deserve that either,\u0026#39;\u0026#34; said Sutherland.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eContributing: Naledi Ushe\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

contentBody:
{
  "contentBody": [{
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "72135520007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eDonald Sutherland,\u003c/a\u003e the versatile Canadian actor whose prolific career in TV shows and movies showed a diverse range, from authority-loathing surgeon \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/opinion/voices/2020/10/30/mash-tv-show-charles-dubin-hawkeye-hope-election-2020-column/6067526002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eHawkeye Pierce\u003c/a\u003e in the \u0026#34;M*A*S*H\u0026#34; movie to authoritarian villain President Snow in \u0026#34;The Hunger Games\u0026#34; franchise, has died. He was 88.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;With a heavy heart, I tell you that my father, Donald Sutherland, has passed away,\u0026#34; his son Kiefer \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/p/C8cgckJJ548/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eposted on social media\u003c/a\u003e Thursday along with a black and white photo of the father-son pair.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eHe added: \u0026#34;I personally think one of the most important actors in the history of film. Never daunted by a role, good, bad or ugly. He loved what he did and did what he loved, and one can never ask for more than that. A life well lived.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eShirley Douglas \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2020/04/05/kiefer-sutherland-mother-actress-shirley-douglas-dies-86/2952047001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eKiefer Sutherland pays tribute to \u0026#39;extraordinary\u0026#39; mother dead at 86\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74158626007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eStarring in more than 200 TV and movies, Sutherland beat an indelible and idiosyncratic path during his six-decade career. He was the pot-smoking professor in 1978\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Animal House,\u0026#34; the titular detective John Klute starring alongside then-lover Jane Fonda in the 1971 thriller \u0026#34;Klute,\u0026#34; a pod person in the 1978 horror remake \u0026#34;Invasion of the Body Snatchers,\u0026#34; an 18th-century Venetian explorer in 1976\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Fellini\u0026#39;s Casanova\u0026#34; with director Frederico Fellini, and an embattled father working to save his emotionally troubled upper-middle-class family in \u0026#34;Ordinary People.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“I’ve always had a horizontally organized career,\u0026#34; Sutherland told \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eUSA TODAY\u003c/a\u003e in 2018. \u0026#34;You’ve got a big plate of fruit and cheese, and you can take a piece here and there. You won’t like all of it, but you’ll like some of it.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eDonald Sutherland interview: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"http://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e Playing \u0026#39;cold\u0026#39; billionaire Getty, and a pint-size \u0026#39;Hunger Games\u0026#39; fan\u0026#39;s request\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAn Emmy winner and the patriarch of his own family of actors and entertainment professionals (including son Kiefer Sutherland, star of \u0026#34;24\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;Designated Survivor\u0026#34;), Sutherland is inarguably the greatest Hollywood actor never to earn a single Oscar nomination. He was most egregiously overlooked for his widely praised \u0026#34;Ordinary People\u0026#34; role, which saw screen wife Mary Tyler Moore earn one of six Oscar nominations  — and newcomer Timothy Hutton win one of four Oscars playing Sutherland\u0026#39;s screen son. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eJohn Bailey, the cinematographer on \u0026#34;Ordinary People,\u0026#34; helped to correct this wrong as the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences president in 2017, calling Sutherland personally to inform the actor that he would be awarded an honorary Oscar.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Thank you for putting my name on this. This is very important to me, to my family,\u0026#34; Sutherland said from the 2017 \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/movies/2017/11/12/hollywood-bestows-honorary-oscars-governors-awards-amid-sexual-harassment-scandal/856166001/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/movies/2017/11/12/hollywood-bestows-honorary-oscars-governors-awards-amid-sexual-harassment-scandal/856166001/\"\u003eGovernors Awards podium\u003c/a\u003e, looking at his Oscar. \u0026#34;I wish I could say thank you to all the characters I have played, thank them for using their lives to inform my life.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "9233363002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBorn to Dorothy and Frederick Sutherland in the seaport city of Saint John, New Brunswick, the young Sutherland found he was destined for character acting during an eye-opening discussion with his mother.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I went to her, and I said, \u0026#39;Mother, am I good-looking?\u0026#39; And my mother looked at me and went. \u0026#39;Your face has character, Donald.\u0026#39; \u0026#34; Sutherland recalled to\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/60-minutes-the-long-unconventional-career-of-donald-sutherland/\"\u003e \u0026#34;60 Minutes\u0026#34; in 2018.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter studying drama and starring in London stage and TV productions, Sutherland earned the one-line part on \u0026#34;The Dirty Dozen,\u0026#34; portraying goofy felon Vernon Pinkley in an all-star cast that included Lee Marvin, Charles Bronson and Telly Savalas. But when actor Clint Walker declined to do a scene where his character impersonates a general, director Robert Aldrich looked at Sutherland.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "9233265002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;He went, \u0026#39;You with the big ears, you do it.\u0026#39; I don\u0026#39;t think he knew my name. But, you know. It changed my life,\u0026#39; \u0026#34; Sutherland told\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/60-minutes-the-long-unconventional-career-of-donald-sutherland/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e 60 Minutes\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSutherland starred in \u0026#39;The Dirty Dozen\u0026#39; and \u0026#39;Kelly\u0026#39;s Heroes\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eSutherland shot into stardom brandishing his own brand of quirky Vietnam War-era contempt in war movie portrayals, starting as convict soldier Vernon Pinkley in \u0026#34;The Dirty Dozen\u0026#34; (1967) and the comical tank driver Sgt. Oddball in the 1970s World War II heist comedy \u0026#34;Kelly\u0026#39;s Heroes.\u0026#34;  He ended the streak as the wise-cracking surgeon in Robert Altman\u0026#39;s 1970 Korean War comedy-drama \u0026#34;M*A*S*H\u0026#34; (Alan Alda portrayed Hawkeye Pierce in the seminal 1970s TV series). \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eDuring his starring role as the enigmatic private detective in the neo-noir hit \u0026#34;Klute\u0026#34; (which earned Fonda a best actress Oscar), Sutherland, still married to his second wife \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2020/04/05/kiefer-sutherland-mother-actress-shirley-douglas-dies-86/2952047001/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/movies/2020/04/05/kiefer-sutherland-mother-actress-shirley-douglas-dies-86/2952047001/\"\u003eShirley Douglas\u003c/a\u003e (mother of twins Rachel and Kiefer), began his relationship with Fonda. The two hit the road in the 1971 anti-Vietnam War road show for GI\u0026#39;s, the \u0026#34;F.T.A.\u0026#34; (\u0026#34;Free the Army\u0026#34;). But the relationship had crashed and burned by the end of the year.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;It broke my heart. I was eviscerated,\u0026#34; Sutherland told \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.theguardian.com/film/2008/mar/30/television.television\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eThe Guardian \u003c/a\u003ein 2008. \u0026#34;It was a wonderful relationship right up to the point we lived together.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe next year, Sutherland met and married actress Francine Racette. He remained married for the rest of his life and had three sons together: Roeg, Rossif, and Angus Sutherland.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSutherland played villain President Snow in \u0026#39;Hunger Games\u0026#39; \u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe actor had a particular skill for playing villains, a spy in 1981\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Eye of the Needle\u0026#34; a sadistic warden in 1989\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Lock Up\u0026#34; a scheming software CEO in 1994\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Disclosure\u0026#34; opposite Michael Douglas and Demi Moore and the cruel Attila in Bernardo Bertolucci\u0026#39;s Italian epic \u0026#34;1900.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter turning 80, Sutherland took on the role of his most famous villain, President Snow, in \u0026#34;The Hunger Games\u0026#34; — the arch-nemesis to Jennifer Lawrence\u0026#39;s Katniss Everdeen for four box office record-breaking films from 2012-2015.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e \u0026#34;My agent sends me these things because I\u0026#39;m 80 and I still like to know what\u0026#39;s going on,\u0026#34; he told Britain\u0026#39;s \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/film/the-hunger-games-mockingjay-part-2/donald-sutherland-interview/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e\u0026#34;The Telegraph.\u0026#34;\u003c/a\u003e \u0026#34;I hadn\u0026#39;t even heard of the books, but it became patently apparent to me that this was something. It was the first thing I\u0026#39;d read in years that could become a creative political stimulus for young people.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "9207830002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eSutherland found a new generation of fans eager to take pictures with him, describing one fan who approached him in an airport. “As we’re waiting for her mother to take the picture, the girl turned and whispered in my ear, ‘Look mean.’ \u0026#34; Sutherland recalled with glee to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\"\u003eUSA Today in 2018\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "72087830007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFinally, accepting his Oscar, Sutherland looked over his showbiz family, including Kiefer’s \u0026#34;Veep\u0026#34; actress daughter, Sarah Sutherland, and dedicated the award to his wife Francine: \u0026#34;From whom everything has come, and to whom everything is owed.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eHe closed the speech quoting comedian Jack Benny when presented with an honor.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;(Benny) said, as I say to you now, \u0026#39;I don\u0026#39;t deserve this, But I have arthritis, and I don\u0026#39;t deserve that either,\u0026#39;\u0026#34; said Sutherland.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eContributing: Naledi Ushe\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72135520007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eDonald Sutherland,\u003c/a\u003e the versatile Canadian actor whose prolific career in TV shows and movies showed a diverse range, from authority-loathing surgeon \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/opinion/voices/2020/10/30/mash-tv-show-charles-dubin-hawkeye-hope-election-2020-column/6067526002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eHawkeye Pierce\u003c/a\u003e in the \u0026#34;M*A*S*H\u0026#34; movie to authoritarian villain President Snow in \u0026#34;The Hunger Games\u0026#34; franchise, has died. He was 88.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;With a heavy heart, I tell you that my father, Donald Sutherland, has passed away,\u0026#34; his son Kiefer \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/p/C8cgckJJ548/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eposted on social media\u003c/a\u003e Thursday along with a black and white photo of the father-son pair.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHe added: \u0026#34;I personally think one of the most important actors in the history of film. Never daunted by a role, good, bad or ugly. He loved what he did and did what he loved, and one can never ask for more than that. A life well lived.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eUSA TODAY has reached out to reps for Sutherland.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74158626007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eStarring in more than 200 TV and movies, Sutherland beat an indelible and idiosyncratic path during his six-decade career. He was the pot-smoking professor in 1978\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Animal House,\u0026#34; the titular detective John Klute starring alongside then-lover Jane Fonda in the 1971 thriller \u0026#34;Klute,\u0026#34; a pod person in the 1978 horror remake \u0026#34;Invasion of the Body Snatchers,\u0026#34; an 18th-century Venetian explorer in 1976\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Fellini\u0026#39;s Casanova\u0026#34; with director Frederico Fellini, and an embattled father working to save his emotionally troubled upper-middle-class family in \u0026#34;Ordinary People.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“I’ve always had a horizontally organized career,\u0026#34; Sutherland told \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eUSA TODAY\u003c/a\u003e in 2018. \u0026#34;You’ve got a big plate of fruit and cheese, and you can take a piece here and there. You won’t like all of it, but you’ll like some of it.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eDonald Sutherland interview: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"http://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e Playing \u0026#39;cold\u0026#39; billionaire Getty, and a pint-size \u0026#39;Hunger Games\u0026#39; fan\u0026#39;s request\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAn Emmy winner and the patriarch of his own family of actors and entertainment professionals (including son Kiefer Sutherland, star of \u0026#34;24\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;Designated Survivor\u0026#34;), Sutherland is inarguably the greatest Hollywood actor never to earn a single Oscar nomination. He was most egregiously overlooked for his widely praised \u0026#34;Ordinary People\u0026#34; role, which saw screen wife Mary Tyler Moore earning one of six Oscar nominations  — and newcomer Timothy Hutton winning one of four Oscars playing Sutherland\u0026#39;s screen son. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJohn Bailey, the cinematographer on \u0026#34;Ordinary People,\u0026#34; helped to correct this wrong as the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences president in 2017, calling Sutherland personally to inform the actor that he would be awarded an honorary Oscar.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Thank you for putting my name on this. This is very important to me, to my family,\u0026#34; Sutherland said from the awards podium, looking at his Oscar. \u0026#34;I wish I could say thank you to all the characters I have played, thank them for using their lives to inform my life.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "9233363002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBorn to Dorothy and Frederick Sutherland in the seaport city of Saint John, New Brunswick, the young Sutherland found he was destined for character acting during an eye-opening discussion with his mother.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I went to her and I said, \u0026#39;Mother, am I good looking?\u0026#39; And my mother looked at me and went. \u0026#39;Your face has character, Donald.\u0026#39; \u0026#34; Sutherland recalled to \u0026#34;60 Minutes.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter studying drama and starring in London stage and TV productions, Sutherland earned the one-line part on \u0026#34;The Dirty Dozen,\u0026#34; portraying goofy felon Vernon Pinkey in an all-star cast that included Lee Marvin, Charles Bronson and Telly Savalas. But when Clint Walker declined to do a scene where his character impersonates a general, director Robert Aldrich looked at Sutherland.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "9233265002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;He went, \u0026#39;You with the big ears, you do it.\u0026#39; I don\u0026#39;t think he knew my name. But, you know. It changed my life,\u0026#39; \u0026#34; Sutherland told\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/60-minutes-the-long-unconventional-career-of-donald-sutherland/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e 60 Minutes\u003c/a\u003e in 2018.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSutherland shot into stardom brandishing his own brand of quirky Vietnam War-era contempt in war movie portrayals, starting as convict soldier Vernon Pinkley in \u0026#34;The Dirty Dozen\u0026#34; (1967) and the comical tank driver Sgt. Oddball in the 1970s World War II heist comedy \u0026#34;Kelly\u0026#39;s Heroes.\u0026#34;  He ended the streak as the wise-cracking surgeon in Robert Altman\u0026#39;s 1970 Korean War comedy-drama \u0026#34;M*A*S*H\u0026#34; (Alan Alda portrayed Hawkeye Pierce in the seminal 1970s TV series). \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDuring his starring role as the enigmatic private detective in the neo-noir hit \u0026#34;Klute,\u0026#34; (which earned Fonda a best actress Oscar) that Sutherland, still married to second wife (mother of twins Rachel and Kiefer), began his relationship with  Fonda. The two hit the road in the 1971 anti-Vietnam War road show for GI\u0026#39;s, the \u0026#34;F.T.A.\u0026#34; (\u0026#34;Free the Army\u0026#34;). But the relationship had crashed and burned by the end of the year.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;It broke my heart. I was eviscerated,\u0026#34; Sutherland told \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.theguardian.com/film/2008/mar/30/television.television\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eThe Guardian \u003c/a\u003ein 2008. \u0026#34;It was a wonderful relationship right up the point we lived together.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e The next year, Sutherland met and married actress Francine Racette, and remained married for the rest of his life, with three sons together: Roeg, Rossif, and Angus Sutherland.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe actor had a particular skill for playing villains, a spy in \u0026#34;Eye of the Needle\u0026#34; a sadistic warden in 1989\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Lock Up\u0026#34; a scheming software CEO in \u0026#34;Disclosure\u0026#34; opposite Michael Douglas and Demi Moore and the cruel Attila in  Bernardo Bertolucci Italian epic \u0026#34;1900.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter turning 80, Sutherland took on the role of his most famous villain, President Snow in \u0026#34;The Hunger Games,\u0026#34; the arch-nemesis to Jennifer Lawrence\u0026#39;s Katniss Everdeen for four box office record breaking films from 2012-2015.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e \u0026#34;My agent sends me these things because I\u0026#39;m 80 and I still like to know what\u0026#39;s going on,\u0026#34; he told Britain\u0026#39;s \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/film/the-hunger-games-mockingjay-part-2/donald-sutherland-interview/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e\u0026#34;The Telegraph.\u0026#34;\u003c/a\u003e \u0026#34;I hadn\u0026#39;t even heard of the books, but it became patently apparent to me that this was something. It was the first thing I\u0026#39;d read in years that could become a creative political stimulus for young people.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "9207830002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSutherland found a new generation of fans eager to take pictures with him, describing one fan who approached him in an airport. “As we’re waiting for her mother to take the picture, the girl turned and whispered in my ear, ‘Look mean.’ \u0026#34; Sutherland recalled with glee.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72087830007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFinally, accepting his Oscar, Sutherland look over his showbiz family, including Kiefer’s \u0026#34;Veep\u0026#34; actress daughter, Sarah Sutherland, and dedicated the award to his wife. \u0026#34;From whom everything has come, and to whom everything is owed.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHe closed the speech quoting comedian Jack Benny when presented with an honor.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;He said, as I say to you now, I don\u0026#39;t deserve this, But I have arthritis, and I don\u0026#39;t deserve that either.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eContributing: Naledi Ushe\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72135520007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eDonald Sutherland,\u003c/a\u003e the versatile Canadian actor whose prolific career in TV shows and movies showed a diverse range, from authority-loathing surgeon \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/opinion/voices/2020/10/30/mash-tv-show-charles-dubin-hawkeye-hope-election-2020-column/6067526002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eHawkeye Pierce\u003c/a\u003e in the \u0026#34;M*A*S*H\u0026#34; movie to authoritarian villain President Snow in \u0026#34;The Hunger Games\u0026#34; franchise, has died. He was 88.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;With a heavy heart, I tell you that my father, Donald Sutherland, has passed away,\u0026#34; his son Kiefer \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/p/C8cgckJJ548/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eposted on social media\u003c/a\u003e Thursday along with a black and white photo of the father-son pair.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHe added: \u0026#34;I personally think one of the most important actors in the history of film. Never daunted by a role, good, bad or ugly. He loved what he did and did what he loved, and one can never ask for more than that. A life well lived.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eUSA TODAY has reached out to reps for Sutherland.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74158626007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eStarring in more than 200 TV and movies, Sutherland beat an indelible and idiosyncratic path during his six-decade career. He was the pot-smoking professor in 1978\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Animal House,\u0026#34; the titular detective John Klute starring alongside then-lover Jane Fonda in the 1971 thriller \u0026#34;Klute,\u0026#34; a pod person in the 1978 horror remake \u0026#34;Invasion of the Body Snatchers,\u0026#34; an 18th-century Venetian explorer in 1976\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Fellini\u0026#39;s Casanova\u0026#34; with director Frederico Fellini, and an embattled father working to save his emotionally troubled upper-middle-class family in \u0026#34;Ordinary People.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“I’ve always had a horizontally organized career,\u0026#34; Sutherland told \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eUSA TODAY\u003c/a\u003e in 2018. \u0026#34;You’ve got a big plate of fruit and cheese, and you can take a piece here and there. You won’t like all of it, but you’ll like some of it.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eDonald Sutherland interview: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"http://www.usatoday.com/story/life/tv/2018/03/15/donald-sutherland-his-rich-resume-and-playing-cold-pragmatic-billionaire-getty-and-his-rich-acting-r/419906002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003e Playing \u0026#39;cold\u0026#39; billionaire Getty, and a pint-size \u0026#39;Hunger Games\u0026#39; fan\u0026#39;s request\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAn Emmy winner and the patriarch of his own family of actors and entertainment professionals (including son Kiefer Sutherland, star of \u0026#34;24\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;Designated Survivor\u0026#34;), Sutherland is inarguably the greatest Hollywood actor never to earn a single Oscar nomination. He was most egregiously overlooked for his widely praised \u0026#34;Ordinary People\u0026#34; role, which saw screen wife Mary Tyler Moore earning one of six Oscar nominations  — and newcomer Timothy Hutton winning one of four Oscars playing Sutherland\u0026#39;s screen son. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJohn Bailey, the cinematographer on \u0026#34;Ordinary People,\u0026#34; helped to correct this wrong as the Academy of Motion Picture Arts and Sciences president in 2017, calling Sutherland personally to inform the actor that he would be awarded an honorary Oscar.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Thank you for putting my name on this. This is very important to me, to my family,\u0026#34; Sutherland said from the awards podium, looking at his Oscar. \u0026#34;I wish I could say thank you to all the characters I have played, thank them for using their lives to inform my life.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "9233363002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBorn to Dorothy and Frederick Sutherland in the seaport city of Saint John, New Brunswick, the young Sutherland found he was destined for character acting during an eye-opening discussion with his mother.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I went to her and I said, \u0026#39;Mother, am I good looking?\u0026#39; And my mother looked at me and went. \u0026#39;Your face has character, Donald.\u0026#39; \u0026#34; Sutherland recalled to \u0026#34;60 Minutes.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter studying drama and starring in London stage and TV productions, Sutherland earned the one-line part on \u0026#34;The Dirty Dozen,\u0026#34; portraying goofy felon Vernon Pinkey in an all-star cast that included Lee Marvin, Charles Bronson and Telly Savalas. But when Clint Walker declined to do a scene where his character impersonates a general, director Robert Aldrich looked at Sutherland.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "9233265002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;He went, \u0026#39;You with the big ears, you do it.\u0026#39; I don\u0026#39;t think he knew my name. But, you know. It changed my life,\u0026#39; \u0026#34; Sutherland told\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cbsnews.com/news/60-minutes-the-long-unconventional-career-of-donald-sutherland/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e 60 Minutes\u003c/a\u003e in 2018.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSutherland shot into stardom brandishing his own brand of quirky Vietnam War-era contempt in war movie portrayals, starting as convict soldier Vernon Pinkley in \u0026#34;The Dirty Dozen\u0026#34; (1967) and the comical tank driver Sgt. Oddball in the 1970s World War II heist comedy \u0026#34;Kelly\u0026#39;s Heroes.\u0026#34;  He ended the streak as the wise-cracking surgeon in Robert Altman\u0026#39;s 1970 Korean War comedy-drama \u0026#34;M*A*S*H\u0026#34; (Alan Alda portrayed Hawkeye Pierce in the seminal 1970s TV series). \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDuring his starring role as the enigmatic private detective in the neo-noir hit \u0026#34;Klute,\u0026#34; (which earned Fonda a best actress Oscar) that Sutherland, still married to second wife (mother of twins Rachel and Kiefer), began his relationship with  Fonda. The two hit the road in the 1971 anti-Vietnam War road show for GI\u0026#39;s, the \u0026#34;F.T.A.\u0026#34; (\u0026#34;Free the Army\u0026#34;). But the relationship had crashed and burned by the end of the year.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;It broke my heart. I was eviscerated,\u0026#34; Sutherland told \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.theguardian.com/film/2008/mar/30/television.television\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eThe Guardian \u003c/a\u003ein 2008. \u0026#34;It was a wonderful relationship right up the point we lived together.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e The next year, Sutherland met and married actress Francine Racette, and remained married for the rest of his life, with three sons together: Roeg, Rossif, and Angus Sutherland.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe actor had a particular skill for playing villains, a spy in \u0026#34;Eye of the Needle\u0026#34; a sadistic warden in 1989\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Lock Up\u0026#34; a scheming software CEO in \u0026#34;Disclosure\u0026#34; opposite Michael Douglas and Demi Moore and the cruel Attila in  Bernardo Bertolucci Italian epic \u0026#34;1900.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter turning 80, Sutherland took on the role of his most famous villain, President Snow in \u0026#34;The Hunger Games,\u0026#34; the arch-nemesis to Jennifer Lawrence\u0026#39;s Katniss Everdeen for four box office record breaking films from 2012-2015.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e \u0026#34;My agent sends me these things because I\u0026#39;m 80 and I still like to know what\u0026#39;s going on,\u0026#34; he told Britain\u0026#39;s \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.telegraph.co.uk/film/the-hunger-games-mockingjay-part-2/donald-sutherland-interview/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e\u0026#34;The Telegraph.\u0026#34;\u003c/a\u003e \u0026#34;I hadn\u0026#39;t even heard of the books, but it became patently apparent to me that this was something. It was the first thing I\u0026#39;d read in years that could become a creative political stimulus for young people.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "9207830002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSutherland found a new generation of fans eager to take pictures with him, describing one fan who approached him in an airport. “As we’re waiting for her mother to take the picture, the girl turned and whispered in my ear, ‘Look mean.’ \u0026#34; Sutherland recalled with glee.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72087830007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFinally, accepting his Oscar, Sutherland look over his showbiz family, including Kiefer’s \u0026#34;Veep\u0026#34; actress daughter, Sarah Sutherland, and dedicated the award to his wife. \u0026#34;From whom everything has come, and to whom everything is owed.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHe closed the speech quoting comedian Jack Benny when presented with an honor.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;He said, as I say to you now, I don\u0026#39;t deserve this, But I have arthritis, and I don\u0026#39;t deserve that either.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eContributing: Naledi Ushe\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

