    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003e Join our Watch Party!  \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://profile.usatoday.com/newsletters/watch-party/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eSign up to receive USA TODAY\u0026#39;s movie and TV recommendations right in your inbox\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74199448007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThat is the $100 million question, the reported budget for the R-rated, 181-minute first chapter. Costner does not even appear until 66 minutes into the movie as Hayes Ellison., a mysterious gunslinger who crosses paths with a local courtesan, Marigold (Abbey Lee).\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe duo\u0026#39;s travails are just two of the myriad stories, with 170 speaking parts, in the often brutal tale of post-Civil War westward expansion.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;In the second feature, things get harder for them. And the third film, things don\u0026#39;t change,\u0026#34; says Costner. \u0026#34;The West was hard.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73427001007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhat\u0026#39;s Costner\u0026#39;s financial stake in \u0026#39;Horizon\u0026#39;? \u0026#39;I try not to let it keep me up at night\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eCostner first started dreaming about the story in 1988, imagining five films. Even cut down to four, it\u0026#39;s a supremely ambitious project for which he\u0026#39;s pieced together financing.  He says the cost of the first two \u0026#34;Horizon\u0026#34; movies, required \u0026#34;a lot more\u0026#34; than the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.gq.com/story/kevin-costner-gq-cover-story\"\u003e$38 million he copped to personally putting down in previous interviews.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I try not to let it keep me up at night,\u0026#34; says Costner. \u0026#34;Entrepreneurially, I just figure out a way. Maybe I\u0026#39;m a mongoose playing with a cobra.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74208210007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe principled and proudly stubborn Costner went through similar drama with predictions of doom for 1990\u0026#39;s \u0026#34;Dances with Wolves\u0026#34; (a box-office hit that went on to win seven Oscars, including best picture and best director) and 1995\u0026#39;s actually troubled \u0026#34;Waterworld,\u0026#34; which eventually eked out a profit.  \u0026#34;Horizon\u0026#34; is a fourfold gamble. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I can\u0026#39;t ignore where my heart wants to go,\u0026#34; says Costner of the \u0026#34;Horizon\u0026#34; spend. \u0026#34;I\u0026#39;m not a fool, but it feels foolish. I don\u0026#39;t honestly know why I do the things I do. I\u0026#39;m not hurting anybody, and it\u0026#39;s my intention to bring a solid piece of entertainment.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBy all accounts, Costner was outwardly unaffected by his burden during the 52-day shoot in picturesque Moab, Utah.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I\u0026#39;m sure he was thinking about putting up his land to help finance it and other stuff he had going on,\u0026#34; says Luke Wilson, who plays Matthew Van Weyden, the captain of a wagon train. \u0026#34;But he just focused on the work. The guy is cool under pressure. I couldn\u0026#39;t believe it.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "8316892001"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhy Costner announced \u0026#39;Yellowstone\u0026#39; departure after editing \u0026#39;Horizon: Chapter 2\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eLeaving a \u0026#34;Chapter 2\u0026#34; editing session last week, Costner officially ended speculation about whether he\u0026#39;d return for the fifth and final \u0026#34;Yellowstone\u0026#34; season as rancher John Dutton.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter a prolonged battle and negotiations with creator Taylor Sheridan and Paramount Studios over pay and shooting schedules, exacerbated by Costner\u0026#39;s ambitious movies and Sheridan\u0026#39;s TV universe, Costner put the nail in the return coffin in an impromptu June 20 video.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I just said, \u0026#39;Bring the camera over here a second.\u0026#39; I just wanted to get it done,\u0026#34; says Costner, who \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/entertainment/tv/2024/06/21/kevin-costner-not-returning-yellowstone/74166723007/\"\u003espoke directly to \u0026#34;Yellowstone\u0026#34; fans, saying, \u0026#34;I just wanted to let you know that I won\u0026#39;t be returning. \u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74235912007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eCostner knew fans wouldn\u0026#39;t be happy with the news that came the same day Paramount announced the final season, shooting in Montana, will premiere Nov. 10. He equates it to a dad breaking the news to his kids \u0026#34;that we\u0026#39;re not going to Hawaii this year.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut officially announcing the \u0026#34;Yellowstone\u0026#34; departure after holding out hope for a return made it even clearer that Costner is putting all his energy and focus into his \u0026#34;Horizon\u0026#34; movie gamble. Costner ended the video by saying, \u0026#34;See you at the movies.\u0026#34;  He hopes, and needs, \u0026#34;Yellowstone\u0026#34; fans to come along for the \u0026#34;Horizon\u0026#34; ride.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I tried to honor that audience as much as I could when making \u0026#39;Yellowstone,\u0026#39;\u0026#34; says Costner. \u0026#34;And I made this movie for people like that, not as a peacemaking moment but as a continuing relationship.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Horizon\u0026#34; certainly is the type of movie a maverick modern-day cattle rancher like John Dutton would make. And in the same hard-headed style.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I could have used John Dutton to help me finance it,\u0026#34; says Costner. \u0026#34;Where\u0026#39;s John Dutton when I need him?\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74160991007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eCostner has yet to complete \u0026#39;Horizon: Chapter 3\u0026#34; or \u0026#34;Chapter 4\u0026#34;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe sunglass-wearing Costner was back in superstar form attending Monday\u0026#39;s Los Angeles premiere with his seven children, including son Hayes, 15, who stars in \u0026#34;Horizon.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eStanding on the gold carpet, Costner spoke to USA TODAY about the hard-fought lessons he\u0026#39;s learned making the first two chapters, which will carry him through finishing the third film (already underway) and the fourth.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;You can\u0026#39;t stand still,\u0026#34; he said. \u0026#34;I\u0026#39;ve had a really blessed life, but it shouldn\u0026#39;t come as a surprise that I bruise like anyone else. It\u0026#39;s really what you do after that. You have to get up. I have children who are watching me. I have to go forward.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

