body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74029475007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBernards showed some early jitters in its first trip to the state final. Then the Mountaineers showed the offensive pop that has changed the notion of what is possible at the small, Somerset County school.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSparked by four goals apiece from David Brothers and Logan Stevens, Bernards knocked off Mountain Lakes, 13-5, in the Group 1 final on Saturday at Ridge High School.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Mountaineers (21-2) had never won a sectional title before this season, but now head to the Kirst Cup as one of the last six teams standing in New Jersey.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eCheck back soon for more.\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
