    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eVeteran McNabb finding a home\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72935932007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThough McNabb recalled \u003ca href\u003d\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Diego_Spirit\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Diego_Spirit\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003egoing to San Diego Spirit games\u003c/a\u003e with her family when they lived in California back in the early 2000s, she hadn\u0026#39;t seriously considered turning pro while growing up. The Women\u0026#39;s United Soccer Association survived only from April 2001 to September 2003. Women\u0026#39;s Professional Soccer launched in 2007, followed by the National Women\u0026#39;s Soccer League in 2012 – her freshman year in college.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eShe\u0026#39;s adjusted to her role as a veteran, though San Diego coach Casey Stoney admitted McNabb is usually a quiet leader. Stoney is hoping McNabb will be more consistent in her third season, settling in at left back.\u003c/p\u003e"
