  "contentBody": [{
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "12037606002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/kristen-mcnabb-492ab413b/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/kristen-mcnabb-492ab413b/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eKristen McNabb\u003c/a\u003e\u0026#39;s fan club will probably be easy to find when the San Diego Wave visits \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.dailyrecord.com/story/sports/soccer/2024/01/19/nj-soccer-gotham-class-of-2024-tierna-davidson-crystal-dunn-rose-lavelle-emily-sonnett/72241599007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.dailyrecord.com/story/sports/soccer/2024/01/19/nj-soccer-gotham-class-of-2024-tierna-davidson-crystal-dunn-rose-lavelle-emily-sonnett/72241599007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eGotham FC\u003c/a\u003e for a National Women\u0026#39;s Soccer League match on Wednesday at Red Bull Arena. Just look for the crowd of matching T-shirts, quite possibly in the Wave\u0026#39;s trademark hot pink.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eHer older sister, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/lindsey-mcnabb-hover-914b9847/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.linkedin.com/in/lindsey-mcnabb-hover-914b9847/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eRutgers alumna Lindsey McNabb Hover\u003c/a\u003e, will likely be leading the cheers.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs the Wave\u0026#39;s starting left back, Kristen McNabb, who grew up in Montville, isn\u0026#39;t used to that kind of attention. She joked about her far more famous teammate, \u0026#34;If they notice me behind Alex Morgan, that\u0026#39;ll be pretty cool. I\u0026#39;ll take it.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut McNabb admitted to getting \u0026#34;an extra driving force\u0026#34; from having friends and family in the stands, something that rarely happens at San Diego\u0026#39;s home matches. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74048513007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Wave and visiting Gotham \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.nwslsoccer.com/match/28ef6e1d54f34bd8ba719783d8053dbc/san-diego-wave-fc-vs-nj-ny-gotham-fc/index\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.nwslsoccer.com/match/28ef6e1d54f34bd8ba719783d8053dbc/san-diego-wave-fc-vs-nj-ny-gotham-fc/index\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eplayed to a 1-1 draw\u003c/a\u003e on May 12. San Diego (3-4-5) is ninth among 14 NWSL teams, with no road wins. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;(New Jersey) does still hold a special place in my heart,\u0026#34; said McNabb, whose sister\u0026#39;s family lives in West Orange. \u0026#34;It\u0026#39;s always nice to look up into the stands and see my loved ones.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eProud to be (sort of) a Jersey girl\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eMcNabb was born in Newport Beach, California, but the family relocated through Louisiana; Massachusetts; Montgomery, New Jersey; and back to California, as dad Mark McNabb – an automotive executive and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/p/1WswuqD2Fp/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/p/1WswuqD2Fp/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eformer NSCAA Division III All-American at Babson\u003c/a\u003e – was transferred. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe McNabbs moved back to New Jersey, settling in Montville in Morris County, when Lindsey was going to be a sophomore and Kristen a seventh grader. Though Lindsey McNabb played one year of high school soccer in Irvine, California, and then one at Montville after the family relocated, Kristen McNabb focused on the club game at \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.pdasoccer.org/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.pdasoccer.org/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ePlayers Development Academy\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eKristen McNabb mainly played center back and defensive midfield, twice captaining PDA Charge to second place in the Elite Club National League. But she tore her left ACL in the spring of her senior year, and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://virginiasports.com/player/kristen-mcnabb/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://virginiasports.com/player/kristen-mcnabb/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003esat out her freshman season at Virginia\u003c/a\u003e. She appeared in 19 matches as a sophomore before tearing her right ACL. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eMcNabb started all but one match in her last two college seasons, usually with her parents – who had moved again, this time to Washington D.C. – in the stands. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.dailyrecord.com/story/sports/soccer/2024/03/13/national-womens-soccer-league-2024-season-list-of-new-jersey-players/72932824007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eMeet the 17 New Jersey soccer players in NWSL as 2024 season begins\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Unless Kristen McNabb plays for you, you don\u0026#39;t understand the quality of player she is and the quality of person she is,\u0026#34; said \u003ca href\u003d\"https://virginiasports.com/sports/wsoc/roster/season/2023-24/coach/steve-swanson/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://virginiasports.com/sports/wsoc/roster/season/2023-24/coach/steve-swanson/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003elongtime Virginia women\u0026#39;s soccer coach Steve Swanson\u003c/a\u003e, who recently visited McNabb and two other alumnae in San Diego. \u0026#34;She does all the little things that are so important to winning. ... She\u0026#39;s the definition of a professional. You know what you\u0026#39;re going to get day in and day out, and they\u0026#39;re going to bring it every single day. It\u0026#39;s going to be real high quality, maximum effort, maximum focus.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eGo west, young player\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eA fan of the East Coast, McNabb was selected by Seattle in the fourth round in 2017. She had two goals and two assists in 87 matches (6,017 minutes) with the Reign. San Diego picked McNabb in the expansion draft in December 2021. She\u0026#39;s played 4,584 minutes in 54 games for the Wave, who earned the 2023 NWSL Shield with the best regular-season record.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut physical issues have continued to follow McNabb, who missed the second half of last season with a hip injury.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;It gave me perspective,\u0026#34; she said of her many injuries. \u0026#34;I have a tendency to be very hard on myself, very intense. I like to win. I like to play. When I had a bad game as a kid, I was a miserable, terrible human, to my parents mainly. Getting that experience when you can\u0026#39;t play, that sucks even more. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;As an older, veteran player, when that happens, you remember to count your blessings that you\u0026#39;re in the situation you\u0026#39;re in,\u0026#34; said McNabb, who turned 30 in April. \u0026#34;At the end of the day, I love to play soccer. That\u0026#39;s the ultimate goal: to get back on the field.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eVeteran McNabb finding a home\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "72935932007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThough McNabb recalled \u003ca href\u003d\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Diego_Spirit\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/San_Diego_Spirit\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003egoing to San Diego Spirit games\u003c/a\u003e with her family when they lived in California back in the early 2000s, she hadn\u0026#39;t seriously considered turning pro while growing up. The Women\u0026#39;s United Soccer Association survived only from April 2001 to September 2003. Women\u0026#39;s Professional Soccer launched in 2007, followed by the National Women\u0026#39;s Soccer League in 2012 – her freshman year in college.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eShe\u0026#39;s adjusted to her role as a veteran, though San Diego coach Casey Stoney admitted McNabb is usually a quiet leader. Stoney is hoping McNabb will be more consistent in her third season, settling in at left back.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;When Kristen is fit, healthy and confident, she\u0026#39;s one of the best left backs in the league,\u0026#34; Stoney said. \u0026#34;She plays simple, plays quick. I\u0026#39;d like to get her more in the attacking third. To get her higher up is a key thing. ... She\u0026#39;s got steely determination to do well.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cem\u003eJane Havsy is a storyteller for the Daily Record and DailyRecord.com, part of the USA TODAY Network. For full access to live scores, breaking news and analysis, \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://cm.dailyrecord.com/specialoffer/?gps-source\u003dCPNAVBARBBB\u0026utm_medium\u003dONSITE\u0026utm_campaign\u003d2019SLJP10\u0026utm_content\u003dCPNAVBARBBB\u0026utm_source\u003dCPNAVBARBBB\u0026onSuccessRedirectURL\u003dhttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.dailyrecord.com%2F\"\u003e\u003cem\u003esubscribe today\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eWant to share your story with me? \u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eEmail: \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"mailto:JHavsy@gannettnj.com\"\u003e\u003cem\u003eJHavsy@gannett.com\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003eTwitter: \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://twitter.com/dailyrecordspts\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003e@dailyrecordspts\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "7540272001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day isn\u0026#39;t exactly like Mother\u0026#39;s Day, we know. We usually don\u0026#39;t serve Dad breakfast in bed, give him flowers or pamper him. But why shouldn\u0026#39;t we, asks our reporter Jim Beckerman, in a story from 2021. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOr we could take him out to dinner, proffers our NorthJerseyEats food team. (They also suggest some great gifts for foodie Dads.) \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOr we could just celebrate him — as many of our stories, photos and videos have over the years. We thought it would be nice to gather them here, and we hope you enjoy reading our tributes, profiles, essays and suggestions for great things to do, make and buy for Father\u0026#39;s Day.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHere\u0026#39;s to Dad!\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/health/2024/06/13/fathers-day-stories-nj-man-beats-testicular-esophageal-cancer/74055385007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/health/2024/06/13/fathers-day-stories-nj-man-beats-testicular-esophageal-cancer/74055385007/\"\u003eNJ man who beat two kinds of cancer celebrates Father\u0026#39;s Day as a granddad of six\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74062298007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs barbecues are fired up across New Jersey this Sunday and neckties and wristwatches are unwrapped, few will appreciate Father\u0026#39;s Day as much as John Keane. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/health/2024/06/13/fathers-day-stories-nj-man-beats-testicular-esophageal-cancer/74055385007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/health/2024/06/13/fathers-day-stories-nj-man-beats-testicular-esophageal-cancer/74055385007/\"\u003eNJ man who beat two kinds of cancer celebrates Father\u0026#39;s Day as a granddad of six\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/columnists/jim-beckerman/2023/06/14/fathers-day-2023-first-without-father/70299555007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eLife Without Father? One Father\u0026#39;s Day, it will happen to you\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "12062607002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThese are among the hundreds of little, unnoticed gifts that all fathers give their children. You probably have similar memories. His gifts to me? I still have them all. And every day, I remember a new one. Happy Father\u0026#39;s Day, dad. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/columnists/jim-beckerman/2023/06/14/fathers-day-2023-first-without-father/70299555007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eMy first Father\u0026#39;s Day without a father.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/sports/mlb/yankees/2023/06/14/gleyber-torres-yankees-player-fathers-day-with-young-son/70317284007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e\u0026#39;I know I have something special\u0026#39;: How Gleyber Torres appreciates fatherhood and baseball\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“In the past, I’d go straight to the house and just think about a bad situation – why did I strike out, or if I make an error,’’ said Torres. “And now, with a baby, I know I have something special when I get back home.\u0026#34; \u003cstrong\u003eRead it: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/sports/mlb/yankees/2023/06/14/gleyber-torres-yankees-player-fathers-day-with-young-son/70317284007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eGleyber Torres on fatherhood.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/health/2023/06/16/fathers-day-2023-nj-twins-lost-dad-cancer-doctors/70317832007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day tribute: NJ twins became doctors and battle cancer in memory of dad\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "12098456002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFakhruddin Danish\u0026#39;s memory lives on every time Dr. Adnan Danish kills a cancer cell with radiation or Dr. Shabbar Danish performs surgery on a brain tumor. The two brothers have become well-regarded physicians in New Jersey, rising to the top of their field with a disease they know all too well. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/health/2023/06/16/fathers-day-2023-nj-twins-lost-dad-cancer-doctors/70317832007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eTwins battle cancer in memory of dad\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/passaic/north-haledon/2023/06/16/north-haledon-nj-man-meets-birth-father-first-time-after-30-years/70320998007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eDNA test allows North Jersey man to meet birth father for first time in his life\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "12117008002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJoseph Federico said the results of his DNA test showed that he had a first cousin in the 23andMe database, living in East Orange. He said he contacted his match — the company allows users to chat online with genetic relatives — and she told him that he resembled her uncle, Sergio. Before too long, Federico’s cousin connected them. And on Dec. 16 — 30 years from the day that he was given up for adoption — father and son were reunited in person. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/passaic/north-haledon/2023/06/16/north-haledon-nj-man-meets-birth-father-first-time-after-30-years/70320998007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eNorth Jersey man meets his father, 30 years later.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.app.com/story/entertainment/events/summer-guide/2022/06/21/nj-breweries-visit-jersey-shore-summer/6921749001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eTake Dad on a beer crawl down the Shore\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "27157115"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFew things say \u0026#34;summer at the Jersey Shore\u0026#34; quite like beaches and beer. So why not combine them? After all, we have plenty of craft breweries in beach towns. Here, for your summertime fun time pleasure, are 27 of them (and yes, beaches on bays, rivers and lakes count), listed geographically from north to south. Read it: Craft brew tour for Dad.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.app.com/story/entertainment/dining/2020/06/02/jersey-made-fathers-day-food-gifts/5212207002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e12 Jersey-made Father\u0026#39;s Day gifts for food-loving dads\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "104731540"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis Father\u0026#39;s Day, consider an edible gift, most made and sold right here in New Jersey. For dads who love their grills and smokers, there\u0026#39;s barbecue sauce to brush on brisket and bacon jam to dollop on burgers. Dad love sweets? Treat him to a flight of cakes or a dessert with his picture on it. Such gifts are doubly delicious: By ordering from these and other local producers, not only will you score a great gift for Dad, you\u0026#39;ll help a small business in tough times. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.app.com/story/entertainment/dining/2020/06/02/jersey-made-fathers-day-food-gifts/5212207002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eFoodie Father\u0026#39;s Day gifts.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2022/06/14/fathers-day-2022-father-son-relationships-theater/7468870001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eIt\u0026#39;s always Father\u0026#39;s Day in the theater, where complicated relationships make great drama\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "99447940"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThere is one sort of person who never stops thinking about father. Someone who obsesses over dad, broods over dad, can\u0026#39;t let dad go. Someone who tries — on a nightly basis — to confront him, exorcise him, forgive him, or be forgiven by him. That person is a playwright. \u0026#34;Oedipus Rex\u0026#34;!  \u0026#34;Hamlet\u0026#34;! \u0026#34;King Lear\u0026#34;! \u0026#34;Death of a Salesman\u0026#34;! \u0026#34;Long Day\u0026#39;s Journey Into Night\u0026#34;! \u0026#34;Fences\u0026#34;! It\u0026#39;s amazing how many of the Great Plays center on confrontations of fathers and sons (sons \u003cem\u003eand\u003c/em\u003e daughters, in the case of \u0026#34;King Lear.\u0026#34;) \u003cstrong\u003eRead it\u003c/strong\u003e: \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2022/06/14/fathers-day-2022-father-son-relationships-theater/7468870001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eIt\u0026#39;s alway Father\u0026#39;s Day in the theater.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/dining/2022/06/13/fathers-day-dinner-near-me-north-jersey-restaurant-specials/7544212001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eBarbecue to escargot: 9 North Jersey restaurants offering Father\u0026#39;s Day dining specials\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "3576351002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEvery dad deserves to eat well on Father\u0026#39;s Day. Here are North Jersey restaurants of diverse creeds offering special meals for dad on June 19. (Don\u0026#39;t worry, there\u0026#39;s plenty of barbecue on here, too.) \u003cem\u003eEditor\u0026#39;s note: This story is from 2022, so specials will have changed. Call ahead. \u003c/em\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRead it:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/dining/2022/06/13/fathers-day-dinner-near-me-north-jersey-restaurant-specials/7544212001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day dining specials\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2021/06/09/fathers-day-gifts-2021-gardening-tools-vegan-cookbook/7534317002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eTies? Golf clubs? Grilling tools? Enough. Try these Father\u0026#39;s Day gifts instead\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt\u0026#39;s 2021. Social roles are evolving. Even the most conventional of us are becoming familiar with terms like \u0026#34;stay-at-home-dad\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;non-binary.\u0026#34; So why, on Father\u0026#39;s Day, are we still giving dad golf clubs? You know your own dad best, of course. But we think that, in the second decade of the twenty-first century, it\u0026#39;s time to think outside the tool box. Here are some alternative suggestions. Read it: Different gifts for Father\u0026#39;s Day.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/life/2021/06/15/alzheimers-disease-dementia-parent/7601336002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eMy dad has dementia, but I’m still learning from him\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "7606164002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn Father’s Day, I will remember the man who took me ice-skating at the local rink every weekend; who listened patiently in the car as I spilled my teenage dating problems; who linked his arm in mine as we walked down the aisle towards my husband-to-be, and whispered how proud he was of me. What makes this Father\u0026#39;s Day especially poignant is that my dad is still around. He’s alive, but he’s not the man who helped raise me and my two younger sisters. At 89, he\u0026#39;s been diagnosed with Alzheimer’s Disease. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/life/2021/06/15/alzheimers-disease-dementia-parent/7601336002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eMy dad has dementia, but I’m still learning from him.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/bergen/2019/06/13/fathers-day-nj-bergen-men-balance-life-dads-and-first-responders/1337895001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eBergen County first responders share the struggles and joys of fatherhood\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "11610050002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn 2019, we asked you to nominate Bergen County first responders who are also fathers. We at (201) Magazine would like to thank all the emergency personnel who protect us on a daily basis, and we honor them by highlighting the five individuals here. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/bergen/2019/06/13/fathers-day-nj-bergen-men-balance-life-dads-and-first-responders/1337895001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eBergen County first responders share the struggles and joys of fatherhood\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/sports/2019/06/13/fathers-day-memory-baseball-player-home-run-caught-his-father/1435717001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eImagine catching a home run hit by your son? This dad did it, and he’ll never forget it\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "1437791001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEvery spring, in the days heading into Father’s Day, Conrad Gregor remembers his unique home run – the one that his own father actually caught. Marty Gregor is reminded every day of the catch he made on his son’s first minor league homer of the 2014 season. “I look at it every morning when I get up and start my day,” Marty said. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/sports/2019/06/13/fathers-day-memory-baseball-player-home-run-caught-his-father/1435717001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eImagine catching a home run hit by your son?\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2017/06/16/stylish/383938001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e7 Bergen dads share their favorite dish, fashion item and plans for Father\u0026#39;s Day \u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "102919280"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eA real estate developer who loves his Montblanc watch. A managing director who would wear Stan Smiths every day, if he could. A small business owner who is obsessed with 7 for All Mankind jeans. These — plus four other fashionable Bergen dads — may gravitate toward different styles, but they all share one thing in common: the love of their kids. With Father\u0026#39;s Day in mind, we asked these Dads to share their favorite things about  North Jersey, from fashion to food to the perfect Father\u0026#39;s Day. Read it: \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2017/06/16/stylish/383938001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e7 Bergen dads share their favorite dish, fashion item and plans for Father\u0026#39;s Day.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.app.com/story/opinion/columnists/2014/06/13/issue-fathers-day/10465407/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day: What do you most admire about Dad?\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "35921811"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day is a time for remembering what it was, and is, that our dads have given us over the years. It is a day to think about the lessons he taught us, intentionally or unintentionally, and how they have stayed with us. In that spirit, we asked our readers to answer the following two questions: What quality or qualities do you/did you most admire in your father? And when did you first begin to appreciate those qualities? We were rewarded with tough, tender, touching and funny responses. Read it: What do you admire about Dad?\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOPINION\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2017/06/02/ervolino-dear-fathers-day-youre-no-mothers-day/355988001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eErvolino: Dear Father\u0026#39;s Day, you\u0026#39;re no Mother\u0026#39;s Day\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "3155500002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWell, no matter how much we love our fathers, many of us have a hard time making Father’s Day plans. Read it: \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2017/06/02/ervolino-dear-fathers-day-youre-no-mothers-day/355988001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eYou\u0026#39;re no Mother\u0026#39;s Day!\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/opinion/2023/06/16/fathers-day-embrace-those-colorful-ties-dad-and-the-memories-too/70323504007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day 2023: Embrace the journey, dads — and those ties, too | Opinion\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eLearning to be a good father did not come naturally to me. I made countless mistakes, but read books, took classes, and spent lots of time talking with my wife and other fathers in order to be a better dad to my kids. Talking to other fathers was a lifesaver, and one thing it taught me was that being a father is never-ending. Even in death, some believe you continue to watch over your children. I believe my dad watches me and one day I will do the same for my kids.. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/opinion/2023/06/16/fathers-day-embrace-those-colorful-ties-dad-and-the-memories-too/70323504007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eEmbrace the journey.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "7540272001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day isn\u0026#39;t exactly like Mother\u0026#39;s Day, we know. We usually don\u0026#39;t serve Dad breakfast in bed, give him flowers or pamper him. But why shouldn\u0026#39;t we, asks our reporter Jim Beckerman, in a story from 2021. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOr we could take him out to dinner, proffers our NorthJerseyEats food team. (They also suggest some great gifts for foodie Dads.) \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOr we could just celebrate him — as many of our stories, photos and videos have over the years. We thought it would be nice to gather them here, and we hope you enjoy reading our tributes, profiles, essays and suggestions for great things to do, make and buy for Father\u0026#39;s Day.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHere\u0026#39;s to Dad!\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/health/2024/06/13/fathers-day-stories-nj-man-beats-testicular-esophageal-cancer/74055385007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/health/2024/06/13/fathers-day-stories-nj-man-beats-testicular-esophageal-cancer/74055385007/\"\u003eNJ man who beat two kinds of cancer celebrates Father\u0026#39;s Day as a granddad of six\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74062298007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs barbecues are fired up across New Jersey this Sunday and neckties and wristwatches are unwrapped, few will appreciate Father\u0026#39;s Day as much as John Keane. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/health/2024/06/13/fathers-day-stories-nj-man-beats-testicular-esophageal-cancer/74055385007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/health/2024/06/13/fathers-day-stories-nj-man-beats-testicular-esophageal-cancer/74055385007/\"\u003eNJ man who beat two kinds of cancer celebrates Father\u0026#39;s Day as a granddad of six\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/columnists/jim-beckerman/2023/06/14/fathers-day-2023-first-without-father/70299555007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eLife Without Father? One Father\u0026#39;s Day, it will happen to you\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "12062607002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThese are among the hundreds of little, unnoticed gifts that all fathers give their children. You probably have similar memories. His gifts to me? I still have them all. And every day, I remember a new one. Happy Father\u0026#39;s Day, dad. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/columnists/jim-beckerman/2023/06/14/fathers-day-2023-first-without-father/70299555007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eMy first Father\u0026#39;s Day without a father.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/sports/mlb/yankees/2023/06/14/gleyber-torres-yankees-player-fathers-day-with-young-son/70317284007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e\u0026#39;I know I have something special\u0026#39;: How Gleyber Torres appreciates fatherhood and baseball\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“In the past, I’d go straight to the house and just think about a bad situation – why did I strike out, or if I make an error,’’ said Torres. “And now, with a baby, I know I have something special when I get back home.\u0026#34; \u003cstrong\u003eRead it: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/sports/mlb/yankees/2023/06/14/gleyber-torres-yankees-player-fathers-day-with-young-son/70317284007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eGleyber Torres on fatherhood.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/health/2023/06/16/fathers-day-2023-nj-twins-lost-dad-cancer-doctors/70317832007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day tribute: NJ twins became doctors and battle cancer in memory of dad\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "12098456002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFakhruddin Danish\u0026#39;s memory lives on every time Dr. Adnan Danish kills a cancer cell with radiation or Dr. Shabbar Danish performs surgery on a brain tumor. The two brothers have become well-regarded physicians in New Jersey, rising to the top of their field with a disease they know all too well. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/health/2023/06/16/fathers-day-2023-nj-twins-lost-dad-cancer-doctors/70317832007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eTwins battle cancer in memory of dad\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/passaic/north-haledon/2023/06/16/north-haledon-nj-man-meets-birth-father-first-time-after-30-years/70320998007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eDNA test allows North Jersey man to meet birth father for first time in his life\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "12117008002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJoseph Federico said the results of his DNA test showed that he had a first cousin in the 23andMe database, living in East Orange. He said he contacted his match — the company allows users to chat online with genetic relatives — and she told him that he resembled her uncle, Sergio. Before too long, Federico’s cousin connected them. And on Dec. 16 — 30 years from the day that he was given up for adoption — father and son were reunited in person. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/passaic/north-haledon/2023/06/16/north-haledon-nj-man-meets-birth-father-first-time-after-30-years/70320998007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eNorth Jersey man meets his father, 30 years later.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.app.com/story/entertainment/events/summer-guide/2022/06/21/nj-breweries-visit-jersey-shore-summer/6921749001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eTake Dad on a beer crawl down the Shore\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "27157115"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFew things say \u0026#34;summer at the Jersey Shore\u0026#34; quite like beaches and beer. So why not combine them? After all, we have plenty of craft breweries in beach towns. Here, for your summertime fun time pleasure, are 27 of them (and yes, beaches on bays, rivers and lakes count), listed geographically from north to south. Read it: Craft brew tour for Dad.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.app.com/story/entertainment/dining/2020/06/02/jersey-made-fathers-day-food-gifts/5212207002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e12 Jersey-made Father\u0026#39;s Day gifts for food-loving dads\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "104731540"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis Father\u0026#39;s Day, consider an edible gift, most made and sold right here in New Jersey. For dads who love their grills and smokers, there\u0026#39;s barbecue sauce to brush on brisket and bacon jam to dollop on burgers. Dad love sweets? Treat him to a flight of cakes or a dessert with his picture on it. Such gifts are doubly delicious: By ordering from these and other local producers, not only will you score a great gift for Dad, you\u0026#39;ll help a small business in tough times. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.app.com/story/entertainment/dining/2020/06/02/jersey-made-fathers-day-food-gifts/5212207002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eFoodie Father\u0026#39;s Day gifts.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2022/06/14/fathers-day-2022-father-son-relationships-theater/7468870001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eIt\u0026#39;s always Father\u0026#39;s Day in the theater, where complicated relationships make great drama\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "99447940"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThere is one sort of person who never stops thinking about father. Someone who obsesses over dad, broods over dad, can\u0026#39;t let dad go. Someone who tries — on a nightly basis — to confront him, exorcise him, forgive him, or be forgiven by him. That person is a playwright. \u0026#34;Oedipus Rex\u0026#34;!  \u0026#34;Hamlet\u0026#34;! \u0026#34;King Lear\u0026#34;! \u0026#34;Death of a Salesman\u0026#34;! \u0026#34;Long Day\u0026#39;s Journey Into Night\u0026#34;! \u0026#34;Fences\u0026#34;! It\u0026#39;s amazing how many of the Great Plays center on confrontations of fathers and sons (sons \u003cem\u003eand\u003c/em\u003e daughters, in the case of \u0026#34;King Lear.\u0026#34;) \u003cstrong\u003eRead it\u003c/strong\u003e: \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2022/06/14/fathers-day-2022-father-son-relationships-theater/7468870001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eIt\u0026#39;s alway Father\u0026#39;s Day in the theater.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/dining/2022/06/13/fathers-day-dinner-near-me-north-jersey-restaurant-specials/7544212001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eBarbecue to escargot: 9 North Jersey restaurants offering Father\u0026#39;s Day dining specials\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "3576351002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEvery dad deserves to eat well on Father\u0026#39;s Day. Here are North Jersey restaurants of diverse creeds offering special meals for dad on June 19. (Don\u0026#39;t worry, there\u0026#39;s plenty of barbecue on here, too.) \u003cem\u003eEditor\u0026#39;s note: This story is from 2022, so specials will have changed. Call ahead. \u003c/em\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRead it:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/dining/2022/06/13/fathers-day-dinner-near-me-north-jersey-restaurant-specials/7544212001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day dining specials\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2021/06/09/fathers-day-gifts-2021-gardening-tools-vegan-cookbook/7534317002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eTies? Golf clubs? Grilling tools? Enough. Try these Father\u0026#39;s Day gifts instead\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt\u0026#39;s 2021. Social roles are evolving. Even the most conventional of us are becoming familiar with terms like \u0026#34;stay-at-home-dad\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;non-binary.\u0026#34; So why, on Father\u0026#39;s Day, are we still giving dad golf clubs? You know your own dad best, of course. But we think that, in the second decade of the twenty-first century, it\u0026#39;s time to think outside the tool box. Here are some alternative suggestions. Read it: Different gifts for Father\u0026#39;s Day.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/life/2021/06/15/alzheimers-disease-dementia-parent/7601336002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eMy dad has dementia, but I’m still learning from him\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "7606164002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn Father’s Day, I will remember the man who took me ice-skating at the local rink every weekend; who listened patiently in the car as I spilled my teenage dating problems; who linked his arm in mine as we walked down the aisle towards my husband-to-be, and whispered how proud he was of me. What makes this Father\u0026#39;s Day especially poignant is that my dad is still around. He’s alive, but he’s not the man who helped raise me and my two younger sisters. At 89, he\u0026#39;s been diagnosed with Alzheimer’s Disease. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/life/2021/06/15/alzheimers-disease-dementia-parent/7601336002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eMy dad has dementia, but I’m still learning from him.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/bergen/2019/06/13/fathers-day-nj-bergen-men-balance-life-dads-and-first-responders/1337895001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eBergen County first responders share the struggles and joys of fatherhood\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "11610050002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn 2019, we asked you to nominate Bergen County first responders who are also fathers. We at (201) Magazine would like to thank all the emergency personnel who protect us on a daily basis, and we honor them by highlighting the five individuals here. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/bergen/2019/06/13/fathers-day-nj-bergen-men-balance-life-dads-and-first-responders/1337895001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eBergen County first responders share the struggles and joys of fatherhood\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/sports/2019/06/13/fathers-day-memory-baseball-player-home-run-caught-his-father/1435717001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eImagine catching a home run hit by your son? This dad did it, and he’ll never forget it\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "1437791001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEvery spring, in the days heading into Father’s Day, Conrad Gregor remembers his unique home run – the one that his own father actually caught. Marty Gregor is reminded every day of the catch he made on his son’s first minor league homer of the 2014 season. “I look at it every morning when I get up and start my day,” Marty said. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/sports/2019/06/13/fathers-day-memory-baseball-player-home-run-caught-his-father/1435717001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eImagine catching a home run hit by your son?\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2017/06/16/stylish/383938001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e7 Bergen dads share their favorite dish, fashion item and plans for Father\u0026#39;s Day \u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "102919280"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eA real estate developer who loves his Montblanc watch. A managing director who would wear Stan Smiths every day, if he could. A small business owner who is obsessed with 7 for All Mankind jeans. These — plus four other fashionable Bergen dads — may gravitate toward different styles, but they all share one thing in common: the love of their kids. With Father\u0026#39;s Day in mind, we asked these Dads to share their favorite things about  North Jersey, from fashion to food to the perfect Father\u0026#39;s Day. Read it: \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2017/06/16/stylish/383938001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e7 Bergen dads share their favorite dish, fashion item and plans for Father\u0026#39;s Day.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.app.com/story/opinion/columnists/2014/06/13/issue-fathers-day/10465407/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day: What do you most admire about Dad?\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "35921811"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day is a time for remembering what it was, and is, that our dads have given us over the years. It is a day to think about the lessons he taught us, intentionally or unintentionally, and how they have stayed with us. In that spirit, we asked our readers to answer the following two questions: What quality or qualities do you/did you most admire in your father? And when did you first begin to appreciate those qualities? We were rewarded with tough, tender, touching and funny responses. Read it: What do you admire about Dad?\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOPINION\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2017/06/02/ervolino-dear-fathers-day-youre-no-mothers-day/355988001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eErvolino: Dear Father\u0026#39;s Day, you\u0026#39;re no Mother\u0026#39;s Day\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "3155500002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWell, no matter how much we love our fathers, many of us have a hard time making Father’s Day plans. Read it: \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2017/06/02/ervolino-dear-fathers-day-youre-no-mothers-day/355988001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eYou\u0026#39;re no Mother\u0026#39;s Day!\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/opinion/2023/06/16/fathers-day-embrace-those-colorful-ties-dad-and-the-memories-too/70323504007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day 2023: Embrace the journey, dads — and those ties, too | Opinion\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eLearning to be a good father did not come naturally to me. I made countless mistakes, but read books, took classes, and spent lots of time talking with my wife and other fathers in order to be a better dad to my kids. Talking to other fathers was a lifesaver, and one thing it taught me was that being a father is never-ending. Even in death, some believe you continue to watch over your children. I believe my dad watches me and one day I will do the same for my kids.. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/opinion/2023/06/16/fathers-day-embrace-those-colorful-ties-dad-and-the-memories-too/70323504007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eEmbrace the journey.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

contentBody:
{
  "contentBody": [{
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "7540272001"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day isn\u0026#39;t exactly like Mother\u0026#39;s Day, we know. We usually don\u0026#39;t serve Dad breakfast in bed, give him flowers or pamper him. But why shouldn\u0026#39;t we, asks our reporter Jim Beckerman, in a story from 2021. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eOr we could take him out to dinner, proffers our NorthJerseyEats food team. (They also suggest some great gifts for foodie Dads.) \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eOr we could just celebrate him — as many of our stories, photos and videos have over the years. We thought it would be nice to gather them here, and we hope you enjoy reading our tributes, profiles, essays and suggestions for great things to do, make and buy for Father\u0026#39;s Day.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eHere\u0026#39;s to Dad!\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/health/2024/06/13/fathers-day-stories-nj-man-beats-testicular-esophageal-cancer/74055385007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/health/2024/06/13/fathers-day-stories-nj-man-beats-testicular-esophageal-cancer/74055385007/\"\u003eNJ man who beat two kinds of cancer celebrates Father\u0026#39;s Day as a granddad of six\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74062298007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs barbecues are fired up across New Jersey this Sunday and neckties and wristwatches are unwrapped, few will appreciate Father\u0026#39;s Day as much as John Keane. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/health/2024/06/13/fathers-day-stories-nj-man-beats-testicular-esophageal-cancer/74055385007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/health/2024/06/13/fathers-day-stories-nj-man-beats-testicular-esophageal-cancer/74055385007/\"\u003eNJ man who beat two kinds of cancer celebrates Father\u0026#39;s Day as a granddad of six\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/columnists/jim-beckerman/2023/06/14/fathers-day-2023-first-without-father/70299555007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eLife Without Father? One Father\u0026#39;s Day, it will happen to you\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "12062607002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThese are among the hundreds of little, unnoticed gifts that all fathers give their children. You probably have similar memories. His gifts to me? I still have them all. And every day, I remember a new one. Happy Father\u0026#39;s Day, dad. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/columnists/jim-beckerman/2023/06/14/fathers-day-2023-first-without-father/70299555007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eMy first Father\u0026#39;s Day without a father.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/sports/mlb/yankees/2023/06/14/gleyber-torres-yankees-player-fathers-day-with-young-son/70317284007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e\u0026#39;I know I have something special\u0026#39;: How Gleyber Torres appreciates fatherhood and baseball\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e“In the past, I’d go straight to the house and just think about a bad situation – why did I strike out, or if I make an error,’’ said Torres. “And now, with a baby, I know I have something special when I get back home.\u0026#34; \u003cstrong\u003eRead it: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/sports/mlb/yankees/2023/06/14/gleyber-torres-yankees-player-fathers-day-with-young-son/70317284007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eGleyber Torres on fatherhood.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/health/2023/06/16/fathers-day-2023-nj-twins-lost-dad-cancer-doctors/70317832007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day tribute: NJ twins became doctors and battle cancer in memory of dad\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "12098456002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFakhruddin Danish\u0026#39;s memory lives on every time Dr. Adnan Danish kills a cancer cell with radiation or Dr. Shabbar Danish performs surgery on a brain tumor. The two brothers have become well-regarded physicians in New Jersey, rising to the top of their field with a disease they know all too well. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/health/2023/06/16/fathers-day-2023-nj-twins-lost-dad-cancer-doctors/70317832007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eTwins battle cancer in memory of dad\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/passaic/north-haledon/2023/06/16/north-haledon-nj-man-meets-birth-father-first-time-after-30-years/70320998007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eDNA test allows North Jersey man to meet birth father for first time in his life\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "12117008002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eJoseph Federico said the results of his DNA test showed that he had a first cousin in the 23andMe database, living in East Orange. He said he contacted his match — the company allows users to chat online with genetic relatives — and she told him that he resembled her uncle, Sergio. Before too long, Federico’s cousin connected them. And on Dec. 16 — 30 years from the day that he was given up for adoption — father and son were reunited in person. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/passaic/north-haledon/2023/06/16/north-haledon-nj-man-meets-birth-father-first-time-after-30-years/70320998007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eNorth Jersey man meets his father, 30 years later.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.app.com/story/entertainment/events/summer-guide/2022/06/21/nj-breweries-visit-jersey-shore-summer/6921749001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eTake Dad on a beer crawl down the Shore\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "27157115"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFew things say \u0026#34;summer at the Jersey Shore\u0026#34; quite like beaches and beer. So why not combine them? After all, we have plenty of craft breweries in beach towns. Here, for your summertime fun time pleasure, are 27 of them (and yes, beaches on bays, rivers and lakes count), listed geographically from north to south. Read it: Craft brew tour for Dad.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.app.com/story/entertainment/dining/2020/06/02/jersey-made-fathers-day-food-gifts/5212207002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e12 Jersey-made Father\u0026#39;s Day gifts for food-loving dads\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "104731540"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis Father\u0026#39;s Day, consider an edible gift, most made and sold right here in New Jersey. For dads who love their grills and smokers, there\u0026#39;s barbecue sauce to brush on brisket and bacon jam to dollop on burgers. Dad love sweets? Treat him to a flight of cakes or a dessert with his picture on it. Such gifts are doubly delicious: By ordering from these and other local producers, not only will you score a great gift for Dad, you\u0026#39;ll help a small business in tough times. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.app.com/story/entertainment/dining/2020/06/02/jersey-made-fathers-day-food-gifts/5212207002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eFoodie Father\u0026#39;s Day gifts.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2022/06/14/fathers-day-2022-father-son-relationships-theater/7468870001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eIt\u0026#39;s always Father\u0026#39;s Day in the theater, where complicated relationships make great drama\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "99447940"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThere is one sort of person who never stops thinking about father. Someone who obsesses over dad, broods over dad, can\u0026#39;t let dad go. Someone who tries — on a nightly basis — to confront him, exorcise him, forgive him, or be forgiven by him. That person is a playwright. \u0026#34;Oedipus Rex\u0026#34;!  \u0026#34;Hamlet\u0026#34;! \u0026#34;King Lear\u0026#34;! \u0026#34;Death of a Salesman\u0026#34;! \u0026#34;Long Day\u0026#39;s Journey Into Night\u0026#34;! \u0026#34;Fences\u0026#34;! It\u0026#39;s amazing how many of the Great Plays center on confrontations of fathers and sons (sons \u003cem\u003eand\u003c/em\u003e daughters, in the case of \u0026#34;King Lear.\u0026#34;) \u003cstrong\u003eRead it\u003c/strong\u003e: \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2022/06/14/fathers-day-2022-father-son-relationships-theater/7468870001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eIt\u0026#39;s alway Father\u0026#39;s Day in the theater.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/dining/2022/06/13/fathers-day-dinner-near-me-north-jersey-restaurant-specials/7544212001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eBarbecue to escargot: 9 North Jersey restaurants offering Father\u0026#39;s Day dining specials\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "3576351002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eEvery dad deserves to eat well on Father\u0026#39;s Day. Here are North Jersey restaurants of diverse creeds offering special meals for dad on June 19. (Don\u0026#39;t worry, there\u0026#39;s plenty of barbecue on here, too.) \u003cem\u003eEditor\u0026#39;s note: This story is from 2022, so specials will have changed. Call ahead. \u003c/em\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRead it:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/dining/2022/06/13/fathers-day-dinner-near-me-north-jersey-restaurant-specials/7544212001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day dining specials\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2021/06/09/fathers-day-gifts-2021-gardening-tools-vegan-cookbook/7534317002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eTies? Golf clubs? Grilling tools? Enough. Try these Father\u0026#39;s Day gifts instead\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt\u0026#39;s 2021. Social roles are evolving. Even the most conventional of us are becoming familiar with terms like \u0026#34;stay-at-home-dad\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;non-binary.\u0026#34; So why, on Father\u0026#39;s Day, are we still giving dad golf clubs? You know your own dad best, of course. But we think that, in the second decade of the twenty-first century, it\u0026#39;s time to think outside the tool box. Here are some alternative suggestions. Read it: Different gifts for Father\u0026#39;s Day.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/life/2021/06/15/alzheimers-disease-dementia-parent/7601336002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eMy dad has dementia, but I’m still learning from him\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "7606164002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn Father’s Day, I will remember the man who took me ice-skating at the local rink every weekend; who listened patiently in the car as I spilled my teenage dating problems; who linked his arm in mine as we walked down the aisle towards my husband-to-be, and whispered how proud he was of me. What makes this Father\u0026#39;s Day especially poignant is that my dad is still around. He’s alive, but he’s not the man who helped raise me and my two younger sisters. At 89, he\u0026#39;s been diagnosed with Alzheimer’s Disease. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/life/2021/06/15/alzheimers-disease-dementia-parent/7601336002/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eMy dad has dementia, but I’m still learning from him.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/bergen/2019/06/13/fathers-day-nj-bergen-men-balance-life-dads-and-first-responders/1337895001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eBergen County first responders share the struggles and joys of fatherhood\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "11610050002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn 2019, we asked you to nominate Bergen County first responders who are also fathers. We at (201) Magazine would like to thank all the emergency personnel who protect us on a daily basis, and we honor them by highlighting the five individuals here. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/bergen/2019/06/13/fathers-day-nj-bergen-men-balance-life-dads-and-first-responders/1337895001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eBergen County first responders share the struggles and joys of fatherhood\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/sports/2019/06/13/fathers-day-memory-baseball-player-home-run-caught-his-father/1435717001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eImagine catching a home run hit by your son? This dad did it, and he’ll never forget it\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "1437791001"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eEvery spring, in the days heading into Father’s Day, Conrad Gregor remembers his unique home run – the one that his own father actually caught. Marty Gregor is reminded every day of the catch he made on his son’s first minor league homer of the 2014 season. “I look at it every morning when I get up and start my day,” Marty said. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/sports/2019/06/13/fathers-day-memory-baseball-player-home-run-caught-his-father/1435717001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eImagine catching a home run hit by your son?\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2017/06/16/stylish/383938001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e7 Bergen dads share their favorite dish, fashion item and plans for Father\u0026#39;s Day \u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "102919280"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eA real estate developer who loves his Montblanc watch. A managing director who would wear Stan Smiths every day, if he could. A small business owner who is obsessed with 7 for All Mankind jeans. These — plus four other fashionable Bergen dads — may gravitate toward different styles, but they all share one thing in common: the love of their kids. With Father\u0026#39;s Day in mind, we asked these Dads to share their favorite things about  North Jersey, from fashion to food to the perfect Father\u0026#39;s Day. Read it: \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2017/06/16/stylish/383938001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003e7 Bergen dads share their favorite dish, fashion item and plans for Father\u0026#39;s Day.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.app.com/story/opinion/columnists/2014/06/13/issue-fathers-day/10465407/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day: What do you most admire about Dad?\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "35921811"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day is a time for remembering what it was, and is, that our dads have given us over the years. It is a day to think about the lessons he taught us, intentionally or unintentionally, and how they have stayed with us. In that spirit, we asked our readers to answer the following two questions: What quality or qualities do you/did you most admire in your father? And when did you first begin to appreciate those qualities? We were rewarded with tough, tender, touching and funny responses. Read it: What do you admire about Dad?\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eOPINION\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2017/06/02/ervolino-dear-fathers-day-youre-no-mothers-day/355988001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eErvolino: Dear Father\u0026#39;s Day, you\u0026#39;re no Mother\u0026#39;s Day\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "3155500002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWell, no matter how much we love our fathers, many of us have a hard time making Father’s Day plans. Read it: \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2017/06/02/ervolino-dear-fathers-day-youre-no-mothers-day/355988001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eYou\u0026#39;re no Mother\u0026#39;s Day!\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/opinion/2023/06/16/fathers-day-embrace-those-colorful-ties-dad-and-the-memories-too/70323504007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day 2023: Embrace the journey, dads — and those ties, too | Opinion\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eLearning to be a good father did not come naturally to me. I made countless mistakes, but read books, took classes, and spent lots of time talking with my wife and other fathers in order to be a better dad to my kids. Talking to other fathers was a lifesaver, and one thing it taught me was that being a father is never-ending. Even in death, some believe you continue to watch over your children. I believe my dad watches me and one day I will do the same for my kids.. \u003cstrong\u003eRead it: \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/opinion/2023/06/16/fathers-day-embrace-those-colorful-ties-dad-and-the-memories-too/70323504007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noopener\"\u003eEmbrace the journey.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73999204007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWith history, nature, sports, music and barbecue, North Jersey has a little bit of everything this weekend.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFor some local history, take a guided tour at the Paterson\u0026#39;s Great Falls Park or learn about the Nubian Heritage Quilters Guild in Montclair. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/environment/2024/06/07/nj-has-lots-of-people-but-also-11-state-forests-to-explore/73974608007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/environment/2024/06/07/nj-has-lots-of-people-but-also-11-state-forests-to-explore/73974608007/\"\u003eThe outdoor types might also enjoy a hike\u003c/a\u003e in Tenafly.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFor some rock music, revisit the \u0026#39;90s in Teaneck with tributes to Nirvana, Hole and Weezer; or the \u0026#39;70s and \u0026#39;80s with Almost Queen. If Latin music is preferred, look no further than the Prudential Center for Grupo Firme. For a more refined musical (and dance!) experience, there\u0026#39;s a chorus and orchestra concert at American Dream, and an afternoon of tango in Rutherford.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003ePlus, local theater productions include \u0026#34;Cartoon\u0026#34; at Bergen Community College and \u0026#34;Applause\u0026#34; in Leonia; there\u0026#39;s a barbecue extravaganza at the Meadowlands Racetrack; and the Red Bulls have a home soccer game in Harrison.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eNot enough? Check out Maddie McGay\u0026#39;s list of more \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/05/29/fathers-day-in-north-jersey-2024-nj-events/73768530007/\"\u003ethings to do this Father\u0026#39;s Day\u003c/a\u003e weekend.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEnjoy!\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eStory continues below gallery\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74050271007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMostly sunny days, possible storms Friday\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAccording to the National Weather Service:\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThursday night:\u003c/strong\u003e Partly cloudy, with a low around 70.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFriday\u003c/strong\u003e: Mostly sunny with a high around 90, but showers are likely, with a possible thunderstorm, in the afternoon and evening. Low in the mid-60s.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSaturday\u003c/strong\u003e: Sunny, with a high in the mid-80s and a low around 60.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day:\u003c/strong\u003e Sunny during the day on Sunday, with a high in the low 80s. Partly cloudy at night, with a low in the mid-60s\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003ePaterson Great Falls orientation walking tour\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eTake \u0026#34;A Stroll Through History\u0026#34; at Paterson Great Falls National Historical Park at 2 p.m. every Wednesday through Sunday until Nov. 30. This free guided tour meets at the Alexander Hamilton Statue near the picnic tables.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe story of Paterson and its Great Falls demonstrates how the natural and cultural diversity of the area helped fuel the economic and social growth of a young nation. Join a staff member for this 45- to 60-minute, one-mile walk to discover how the natural world inspired a founding father, entrepreneurs, immigrants, poets and artists to build the nation\u0026#39;s first industrial city.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWear comfortable and weather-appropriate clothing/shoes. The walk will be on along paved and unpaved paths with uneven footing. Guided tours led by the National Park Service or its designees can follow paved, wheelchair-accessible routes (assistance may be required, especially along narrow city sidewalks). If you have any concerns or questions, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.nps.gov/pagr/contacts.htm\"\u003econtact the park\u003c/a\u003e and review the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.nps.gov/pagr/planyourvisit/accessibility.htm\"\u003eaccessibility resources\u003c/a\u003e. Tours are provided on weekends as staffing permits. Call 973-523-0370 the day of your visit to ensure availability\u003cem\u003e.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e A Stroll Through History at Paterson Great Falls National Historical Park, 72 McBride Ave. Extension. 1 p.m. Wednesday through Sunday. Free.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72012665007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNubian Heritage Quilters Guild at Montclair History Center\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe NHQG celebrates its 29th anniversary with its exhibit, \u0026#34;Honoring Our Heritage: One Stitch at a Time,\u0026#34; at the Crane House \u0026amp; Historic YWCA Museum in Montclair, on view every Sunday through July 14. In addition to a variety of a quilting styles, NHQG will present quilts and wall hangings that showcase patchwork, applique, collage and abstract textiles. Additional special exhibits include Legacy of Black Mermaids, African American Suffragists, African Gala, Mardi Gras Masks, NHQG Retreat, Unique Pincushions and African Village. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe schedule includes workshops and demonstrations for families this Saturday and Sunday. Plus, join the NHQG on Zoom for \u0026#34;History at Home: Legacy of Black Mermaids with the Nubian Heritage Quilters Guild\u0026#34; on Thursday. Drawn from the rich folklore of Water Goddesses and Mermen, Black Mermaids traveled with the enslaved to comfort them on the ships that took them away from their homeland. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e  \u0026#34;Honoring Our Heritage: One Stitch at a Time\u0026#34; at Montclair History Center\u0026#39;s Crane House \u0026amp; Historic YMCA Museum, 110 Orange Road, Montclair. Noon to 3 p.m. Saturday and Sunday. In lieu of regular tour admission prices, suggested donations of $5 per visitor will be honored. The program is free but registration is required at \u003ca href\u003d\"http://montclairhistory.org/all-events\"\u003emontclairhistory.org/all-events\u003c/a\u003e. Visit \u003ca href\u003d\"http://nubianquilters.org\"\u003enubianquilters.org\u003c/a\u003e for information about NHQG. \u0026#34;History at Home: Legacy of Black Mermaids with the Nubian Heritage Quilters Guild\u0026#34; via Zoom, 7 p.m. Thursday; free.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBergen Alumni Theatre production of \u0026#39;Cartoon\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBergenstages and the Bergen Institute for the Creative Arts at Bergen Community College presents the Bergen Alumni Theatre production of \u0026#34;Cartoon\u0026#34; by Steve Yockey, directed by Christine Dunning with fight direction by Kevin Maphis, on Friday and Saturday.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJoin the exploits of a band of mismatched cartoon stereotypes on a wild ride through an animated world. Presented in the style of a Commedia dell’Arte scenario gone berserk, \u0026#34;Cartoon\u0026#34; is a devilishly violent, PG-13 rated social commentary that explores the rapid coalescence of media, politics and consumer giants. A young, idealistic upstart named Trouble steals the giant hammer that Esther, the bratty dictator, uses to maintain a monotonous but peaceful order. Chaos ensues. Bombs explode. Puppets are set free. Anime girls fight. And as the bodies pile up, the violence begins to creep off the stage. There’s nothing like a punch in the face to really get the blood moving. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e\u0026#34;Cartoon\u0026#34; at the Ender Hall Lab Theatre on the campus of Bergen Community College, 400 Paramus Road, Paramus. 7:30 p.m. Friday; 2 and 7:30 p.m. Saturday. $5 to $15.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMeadowlands Racetrack BBQ Extravaganza\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn Saturday at Meadowlands Racing \u0026amp; Entertainment, chow down on some barbecue from area food trucks and restaurants in the area. The vendors will compete for $2,500 in prize money in categories such as chicken, pulled pork, brisket, ribs and people’s choice. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFood trucks will include Magic Mike\u0026#39;s Smoked Meat, Fire \u0026amp; Coal BBQ Grill, DAW Concessions, Uncle Bob’s Kettle Corn, Freakin Empanadas, Totally Nutz, Latin Bites, Antojitos de mi Tierra, Bitchn’ Bacon, Cyldes Homemade Italian Ice \u0026amp; Ice Cream, Cat Like Reflexes, Rods Fish N Chips, Delicious Lola Josefa’s, Holy Grail Burgers, Michael’s Backyard BBQ, Love JoJo’s Cookies, Top Tea Plug, The Jamaican Food Truck, Kimchi Smoke, The Hen \u0026amp; The Hog, Rhythm + Ribz Smokehouse, Wild Bill’s Craft Beverage Co, Uncle Eddies Touch of Sauce, Gringo Arepas and Highland Bites.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e BBQ Extravaganza at Meadowlands Racetrack in East Rutherford. 5 to 11 p.m. Saturday. Live racing begins at 6:20. Food truck winners will be announced at 9. Free admission. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://playmeadowlands.com/event/meadowlands-racetrack-bbq-extravaganza/\"\u003eplaymeadowlands.com\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003ePlayers Guild of Leonia presents \u0026#39;Applause\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWith sass, wit and a pulsing 1970s score, \u0026#34;Applause\u0026#34; presents show biz in all its glory and ferocity on Friday, Saturday and Sunday. The updated musical version of Mary Orr\u0026#39;s story \u0026#34;All About Eve\u0026#34; concerns superstar Margot Channing and her ambitious, scheming assistant, Eve Harrington. Directed by Craig M. Tiede, book by Betty Comden and Adolph Green, music by Charles Strouse, lyrics by Lee Adams. The musical\u0026#39;s songs include \u0026#34;But Alive,\u0026#34; \u0026#34;Applause,\u0026#34; \u0026#34;Welcome to the Theater\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;Something Greater.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The strength of \u0026#39;All About Eve,\u0026#39; so soundly conceived and executed on the screen, lay in the timelessness of its basic story,\u0026#34; wrote Comden and Green. \u0026#34;It is a tale of treachery…told in terms of the witty, glamorous theatre star and the mousy, adoring girl from the sticks who ingratiates herself into the star\u0026#39;s private world, and then systematically attempts to take over her career, her lover and her life.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026#34;Applause\u0026#34; at the Players Guild of Leonia, 130 Grand Ave. 8 p.m. Friday and Saturday, 2 p.m. Sunday. $29; $25 for seniors and students. Free parking is available at the Leonia Swim Club on Moore Street, just off of Grand Avenue. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.leoniaplayers.org/\"\u003eleoniaplayers.org\u003c/a\u003e for information, showtix4u.com for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.showtix4u.com/event-details/76050\"\u003etickets\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eArgentine tango comes to Williams Center\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSpend your afternoon in Rutherford and experience Argentine tango with a beginner’s class, performance and music for dancing. Plus, taste original empanadas recipes and ice cream from Argentina by Cones. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFrom the international show, “Tango Lovers,” and the “Tango Houses” Cafe de los Angelitos and Rojo Tango/Faena Hotel in Buenos Aires, Yesica Esquivel and Ariel Leguizamon will teach and perform. DJ Rainier Pereira will provide the music. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEsquivel and Leguizamon are professional dancers of Argentine tango and folklore. They been dancing together for 17 years, and they have toured with Roberto Herrera’s company, “Tanguera, The Musical,” “Estampas Porteñas” and “Tango Legends;” and in Buenos Aires at the dinner tango shows, “Piazzolla Tango,” “Catulo Tango,” “Candilejas,” “La Casa de Anibal Troilo” and “Taconeando.” They were champions of Pelando Variaciones 2016 and guest artists and teachers at Portland Tango Festival 2017, Baden-Baden tango festival 2019/2022 (Germany) and CITA 2022 (Argentina). \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOrganized by Rougertango and the Williams Center, Rougertango reveals the pulse of the Porteña Culture, the culture of the birthplace of Argentine Tango, Buenos Aires, through live music by musicians and singers, dance performances, lessons and workshops, and the poetry of tango lyrics.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Argentine Tango at the Williams Center, 15 Sylvan St., Rutherford. Saturday. Doors open at 2 p.m., beginner\u0026#39;s class from 2:30 to 3:15, performance at 4, dancing until 6. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.williamscenter.co/events/argentine-tango\"\u003ewilliamscenter.co\u003c/a\u003e. $21.79.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNirvana, Hole, Weezer tributes in Teaneck\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eExperience the soundtrack of the \u0026#39;90s with Lounge Act - A Tribute to Nirvana, performing Saturday at Debonair Music Hall, along with All Violet - Hole Tribute and Say It Ain\u0026#39;t Scorcho - A Weezer Tribute at this all-ages show.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eLounge Act, All Violet and Say It Ain\u0026#39;t Scorcho at Debonair Music Hall, 1409 Queen Anne Road, Teaneck. 7:30 p.m. Saturday. Doors open at 7. $15 general admission; $20 reserved seating; $5 more at the door. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://debonairmusichall.com/?page_id\u003d565#/events/96852\"\u003edebonairmusichall.com\u003c/a\u003e, 201-833-0011. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eGrupo Firme at Prudential Center\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "10915915002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003ePart of the arena\u0026#39;s Latin Concert Series, presented by Goya, Grupo Firme bring their La Ultima Peda Tour to Prudential Center on Saturday.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Grupo Firme at Prudential Center, 25 Lafeyette St., Newark. 8 p.m. Saturday. Doors open at 7. $59.50 to $399.50.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eRed Bulls soccer in Harrison\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe New York Red Bulls face the Nashville SC on Saturday at Red Bull Arena in Harrison. It\u0026#39;s Collectible Night, with a soccer player mini-figurine giveaway.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Red Bulls soccer at Red Bull Arena, 600 Cape May St., Harrison. 7:30 p.m. Saturday. $14 to $256. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.newyorkredbulls.com/competitions/mls-regular-season/2024/matches/rbnyvsnsh-06-15-2024/\"\u003enewyorkredbulls.com\u003c/a\u003e for information. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.ticketmaster.com/new-york-red-bulls-vs-nashville-harrison-new-jersey-06-15-2024/event/00005F93709C0D68?_ga\u003d2.15827263.82229968.1717775083-1424301529.1709312262\u0026_gl\u003d1*oua3t8*_ga*MTQyNDMwMTUyOS4xNzA5MzEyMjYy*_ga_XS1HJ3N9M1*MTcxNzc3NTA4NC4yLjEuMTcxNzc3NTM5My4wLjAuMA..\"\u003eticketmaster.com\u003c/a\u003e for tickets.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eA Tribute to Queen at BergenPAC\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDonning genuine costumes, Almost Queen will deliver a live performance on Saturday showcasing the signature four-part harmonies and intricate musical interludes of the original band. The Steve Leonard Trio will open the show.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Almost Queen: A Tribute to Queen at BergenPAC, 30 N. Van Brunt St., Englewood. 8 p.m. Saturday. $45 to $85. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.bergenpac.org/events/detail/almost-queen-a-tribute-to-queen\"\u003ebergenpac.org\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "32862765"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSummer Family Hike at Tenafly Nature Center\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCelebrate Father\u0026#39;s Day and family with a guided walk with a TNC Environmental Educator on Sunday. Whether you’re an outdoor enthusiast or just hoping for a pretty photo op with the family, celebrate the day with a walk in nature. All ages welcome. Children must be accompanied by an adult. No strollers. In case of inclement weather, the program will be cancelled. Space is limited and advance registration is required.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Summer Family Hike at the Tenafly Nature Center, 313 Hudson Ave., Tenafly. 11 a.m. to 1 p.m. Sunday. $5 for members; $10 for non-members; free for children under age 2. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://tncnj.org/widget/event-5616480?CalendarViewType\u003d1\u0026SelectedDate\u003d5/28/2024\"\u003ehttps://tenaflynaturecenter.org/seasonal-programs/\u003c/a\u003e, 201-568-6093.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "36353333"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day concert at American Dream\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Edison Chinese Chorus and Edison Philharmonic Orchestra will present a hundred-member choir, conducted by Chunhe Zhang, with a cello solo by David Yu, a baritone performance by Xuefeng Wan and a Chinese folk dance.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Father\u0026#39;s Day concert by the Edison Chinese Chorus and Edison Philharmonic Orchestra at American Dream (Dream Stage, Court A, Level 1) in East Rutherford. 2 to 4 p.m Sunday. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.americandream.com/events/category\"\u003eamericandream.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eHave an event coming up? Tell us about it. Write to Daniel Galioto at galiotod@northjersey.com.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73999204007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWith history, nature, sports, music and barbecue, North Jersey has a little bit of everything this weekend.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFor some local history, take a guided tour at the Paterson\u0026#39;s Great Falls Park or learn about the Nubian Heritage Quilters Guild in Montclair. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/environment/2024/06/07/nj-has-lots-of-people-but-also-11-state-forests-to-explore/73974608007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/environment/2024/06/07/nj-has-lots-of-people-but-also-11-state-forests-to-explore/73974608007/\"\u003eThe outdoor types might also enjoy a hike\u003c/a\u003e in Tenafly.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFor some rock music, revisit the \u0026#39;90s in Teaneck with tributes to Nirvana, Hole and Weezer; or the \u0026#39;70s and \u0026#39;80s with Almost Queen. If Latin music is preferred, look no further than the Prudential Center for Grupo Firme. For a more refined musical (and dance!) experience, there\u0026#39;s a chorus and orchestra concert at American Dream, and an afternoon of tango in Rutherford.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003ePlus, local theater productions include \u0026#34;Cartoon\u0026#34; at Bergen Community College and \u0026#34;Applause\u0026#34; in Leonia; there\u0026#39;s a barbecue extravaganza at the Meadowlands Racetrack; and the Red Bulls have a home soccer game in Harrison.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eNot enough? Check out Maddie McGay\u0026#39;s list of more \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/05/29/fathers-day-in-north-jersey-2024-nj-events/73768530007/\"\u003ethings to do this Father\u0026#39;s Day\u003c/a\u003e weekend.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEnjoy!\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eStory continues below gallery\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74050271007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMostly sunny days, possible storms Friday\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAccording to the National Weather Service:\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThursday night:\u003c/strong\u003e Partly cloudy, with a low around 70.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFriday\u003c/strong\u003e: Mostly sunny with a high around 90, but showers are likely, with a possible thunderstorm, in the afternoon and evening. Low in the mid-60s.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSaturday\u003c/strong\u003e: Sunny, with a high in the mid-80s and a low around 60.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day:\u003c/strong\u003e Sunny during the day on Sunday, with a high in the low 80s. Partly cloudy at night, with a low in the mid-60s\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003ePaterson Great Falls orientation walking tour\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eTake \u0026#34;A Stroll Through History\u0026#34; at Paterson Great Falls National Historical Park at 2 p.m. every Wednesday through Sunday until Nov. 30. This free guided tour meets at the Alexander Hamilton Statue near the picnic tables.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe story of Paterson and its Great Falls demonstrates how the natural and cultural diversity of the area helped fuel the economic and social growth of a young nation. Join a staff member for this 45- to 60-minute, one-mile walk to discover how the natural world inspired a founding father, entrepreneurs, immigrants, poets and artists to build the nation\u0026#39;s first industrial city.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWear comfortable and weather-appropriate clothing/shoes. The walk will be on along paved and unpaved paths with uneven footing. Guided tours led by the National Park Service or its designees can follow paved, wheelchair-accessible routes (assistance may be required, especially along narrow city sidewalks). If you have any concerns or questions, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.nps.gov/pagr/contacts.htm\"\u003econtact the park\u003c/a\u003e and review the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.nps.gov/pagr/planyourvisit/accessibility.htm\"\u003eaccessibility resources\u003c/a\u003e. Tours are provided on weekends as staffing permits. Call 973-523-0370 the day of your visit to ensure availability\u003cem\u003e.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e A Stroll Through History at Paterson Great Falls National Historical Park, 72 McBride Ave. Extension. 1 p.m. Wednesday through Sunday. Free.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72012665007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNubian Heritage Quilters Guild at Montclair History Center\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe NHQG celebrates its 29th anniversary with its exhibit, \u0026#34;Honoring Our Heritage: One Stitch at a Time,\u0026#34; at the Crane House \u0026amp; Historic YWCA Museum in Montclair, on view every Sunday through July 14. In addition to a variety of a quilting styles, NHQG will present quilts and wall hangings that showcase patchwork, applique, collage and abstract textiles. Additional special exhibits include Legacy of Black Mermaids, African American Suffragists, African Gala, Mardi Gras Masks, NHQG Retreat, Unique Pincushions and African Village. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe schedule includes workshops and demonstrations for families this Saturday and Sunday. Plus, join the NHQG on Zoom for \u0026#34;History at Home: Legacy of Black Mermaids with the Nubian Heritage Quilters Guild\u0026#34; on Thursday. Drawn from the rich folklore of Water Goddesses and Mermen, Black Mermaids traveled with the enslaved to comfort them on the ships that took them away from their homeland. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e  \u0026#34;Honoring Our Heritage: One Stitch at a Time\u0026#34; at Montclair History Center\u0026#39;s Crane House \u0026amp; Historic YMCA Museum, 110 Orange Road, Montclair. Noon to 3 p.m. Saturday and Sunday. In lieu of regular tour admission prices, suggested donations of $5 per visitor will be honored. The program is free but registration is required at \u003ca href\u003d\"http://montclairhistory.org/all-events\"\u003emontclairhistory.org/all-events\u003c/a\u003e. Visit \u003ca href\u003d\"http://nubianquilters.org\"\u003enubianquilters.org\u003c/a\u003e for information about NHQG. \u0026#34;History at Home: Legacy of Black Mermaids with the Nubian Heritage Quilters Guild\u0026#34; via Zoom, 7 p.m. Thursday; free.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBergen Alumni Theatre production of \u0026#39;Cartoon\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBergenstages and the Bergen Institute for the Creative Arts at Bergen Community College presents the Bergen Alumni Theatre production of \u0026#34;Cartoon\u0026#34; by Steve Yockey, directed by Christine Dunning with fight direction by Kevin Maphis, on Friday and Saturday.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJoin the exploits of a band of mismatched cartoon stereotypes on a wild ride through an animated world. Presented in the style of a Commedia dell’Arte scenario gone berserk, \u0026#34;Cartoon\u0026#34; is a devilishly violent, PG-13 rated social commentary that explores the rapid coalescence of media, politics and consumer giants. A young, idealistic upstart named Trouble steals the giant hammer that Esther, the bratty dictator, uses to maintain a monotonous but peaceful order. Chaos ensues. Bombs explode. Puppets are set free. Anime girls fight. And as the bodies pile up, the violence begins to creep off the stage. There’s nothing like a punch in the face to really get the blood moving. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e\u0026#34;Cartoon\u0026#34; at the Ender Hall Lab Theatre on the campus of Bergen Community College, 400 Paramus Road, Paramus. 7:30 p.m. Friday; 2 and 7:30 p.m. Saturday. $5 to $15.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMeadowlands Racetrack BBQ Extravaganza\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn Saturday at Meadowlands Racing \u0026amp; Entertainment, chow down on some barbecue from area food trucks and restaurants in the area. The vendors will compete for $2,500 in prize money in categories such as chicken, pulled pork, brisket, ribs and people’s choice. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFood trucks will include Magic Mike\u0026#39;s Smoked Meat, Fire \u0026amp; Coal BBQ Grill, DAW Concessions, Uncle Bob’s Kettle Corn, Freakin Empanadas, Totally Nutz, Latin Bites, Antojitos de mi Tierra, Bitchn’ Bacon, Cyldes Homemade Italian Ice \u0026amp; Ice Cream, Cat Like Reflexes, Rods Fish N Chips, Delicious Lola Josefa’s, Holy Grail Burgers, Michael’s Backyard BBQ, Love JoJo’s Cookies, Top Tea Plug, The Jamaican Food Truck, Kimchi Smoke, The Hen \u0026amp; The Hog, Rhythm + Ribz Smokehouse, Wild Bill’s Craft Beverage Co, Uncle Eddies Touch of Sauce, Gringo Arepas and Highland Bites.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e BBQ Extravaganza at Meadowlands Racetrack in East Rutherford. 5 to 11 p.m. Saturday. Live racing begins at 6:20. Food truck winners will be announced at 9. Free admission. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://playmeadowlands.com/event/meadowlands-racetrack-bbq-extravaganza/\"\u003eplaymeadowlands.com\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003ePlayers Guild of Leonia presents \u0026#39;Applause\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWith sass, wit and a pulsing 1970s score, \u0026#34;Applause\u0026#34; presents show biz in all its glory and ferocity on Friday, Saturday and Sunday. The updated musical version of Mary Orr\u0026#39;s story \u0026#34;All About Eve\u0026#34; concerns superstar Margot Channing and her ambitious, scheming assistant, Eve Harrington. Directed by Craig M. Tiede, book by Betty Comden and Adolph Green, music by Charles Strouse, lyrics by Lee Adams. The musical\u0026#39;s songs include \u0026#34;But Alive,\u0026#34; \u0026#34;Applause,\u0026#34; \u0026#34;Welcome to the Theater\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;Something Greater.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The strength of \u0026#39;All About Eve,\u0026#39; so soundly conceived and executed on the screen, lay in the timelessness of its basic story,\u0026#34; wrote Comden and Green. \u0026#34;It is a tale of treachery…told in terms of the witty, glamorous theatre star and the mousy, adoring girl from the sticks who ingratiates herself into the star\u0026#39;s private world, and then systematically attempts to take over her career, her lover and her life.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026#34;Applause\u0026#34; at the Players Guild of Leonia, 130 Grand Ave. 8 p.m. Friday and Saturday, 2 p.m. Sunday. $29; $25 for seniors and students. Free parking is available at the Leonia Swim Club on Moore Street, just off of Grand Avenue. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.leoniaplayers.org/\"\u003eleoniaplayers.org\u003c/a\u003e for information, showtix4u.com for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.showtix4u.com/event-details/76050\"\u003etickets\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eArgentine tango comes to Williams Center\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSpend your afternoon in Rutherford and experience Argentine tango with a beginner’s class, performance and music for dancing. Plus, taste original empanadas recipes and ice cream from Argentina by Cones. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFrom the international show, “Tango Lovers,” and the “Tango Houses” Cafe de los Angelitos and Rojo Tango/Faena Hotel in Buenos Aires, Yesica Esquivel and Ariel Leguizamon will teach and perform. DJ Rainier Pereira will provide the music. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEsquivel and Leguizamon are professional dancers of Argentine tango and folklore. They been dancing together for 17 years, and they have toured with Roberto Herrera’s company, “Tanguera, The Musical,” “Estampas Porteñas” and “Tango Legends;” and in Buenos Aires at the dinner tango shows, “Piazzolla Tango,” “Catulo Tango,” “Candilejas,” “La Casa de Anibal Troilo” and “Taconeando.” They were champions of Pelando Variaciones 2016 and guest artists and teachers at Portland Tango Festival 2017, Baden-Baden tango festival 2019/2022 (Germany) and CITA 2022 (Argentina). \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOrganized by Rougertango and the Williams Center, Rougertango reveals the pulse of the Porteña Culture, the culture of the birthplace of Argentine Tango, Buenos Aires, through live music by musicians and singers, dance performances, lessons and workshops, and the poetry of tango lyrics.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Argentine Tango at the Williams Center, 15 Sylvan St., Rutherford. Saturday. Doors open at 2 p.m., beginner\u0026#39;s class from 2:30 to 3:15, performance at 4, dancing until 6. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.williamscenter.co/events/argentine-tango\"\u003ewilliamscenter.co\u003c/a\u003e. $21.79.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNirvana, Hole, Weezer tributes in Teaneck\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eExperience the soundtrack of the \u0026#39;90s with Lounge Act - A Tribute to Nirvana, performing Saturday at Debonair Music Hall, along with All Violet - Hole Tribute and Say It Ain\u0026#39;t Scorcho - A Weezer Tribute at this all-ages show.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eLounge Act, All Violet and Say It Ain\u0026#39;t Scorcho at Debonair Music Hall, 1409 Queen Anne Road, Teaneck. 7:30 p.m. Saturday. Doors open at 7. $15 general admission; $20 reserved seating; $5 more at the door. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://debonairmusichall.com/?page_id\u003d565#/events/96852\"\u003edebonairmusichall.com\u003c/a\u003e, 201-833-0011. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eGrupo Firme at Prudential Center\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "10915915002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003ePart of the arena\u0026#39;s Latin Concert Series, presented by Goya, Grupo Firme bring their La Ultima Peda Tour to Prudential Center on Saturday.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Grupo Firme at Prudential Center, 25 Lafeyette St., Newark. 8 p.m. Saturday. Doors open at 7. $59.50 to $399.50.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eRed Bulls soccer in Harrison\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe New York Red Bulls face the Nashville SC on Saturday at Red Bull Arena in Harrison. It\u0026#39;s Collectible Night, with a soccer player mini-figurine giveaway.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Red Bulls soccer at Red Bull Arena, 600 Cape May St., Harrison. 7:30 p.m. Saturday. $14 to $256. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.newyorkredbulls.com/competitions/mls-regular-season/2024/matches/rbnyvsnsh-06-15-2024/\"\u003enewyorkredbulls.com\u003c/a\u003e for information. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.ticketmaster.com/new-york-red-bulls-vs-nashville-harrison-new-jersey-06-15-2024/event/00005F93709C0D68?_ga\u003d2.15827263.82229968.1717775083-1424301529.1709312262\u0026_gl\u003d1*oua3t8*_ga*MTQyNDMwMTUyOS4xNzA5MzEyMjYy*_ga_XS1HJ3N9M1*MTcxNzc3NTA4NC4yLjEuMTcxNzc3NTM5My4wLjAuMA..\"\u003eticketmaster.com\u003c/a\u003e for tickets.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eA Tribute to Queen at BergenPAC\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDonning genuine costumes, Almost Queen will deliver a live performance on Saturday showcasing the signature four-part harmonies and intricate musical interludes of the original band. The Steve Leonard Trio will open the show.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Almost Queen: A Tribute to Queen at BergenPAC, 30 N. Van Brunt St., Englewood. 8 p.m. Saturday. $45 to $85. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.bergenpac.org/events/detail/almost-queen-a-tribute-to-queen\"\u003ebergenpac.org\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "32862765"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSummer Family Hike at Tenafly Nature Center\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCelebrate Father\u0026#39;s Day and family with a guided walk with a TNC Environmental Educator on Sunday. Whether you’re an outdoor enthusiast or just hoping for a pretty photo op with the family, celebrate the day with a walk in nature. All ages welcome. Children must be accompanied by an adult. No strollers. In case of inclement weather, the program will be cancelled. Space is limited and advance registration is required.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Summer Family Hike at the Tenafly Nature Center, 313 Hudson Ave., Tenafly. 11 a.m. to 1 p.m. Sunday. $5 for members; $10 for non-members; free for children under age 2. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://tncnj.org/widget/event-5616480?CalendarViewType\u003d1\u0026SelectedDate\u003d5/28/2024\"\u003ehttps://tenaflynaturecenter.org/seasonal-programs/\u003c/a\u003e, 201-568-6093.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "36353333"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day concert at American Dream\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Edison Chinese Chorus and Edison Philharmonic Orchestra will present a hundred-member choir, conducted by Chunhe Zhang, with a cello solo by David Yu, a baritone performance by Xuefeng Wan and a Chinese folk dance.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Father\u0026#39;s Day concert by the Edison Chinese Chorus and Edison Philharmonic Orchestra at American Dream (Dream Stage, Court A, Level 1) in East Rutherford. 2 to 4 p.m Sunday. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.americandream.com/events/category\"\u003eamericandream.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eHave an event coming up? Tell us about it. Write to Daniel Galioto at galiotod@northjersey.com.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

contentBody:
{
  "contentBody": [{
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73999204007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWith history, nature, sports, music and barbecue, North Jersey has a little bit of everything this weekend.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFor some local history, take a guided tour at the Paterson\u0026#39;s Great Falls Park or learn about the Nubian Heritage Quilters Guild in Montclair. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/environment/2024/06/07/nj-has-lots-of-people-but-also-11-state-forests-to-explore/73974608007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/environment/2024/06/07/nj-has-lots-of-people-but-also-11-state-forests-to-explore/73974608007/\"\u003eThe outdoor types might also enjoy a hike\u003c/a\u003e in Tenafly.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFor some rock music, revisit the \u0026#39;90s in Teaneck with tributes to Nirvana, Hole and Weezer; or the \u0026#39;70s and \u0026#39;80s with Almost Queen. If Latin music is preferred, look no further than the Prudential Center for Grupo Firme. For a more refined musical (and dance!) experience, there\u0026#39;s a chorus and orchestra concert at American Dream, and an afternoon of tango in Rutherford.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003ePlus, local theater productions include \u0026#34;Cartoon\u0026#34; at Bergen Community College and \u0026#34;Applause\u0026#34; in Leonia; there\u0026#39;s a barbecue extravaganza at the Meadowlands Racetrack; and the Red Bulls have a home soccer game in Harrison.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eNot enough? Check out Maddie McGay\u0026#39;s list of more \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/05/29/fathers-day-in-north-jersey-2024-nj-events/73768530007/\"\u003ethings to do this Father\u0026#39;s Day\u003c/a\u003e weekend.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eEnjoy!\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eStory continues below gallery\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74050271007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMostly sunny days, possible storms Friday\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAccording to the National Weather Service:\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThursday night:\u003c/strong\u003e Partly cloudy, with a low around 70.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFriday\u003c/strong\u003e: Mostly sunny with a high around 90, but showers are likely, with a possible thunderstorm, in the afternoon and evening. Low in the mid-60s.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSaturday\u003c/strong\u003e: Sunny, with a high in the mid-80s and a low around 60.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day:\u003c/strong\u003e Sunny during the day on Sunday, with a high in the low 80s. Partly cloudy at night, with a low in the mid-60s\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003ePaterson Great Falls orientation walking tour\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eTake \u0026#34;A Stroll Through History\u0026#34; at Paterson Great Falls National Historical Park at 2 p.m. every Wednesday through Sunday until Nov. 30. This free guided tour meets at the Alexander Hamilton Statue near the picnic tables.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe story of Paterson and its Great Falls demonstrates how the natural and cultural diversity of the area helped fuel the economic and social growth of a young nation. Join a staff member for this 45- to 60-minute, one-mile walk to discover how the natural world inspired a founding father, entrepreneurs, immigrants, poets and artists to build the nation\u0026#39;s first industrial city.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWear comfortable and weather-appropriate clothing/shoes. The walk will be on along paved and unpaved paths with uneven footing. Guided tours led by the National Park Service or its designees can follow paved, wheelchair-accessible routes (assistance may be required, especially along narrow city sidewalks). If you have any concerns or questions, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.nps.gov/pagr/contacts.htm\"\u003econtact the park\u003c/a\u003e and review the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.nps.gov/pagr/planyourvisit/accessibility.htm\"\u003eaccessibility resources\u003c/a\u003e. Tours are provided on weekends as staffing permits. Call 973-523-0370 the day of your visit to ensure availability\u003cem\u003e.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e A Stroll Through History at Paterson Great Falls National Historical Park, 72 McBride Ave. Extension. 1 p.m. Wednesday through Sunday. Free.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "72012665007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNubian Heritage Quilters Guild at Montclair History Center\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe NHQG celebrates its 29th anniversary with its exhibit, \u0026#34;Honoring Our Heritage: One Stitch at a Time,\u0026#34; at the Crane House \u0026amp; Historic YWCA Museum in Montclair, on view every Sunday through July 14. In addition to a variety of a quilting styles, NHQG will present quilts and wall hangings that showcase patchwork, applique, collage and abstract textiles. Additional special exhibits include Legacy of Black Mermaids, African American Suffragists, African Gala, Mardi Gras Masks, NHQG Retreat, Unique Pincushions and African Village. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe schedule includes workshops and demonstrations for families this Saturday and Sunday. Plus, join the NHQG on Zoom for \u0026#34;History at Home: Legacy of Black Mermaids with the Nubian Heritage Quilters Guild\u0026#34; on Thursday. Drawn from the rich folklore of Water Goddesses and Mermen, Black Mermaids traveled with the enslaved to comfort them on the ships that took them away from their homeland. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e  \u0026#34;Honoring Our Heritage: One Stitch at a Time\u0026#34; at Montclair History Center\u0026#39;s Crane House \u0026amp; Historic YMCA Museum, 110 Orange Road, Montclair. Noon to 3 p.m. Saturday and Sunday. In lieu of regular tour admission prices, suggested donations of $5 per visitor will be honored. The program is free but registration is required at \u003ca href\u003d\"http://montclairhistory.org/all-events\"\u003emontclairhistory.org/all-events\u003c/a\u003e. Visit \u003ca href\u003d\"http://nubianquilters.org\"\u003enubianquilters.org\u003c/a\u003e for information about NHQG. \u0026#34;History at Home: Legacy of Black Mermaids with the Nubian Heritage Quilters Guild\u0026#34; via Zoom, 7 p.m. Thursday; free.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBergen Alumni Theatre production of \u0026#39;Cartoon\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBergenstages and the Bergen Institute for the Creative Arts at Bergen Community College presents the Bergen Alumni Theatre production of \u0026#34;Cartoon\u0026#34; by Steve Yockey, directed by Christine Dunning with fight direction by Kevin Maphis, on Friday and Saturday.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eJoin the exploits of a band of mismatched cartoon stereotypes on a wild ride through an animated world. Presented in the style of a Commedia dell’Arte scenario gone berserk, \u0026#34;Cartoon\u0026#34; is a devilishly violent, PG-13 rated social commentary that explores the rapid coalescence of media, politics and consumer giants. A young, idealistic upstart named Trouble steals the giant hammer that Esther, the bratty dictator, uses to maintain a monotonous but peaceful order. Chaos ensues. Bombs explode. Puppets are set free. Anime girls fight. And as the bodies pile up, the violence begins to creep off the stage. There’s nothing like a punch in the face to really get the blood moving. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e\u0026#34;Cartoon\u0026#34; at the Ender Hall Lab Theatre on the campus of Bergen Community College, 400 Paramus Road, Paramus. 7:30 p.m. Friday; 2 and 7:30 p.m. Saturday. $5 to $15.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMeadowlands Racetrack BBQ Extravaganza\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn Saturday at Meadowlands Racing \u0026amp; Entertainment, chow down on some barbecue from area food trucks and restaurants in the area. The vendors will compete for $2,500 in prize money in categories such as chicken, pulled pork, brisket, ribs and people’s choice. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFood trucks will include Magic Mike\u0026#39;s Smoked Meat, Fire \u0026amp; Coal BBQ Grill, DAW Concessions, Uncle Bob’s Kettle Corn, Freakin Empanadas, Totally Nutz, Latin Bites, Antojitos de mi Tierra, Bitchn’ Bacon, Cyldes Homemade Italian Ice \u0026amp; Ice Cream, Cat Like Reflexes, Rods Fish N Chips, Delicious Lola Josefa’s, Holy Grail Burgers, Michael’s Backyard BBQ, Love JoJo’s Cookies, Top Tea Plug, The Jamaican Food Truck, Kimchi Smoke, The Hen \u0026amp; The Hog, Rhythm + Ribz Smokehouse, Wild Bill’s Craft Beverage Co, Uncle Eddies Touch of Sauce, Gringo Arepas and Highland Bites.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e BBQ Extravaganza at Meadowlands Racetrack in East Rutherford. 5 to 11 p.m. Saturday. Live racing begins at 6:20. Food truck winners will be announced at 9. Free admission. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://playmeadowlands.com/event/meadowlands-racetrack-bbq-extravaganza/\"\u003eplaymeadowlands.com\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003ePlayers Guild of Leonia presents \u0026#39;Applause\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWith sass, wit and a pulsing 1970s score, \u0026#34;Applause\u0026#34; presents show biz in all its glory and ferocity on Friday, Saturday and Sunday. The updated musical version of Mary Orr\u0026#39;s story \u0026#34;All About Eve\u0026#34; concerns superstar Margot Channing and her ambitious, scheming assistant, Eve Harrington. Directed by Craig M. Tiede, book by Betty Comden and Adolph Green, music by Charles Strouse, lyrics by Lee Adams. The musical\u0026#39;s songs include \u0026#34;But Alive,\u0026#34; \u0026#34;Applause,\u0026#34; \u0026#34;Welcome to the Theater\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;Something Greater.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The strength of \u0026#39;All About Eve,\u0026#39; so soundly conceived and executed on the screen, lay in the timelessness of its basic story,\u0026#34; wrote Comden and Green. \u0026#34;It is a tale of treachery…told in terms of the witty, glamorous theatre star and the mousy, adoring girl from the sticks who ingratiates herself into the star\u0026#39;s private world, and then systematically attempts to take over her career, her lover and her life.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026#34;Applause\u0026#34; at the Players Guild of Leonia, 130 Grand Ave. 8 p.m. Friday and Saturday, 2 p.m. Sunday. $29; $25 for seniors and students. Free parking is available at the Leonia Swim Club on Moore Street, just off of Grand Avenue. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.leoniaplayers.org/\"\u003eleoniaplayers.org\u003c/a\u003e for information, showtix4u.com for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.showtix4u.com/event-details/76050\"\u003etickets\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eArgentine tango comes to Williams Center\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eSpend your afternoon in Rutherford and experience Argentine tango with a beginner’s class, performance and music for dancing. Plus, taste original empanadas recipes and ice cream from Argentina by Cones. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFrom the international show, “Tango Lovers,” and the “Tango Houses” Cafe de los Angelitos and Rojo Tango/Faena Hotel in Buenos Aires, Yesica Esquivel and Ariel Leguizamon will teach and perform. DJ Rainier Pereira will provide the music. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eEsquivel and Leguizamon are professional dancers of Argentine tango and folklore. They been dancing together for 17 years, and they have toured with Roberto Herrera’s company, “Tanguera, The Musical,” “Estampas Porteñas” and “Tango Legends;” and in Buenos Aires at the dinner tango shows, “Piazzolla Tango,” “Catulo Tango,” “Candilejas,” “La Casa de Anibal Troilo” and “Taconeando.” They were champions of Pelando Variaciones 2016 and guest artists and teachers at Portland Tango Festival 2017, Baden-Baden tango festival 2019/2022 (Germany) and CITA 2022 (Argentina). \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eOrganized by Rougertango and the Williams Center, Rougertango reveals the pulse of the Porteña Culture, the culture of the birthplace of Argentine Tango, Buenos Aires, through live music by musicians and singers, dance performances, lessons and workshops, and the poetry of tango lyrics.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Argentine Tango at the Williams Center, 15 Sylvan St., Rutherford. Saturday. Doors open at 2 p.m., beginner\u0026#39;s class from 2:30 to 3:15, performance at 4, dancing until 6. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.williamscenter.co/events/argentine-tango\"\u003ewilliamscenter.co\u003c/a\u003e. $21.79.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNirvana, Hole, Weezer tributes in Teaneck\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eExperience the soundtrack of the \u0026#39;90s with Lounge Act - A Tribute to Nirvana, performing Saturday at Debonair Music Hall, along with All Violet - Hole Tribute and Say It Ain\u0026#39;t Scorcho - A Weezer Tribute at this all-ages show.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eLounge Act, All Violet and Say It Ain\u0026#39;t Scorcho at Debonair Music Hall, 1409 Queen Anne Road, Teaneck. 7:30 p.m. Saturday. Doors open at 7. $15 general admission; $20 reserved seating; $5 more at the door. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://debonairmusichall.com/?page_id\u003d565#/events/96852\"\u003edebonairmusichall.com\u003c/a\u003e, 201-833-0011. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eGrupo Firme at Prudential Center\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "10915915002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003ePart of the arena\u0026#39;s Latin Concert Series, presented by Goya, Grupo Firme bring their La Ultima Peda Tour to Prudential Center on Saturday.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Grupo Firme at Prudential Center, 25 Lafeyette St., Newark. 8 p.m. Saturday. Doors open at 7. $59.50 to $399.50.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eRed Bulls soccer in Harrison\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe New York Red Bulls face the Nashville SC on Saturday at Red Bull Arena in Harrison. It\u0026#39;s Collectible Night, with a soccer player mini-figurine giveaway.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Red Bulls soccer at Red Bull Arena, 600 Cape May St., Harrison. 7:30 p.m. Saturday. $14 to $256. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.newyorkredbulls.com/competitions/mls-regular-season/2024/matches/rbnyvsnsh-06-15-2024/\"\u003enewyorkredbulls.com\u003c/a\u003e for information. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.ticketmaster.com/new-york-red-bulls-vs-nashville-harrison-new-jersey-06-15-2024/event/00005F93709C0D68?_ga\u003d2.15827263.82229968.1717775083-1424301529.1709312262\u0026_gl\u003d1*oua3t8*_ga*MTQyNDMwMTUyOS4xNzA5MzEyMjYy*_ga_XS1HJ3N9M1*MTcxNzc3NTA4NC4yLjEuMTcxNzc3NTM5My4wLjAuMA..\"\u003eticketmaster.com\u003c/a\u003e for tickets.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eA Tribute to Queen at BergenPAC\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eDonning genuine costumes, Almost Queen will deliver a live performance on Saturday showcasing the signature four-part harmonies and intricate musical interludes of the original band. The Steve Leonard Trio will open the show.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Almost Queen: A Tribute to Queen at BergenPAC, 30 N. Van Brunt St., Englewood. 8 p.m. Saturday. $45 to $85. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.bergenpac.org/events/detail/almost-queen-a-tribute-to-queen\"\u003ebergenpac.org\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "32862765"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSummer Family Hike at Tenafly Nature Center\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eCelebrate Father\u0026#39;s Day and family with a guided walk with a TNC Environmental Educator on Sunday. Whether you’re an outdoor enthusiast or just hoping for a pretty photo op with the family, celebrate the day with a walk in nature. All ages welcome. Children must be accompanied by an adult. No strollers. In case of inclement weather, the program will be cancelled. Space is limited and advance registration is required.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Summer Family Hike at the Tenafly Nature Center, 313 Hudson Ave., Tenafly. 11 a.m. to 1 p.m. Sunday. $5 for members; $10 for non-members; free for children under age 2. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://tncnj.org/widget/event-5616480?CalendarViewType\u003d1\u0026SelectedDate\u003d5/28/2024\"\u003ehttps://tenaflynaturecenter.org/seasonal-programs/\u003c/a\u003e, 201-568-6093.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "36353333"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eFather\u0026#39;s Day concert at American Dream\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Edison Chinese Chorus and Edison Philharmonic Orchestra will present a hundred-member choir, conducted by Chunhe Zhang, with a cello solo by David Yu, a baritone performance by Xuefeng Wan and a Chinese folk dance.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Father\u0026#39;s Day concert by the Edison Chinese Chorus and Edison Philharmonic Orchestra at American Dream (Dream Stage, Court A, Level 1) in East Rutherford. 2 to 4 p.m Sunday. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.americandream.com/events/category\"\u003eamericandream.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eHave an event coming up? Tell us about it. Write to Daniel Galioto at galiotod@northjersey.com.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

