body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73976509007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJuly 4 and the long weekend surrounding it are all about fireworks, festivals and parades to celebrate America\u0026#39;s independence from Britain in 1776.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut what if you\u0026#39;re looking for something to do that\u0026#39;s a little different? Something a little less pomp and pageantry?\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWell, NorthJersey.com readers, there are activities that fit the bill in Bergen, Essex, Morris, Passaic and Sussex counties, including board-game playing and Shakespeare.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBergen County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "7289206001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Williams Center, 15 Sylvan St. in \u003cstrong\u003eRutherford\u003c/strong\u003e, has a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.williamscenter.co/events/boardgamenight8-hrjnj-83tn7-xk3g7-c4rb5-gh5pz-frdkr\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.williamscenter.co/events/boardgamenight8-hrjnj-83tn7-xk3g7-c4rb5-gh5pz-frdkr\"\u003eBoard Game Night\u003c/a\u003e every Thursday at 7 p.m. That will not change for July 4, according to Jordan Fried, the center\u0026#39;s operations manager. The public can bring their board games and there will also be board games provided to play.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eEssex County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe 4th of July Skate will be held at the Branch Brook Park Roller Skating Center, 7th Avenue in \u003cstrong\u003eNewark\u003c/strong\u003e, from 12 to 4 p.m. Admission is $16 for admission and skate rental (plus service fee), $10 for those with their own skates (plus service fee) and $5 for non-skating adult spectators (plus service fee). Tickets can be purchased through \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/4th-of-july-tickets-907178042947?aff\u003doddtdtcreator\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/4th-of-july-tickets-907178042947?aff\u003doddtdtcreator\"\u003eEventbrite\u003c/a\u003e. All guests, whether skating or not, must sign a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.unitedskates.com/branch-brook-park/event/summer-fun-skate-5-2024-07-04/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.unitedskates.com/branch-brook-park/event/summer-fun-skate-5-2024-07-04/\"\u003ewaiver\u003c/a\u003e online. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMorris County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Morris Museum, 6 Normandy Heights Road in \u003cstrong\u003eMorristown\u003c/strong\u003e, will be opened on the Fourth of July. That will enable visitors to see the various exhibits on display such as \u003ca href\u003d\"https://morrismuseum.org/on-view/current/like-clockwork-guinness-collection-conservation-at-the-morris-museum\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://morrismuseum.org/on-view/current/like-clockwork-guinness-collection-conservation-at-the-morris-museum\"\u003eLike Clockwork!: Guinness Collection Conservation at the Morris Museum\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://morrismuseum.org/on-view/current/set-in-motion-kinetic-worlds-from-the-studio-of-richard-whitten\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://morrismuseum.org/on-view/current/set-in-motion-kinetic-worlds-from-the-studio-of-richard-whitten\"\u003eSet in Motion: Kinetic Worlds from the Studio of Richard Whitten\u003c/a\u003e. For more information, call (973) 971-3700 or email: info@morrismuseum.org.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIf you are in the mood for some William Shakespeare on July 4 and happen to be in Morris County, the bad news is there won\u0026#39;t be any staging of the Bard\u0026#39;s work that day. The good news is the day before and the day after, the Shakespeare Theatre of New Jersey will be \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.shakespearenj.org/events/detail/as-you-like-it\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.shakespearenj.org/events/detail/as-you-like-it\"\u003epresenting\u003c/a\u003e \u0026#34;As You Like It,\u0026#34; at its outdoor stage on the campus of Saint Elizabeth College in \u003cstrong\u003eMadison\u003c/strong\u003e. The showtimes on July 3 and July 5 are at 8 p.m. Tickets can be purchased at the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.shakespearenj.org/events/detail/as-you-like-it\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.shakespearenj.org/events/detail/as-you-like-it\"\u003etheater\u0026#39;s website\u003c/a\u003e and are $40 for regular price, $30 for customers under the age of 30, $15 for student (with ID) and free for those ages 17 and under.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003ePassaic County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "8383862001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Wayne Ale House \u0026amp; Pizza, 611 Ratzer Road in \u003cstrong\u003eWayne\u003c/strong\u003e, home of the 24-inch \u0026#34;Supersize Me\u0026#34; slice, will host \u003ca href\u003d\"https://waynealehouse.com/events/category/trivia/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://waynealehouse.com/events/category/trivia/\"\u003eTrivia Night Hosted by Joe Trivia\u003c/a\u003e on July 4 from 7 to 9 p.m. For more information, call the venue at (973) 706-5505 or call Joe Trivia at (201) 390-7351.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDominican rapper Yaisel LM will be giving a concert performance to celebrate Indpendence Day on July 3 at 9 p.m. at the Serie 92 Bar and Lounge, 21 West Broadway in \u003cstrong\u003ePaterson\u003c/strong\u003e. Yaisel LM performs in the Dembow music genre, an offshoot of dancehall and reggaeton music. The tickets are $50 and can purchased at the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.boletosexpress.com/ezequiel-martinez/76507/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.boletosexpress.com/ezequiel-martinez/76507/\"\u003eBoletos Express\u003c/a\u003e website.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSussex County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72153118007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe New Jersey-based country blues/rock band Whiskey Crossing will perform \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.reverbnation.com/show/26101881?utm_campaign\u003dHTML5_ShowSchedule_Widget_Details\u0026utm_content\u003dshow_details_link\u0026utm_medium\u003dwidget\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.reverbnation.com/show/26101881?utm_campaign\u003dHTML5_ShowSchedule_Widget_Details\u0026utm_content\u003dshow_details_link\u0026utm_medium\u003dwidget\"\u003ein concert\u003c/a\u003e on July 4 at Lola\u0026#39;s Waterfront Tex-Mex Restaurant, 300 Lakeside Ave. in \u003cstrong\u003eAndover\u003c/strong\u003e. The performance, part of a tour of the state, will be at 6 p.m. For more information, visit the Whiskey Crossing \u003ca href\u003d\"https://whiskeycrossing.com/tour/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://whiskeycrossing.com/tour/\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73000399007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCelebrate America\u0026#39;s birthday with taking in America\u0026#39;s pastime. A July 4 minor league baseball battle between the New Jersey Jackals and the Sussex County Miners at Skylands Stadium, 94 Championship Place in \u003cstrong\u003eAugusta\u003c/strong\u003e, at 6:35 p.m. There will be a Hometown Heroes Parade before the game and post-game fireworks if you choose to take in both activities. Gates open at 4:35 p.m. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://vivenu.com/event/game-24-vs-new-jersey-yiidu5\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://vivenu.com/event/game-24-vs-new-jersey-yiidu5\"\u003eTickets\u003c/a\u003e range from $17 for general seating to $137.50 for seating in suites and can be purchased at the website Vivenu.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eRicardo Kaulessar covers race, immigration, and culture for NorthJersey.com. For unlimited access to the most important news from your local community, please subscribe or activate your digital account today.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eEmail: kaulessar@northjersey.com\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eTwitter: @ricardokaul\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73976509007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJuly 4 and the long weekend surrounding it are all about fireworks, festivals and parades to celebrate America\u0026#39;s independence from Britain in 1776.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut what if you\u0026#39;re looking for something to do that\u0026#39;s a little different? Something a little less pomp and pageantry?\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWell, NorthJersey.com readers, there are activities that fit the bill in Bergen, Essex, Morris, Passaic and Sussex counties, including board-game playing and Shakespeare.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBergen County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "7289206001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Williams Center, 15 Sylvan St. in \u003cstrong\u003eRutherford\u003c/strong\u003e, has a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.williamscenter.co/events/boardgamenight8-hrjnj-83tn7-xk3g7-c4rb5-gh5pz-frdkr\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.williamscenter.co/events/boardgamenight8-hrjnj-83tn7-xk3g7-c4rb5-gh5pz-frdkr\"\u003eBoard Game Night\u003c/a\u003e every Thursday at 7 p.m. That will not change for July 4, according to Jordan Fried, the center\u0026#39;s operations manager. The public can bring their board games and there will also be board games provided to play.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eEssex County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe 4th of July Skate will be held at the Branch Brook Park Roller Skating Center, 7th Avenue in \u003cstrong\u003eNewark\u003c/strong\u003e, from 12 to 4 p.m. Admission is $16 for admission and skate rental (plus service fee), $10 for those with their own skates (plus service fee) and $5 for non-skating adult spectators (plus service fee). Tickets can be purchased through \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/4th-of-july-tickets-907178042947?aff\u003doddtdtcreator\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/4th-of-july-tickets-907178042947?aff\u003doddtdtcreator\"\u003eEventbrite\u003c/a\u003e. All guests, whether skating or not, must sign a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.unitedskates.com/branch-brook-park/event/summer-fun-skate-5-2024-07-04/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.unitedskates.com/branch-brook-park/event/summer-fun-skate-5-2024-07-04/\"\u003ewaiver\u003c/a\u003e online. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMorris County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Morris Museum, 6 Normandy Heights Road in \u003cstrong\u003eMorristown\u003c/strong\u003e, will be opened on the Fourth of July. That will enable visitors to see the various exhibits on display such as \u003ca href\u003d\"https://morrismuseum.org/on-view/current/like-clockwork-guinness-collection-conservation-at-the-morris-museum\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://morrismuseum.org/on-view/current/like-clockwork-guinness-collection-conservation-at-the-morris-museum\"\u003eLike Clockwork!: Guinness Collection Conservation at the Morris Museum\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://morrismuseum.org/on-view/current/set-in-motion-kinetic-worlds-from-the-studio-of-richard-whitten\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://morrismuseum.org/on-view/current/set-in-motion-kinetic-worlds-from-the-studio-of-richard-whitten\"\u003eSet in Motion: Kinetic Worlds from the Studio of Richard Whitten\u003c/a\u003e. For more information, call (973) 971-3700 or email: info@morrismuseum.org.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIf you are in the mood for some William Shakespeare on July 4 and happen to be in Morris County, the bad news is there won\u0026#39;t be any staging of the Bard\u0026#39;s work that day. The good news is the day before and the day after, the Shakespeare Theatre of New Jersey will be \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.shakespearenj.org/events/detail/as-you-like-it\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.shakespearenj.org/events/detail/as-you-like-it\"\u003epresenting\u003c/a\u003e \u0026#34;As You Like It,\u0026#34; at its outdoor stage on the campus of Saint Elizabeth College in \u003cstrong\u003eMadison\u003c/strong\u003e. The showtimes on July 3 and July 5 are at 8 p.m. Tickets can be purchased at the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.shakespearenj.org/events/detail/as-you-like-it\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.shakespearenj.org/events/detail/as-you-like-it\"\u003etheater\u0026#39;s website\u003c/a\u003e and are $40 for regular price, $30 for customers under the age of 30, $15 for student (with ID) and free for those ages 17 and under.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003ePassaic County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "8383862001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Wayne Ale House \u0026amp; Pizza, 611 Ratzer Road in \u003cstrong\u003eWayne\u003c/strong\u003e, home of the 24-inch \u0026#34;Supersize Me\u0026#34; slice, will host \u003ca href\u003d\"https://waynealehouse.com/events/category/trivia/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://waynealehouse.com/events/category/trivia/\"\u003eTrivia Night Hosted by Joe Trivia\u003c/a\u003e on July 4 from 7 to 9 p.m. For more information, call the venue at (973) 706-5505 or call Joe Trivia at (201) 390-7351.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDominican rapper Yaisel LM will be giving a concert performance to celebrate Indpendence Day on July 3 at 9 p.m. at the Serie 92 Bar and Lounge, 21 West Broadway in \u003cstrong\u003ePaterson\u003c/strong\u003e. Yaisel LM performs in the Dembow music genre, an offshoot of dancehall and reggaeton music. The tickets are $50 and can purchased at the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.boletosexpress.com/ezequiel-martinez/76507/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.boletosexpress.com/ezequiel-martinez/76507/\"\u003eBoletos Express\u003c/a\u003e website.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSussex County\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72153118007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe New Jersey-based country blues/rock band Whiskey Crossing will perform \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.reverbnation.com/show/26101881?utm_campaign\u003dHTML5_ShowSchedule_Widget_Details\u0026utm_content\u003dshow_details_link\u0026utm_medium\u003dwidget\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.reverbnation.com/show/26101881?utm_campaign\u003dHTML5_ShowSchedule_Widget_Details\u0026utm_content\u003dshow_details_link\u0026utm_medium\u003dwidget\"\u003ein concert\u003c/a\u003e on July 4 at Lola\u0026#39;s Waterfront Tex-Mex Restaurant, 300 Lakeside Ave. in \u003cstrong\u003eAndover\u003c/strong\u003e. The performance, part of a tour of the state, will be at 6 p.m. For more information, visit the Whiskey Crossing \u003ca href\u003d\"https://whiskeycrossing.com/tour/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://whiskeycrossing.com/tour/\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73000399007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCelebrate America\u0026#39;s birthday with taking in America\u0026#39;s pastime. A July 4 minor league baseball battle between the New Jersey Jackals and the Sussex County Miners at Skylands Stadium, 94 Championship Place in \u003cstrong\u003eAugusta\u003c/strong\u003e, at 6:35 p.m. There will be a Hometown Heroes Parade before the game and post-game fireworks if you choose to take in both activities. Gates open at 4:35 p.m. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://vivenu.com/event/game-24-vs-new-jersey-yiidu5\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://vivenu.com/event/game-24-vs-new-jersey-yiidu5\"\u003eTickets\u003c/a\u003e range from $17 for general seating to $137.50 for seating in suites and can be purchased at the website Vivenu.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eRicardo Kaulessar covers race, immigration, and culture for NorthJersey.com. For unlimited access to the most important news from your local community, please subscribe or activate your digital account today.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eEmail: kaulessar@northjersey.com\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eTwitter: @ricardokaul\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

contentBody:
{
  "contentBody": [{
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73976509007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eJuly 4 and the long weekend surrounding it are all about fireworks, festivals and parades to celebrate America\u0026#39;s independence from Britain in 1776.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut what if you\u0026#39;re looking for something to do that\u0026#39;s a little different? Something a little less pomp and pageantry?\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWell, NorthJersey.com readers, there are activities that fit the bill in Bergen, Essex, Morris, Passaic and Sussex counties, including board-game playing and Shakespeare.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBergen County\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "7289206001"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Williams Center, 15 Sylvan St. in \u003cstrong\u003eRutherford\u003c/strong\u003e, has a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.williamscenter.co/events/boardgamenight8-hrjnj-83tn7-xk3g7-c4rb5-gh5pz-frdkr\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.williamscenter.co/events/boardgamenight8-hrjnj-83tn7-xk3g7-c4rb5-gh5pz-frdkr\"\u003eBoard Game Night\u003c/a\u003e every Thursday at 7 p.m. That will not change for July 4, according to Jordan Fried, the center\u0026#39;s operations manager. The public can bring their board games and there will also be board games provided to play.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eEssex County\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe 4th of July Skate will be held at the Branch Brook Park Roller Skating Center, 7th Avenue in \u003cstrong\u003eNewark\u003c/strong\u003e, from 12 to 4 p.m. Admission is $16 for admission and skate rental (plus service fee), $10 for those with their own skates (plus service fee) and $5 for non-skating adult spectators (plus service fee). Tickets can be purchased through \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/4th-of-july-tickets-907178042947?aff\u003doddtdtcreator\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/4th-of-july-tickets-907178042947?aff\u003doddtdtcreator\"\u003eEventbrite\u003c/a\u003e. All guests, whether skating or not, must sign a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.unitedskates.com/branch-brook-park/event/summer-fun-skate-5-2024-07-04/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.unitedskates.com/branch-brook-park/event/summer-fun-skate-5-2024-07-04/\"\u003ewaiver\u003c/a\u003e online. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMorris County\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Morris Museum, 6 Normandy Heights Road in \u003cstrong\u003eMorristown\u003c/strong\u003e, will be opened on the Fourth of July. That will enable visitors to see the various exhibits on display such as \u003ca href\u003d\"https://morrismuseum.org/on-view/current/like-clockwork-guinness-collection-conservation-at-the-morris-museum\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://morrismuseum.org/on-view/current/like-clockwork-guinness-collection-conservation-at-the-morris-museum\"\u003eLike Clockwork!: Guinness Collection Conservation at the Morris Museum\u003c/a\u003e and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://morrismuseum.org/on-view/current/set-in-motion-kinetic-worlds-from-the-studio-of-richard-whitten\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://morrismuseum.org/on-view/current/set-in-motion-kinetic-worlds-from-the-studio-of-richard-whitten\"\u003eSet in Motion: Kinetic Worlds from the Studio of Richard Whitten\u003c/a\u003e. For more information, call (973) 971-3700 or email: info@morrismuseum.org.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIf you are in the mood for some William Shakespeare on July 4 and happen to be in Morris County, the bad news is there won\u0026#39;t be any staging of the Bard\u0026#39;s work that day. The good news is the day before and the day after, the Shakespeare Theatre of New Jersey will be \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.shakespearenj.org/events/detail/as-you-like-it\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.shakespearenj.org/events/detail/as-you-like-it\"\u003epresenting\u003c/a\u003e \u0026#34;As You Like It,\u0026#34; at its outdoor stage on the campus of Saint Elizabeth College in \u003cstrong\u003eMadison\u003c/strong\u003e. The showtimes on July 3 and July 5 are at 8 p.m. Tickets can be purchased at the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.shakespearenj.org/events/detail/as-you-like-it\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.shakespearenj.org/events/detail/as-you-like-it\"\u003etheater\u0026#39;s website\u003c/a\u003e and are $40 for regular price, $30 for customers under the age of 30, $15 for student (with ID) and free for those ages 17 and under.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003ePassaic County\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "8383862001"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Wayne Ale House \u0026amp; Pizza, 611 Ratzer Road in \u003cstrong\u003eWayne\u003c/strong\u003e, home of the 24-inch \u0026#34;Supersize Me\u0026#34; slice, will host \u003ca href\u003d\"https://waynealehouse.com/events/category/trivia/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://waynealehouse.com/events/category/trivia/\"\u003eTrivia Night Hosted by Joe Trivia\u003c/a\u003e on July 4 from 7 to 9 p.m. For more information, call the venue at (973) 706-5505 or call Joe Trivia at (201) 390-7351.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eDominican rapper Yaisel LM will be giving a concert performance to celebrate Indpendence Day on July 3 at 9 p.m. at the Serie 92 Bar and Lounge, 21 West Broadway in \u003cstrong\u003ePaterson\u003c/strong\u003e. Yaisel LM performs in the Dembow music genre, an offshoot of dancehall and reggaeton music. The tickets are $50 and can purchased at the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.boletosexpress.com/ezequiel-martinez/76507/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.boletosexpress.com/ezequiel-martinez/76507/\"\u003eBoletos Express\u003c/a\u003e website.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSussex County\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "72153118007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe New Jersey-based country blues/rock band Whiskey Crossing will perform \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.reverbnation.com/show/26101881?utm_campaign\u003dHTML5_ShowSchedule_Widget_Details\u0026utm_content\u003dshow_details_link\u0026utm_medium\u003dwidget\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.reverbnation.com/show/26101881?utm_campaign\u003dHTML5_ShowSchedule_Widget_Details\u0026utm_content\u003dshow_details_link\u0026utm_medium\u003dwidget\"\u003ein concert\u003c/a\u003e on July 4 at Lola\u0026#39;s Waterfront Tex-Mex Restaurant, 300 Lakeside Ave. in \u003cstrong\u003eAndover\u003c/strong\u003e. The performance, part of a tour of the state, will be at 6 p.m. For more information, visit the Whiskey Crossing \u003ca href\u003d\"https://whiskeycrossing.com/tour/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://whiskeycrossing.com/tour/\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73000399007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eCelebrate America\u0026#39;s birthday with taking in America\u0026#39;s pastime. A July 4 minor league baseball battle between the New Jersey Jackals and the Sussex County Miners at Skylands Stadium, 94 Championship Place in \u003cstrong\u003eAugusta\u003c/strong\u003e, at 6:35 p.m. There will be a Hometown Heroes Parade before the game and post-game fireworks if you choose to take in both activities. Gates open at 4:35 p.m. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://vivenu.com/event/game-24-vs-new-jersey-yiidu5\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://vivenu.com/event/game-24-vs-new-jersey-yiidu5\"\u003eTickets\u003c/a\u003e range from $17 for general seating to $137.50 for seating in suites and can be purchased at the website Vivenu.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eRicardo Kaulessar covers race, immigration, and culture for NorthJersey.com. For unlimited access to the most important news from your local community, please subscribe or activate your digital account today.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eEmail: kaulessar@northjersey.com\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eTwitter: @ricardokaul\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "1538119001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Meadowlands state fair is returning to MetLife with an assortment of rides, fun games and variety of food on Thursday and will operate until July 7. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Meadowlands fair is open every day of the week except for June 25 as MetLife Stadium is set to host a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/new-jersey/2024/05/13/copa-america-comes-to-metlife-next-month-what-you-need-to-know/73646064007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/new-jersey/2024/05/13/copa-america-comes-to-metlife-next-month-what-you-need-to-know/73646064007/\"\u003eCopa America\u003c/a\u003e game that Tuesday. Tickets for the fair are available for purchase on its \u003ca href\u003d\"https://njfair.com/ticketsschedules/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://njfair.com/ticketsschedules/\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe fair\u0026#39;s fun pass must be purchased online in advance as there is no general admission ticket. The fun pass is valid for only one day and gives access to admission, free parking, petting zoo, free shows, unlimited rides (with applicable fees) and other entertainment. Special attractions, live animal rides, games and food and beverages are not included in the fun pass. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "12168982002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe fair, located in East Rutherford at the MetLife Stadium parking lots, typically closes at midnight or 1 a.m. and opens either at 2 p.m. or 6 p.m. depending on the day. The box office closes at 10:30 p.m. on select dates at 11:30 p.m. on other days. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSome shows offered at the fair are Magician Jay Mattioli and Lance Gifford, a Michael Jackson tribute, racing pigs, Jurassic Kingdom, Circus Lena and Cycle Circus. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOver 100 rides are offered at the state fair, including a \u0026#34;kiddie land\u0026#34; for young children. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhen someone is not on the ferris wheel or trying to pop some balloons for a prize, they can enjoy food from across over 50 different vendors including fried Oreos and lemonade. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe fair will also offer a fireworks show on July 3 and 4. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe first fair that took place at the Meadowlands occurred in 1986 as a six-day event as said on their website. Now the fair spans just over two weeks as last year\u0026#39;s attendance topped over 400,000 visitors. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe fair generates almost $1 million in New Jersey State Tax Revenue, according to the website. All rides are licensed by the state and have been inspected and approved prior to the opening.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "1538119001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Meadowlands state fair is returning to MetLife with an assortment of rides, fun games and variety of food on Thursday and will operate until July 7. \u003c/p\u003e"
