    }]
  }
}

contentBody:
{
  "contentBody": [{
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "1538119001"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Meadowlands state fair is returning to MetLife with an assortment of rides, fun games and variety of food on Thursday and will operate until July 7. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Meadowlands fair is open every day of the week except for June 25 as MetLife Stadium is set to host a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/new-jersey/2024/05/13/copa-america-comes-to-metlife-next-month-what-you-need-to-know/73646064007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/new-jersey/2024/05/13/copa-america-comes-to-metlife-next-month-what-you-need-to-know/73646064007/\"\u003eCopa America\u003c/a\u003e game that Tuesday. Tickets for the fair are available for purchase on its \u003ca href\u003d\"https://njfair.com/ticketsschedules/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://njfair.com/ticketsschedules/\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e.  \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe fair\u0026#39;s fun pass must be purchased online in advance as there is no general admission ticket. The fun pass is valid for only one day and gives access to admission, free parking, petting zoo, free shows, unlimited rides (with applicable fees) and other entertainment. Special attractions, live animal rides, games and food and beverages are not included in the fun pass. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "12168982002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe fair, located in East Rutherford at the MetLife Stadium parking lots, typically closes at midnight or 1 a.m. and opens either at 2 p.m. or 6 p.m. depending on the day. The box office closes at 10:30 p.m. on select dates at 11:30 p.m. on other days. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eSome shows offered at the fair are Magician Jay Mattioli and Lance Gifford, a Michael Jackson tribute, racing pigs, Jurassic Kingdom, Circus Lena and Cycle Circus. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eOver 100 rides are offered at the state fair, including a \u0026#34;kiddie land\u0026#34; for young children. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhen someone is not on the ferris wheel or trying to pop some balloons for a prize, they can enjoy food from across over 50 different vendors including fried Oreos and lemonade. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe fair will also offer a fireworks show on July 3 and 4. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe first fair that took place at the Meadowlands occurred in 1986 as a six-day event as said on their website. Now the fair spans just over two weeks as last year\u0026#39;s attendance topped over 400,000 visitors. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe fair generates almost $1 million in New Jersey State Tax Revenue, according to the website. All rides are licensed by the state and have been inspected and approved prior to the opening.  \u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

