      "value": "74210656007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWe were just about done with our tour when Karlitz was distracted by golf legend, Lee Trevino. Excusing himself, the businessman urged me to enjoy my evening, promising we\u0026#39;d catch up later.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eConsidering he knew \u0026#34;every chef in Manhattan,\u0026#34; and I was a fan of, well, \u003cem\u003eall of them\u003c/em\u003e, I promised to hold him to that.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eI didn\u0026#39;t mind, though, the chance to explore the space on my own — and start trying those bougie bites.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSampling sashimi, oxtail and more\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74210657007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter Karlitz left, I headed to the pool deck with my friend Ryan. About 15 food stations were set up in the area, ran by the chefs of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/tatianabychefkwame/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eTatiana\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/melbasharlem/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eMelba\u0026#39;s\u003c/a\u003e and more. We started at the far corner of the space — where San Pellegrino was sponsoring the event with its crisp, cool lemonade — and worked our way around.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe first dish of the evening we tried was a live scallop crudo, prepared by chef Andy Kitko of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/oceansnewyork/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eOceans New York\u003c/a\u003e. Following that, we sampled bite-sized oxtail tacos from Melba\u0026#39;s, and fluke tostadas from Brooklyn\u0026#39;s \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/ensenadanyc/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eEnsenada\u003c/a\u003e. I remarked on the impressive flavor of the latter, while Ryan stopped at the bar for a drink. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The sauce on the scallop was really creamy,\u0026#34; he said, \u0026#34;Like, totally banging.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHe knows what he likes. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74210658007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWe finished the section with some burnt end \u0026#34;candy\u0026#34; from \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/butcherbar/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eButcher Bar\u003c/a\u003e and papaya piri piri from Tatiana (prepared by sous chef \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/chefsamzitro/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSam Zitro\u003c/a\u003e, because \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/chefkwameonwuachi/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eKwame\u003c/a\u003e was somewhere playing golf) before heading to the main patio.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eThe main promenade\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe set up on the patio was about triple the size of the pool deck, maybe more, with chefs just as prominent as the \u003cem\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.bravotv.com/top-chef\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eTop Chef\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/em\u003e champions and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.jamesbeard.org/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eJames Beard\u003c/a\u003e winners we\u0026#39;d just passed.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eKarlitz traversed the space, eager to introduce me to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/FoodieMagician/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eJosh Beckerman\u003c/a\u003e, \u0026#34;The Foodie Magician.\u0026#34; He was quickly distracted again by another pro athlete, though (this time, a tennis star), and was off.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs somewhat of a decorated athlete \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/karanicolev/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003emyself\u003c/a\u003e, however, I understood his excitement.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74210652007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;This place is crawling with celebrities,\u0026#34; Ryan said, grabbing another drink.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhether they were truly there for the charity — or to party and flex their assets with those they assumed were on the same plane — I couldn\u0026#39;t tell.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut, when a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/goldmansachs/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eGoldman Sachs\u003c/a\u003e higher-up passed between Ryan and the bar, it was obvious the place was a hotbed for networking. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd we thought that was pretty cool.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eThe best dish of the night\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74210659007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eRyan and I were working our way through the patio (trying grand cru galbi ssam from Michelin-starred \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/cotekoreansteakhouse/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eCOTE\u003c/a\u003e and king crab rolls by chef \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/chefmarcusware/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eMarcus Ware\u003c/a\u003e on our journey) when we saw it: the top dish of the night.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eApproaching the table, which belonged to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.kanopievents.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eThe Restaurant at Kanopi\u003c/a\u003e, a chef described the appetizer as the restaurant\u0026#39;s play on beef tartare.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFeaturing dry-aged meat, house-made hollandaise and some sort of rich espuma inside a crispy round shell — that resembled a golf ball itself — the amuse-bouche was a salty, fatty, melt-in-your-mouth showstopper. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74210678007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eI grabbed a plate of four more; originally determined to guard them with my life, but eventually swayed to share them with the biggest names in attendance (because, of course, they ran out).\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt\u0026#39;s important to note, though, that the poppers only won the night by a margin — because every complexly-flavored hors d\u0026#39;oeuvre was \u003cem\u003ethat good\u003c/em\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNorth Jersey\u0026#39;s must-attend culinary event of the year\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe sun went down late on the night of the tournament. Slowing removing its soft light from the club\u0026#39;s manicured lawns, it took the guests with it.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBy 9:15 p.m., Karlitz and I — apart from a few distant chefs — stood alone.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74210691007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;This isn\u0026#39;t real life,\u0026#34; he said, scanning the serene landscape as the maintenance staff carried away tables. \u0026#34;Real life is what City Harvest deals with. Real life is 40% of people struggling with food insecurity.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;But that\u0026#39;s why this event is so important,\u0026#34; I responded.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eKarlitz nodded. \u0026#34;Exactly. Because, if I can put this on for one night, 944,000 people can also eat for a night.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74210670007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd it\u0026#39;s that reality — more important than the thin-sliced truffle, peach-infused bourbon and celebrity elbow brushes — that affirmed my stated thesis: The tournament is, and in the future will persist to be, North Jersey\u0026#39;s must-attend gastronomic evening of the year.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eKara VanDooijeweert is a food writer for NorthJersey.com and The Record. If you can\u0026#39;t find her in Jersey\u0026#39;s best restaurants, she\u0026#39;s probably off running a race course in the mountains. Catch her on Instagram: \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/karanicolev/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003e@karanicolev\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e \u0026amp; \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/northjerseyeats/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003e@northjerseyeats\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e, and sign up for her \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://profile.northjersey.com/newsletters/north-jersey-eats\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003eNorth Jersey Eats newsletter\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

contentBody:
{
  "contentBody": [{
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74210617007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;It\u0026#39;s a golf tournament,\u0026#34; Herb Karlitz, owner of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/karlitz_co/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eKarlitz \u0026amp; Co.\u003c/a\u003e events marketing company, said. \u0026#34;But it\u0026#39;s not \u003cem\u003ereally \u003c/em\u003ea golf tournament.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eI looked around at the rolling hills of Bergen County\u0026#39;s most picturesque country club, which, for the day, was adorned with linen-topped tables, pop-up bars and big green smokers.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;It\u0026#39;s kind of like day camp for chefs.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74210693007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eMeeting each other for the first time, he welcomed me to his annual \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/dining/2024/06/10/you-can-eat-with-celebrities-at-this-star-studded-new-jersey-golf-event/73910868007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eCelebrity Chefs \u0026amp; Friends Golf and Tennis Tournament\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAccording to our former food editor Esther Davidowitz: \u0026#34;A food festival that just happens to take place on a golf course.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd, according to me? Bergen County\u0026#39;s culinary event of the year.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eArriving at a Bergen\u0026#39;s most lavish food festival\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74210628007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eMy attention was originally drawn to Karlitz\u0026#39; \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cityharvest.org/event/golf-and-tennis-2024/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eCelebrity Chefs Golf Tournament\u003c/a\u003e by an email that described the event as a charity endeavor featuring 60(+) of the NYC-metro area\u0026#39;s most talented chefs. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eTo be held at the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/alpinecountryclub1928/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eAlpine Country Club\u003c/a\u003e, the day would begin with a few rounds of golf and tennis, followed by a lavish reception of decadent eats and stunning drinks. At the end of the evening, all proceeds would be donated to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.cityharvest.org/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eCity Harvest\u003c/a\u003e, New York\u0026#39;s largest food rescue organization.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIntrigued by the prospect of great eats for an equivalently great cause, I added my name to the guest list.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74210677007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;We\u0026#39;ve got \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/chefcapon/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eJosh Capon\u003c/a\u003e making lamb chops back there,\u0026#34; Karlitz said, walking me around the club\u0026#39;s patio, \u0026#34;And \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/chefmarcmurphy/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eMarc Murphy\u0026#39;s\u003c/a\u003e here with the pesto.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eHe motioned to the right, where Murphy, a Food Network star, stood with a pan of fresh cavatelli. He lifted pasta scoops into little wooden bowls — the aforementioned sauce dripping slowly down the sides of the serving spoon.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eI vowed I would be back.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eA walk amongst culinary stars\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;This is amazing,\u0026#34; I said, passing the table where \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/danielboulud/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eDaniel Boulud\u003c/a\u003e\u0026#39;s sous chef was preparing a geometrically flawless pâté en croûte. \u0026#34;I\u0026#39;ve never seen so much caviar and foie gras in the same place.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;It really is,\u0026#34; Karlitz responded, \u0026#34;But what\u0026#39;s even more amazing is that every one of these chefs is donating their time. They\u0026#39;re donating their products, they\u0026#39;re donating their evening — everything is benefitting City Harvest. It really is all about the charity.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd the guests? Paid $1,000 to $15,000 (depending on how many, if any, golfers their party would be bringing) to do the same.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74210656007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWe were just about done with our tour when Karlitz was distracted by golf legend, Lee Trevino. Excusing himself, the businessman urged me to enjoy my evening, promising we\u0026#39;d catch up later.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eConsidering he knew \u0026#34;every chef in Manhattan,\u0026#34; and I was a fan of, well, \u003cem\u003eall of them\u003c/em\u003e, I promised to hold him to that.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eI didn\u0026#39;t mind, though, the chance to explore the space on my own — and start trying those bougie bites.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSampling sashimi, oxtail and more\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74210657007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter Karlitz left, I headed to the pool deck with my friend Ryan. About 15 food stations were set up in the area, ran by the chefs of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/tatianabychefkwame/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eTatiana\u003c/a\u003e, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/melbasharlem/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eMelba\u0026#39;s\u003c/a\u003e and more. We started at the far corner of the space — where San Pellegrino was sponsoring the event with its crisp, cool lemonade — and worked our way around.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe first dish of the evening we tried was a live scallop crudo, prepared by chef Andy Kitko of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/oceansnewyork/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eOceans New York\u003c/a\u003e. Following that, we sampled bite-sized oxtail tacos from Melba\u0026#39;s, and fluke tostadas from Brooklyn\u0026#39;s \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/ensenadanyc/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eEnsenada\u003c/a\u003e. I remarked on the impressive flavor of the latter, while Ryan stopped at the bar for a drink. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The sauce on the scallop was really creamy,\u0026#34; he said, \u0026#34;Like, totally banging.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eHe knows what he likes. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74210658007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWe finished the section with some burnt end \u0026#34;candy\u0026#34; from \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/butcherbar/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eButcher Bar\u003c/a\u003e and papaya piri piri from Tatiana (prepared by sous chef \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/chefsamzitro/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eSam Zitro\u003c/a\u003e, because \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/chefkwameonwuachi/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eKwame\u003c/a\u003e was somewhere playing golf) before heading to the main patio.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eThe main promenade\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe set up on the patio was about triple the size of the pool deck, maybe more, with chefs just as prominent as the \u003cem\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.bravotv.com/top-chef\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eTop Chef\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/em\u003e champions and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.jamesbeard.org/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eJames Beard\u003c/a\u003e winners we\u0026#39;d just passed.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eKarlitz traversed the space, eager to introduce me to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/FoodieMagician/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eJosh Beckerman\u003c/a\u003e, \u0026#34;The Foodie Magician.\u0026#34; He was quickly distracted again by another pro athlete, though (this time, a tennis star), and was off.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs somewhat of a decorated athlete \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/karanicolev/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003emyself\u003c/a\u003e, however, I understood his excitement.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74210652007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;This place is crawling with celebrities,\u0026#34; Ryan said, grabbing another drink.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhether they were truly there for the charity — or to party and flex their assets with those they assumed were on the same plane — I couldn\u0026#39;t tell.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut, when a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/goldmansachs/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eGoldman Sachs\u003c/a\u003e higher-up passed between Ryan and the bar, it was obvious the place was a hotbed for networking. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd we thought that was pretty cool.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eThe best dish of the night\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74210659007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eRyan and I were working our way through the patio (trying grand cru galbi ssam from Michelin-starred \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/cotekoreansteakhouse/?hl\u003den\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eCOTE\u003c/a\u003e and king crab rolls by chef \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/chefmarcusware/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eMarcus Ware\u003c/a\u003e on our journey) when we saw it: the top dish of the night.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eApproaching the table, which belonged to \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.kanopievents.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eThe Restaurant at Kanopi\u003c/a\u003e, a chef described the appetizer as the restaurant\u0026#39;s play on beef tartare.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFeaturing dry-aged meat, house-made hollandaise and some sort of rich espuma inside a crispy round shell — that resembled a golf ball itself — the amuse-bouche was a salty, fatty, melt-in-your-mouth showstopper. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74210678007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eI grabbed a plate of four more; originally determined to guard them with my life, but eventually swayed to share them with the biggest names in attendance (because, of course, they ran out).\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt\u0026#39;s important to note, though, that the poppers only won the night by a margin — because every complexly-flavored hors d\u0026#39;oeuvre was \u003cem\u003ethat good\u003c/em\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNorth Jersey\u0026#39;s must-attend culinary event of the year\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe sun went down late on the night of the tournament. Slowing removing its soft light from the club\u0026#39;s manicured lawns, it took the guests with it.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBy 9:15 p.m., Karlitz and I — apart from a few distant chefs — stood alone.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74210691007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;This isn\u0026#39;t real life,\u0026#34; he said, scanning the serene landscape as the maintenance staff carried away tables. \u0026#34;Real life is what City Harvest deals with. Real life is 40% of people struggling with food insecurity.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;But that\u0026#39;s why this event is so important,\u0026#34; I responded.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eKarlitz nodded. \u0026#34;Exactly. Because, if I can put this on for one night, 944,000 people can also eat for a night.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74210670007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd it\u0026#39;s that reality — more important than the thin-sliced truffle, peach-infused bourbon and celebrity elbow brushes — that affirmed my stated thesis: The tournament is, and in the future will persist to be, North Jersey\u0026#39;s must-attend gastronomic evening of the year.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eKara VanDooijeweert is a food writer for NorthJersey.com and The Record. If you can\u0026#39;t find her in Jersey\u0026#39;s best restaurants, she\u0026#39;s probably off running a race course in the mountains. Catch her on Instagram: \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/karanicolev/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003e@karanicolev\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e \u0026amp; \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.instagram.com/northjerseyeats/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003e@northjerseyeats\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e, and sign up for her \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://profile.northjersey.com/newsletters/north-jersey-eats\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003eNorth Jersey Eats newsletter\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74138091007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt\u0026#39;s officially the first weekend of summer, so what will you be doing in North Jersey? Here are some options we\u0026#39;ve curated for you:\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSummertime is the time for fairs and there\u0026#39;s none bigger than \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/19/nj-state-fair-returns-meadowlands-what-to-know/74139760007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/19/nj-state-fair-returns-meadowlands-what-to-know/74139760007/\"\u003eState Fair Meadowlands, which starts on Thursday. \u003c/a\u003eAnother way to celebrate the arrival of the season is with a summer solstice campfire and hike at Tenafly Nature Center.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThere is always plenty of music in North Jersey, and this week\u0026#39;s concerts include tributes to the Grateful Dead and Elvis Presley. There is also a cabaret show by Alan Cumming and a dance performance by Aatma Performing Arts.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWe\u0026#39;ve also got sports, with Jackals baseball and the New York/New Jersey Gotham Football Club both at home this weekend; and art, with a local artist exhibit in Clifton. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd, for girls planning their quinceañera, there\u0026#39;s a free expo this weekend. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003ePlus, it\u0026#39;s Pride Month, so check out our\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/life/events/2024/05/31/pride-month-2024-events-celebrate-north-jersey-nj/72809698007/\"\u003e big list of Pride events\u003c/a\u003e, some of which are also included below.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEnjoy!\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSunny and hot, with only a small chance of showers\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAccording to the National Weather Service:\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThursday night:\u003c/strong\u003e Partly cloudy, with a low around 75.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFriday\u003c/strong\u003e: Mostly sunny with a high at almost 100, with mostly cloudy skies at night and a low in the mid-70s.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSaturday\u003c/strong\u003e: Partly sunny, with a high in the mid-90s and chance of showers. Mostly cloudy at night and more possible showers, with a low in the mid-70s\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSunday:\u003c/strong\u003e Partly sunny, with a high in the low 90s and a chance of showers.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Artists’ Perspectives\u0026#39; at Clifton Arts Center\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThrough June 29, the “Artists’ Perspectives” exhibition by the Community Arts Association will be on display at the Clifton Arts Center. The exhibit is about how artists use perspective techniques to create realistic and non-realistic impressions. The artist’s perspective values process, communication and understanding. It embraces emotion and encourages connection. When artists communicate information, in this case through paintings, their perspectives can help make that visual information accessible, comprehensible and approachable. The artist’s perspective can also shape how we think about and act with each other as a community at large.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Community Arts Association originated in Allendale in 1965. Meetings were originally held in the Highlands Presbyterian Church before relocating to Northern Highlands Regional School, Archer United Methodist Church and finally to Trinity Episcopal Church. Community Arts Association sponsors workshops, hosts demonstrations, lectures, day trips, and art scholarships for graduating high schoolers.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026#34;Artists\u0026#39; Perspectives\u0026#34; by the Community Arts Association at Clifton Arts Center, 900 Clifton Ave. $3 admission. Normal gallery hours are Wednesday through Saturday, 1 to 4 p.m. 973-472-5499. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://cliftonartscenter.org/gallery-exhibits\"\u003ecliftonartscenter.org\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eState Fair Meadowlands at MetLife Stadium\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "12168980002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe fair is back with a lineup of new and favorite all-ages entertainment. This year’s program is packed with stunts and acrobatic acts, amusement rides, magicians, musicians, racing pigs and food. For the next 17 days, the fair will be open in the stadium\u0026#39;s parking lots E and F, on weeknights (except June 25) and with extended hours on weekends and July 4. Parking is free in lots G, J and L for all fairgoers.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/19/nj-state-fair-returns-meadowlands-what-to-know/74139760007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/19/nj-state-fair-returns-meadowlands-what-to-know/74139760007/\"\u003eState Fair Meadowlands at MetLife Stadium\u003c/a\u003e in East Rutherford. Thursday, Monday and Wednesday, 6 p.m. to midnight; Friday, 6 p.m. to 1 a.m.; Saturday, 2 p.m. to 1 a.m.; Sunday, 2 p.m. to midnight. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.metlifestadium.com/event/2024/06/20/metlife-stadium/state-fair\"\u003emetlifestadium.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eGrateful Dead tribute in Millburn\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe music of the Grateful Dead continues to grow and evolve, long after the band played their last show. The members of Workingman\u0026#39;s Jed share a common love for the Dead’s musical canon, jams and multi-part vocal harmonies. They strive to honor the original compositions through their individual styles and musical experiences, to create something familiar, yet different and special. They design unique set lists for each show, merge songs together in original ways, and try to do new things. ​\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Workingman\u0026#39;s Jed at Taylor Park, 110 Main St., Millburn. 7 to 8:30 p.m. Thursday (rain date is June 27). Free. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://twp.millburn.nj.us/461/Summer-Concerts-in-Taylor-Park\"\u003etwp.millburn.nj.us\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eJackals baseball at Hinchliffe Stadium\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73636884007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Jackals are home in Paterson this weekend, with a three-game series against the Quebec Capitales. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFriday is \u0026#39;70s Night, so dress up in your best \u0026#39;70s outfit. On Saturday, there will be a mini-bat giveaway and a post-game firework show. Sunday is Family Day with $5 tickets for kids age 12 and under and seniors age 55 and over.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e New Jersey Jackals at Hinchliffe Stadium, 1 Jasper St., Paterson. 6:35 p.m. Friday, 6:05 p.m. Saturday, 4:35 p.m. Sunday, $5 to $25. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://jackals.com/\"\u003ejackals.com\u003c/a\u003e, 973-746-7434, contact@jackals.com. Gates open an hour prior to the start of the game.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Big Gay Cabaret\u0026#39; in Fair Lawn\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCelebrate Pride Month at this fundraiser for the Old Library Theatre and the Bergen County LGBTQ+ Alliance, Friday and Saturday at the George Frey Performing Arts Center. The show is co-directed by Jeff Parsons and Dave Toussas, with musical direction by Christopher Vehmas.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026#34;Big Gay Cabaret\u0026#34; at the George Frey Performing Arts Center, 10-10 20th St., Fair Lawn. 7:30 p.m. Friday and Saturday. $25. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.oldlibrarytheatre.com/\"\u003eoldlibrarytheatre.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Sounds of My Soul\u0026#39; dance showcase at NJPAC\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAatma Performing Arts celebrates its 15-year anniversary with “Sounds of My Soul” on Saturday. Directed by Amit Shah, the show features hits from Bollywood films and an eclectic fusion of Indian folk and western pop music. Highlights include handmade costumes and excerpts from Aatma’s newest touring production, “Finding Home: An Indian Musical.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Aatma Performing Arts presents \u0026#34;Sounds of My Soul\u0026#34; at NJPAC, Prudential Hall, Betty Wold Johnson Stage. 6 p.m. Saturday. $59 to $149. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.njpac.org/event/aatma-performing-arts-sounds-of-my-soul/\"\u003enjpac.org\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eThe David Drumgold Variety Show – Pride Edition\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73961064007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eActor and Broadway/TV/film producer David Drumgold brings a special Pride edition of his variety show to the Puffin Cultural Forum in Teaneck on Saturday. Hearkening back to the variety shows of the \u0026#39;60s and \u0026#39;70s - like \u0026#34;The Carol Burnett Show,\u0026#34; \u0026#34;The Flip Wilson Show,\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;The Cher Show\u0026#34; - Drumgold\u0026#39;s variety show features good old-fashioned talent, cheer and the escapism of a good time. It celebrates everything magical about art, and features comedy, drag, dance and musicians.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFeatured performers include the New York Metropolitan Opera soprano Brandie Inez Sutton, pianist Yasuhiko Fukuoka, and R\u0026amp;B/soul singer Diana Taylor. Plus, the newest addition to the lineup is Pissi Myles, a drag comedian, singer and hostess.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eN95 or equivalent masks are required. A limited quantity will be available at the door.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026#34;The David Drumgold Variety Show – Pride Edition\u0026#34; at the Puffin Cultural Forum, 20 Puffin Way, Teaneck. 7 p.m. Saturday. $10 suggested donation. RSVP at \u003ca href\u003d\"https://daviddrumgoldprideatpuffin.eventbrite.com\"\u003edaviddrumgoldprideatpuffin.eventbrite.com\u003c/a\u003e or call 201-836-3499. Those who cannot pay the suggested donation may call (or write to aortega@puffinfoundation.org) to make free reservations. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eAlan Cumming at State Theatre\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73789631007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Alan Cumming: Uncut - With Henry Koperski at the Piano\u0026#34; - Cumming\u0026#39;s new cabaret show - comes to State Theatre New Jersey in New Brunswick on Saturday.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eA longtime TV, film and stage actor, Cumming premiered his first cabaret show, \u0026#34;Alan Cumming Sings Sappy Songs,\u0026#34; in 2015 in New York City. His next cabaret show, \u0026#34;Legal Immigrant,\u0026#34; debuted in 2018, followed by \u0026#34;Alan Cumming Is Not Acting His Age,\u0026#34; which toured the world and ended up on Broadway. He is currently touring with NPR’s Ari Shapiro in \u0026#34;Och and Oy: A Considered Cabaret!,\u0026#34; as well as \u0026#34;Uncut,\u0026#34; which he developed at the Yaddo artists retreat and premiered in April.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis show is recommended for ages 18 and up. Everyone, regardless of age, entering the theater must purchase a ticket.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026#34;Alan Cumming: Uncut\u0026#34; at State Theatre of New Jersey, 15 Livingston Ave., New Brunswick. 8 p.m. Saturday. $39 to $69. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.stnj.org/events/detail/alan-cumming\"\u003estnj.org\u003c/a\u003e, 732-246-7469.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNY/NJ Gotham soccer in Harrison Sunday\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "11393637002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSunday is Kids Day at the Red Bull Arena, with a Fan Fest before the New York/New Jersey Gotham Football Club takes on the Washington Spirit in women\u0026#39;s pro soccer action. The Fan Fest will feature an Eli Manning meet-and-greet, balloon artists, face paint, friendship bracelet-making and food trucks.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e NY/NJ Gotham FC with Fan Fest at Red Bull Arena, 600 Cape May St., Harrison. Sunday. Fan Fest at 11 a.m. Game at 1:30 p.m. $15 to $270.21. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.gothamfc.com/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.gothamfc.com/\"\u003egothamfc.com.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eQuinceañera Expo in Saddle Brook\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eYoung ladies and their parents planning their quinceañera celebrations can attend NJ Quinceañera Expo 2024 in Saddle Brook on Sunday. The expo will feature an array of vendors and exhibitors showcasing the latest trends in quinceañera dresses, decorations, photography, catering, entertainment and more. Attendees will have the opportunity to connect with industry professionals, discover unique ideas and find everything needed to create a memorable quinceañera.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHighlights of the expo include a fashion show with the latest gown designs on the runway, vendor booths, exclusive offers, raffles and prizes, and expert advice to help make your quinceañera dream a reality.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eNJ Quinceañera Expo 2024 at Crowne Plaza, 50 Kenny Place, Saddle Brook. 2 to 7 p.m. Sunday. Free admission. For information, call 862-600-1769. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSummer Solstice campfire and night hike\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCelebrate the longest day of the year and the official start of the summer with the Tenafly Nature Center. A TNC naturalist will lead participants on a night hike to experience the sounds of summer, followed by a campfire and s\u0026#39;mores. The program is intended for adults and families with children 5 and up. Children must be accompanied by an adult. The program will be held entirely outdoors. In case of inclement weather, it will be held under cover. Social distancing in effect. Space is limited and advance registration is required. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Summer Family Hike at the Tenafly Nature Center, 313 Hudson Ave., Tenafly. 7 to 9 p.m. Sunday. $8 for members; $12 for non-members; free for children under age 2. \u003ca href\u003d\"http://tenaflynaturecenter.org\"\u003etenaflynaturecenter.org\u003c/a\u003e, 201-568-6093.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eJesse Garron\u0026#39;s Tribute To Elvis\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "92928626"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBilled as \u0026#34;The Closest Thing to the King,\u0026#34; Garron uses the name of Elvis Presley\u0026#39;s twin brother who died at birth as he pays tribute to Elvis and his legacy. Inspired by Elvis at the age of four, Garron was always mesmerized by Elvis\u0026#39; voice and intrigued by everything Elvis from his music to his movies. He got his first break to pay him tribute at the age of 17 in a high school talent show and won the popular vote. Since his first performance in 1997, he has performed around the country and the world. In 2019, he was inducted into the International Elvis Tribute Artist Hall of Fame for his dedication to keeping Elvis\u0026#39; legacy alive. Garron performs with a four-piece band and three backing vocalists.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Jesse Garron\u0026#39;s Tribute to Elvis at the Florham Park gazebo, 111 Ridgedale Ave., on the Great Lawn, at 7 p.m. Sunday. If weather is questionable, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"http://florhamparkgazebo.com\"\u003eflorhamparkgazebo.com\u003c/a\u003e for updates. Free.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eHave an event coming up? Tell us about it. Write to Daniel Galioto at galiotod@northjersey.com.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74138091007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt\u0026#39;s officially the first weekend of summer, so what will you be doing in North Jersey? Here are some options we\u0026#39;ve curated for you:\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSummertime is the time for fairs and there\u0026#39;s none bigger than \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/19/nj-state-fair-returns-meadowlands-what-to-know/74139760007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/19/nj-state-fair-returns-meadowlands-what-to-know/74139760007/\"\u003eState Fair Meadowlands, which starts on Thursday. \u003c/a\u003eAnother way to celebrate the arrival of the season is with a summer solstice campfire and hike at Tenafly Nature Center.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThere is always plenty of music in North Jersey, and this week\u0026#39;s concerts include tributes to the Grateful Dead and Elvis Presley. There is also a cabaret show by Alan Cumming and a dance performance by Aatma Performing Arts.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWe\u0026#39;ve also got sports, with Jackals baseball and the New York/New Jersey Gotham Football Club both at home this weekend; and art, with a local artist exhibit in Clifton. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd, for girls planning their quinceañera, there\u0026#39;s a free expo this weekend. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003ePlus, it\u0026#39;s Pride Month, so check out our\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/life/events/2024/05/31/pride-month-2024-events-celebrate-north-jersey-nj/72809698007/\"\u003e big list of Pride events\u003c/a\u003e, some of which are also included below.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEnjoy!\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSunny and hot, with only a small chance of showers\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAccording to the National Weather Service:\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThursday night:\u003c/strong\u003e Partly cloudy, with a low around 75.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFriday\u003c/strong\u003e: Mostly sunny with a high at almost 100, with mostly cloudy skies at night and a low in the mid-70s.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSaturday\u003c/strong\u003e: Partly sunny, with a high in the mid-90s and chance of showers. Mostly cloudy at night and more possible showers, with a low in the mid-70s\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSunday:\u003c/strong\u003e Partly sunny, with a high in the low 90s and a chance of showers.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Artists’ Perspectives\u0026#39; at Clifton Arts Center\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThrough June 29, the “Artists’ Perspectives” exhibition by the Community Arts Association will be on display at the Clifton Arts Center. The exhibit is about how artists use perspective techniques to create realistic and non-realistic impressions. The artist’s perspective values process, communication and understanding. It embraces emotion and encourages connection. When artists communicate information, in this case through paintings, their perspectives can help make that visual information accessible, comprehensible and approachable. The artist’s perspective can also shape how we think about and act with each other as a community at large.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Community Arts Association originated in Allendale in 1965. Meetings were originally held in the Highlands Presbyterian Church before relocating to Northern Highlands Regional School, Archer United Methodist Church and finally to Trinity Episcopal Church. Community Arts Association sponsors workshops, hosts demonstrations, lectures, day trips, and art scholarships for graduating high schoolers.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026#34;Artists\u0026#39; Perspectives\u0026#34; by the Community Arts Association at Clifton Arts Center, 900 Clifton Ave. $3 admission. Normal gallery hours are Wednesday through Saturday, 1 to 4 p.m. 973-472-5499. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://cliftonartscenter.org/gallery-exhibits\"\u003ecliftonartscenter.org\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eState Fair Meadowlands at MetLife Stadium\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "12168980002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe fair is back with a lineup of new and favorite all-ages entertainment. This year’s program is packed with stunts and acrobatic acts, amusement rides, magicians, musicians, racing pigs and food. For the next 17 days, the fair will be open in the stadium\u0026#39;s parking lots E and F, on weeknights (except June 25) and with extended hours on weekends and July 4. Parking is free in lots G, J and L for all fairgoers.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/19/nj-state-fair-returns-meadowlands-what-to-know/74139760007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/19/nj-state-fair-returns-meadowlands-what-to-know/74139760007/\"\u003eState Fair Meadowlands at MetLife Stadium\u003c/a\u003e in East Rutherford. Thursday, Monday and Wednesday, 6 p.m. to midnight; Friday, 6 p.m. to 1 a.m.; Saturday, 2 p.m. to 1 a.m.; Sunday, 2 p.m. to midnight. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.metlifestadium.com/event/2024/06/20/metlife-stadium/state-fair\"\u003emetlifestadium.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eGrateful Dead tribute in Millburn\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe music of the Grateful Dead continues to grow and evolve, long after the band played their last show. The members of Workingman\u0026#39;s Jed share a common love for the Dead’s musical canon, jams and multi-part vocal harmonies. They strive to honor the original compositions through their individual styles and musical experiences, to create something familiar, yet different and special. They design unique set lists for each show, merge songs together in original ways, and try to do new things. ​\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Workingman\u0026#39;s Jed at Taylor Park, 110 Main St., Millburn. 7 to 8:30 p.m. Thursday (rain date is June 27). Free. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://twp.millburn.nj.us/461/Summer-Concerts-in-Taylor-Park\"\u003etwp.millburn.nj.us\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eJackals baseball at Hinchliffe Stadium\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73636884007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Jackals are home in Paterson this weekend, with a three-game series against the Quebec Capitales. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFriday is \u0026#39;70s Night, so dress up in your best \u0026#39;70s outfit. On Saturday, there will be a mini-bat giveaway and a post-game firework show. Sunday is Family Day with $5 tickets for kids age 12 and under and seniors age 55 and over.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e New Jersey Jackals at Hinchliffe Stadium, 1 Jasper St., Paterson. 6:35 p.m. Friday, 6:05 p.m. Saturday, 4:35 p.m. Sunday, $5 to $25. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://jackals.com/\"\u003ejackals.com\u003c/a\u003e, 973-746-7434, contact@jackals.com. Gates open an hour prior to the start of the game.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Big Gay Cabaret\u0026#39; in Fair Lawn\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCelebrate Pride Month at this fundraiser for the Old Library Theatre and the Bergen County LGBTQ+ Alliance, Friday and Saturday at the George Frey Performing Arts Center. The show is co-directed by Jeff Parsons and Dave Toussas, with musical direction by Christopher Vehmas.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026#34;Big Gay Cabaret\u0026#34; at the George Frey Performing Arts Center, 10-10 20th St., Fair Lawn. 7:30 p.m. Friday and Saturday. $25. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.oldlibrarytheatre.com/\"\u003eoldlibrarytheatre.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Sounds of My Soul\u0026#39; dance showcase at NJPAC\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAatma Performing Arts celebrates its 15-year anniversary with “Sounds of My Soul” on Saturday. Directed by Amit Shah, the show features hits from Bollywood films and an eclectic fusion of Indian folk and western pop music. Highlights include handmade costumes and excerpts from Aatma’s newest touring production, “Finding Home: An Indian Musical.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Aatma Performing Arts presents \u0026#34;Sounds of My Soul\u0026#34; at NJPAC, Prudential Hall, Betty Wold Johnson Stage. 6 p.m. Saturday. $59 to $149. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.njpac.org/event/aatma-performing-arts-sounds-of-my-soul/\"\u003enjpac.org\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eThe David Drumgold Variety Show – Pride Edition\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73961064007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eActor and Broadway/TV/film producer David Drumgold brings a special Pride edition of his variety show to the Puffin Cultural Forum in Teaneck on Saturday. Hearkening back to the variety shows of the \u0026#39;60s and \u0026#39;70s - like \u0026#34;The Carol Burnett Show,\u0026#34; \u0026#34;The Flip Wilson Show,\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;The Cher Show\u0026#34; - Drumgold\u0026#39;s variety show features good old-fashioned talent, cheer and the escapism of a good time. It celebrates everything magical about art, and features comedy, drag, dance and musicians.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFeatured performers include the New York Metropolitan Opera soprano Brandie Inez Sutton, pianist Yasuhiko Fukuoka, and R\u0026amp;B/soul singer Diana Taylor. Plus, the newest addition to the lineup is Pissi Myles, a drag comedian, singer and hostess.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eN95 or equivalent masks are required. A limited quantity will be available at the door.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026#34;The David Drumgold Variety Show – Pride Edition\u0026#34; at the Puffin Cultural Forum, 20 Puffin Way, Teaneck. 7 p.m. Saturday. $10 suggested donation. RSVP at \u003ca href\u003d\"https://daviddrumgoldprideatpuffin.eventbrite.com\"\u003edaviddrumgoldprideatpuffin.eventbrite.com\u003c/a\u003e or call 201-836-3499. Those who cannot pay the suggested donation may call (or write to aortega@puffinfoundation.org) to make free reservations. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eAlan Cumming at State Theatre\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73789631007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Alan Cumming: Uncut - With Henry Koperski at the Piano\u0026#34; - Cumming\u0026#39;s new cabaret show - comes to State Theatre New Jersey in New Brunswick on Saturday.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eA longtime TV, film and stage actor, Cumming premiered his first cabaret show, \u0026#34;Alan Cumming Sings Sappy Songs,\u0026#34; in 2015 in New York City. His next cabaret show, \u0026#34;Legal Immigrant,\u0026#34; debuted in 2018, followed by \u0026#34;Alan Cumming Is Not Acting His Age,\u0026#34; which toured the world and ended up on Broadway. He is currently touring with NPR’s Ari Shapiro in \u0026#34;Och and Oy: A Considered Cabaret!,\u0026#34; as well as \u0026#34;Uncut,\u0026#34; which he developed at the Yaddo artists retreat and premiered in April.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis show is recommended for ages 18 and up. Everyone, regardless of age, entering the theater must purchase a ticket.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026#34;Alan Cumming: Uncut\u0026#34; at State Theatre of New Jersey, 15 Livingston Ave., New Brunswick. 8 p.m. Saturday. $39 to $69. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.stnj.org/events/detail/alan-cumming\"\u003estnj.org\u003c/a\u003e, 732-246-7469.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNY/NJ Gotham soccer in Harrison Sunday\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "11393637002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSunday is Kids Day at the Red Bull Arena, with a Fan Fest before the New York/New Jersey Gotham Football Club takes on the Washington Spirit in women\u0026#39;s pro soccer action. The Fan Fest will feature an Eli Manning meet-and-greet, balloon artists, face paint, friendship bracelet-making and food trucks.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e NY/NJ Gotham FC with Fan Fest at Red Bull Arena, 600 Cape May St., Harrison. Sunday. Fan Fest at 11 a.m. Game at 1:30 p.m. $15 to $270.21. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.gothamfc.com/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.gothamfc.com/\"\u003egothamfc.com.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eQuinceañera Expo in Saddle Brook\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eYoung ladies and their parents planning their quinceañera celebrations can attend NJ Quinceañera Expo 2024 in Saddle Brook on Sunday. The expo will feature an array of vendors and exhibitors showcasing the latest trends in quinceañera dresses, decorations, photography, catering, entertainment and more. Attendees will have the opportunity to connect with industry professionals, discover unique ideas and find everything needed to create a memorable quinceañera.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHighlights of the expo include a fashion show with the latest gown designs on the runway, vendor booths, exclusive offers, raffles and prizes, and expert advice to help make your quinceañera dream a reality.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eNJ Quinceañera Expo 2024 at Crowne Plaza, 50 Kenny Place, Saddle Brook. 2 to 7 p.m. Sunday. Free admission. For information, call 862-600-1769. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSummer Solstice campfire and night hike\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCelebrate the longest day of the year and the official start of the summer with the Tenafly Nature Center. A TNC naturalist will lead participants on a night hike to experience the sounds of summer, followed by a campfire and s\u0026#39;mores. The program is intended for adults and families with children 5 and up. Children must be accompanied by an adult. The program will be held entirely outdoors. In case of inclement weather, it will be held under cover. Social distancing in effect. Space is limited and advance registration is required. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Summer Family Hike at the Tenafly Nature Center, 313 Hudson Ave., Tenafly. 7 to 9 p.m. Sunday. $8 for members; $12 for non-members; free for children under age 2. \u003ca href\u003d\"http://tenaflynaturecenter.org\"\u003etenaflynaturecenter.org\u003c/a\u003e, 201-568-6093.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eJesse Garron\u0026#39;s Tribute To Elvis\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "92928626"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBilled as \u0026#34;The Closest Thing to the King,\u0026#34; Garron uses the name of Elvis Presley\u0026#39;s twin brother who died at birth as he pays tribute to Elvis and his legacy. Inspired by Elvis at the age of four, Garron was always mesmerized by Elvis\u0026#39; voice and intrigued by everything Elvis from his music to his movies. He got his first break to pay him tribute at the age of 17 in a high school talent show and won the popular vote. Since his first performance in 1997, he has performed around the country and the world. In 2019, he was inducted into the International Elvis Tribute Artist Hall of Fame for his dedication to keeping Elvis\u0026#39; legacy alive. Garron performs with a four-piece band and three backing vocalists.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Jesse Garron\u0026#39;s Tribute to Elvis at the Florham Park gazebo, 111 Ridgedale Ave., on the Great Lawn, at 7 p.m. Sunday. If weather is questionable, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"http://florhamparkgazebo.com\"\u003eflorhamparkgazebo.com\u003c/a\u003e for updates. Free.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eHave an event coming up? Tell us about it. Write to Daniel Galioto at galiotod@northjersey.com.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

contentBody:
{
  "contentBody": [{
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74138091007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt\u0026#39;s officially the first weekend of summer, so what will you be doing in North Jersey? Here are some options we\u0026#39;ve curated for you:\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eSummertime is the time for fairs and there\u0026#39;s none bigger than \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/19/nj-state-fair-returns-meadowlands-what-to-know/74139760007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/19/nj-state-fair-returns-meadowlands-what-to-know/74139760007/\"\u003eState Fair Meadowlands, which starts on Thursday. \u003c/a\u003eAnother way to celebrate the arrival of the season is with a summer solstice campfire and hike at Tenafly Nature Center.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThere is always plenty of music in North Jersey, and this week\u0026#39;s concerts include tributes to the Grateful Dead and Elvis Presley. There is also a cabaret show by Alan Cumming and a dance performance by Aatma Performing Arts.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWe\u0026#39;ve also got sports, with Jackals baseball and the New York/New Jersey Gotham Football Club both at home this weekend; and art, with a local artist exhibit in Clifton. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd, for girls planning their quinceañera, there\u0026#39;s a free expo this weekend. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003ePlus, it\u0026#39;s Pride Month, so check out our\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/life/events/2024/05/31/pride-month-2024-events-celebrate-north-jersey-nj/72809698007/\"\u003e big list of Pride events\u003c/a\u003e, some of which are also included below.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eEnjoy!\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSunny and hot, with only a small chance of showers\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAccording to the National Weather Service:\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThursday night:\u003c/strong\u003e Partly cloudy, with a low around 75.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFriday\u003c/strong\u003e: Mostly sunny with a high at almost 100, with mostly cloudy skies at night and a low in the mid-70s.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSaturday\u003c/strong\u003e: Partly sunny, with a high in the mid-90s and chance of showers. Mostly cloudy at night and more possible showers, with a low in the mid-70s\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSunday:\u003c/strong\u003e Partly sunny, with a high in the low 90s and a chance of showers.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Artists’ Perspectives\u0026#39; at Clifton Arts Center\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThrough June 29, the “Artists’ Perspectives” exhibition by the Community Arts Association will be on display at the Clifton Arts Center. The exhibit is about how artists use perspective techniques to create realistic and non-realistic impressions. The artist’s perspective values process, communication and understanding. It embraces emotion and encourages connection. When artists communicate information, in this case through paintings, their perspectives can help make that visual information accessible, comprehensible and approachable. The artist’s perspective can also shape how we think about and act with each other as a community at large.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Community Arts Association originated in Allendale in 1965. Meetings were originally held in the Highlands Presbyterian Church before relocating to Northern Highlands Regional School, Archer United Methodist Church and finally to Trinity Episcopal Church. Community Arts Association sponsors workshops, hosts demonstrations, lectures, day trips, and art scholarships for graduating high schoolers.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026#34;Artists\u0026#39; Perspectives\u0026#34; by the Community Arts Association at Clifton Arts Center, 900 Clifton Ave. $3 admission. Normal gallery hours are Wednesday through Saturday, 1 to 4 p.m. 973-472-5499. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://cliftonartscenter.org/gallery-exhibits\"\u003ecliftonartscenter.org\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eState Fair Meadowlands at MetLife Stadium\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "12168980002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe fair is back with a lineup of new and favorite all-ages entertainment. This year’s program is packed with stunts and acrobatic acts, amusement rides, magicians, musicians, racing pigs and food. For the next 17 days, the fair will be open in the stadium\u0026#39;s parking lots E and F, on weeknights (except June 25) and with extended hours on weekends and July 4. Parking is free in lots G, J and L for all fairgoers.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/19/nj-state-fair-returns-meadowlands-what-to-know/74139760007/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/06/19/nj-state-fair-returns-meadowlands-what-to-know/74139760007/\"\u003eState Fair Meadowlands at MetLife Stadium\u003c/a\u003e in East Rutherford. Thursday, Monday and Wednesday, 6 p.m. to midnight; Friday, 6 p.m. to 1 a.m.; Saturday, 2 p.m. to 1 a.m.; Sunday, 2 p.m. to midnight. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.metlifestadium.com/event/2024/06/20/metlife-stadium/state-fair\"\u003emetlifestadium.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eGrateful Dead tribute in Millburn\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe music of the Grateful Dead continues to grow and evolve, long after the band played their last show. The members of Workingman\u0026#39;s Jed share a common love for the Dead’s musical canon, jams and multi-part vocal harmonies. They strive to honor the original compositions through their individual styles and musical experiences, to create something familiar, yet different and special. They design unique set lists for each show, merge songs together in original ways, and try to do new things. ​\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Workingman\u0026#39;s Jed at Taylor Park, 110 Main St., Millburn. 7 to 8:30 p.m. Thursday (rain date is June 27). Free. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://twp.millburn.nj.us/461/Summer-Concerts-in-Taylor-Park\"\u003etwp.millburn.nj.us\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eJackals baseball at Hinchliffe Stadium\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73636884007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Jackals are home in Paterson this weekend, with a three-game series against the Quebec Capitales. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFriday is \u0026#39;70s Night, so dress up in your best \u0026#39;70s outfit. On Saturday, there will be a mini-bat giveaway and a post-game firework show. Sunday is Family Day with $5 tickets for kids age 12 and under and seniors age 55 and over.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e New Jersey Jackals at Hinchliffe Stadium, 1 Jasper St., Paterson. 6:35 p.m. Friday, 6:05 p.m. Saturday, 4:35 p.m. Sunday, $5 to $25. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://jackals.com/\"\u003ejackals.com\u003c/a\u003e, 973-746-7434, contact@jackals.com. Gates open an hour prior to the start of the game.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Big Gay Cabaret\u0026#39; in Fair Lawn\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eCelebrate Pride Month at this fundraiser for the Old Library Theatre and the Bergen County LGBTQ+ Alliance, Friday and Saturday at the George Frey Performing Arts Center. The show is co-directed by Jeff Parsons and Dave Toussas, with musical direction by Christopher Vehmas.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026#34;Big Gay Cabaret\u0026#34; at the George Frey Performing Arts Center, 10-10 20th St., Fair Lawn. 7:30 p.m. Friday and Saturday. $25. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.oldlibrarytheatre.com/\"\u003eoldlibrarytheatre.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Sounds of My Soul\u0026#39; dance showcase at NJPAC\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAatma Performing Arts celebrates its 15-year anniversary with “Sounds of My Soul” on Saturday. Directed by Amit Shah, the show features hits from Bollywood films and an eclectic fusion of Indian folk and western pop music. Highlights include handmade costumes and excerpts from Aatma’s newest touring production, “Finding Home: An Indian Musical.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Aatma Performing Arts presents \u0026#34;Sounds of My Soul\u0026#34; at NJPAC, Prudential Hall, Betty Wold Johnson Stage. 6 p.m. Saturday. $59 to $149. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.njpac.org/event/aatma-performing-arts-sounds-of-my-soul/\"\u003enjpac.org\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eThe David Drumgold Variety Show – Pride Edition\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73961064007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eActor and Broadway/TV/film producer David Drumgold brings a special Pride edition of his variety show to the Puffin Cultural Forum in Teaneck on Saturday. Hearkening back to the variety shows of the \u0026#39;60s and \u0026#39;70s - like \u0026#34;The Carol Burnett Show,\u0026#34; \u0026#34;The Flip Wilson Show,\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;The Cher Show\u0026#34; - Drumgold\u0026#39;s variety show features good old-fashioned talent, cheer and the escapism of a good time. It celebrates everything magical about art, and features comedy, drag, dance and musicians.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFeatured performers include the New York Metropolitan Opera soprano Brandie Inez Sutton, pianist Yasuhiko Fukuoka, and R\u0026amp;B/soul singer Diana Taylor. Plus, the newest addition to the lineup is Pissi Myles, a drag comedian, singer and hostess.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eN95 or equivalent masks are required. A limited quantity will be available at the door.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026#34;The David Drumgold Variety Show – Pride Edition\u0026#34; at the Puffin Cultural Forum, 20 Puffin Way, Teaneck. 7 p.m. Saturday. $10 suggested donation. RSVP at \u003ca href\u003d\"https://daviddrumgoldprideatpuffin.eventbrite.com\"\u003edaviddrumgoldprideatpuffin.eventbrite.com\u003c/a\u003e or call 201-836-3499. Those who cannot pay the suggested donation may call (or write to aortega@puffinfoundation.org) to make free reservations. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eAlan Cumming at State Theatre\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73789631007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Alan Cumming: Uncut - With Henry Koperski at the Piano\u0026#34; - Cumming\u0026#39;s new cabaret show - comes to State Theatre New Jersey in New Brunswick on Saturday.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eA longtime TV, film and stage actor, Cumming premiered his first cabaret show, \u0026#34;Alan Cumming Sings Sappy Songs,\u0026#34; in 2015 in New York City. His next cabaret show, \u0026#34;Legal Immigrant,\u0026#34; debuted in 2018, followed by \u0026#34;Alan Cumming Is Not Acting His Age,\u0026#34; which toured the world and ended up on Broadway. He is currently touring with NPR’s Ari Shapiro in \u0026#34;Och and Oy: A Considered Cabaret!,\u0026#34; as well as \u0026#34;Uncut,\u0026#34; which he developed at the Yaddo artists retreat and premiered in April.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis show is recommended for ages 18 and up. Everyone, regardless of age, entering the theater must purchase a ticket.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026#34;Alan Cumming: Uncut\u0026#34; at State Theatre of New Jersey, 15 Livingston Ave., New Brunswick. 8 p.m. Saturday. $39 to $69. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.stnj.org/events/detail/alan-cumming\"\u003estnj.org\u003c/a\u003e, 732-246-7469.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNY/NJ Gotham soccer in Harrison Sunday\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "11393637002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eSunday is Kids Day at the Red Bull Arena, with a Fan Fest before the New York/New Jersey Gotham Football Club takes on the Washington Spirit in women\u0026#39;s pro soccer action. The Fan Fest will feature an Eli Manning meet-and-greet, balloon artists, face paint, friendship bracelet-making and food trucks.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e NY/NJ Gotham FC with Fan Fest at Red Bull Arena, 600 Cape May St., Harrison. Sunday. Fan Fest at 11 a.m. Game at 1:30 p.m. $15 to $270.21. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.gothamfc.com/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.gothamfc.com/\"\u003egothamfc.com.\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eQuinceañera Expo in Saddle Brook\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eYoung ladies and their parents planning their quinceañera celebrations can attend NJ Quinceañera Expo 2024 in Saddle Brook on Sunday. The expo will feature an array of vendors and exhibitors showcasing the latest trends in quinceañera dresses, decorations, photography, catering, entertainment and more. Attendees will have the opportunity to connect with industry professionals, discover unique ideas and find everything needed to create a memorable quinceañera.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eHighlights of the expo include a fashion show with the latest gown designs on the runway, vendor booths, exclusive offers, raffles and prizes, and expert advice to help make your quinceañera dream a reality.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eNJ Quinceañera Expo 2024 at Crowne Plaza, 50 Kenny Place, Saddle Brook. 2 to 7 p.m. Sunday. Free admission. For information, call 862-600-1769. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSummer Solstice campfire and night hike\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eCelebrate the longest day of the year and the official start of the summer with the Tenafly Nature Center. A TNC naturalist will lead participants on a night hike to experience the sounds of summer, followed by a campfire and s\u0026#39;mores. The program is intended for adults and families with children 5 and up. Children must be accompanied by an adult. The program will be held entirely outdoors. In case of inclement weather, it will be held under cover. Social distancing in effect. Space is limited and advance registration is required. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Summer Family Hike at the Tenafly Nature Center, 313 Hudson Ave., Tenafly. 7 to 9 p.m. Sunday. $8 for members; $12 for non-members; free for children under age 2. \u003ca href\u003d\"http://tenaflynaturecenter.org\"\u003etenaflynaturecenter.org\u003c/a\u003e, 201-568-6093.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eJesse Garron\u0026#39;s Tribute To Elvis\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "92928626"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBilled as \u0026#34;The Closest Thing to the King,\u0026#34; Garron uses the name of Elvis Presley\u0026#39;s twin brother who died at birth as he pays tribute to Elvis and his legacy. Inspired by Elvis at the age of four, Garron was always mesmerized by Elvis\u0026#39; voice and intrigued by everything Elvis from his music to his movies. He got his first break to pay him tribute at the age of 17 in a high school talent show and won the popular vote. Since his first performance in 1997, he has performed around the country and the world. In 2019, he was inducted into the International Elvis Tribute Artist Hall of Fame for his dedication to keeping Elvis\u0026#39; legacy alive. Garron performs with a four-piece band and three backing vocalists.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Jesse Garron\u0026#39;s Tribute to Elvis at the Florham Park gazebo, 111 Ridgedale Ave., on the Great Lawn, at 7 p.m. Sunday. If weather is questionable, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"http://florhamparkgazebo.com\"\u003eflorhamparkgazebo.com\u003c/a\u003e for updates. Free.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eHave an event coming up? Tell us about it. Write to Daniel Galioto at galiotod@northjersey.com.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

