    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eFor more information...\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://northtoshore.com/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://northtoshore.com/\"\u003eNorthtoshore.com\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "11466422002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe blues is music.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe blues is a mental condition.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe blues is music \u003cem\u003eabout\u003c/em\u003e a mental condition. Specifically, the condition of sadness. More specifically: sadness as the result of oppression, injustice and waking up this morning to find your baby gone.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSo it\u0026#39;s not so far-fetched that this summer\u0026#39;s second annual North to Shore Festival, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://northtoshore.com/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://northtoshore.com/\"\u003erunning through June 30\u003c/a\u003e, should feature among its 200 attractions a program called \u0026#34;Chasing the Blues Away, featuring The Blues People and NJ Mental Health Players.\u0026#34; (June 26). \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73092329007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt\u0026#39;s a collaboration between a blues band and an acting collective — one that specializes in scenarios related to mental health. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Music in general, and particularly the blues, is about sharing life experiences,\u0026#34; said David Rodriguez, executive producer of the festival, and himself a musician. \u0026#34;And sometimes those experiences are more clouds than sunshine. The sharing of pain as well as the sharing of happiness is part of the process. Highlighting that in the festival is a critical way to deal with these issues upfront.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd it\u0026#39;s one of many examples of how the month-long, three-city, multi-venue arts festival is using the arts to address issues of wellness — both mental and physical. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I think the whole thought of the program is to really make it a festival with a soul,\u0026#34; Rodriguez said. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eComing to North Jersey\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe North Jersey leg of the festival — centering around Newark — runs June 23 to 30. Two earlier parts of the festival are based in Asbury Park (June 10 to 16) and Atlantic City (June 17 to 23). \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAll of them feature an eclectic mix of entertainment: stars and unknowns, music and comedy, film and visual arts and discussion groups and tech talks. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I think the whole thought of the program is to really make it a festival with a soul,\u0026#34; Rodriguez said. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "68645932007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Newark segment, featuring over 50 attractions, includes some big name entertainers, including Matchbox Twenty (June 27), A Day to Remember (June 26), Jeezy and Scarface (June 28), writer-director Kevin Smith (June 30), comedian Kevin Hart (June 30), and — a late breaking addendum, in association with the Montclair Film Festival — actor Paul Giamatti in conversation with Stephen Colbert (July 26). \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut this year, issues of mental and physical health were never very far from the programmers\u0026#39; thinking. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The cornerstone is, we\u0026#39;re not doctors, we\u0026#39;re not psychologists, we\u0026#39;re not any of that,\u0026#34; said Rodriguez, an Englewood resident. \u0026#34;But we can share a message for people who might otherwise not hear it. The one thing the arts can do better than anything is bring people together, and share messages that affect not only them but friends and family members.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "12258549002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis year\u0026#39;s festival includes a New Davonhaime Food Bank Distribution Day, combining art and nourishment (June 24 and 25). There is a \u0026#34;Rest Fest\u0026#34; at The Newark Museum of Art (June 30). \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe NJ Mental Health Players make an appearance on several other bills including The Ultimate Jazz and R\u0026amp;B Jam (June 25) and Jazz and Joy featuring Lynette Sheard Experience (June 28). And a virtual program on June 26 is called Prescribing Creativity: Promoting Health Equity through Arts-on-Prescription.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Mental wellness is a great part of physical wellness,\u0026#34; Rodriguez said. \u0026#34;We\u0026#39;re working with Horizon and RWJBarnabas. Physicians can prescribe arts activities, whether it be Zumba classes or a ticket to a comedy show or tickets for family activities. The arts can be a vehicle to enhance physical wellness through mental wellness.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis is the second year of North to Shore — N2S — the Garden State\u0026#39;s answer to South by Southwest — SXSW. Last year\u0026#39;s inaugural festival drew 220,000 people over the month. This year, they\u0026#39;re expecting more.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "11248231002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The first year, it was all we could do to make it successful,\u0026#34; Rodriguez said. \u0026#34;The second year, we\u0026#39;re saying, how can we make what we\u0026#39;ve created impactful? And our hope is that next year, the impact becomes even greater.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNorth to Shore Festival, 2024: Newark\u003c/h2\u003e"
