  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 29 and 30. Newark Museum of Art. 10 a.m. to 5 p.m. 49 Washington Street. Free access to festival attendees. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 29. Lincoln Park Music Festival powers up Yogi Fest by Ty Daye: North to Shore Edition. 11 a.m. to 8 p.m. Lincoln Park, 450 Washington Street.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 29. Family Fun Day: An Interactive STEAM Fair. 12 p.m. Newark Public Library, 5 Washington Street.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 29. International Pride Month Celebration. 12 p.m.  NJCRI Pride Center of Newark, 17 Academy St, Newark. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 29. CURRENTS: Collaborative Art and Ecology on the Passaic River. 1 p.m. Newark Riverfront Park, Somme Street Entrance, 709 Raymond Blvd. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 29. Newark Arts Presents Murals \u0026amp; Martinis: Public Art Tour. 1 p.m. Newark ArtSpace at Vermella Broad Street, 355 Broad St. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 29. Newark Alliance: Night Market. 3 p.m. to 9 p.m., Halsey Street between New and Bleeker Streets. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 29. Newark Levels: The Muses of Brick City. 6:30 p.m., \u003dSPACE, Newark. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 29. Sommore. 7 p.m. and 9:30 p.m., Victoria Theater, NJPAC, Newark. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 29. \u0026#34;Hey! I Heard You\u0026#39;re Black\u0026#34; (Play). 7:30 p.m. NJPAC Center for Arts Education, Newark.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 29. Jhené Aiko: The Magic Hour Tour. 8 p.m., Prudential Center.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 29. A Night at Bunkr. 9 p.m., BNKR. Lower Level, 25 Halsey St, Newark.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 29. Luv + Grind International Music Series. 9 p.m., Tinjune Downtown, 494 Broad St, Newark. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 30. Newark Historical Renaissance Black Ivy Ride. 10 a.m. to 2:30 p.m., Harriet Tubman Park.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 30. Rest Fest. 11 a.m. to 4 p.m., The Newark Museum of Art.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 30. Taste of the City \u0026amp; Sounds of the Ironbound — Randy Haze Trio and Troubleman Band. 12 p.m., 130 Ferry St, Newark. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 30. Taste of the City \u0026amp; Sounds of the Ironbound — Bira. 12 p.m., Casa Nova Grill, 264 Ferry St, Newark. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 30. Taste of the City \u0026amp; Sounds of the Ironbound — Samuca Moretti. 12 p.m,. Sabor Unido Restaurant, 77 Jefferson Street, Newark. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 30. Taste of the City \u0026amp; Sounds of the Ironbound — Mike Santos. 12 p.m., Five Corners Ristorante, 10 Wilson Avenue, Newark. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 30. Taste of the City \u0026amp; Sounds of the Ironbound — DJ Nokas. 12 p.m., Sol-Mar Restaurant \u0026amp; Marisqueira, 267 Ferry St, Newark. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 30. Taste of the City \u0026amp; Sounds of the Ironbound — DJ Miguel Casimiro. 12 p.m., Allegra Grill, 58 Kossuth St, Newark. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 30. Taste of the City \u0026amp; Sounds of the Ironbound — Marcelo Buby. 12 p.m., Boi na Brasa Bar \u0026amp; Grill, 1 Merchant St, Newark. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 30. Taste of the City \u0026amp; Sounds of the Ironbound — Janetza. 12 p.m., Newark Standard Cafe, 68 Wilson Ave, Newark. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 30. Down in the Ro\u0026#39; Open Mic Experience. 1 p.m., Tinjune Restaurant, Newark. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 30. Samar Newsome presents Glory in the Garden: A Newark Celebration of Gospel Music. 2 p.m., Newark Lab High School, 18 Norfolk Street, Newark. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 30. The Coming Home Community Cookout! 3 p.m., West End Ave. Park, Newark. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 30. Kevin Smith — Jersey Sure. 3 p.m., Victoria Theater, NJPAC, Newark.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 30. Roc \u0026amp; The Collective RnB Night. 5 p.m., The Yard, Newark. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 30. The Vibes in the City Experience + Awards Ceremony. 6 p.m., Larouge Lounge, 972 Broad St, Newark. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ June 30. Kevin Hart: Acting My Age Tour 2024. 7 p.m., Prudential Center.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e∎ July 26. A Conversation with Stephen Colbert \u0026amp; Paul Giamatti. 8 p.m., NJPAC,  Newark. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eFor more information...\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://northtoshore.com/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://northtoshore.com/\"\u003eNorthtoshore.com\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "71894400007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe first Broadway revival of Samm-Art Williams’ “Home” is full of joy and pain, heart and hope.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd sorrow, for the playwright passed away days before the first preview. But rest assured Williams is smiling from above after every performance, for this atypical work is engrossing and entertaining   \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe story is about Cephus Miles (Tory Kittles), a Black farmer in North Carolina. He’s in love with Pattie Mae (Brittany Inge), who goes off to college. But things take a turn when he is thrown in jail for opposing the Vietnam War draft. And when he moves to the big city, his life becomes dangerous and complicated.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDirected by the Tony Award-winning Kenny Leon, the script in this 90-minute show is packed with poetry, melody, rhythm and song. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74048330007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThere\u0026#39;s talk of land, soil, sun, rain and crops. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eGod, faith and family — and America.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThere are dozens of characters, but only three people in this small-scale but mighty production. The acting is first-rate. Stori Ayers is identified as Woman Two in the program, but she portrays everyone from a a youngster to a prison guard to a bus driver. Watching her transform from one moment to the next is one of the highlights of the night.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe audience warms up to Kittles quickly. He allows us to share Cephus\u0026#39; tragedy as he goes from the comforts of home to jail to being lost among the masses, peddling for cash any way he can.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eInge plays multiple characters, too, but she shines bright as Pattie Mae. Maybe it\u0026#39;s her eyes? Her smile? There\u0026#39;s real chemistry between Inge and Kittles that is wonderful to see.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74048433007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe minimal set by Arnulfo Maldonado works, as does lighting by Allen Lee Hughes, costumes by Dede Ayite, sound design by Justin Ellington, and hair and wig design by Nikiya Mathis. Kate Wilson deserves mention as voice coach.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEverything comes together to make this a feel-good evening. The ending may be predictable, but that’s OK.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“Home” opens the 2024-25 season, and it’s timing could not be better. What are the tens of thousands of migrants looking for? Jobs, opportunities, a place to start again.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe work also gives voice to the poor and lonely and homeless — and anyone in America looking for a place to fit in, to belong. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAnd it\u0026#39;s a reminder that no matter how far away we go, we can’t escape who we are, where we come from.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHome will always be a part of us.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "12148395002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo\u003c/strong\u003e: “Home,” through July 21, Todd Haimes Theatre, 227 W. 42nd St., New York, $49 to $149; 212-719-1300, roundabouttheatre.org.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eBill Canacci can be reached at \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"mailto:bcanacci@gannettnj.com\"\u003e\u003cem\u003ebcanacci@gannettnj.com\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "71894400007"
    }, {
