body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "7799415002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBergen County residents have a new opportunity to engage in friendly competition, where swimmers need to put their running shoes on — and runners need to bring a bathing suit.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe River Edge Swim Club holds its first-ever Splash N’ Dash Biathlon on Saturday, June 22. All Bergen County residents are welcome to compete in the event. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eContestants will swim laps in the 25-meter-laned pool, then run on the swim club grounds and nearby athletic field.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eStory continues below photo gallery\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "872241002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThere are 14 events, and ages range from 5 to 18 and over. The number of pool laps and running distance is based on the seven different age brackets. For each age group, there is a male and female race. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe event is open to all residents because the club wanted to “engage in real friendly county competition,” said Christopher McGee, a member of the River Edge Swim Club board of trustees. Local swim clubs, gyms, and high school swim teams were invited to broaden the reach of the event. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMcGee says the race gives competitors who are solely runners or swimmers a chance to try something different and get out of their comfort zone, as well as a fun opportunity for kids to compete against each other.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“When I was little, everyone was swimming. Swimming is something kids don’t normally do anymore,” said River Edge swim coach Ryan Berman. “It is a great way to get kids involved that they may not ever compete in.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBerman is the head coach of the 11 and up swim team and wants her team to try hard, but especially have fun. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSwim clubs dwindling\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe club hopes the event encourages kids to spend more time outside — and swimming. “Any way of getting kids out and moving is a good idea, go out and go for a swim, do a little exercise,” said Teresa Donohue, head of the aquatics program and club president. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74148606007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCOVID-19 hurt the club\u0026#39;s participation the past few years, but the biathlon offers a chance to start fresh. “Things have been different since COVID,\u0026#34; said McGee. \u0026#34;Getting the kids back together and thinking of new ways to get everyone at the pool is amazing.”  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMcGee said swim clubs are dwindling, due to closures spurred by financial issues. McGee said the event can show residents that “we have a great swim club in the county.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“Swim clubs have been the life and blood of summertime in Bergen County,” he said.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDonohue agreed. “We hope that people coming and seeing what we have to offer will get us new members,” she said. “We just want people to have a good time. It accomplishes some good will between towns, and people that don’t know each other will chat while waiting for their turn to swim.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "7799415002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBergen County residents have a new opportunity to engage in friendly competition, where swimmers need to put their running shoes on — and runners need to bring a bathing suit.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe River Edge Swim Club holds its first-ever Splash N’ Dash Biathlon on Saturday, June 22. All Bergen County residents are welcome to compete in the event. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eContestants will swim laps in the 25-meter-laned pool, then run on the swim club grounds and nearby athletic field.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eStory continues below photo gallery\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "872241002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThere are 14 events, and ages range from 5 to 18 and over. The number of pool laps and running distance is based on the seven different age brackets. For each age group, there is a male and female race. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe event is open to all residents because the club wanted to “engage in real friendly county competition,” said Christopher McGee, a member of the River Edge Swim Club board of trustees. Local swim clubs, gyms, and high school swim teams were invited to broaden the reach of the event. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMcGee says the race gives competitors who are solely runners or swimmers a chance to try something different and get out of their comfort zone, as well as a fun opportunity for kids to compete against each other.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“When I was little, everyone was swimming. Swimming is something kids don’t normally do anymore,” said River Edge swim coach Ryan Berman. “It is a great way to get kids involved that they may not ever compete in.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBerman is the head coach of the 11 and up swim team and wants her team to try hard, but especially have fun. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSwim clubs dwindling\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe club hopes the event encourages kids to spend more time outside — and swimming. “Any way of getting kids out and moving is a good idea, go out and go for a swim, do a little exercise,” said Teresa Donohue, head of the aquatics program and club president. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74148606007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCOVID-19 hurt the club\u0026#39;s participation the past few years, but the biathlon offers a chance to start fresh. “Things have been different since COVID,\u0026#34; said McGee. \u0026#34;Getting the kids back together and thinking of new ways to get everyone at the pool is amazing.”  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMcGee said swim clubs are dwindling, due to closures spurred by financial issues. McGee said the event can show residents that “we have a great swim club in the county.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“Swim clubs have been the life and blood of summertime in Bergen County,” he said.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDonohue agreed. “We hope that people coming and seeing what we have to offer will get us new members,” she said. “We just want people to have a good time. It accomplishes some good will between towns, and people that don’t know each other will chat while waiting for their turn to swim.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

contentBody:
{
  "contentBody": [{
