      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn at least two cases in New Jersey, Warraich said women were “given a hard time” when they asked to wear a hijab in training or on the job as police officers. He called for the state to issue guidance or a directive for police department on religious exceptions to dress codes.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“It’s a problem because it’s left up to the discretion of the people in charge,” Warraich said. “A solution is a directive which would just tell anyone that any religious article, like a yarmulke or a turban for a Sikh male or a head covering for a Muslim or Sikh female, any religious item, should be allowed.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
