  "contentBody": [{
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73970952007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "<p><em>Editor&#39;s Note: The results of the local races will be added to this file as they become available. Please check back often for updated results.</em> <em>Early results may only represent mail-in ballots.</em></p>"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "<p>Ten municipalities in Bergen County had contested primary races on Tuesday. </p>"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "<p>There were contested Democratic races in Alpine, Bogota, Englewood and Tenafly and contested Republican races in Franklin Lakes, Oakland, Old Tappan, Ridgefield and Wyckoff. Palisades Park was the only borough to have contested races on both sides of the aisle. </p>"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "<p><span class="exclude-from-newsgate"><strong style="margin-right:3px;">More: </strong><a href="https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/2024/05/21/everything-you-need-to-know-to-vote-in-june-4-primary-election/73771434007/" target="_blank">NJ&#39;s primary election is June 4. Here&#39;s everything you need to know cast your ballot</a></span></p>"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "<p>The following show votes reported in each of the Bergen County races: </p>"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "<h2 class="presto-h2 wp-block-heading">Alpine election results</h2>"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "<p>Four Democrats ran for two council seats.</p>"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "<ul>
<li>Steven E. Cohen* - Democratic Committee of Bergen County - 140 votes received </li>



<li>Geroge A. Abad - Democratic Committee of Bergen County - 154 votes received </li>



<li>Faisel Hussein - Our Safety, Our Community, Our Alpine - 33 votes received </li>



<li>Charles Kim - Our Safety, Our Community, Our Alpine - 33 votes received </li>
</ul>"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "<h2 class="presto-h2 wp-block-heading">Bogota election results</h2>"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "<p>Four Democrats ran for two council seats.</p>"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "<ul>
<li>Robert Robbins* - Democrats for Progress - 146 votes received </li>



<li>Jo-Ellen Granquist - Democrats for Progress - 188 votes received </li>



<li>Consuelo M. Carpenter* - Democratic Committee of Bergen County - 340 votes received </li>



<li>William R. Hordern - Democratic Committee of Bergen County - 236 votes received </li>
</ul>"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73969924007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "<h2 class="presto-h2 wp-block-heading">Englewood election results</h2>"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "<p>Four Democrats ran for one at-large council seat.</p>"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "<ul>
<li>Charles Cobb* - Democratic Committee of Bergen County - 461 votes received </li>



<li>Horace H. Ragbir - Real Englewood Democrat - 36 votes received </li>



<li>Dan B. Tokayer - Real Englewood Democrat - 404 votes received </li>



<li>Sara Stroman - Englewood-Transparency, Equity Change - 99 votes received </li>
</ul>"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "<h2 class="presto-h2 wp-block-heading">Palisades Park election results</h2>"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "<p><a href="https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/bergen/palisades-park/2024/06/03/palisades-park-nj-council-election-results-2024-june-primary-elections/73961684007/">Four Democrats competed for two seats.</a></p>"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "<ul>
<li>Anthony Hwan Kim -  355 votes received </li>



<li>Elynn Kim - 303 votes received </li>



<li>Sang H. Lee* - Democratic Committee of Bergen County - 509 votes received </li>



<li>Charlie Changkyun Shin - 510 votes received </li>
</ul>"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "<p>Four Republicans ran for two seats.</p>"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "<ul>
<li>Stephanie Jang* - Republicans for Citizens - 153 votes received </li>



<li>Neris Papoters - Republicans for Citizens - 79 votes received </li>



