body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOAKLAND —  Mert Ozer walked to the edge of the steps leading to the Indian Hills High School cafeteria last week and went down hands-free. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eNot an easy feat for the blind exchange student from Istanbul, Turkey.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eLeading the way to the school\u0026#39;s guidance office, Mert stopped precisely at the wood door leading to the department. He explained that the door reflects sound differently than the cinderblock walls around it, so he knows where to stop.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73920155007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;They brought me in before school started to walk me around so I could find my way,\u0026#34; Mert said. \u0026#34;At first, I had an aide with me all the time, but I showed them I could get around on my own and that stopped.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMert, 16, is finishing his junior year in the school. His student exchange year was facilitated through the American Field Service\u0026#39;s Youth Exchange and Study program.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eYouth Exchange and Study students come from predominantly Muslim countries to spend a year in an American public school as part of a cultural exchange. Of the 1,000 American Field Service students hosted by the program this school year, 171 came through the Youth Exchange and Study program. Two of those students listed a disability. Ten other schools were approached before Indian Hills agreed to take Mert.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73920415007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;We\u0026#39;ve had exchange students before, but he was our first blind student,\u0026#34; said Indian Hills Principal Gregory Vacca. \u0026#34;Our question was whether we could provide all he would need. Safety was a concern. We already had a relationship with the host parent, Ann Ford, so that helped.  We had to start with a little trust on both sides.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFor Ford, Mert is her eighth exchange student. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Mert had to go to Oregon first for some training,\u0026#34; Ford said. \u0026#34;I made a few adjustments. He didn\u0026#39;t need bedside lamps, they just got in his way. I had to teach him the beeps on the microwave. But now he doesn\u0026#39;t use his cane in the house. He gets around on his own.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMert\u0026#39;s English was good when he arrived, Ford said, however, she said he became more fluent and acquired something of a North Jersey accent as the year went on.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73920288007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;He came out the first day after class with two students who had volunteered to make sure he found me,\u0026#34; Ford said.  \u0026#34;He did great.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt was a mutual learning experience for Mert and the faculty, according to Vacca. Mert had to demonstrate his keyboarding and computer skills using programs for the blind so teachers could understand how he could function in a mainstream classroom.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Our students have MacBooks, and he had his own PC,\u0026#34; said Guidance Counselor Susan Wiener. \u0026#34;He has an electronic device attached to his laptop that displays Braille. His biggest concern was that the constant presence of an aide made it difficult for him to interact with other students. It took awhile, but we figured it out. We even had to move him to a more challenging English class.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73894923007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe teachers also improvised. Physics teacher Timothy Walkowich devised a tactile graph-drawing system using foam rubber sheets in various shapes so Mert could conceptualize how to chart results.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Our physical education teachers had to create ways for Mert to participate in class, and the students were good about making sure he was included,\u0026#34; Vacca said. \u0026#34;Everyone went above and beyond to find ways to help. The full community came together.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMert\u0026#39;s musical gifts provided another way for him to interact with his fellow students. Self-taught on the piano, Mert picked up the guitar in New Jersey, although he concedes he still needs help \u0026#34;where to put my fingers.\u0026#34; His voice got him a lead role in the school\u0026#39;s fall \u0026#34;Four Seasons\u0026#34; production, and the part of the Electric Skate in their spring musical \u0026#34;SpongeBob SquarePants.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I had to dance, and didn\u0026#39;t know if I could,\u0026#34; Mert said. \u0026#34;Victoria Fox was our choreographer, and she was really helpful. I even had to learn how to bow.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73920033007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHis efforts earned him several awards at the year-end ceremonies on Wednesday.  He was awarded The Instrumentalist Magazine Musicianship Award in band, the Chamber Choir Gold Pin in choir, the Musicianship Certificate for \u0026#34;Outstanding Soloist\u0026#34; and the Merit Certificate for Tenor in the school\u0026#39;s Chamber Choir.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFord said Mert has enjoyed a full year of music and travel, venturing into New York City with friends and attending several concerts including singers Andrea Bocelli, Billy Joel and Barry Manilow.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;We were up in the rafters at one concert, and the staff quietly came and invited us to take open orchestra seats because they could see he was blind,\u0026#34; Ford said.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73920256007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAmong Mert\u0026#39;s travels was a trip to Boston where he fell in love with its accessibility, its signaled traffic lights, and consequently its Berklee College of Music, which he hopes to attend after graduation in Turkey.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJust before a trip to prom with former exchange student Yazgi Akata, Mert presented the school with a \u0026#34;Medallion Member Recognition\u0026#34; certificate for providing him with a supportive educational community during his visit.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;What I learned was don\u0026#39;t hesitate to ask for help,\u0026#34; Mert said. \u0026#34;Direct communication is the most important. Don\u0026#39;t assume earlier than you have to.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn that regard, Mert said for all his exposure to an American teen diet of hamburgers and pizza, there was something he was looking forward to back home.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;My mother is the best cook,\u0026#34; Mert said. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOAKLAND —  Mert Ozer walked to the edge of the steps leading to the Indian Hills High School cafeteria last week and went down hands-free. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eNot an easy feat for the blind exchange student from Istanbul, Turkey.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eLeading the way to the school\u0026#39;s guidance office, Mert stopped precisely at the wood door leading to the department. He explained that the door reflects sound differently than the cinderblock walls around it, so he knows where to stop.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73920155007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;They brought me in before school started to walk me around so I could find my way,\u0026#34; Mert said. \u0026#34;At first, I had an aide with me all the time, but I showed them I could get around on my own and that stopped.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMert, 16, is finishing his junior year in the school. His student exchange year was facilitated through the American Field Service\u0026#39;s Youth Exchange and Study program.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eYouth Exchange and Study students come from predominantly Muslim countries to spend a year in an American public school as part of a cultural exchange. Of the 1,000 American Field Service students hosted by the program this school year, 171 came through the Youth Exchange and Study program. Two of those students listed a disability. Ten other schools were approached before Indian Hills agreed to take Mert.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73920415007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;We\u0026#39;ve had exchange students before, but he was our first blind student,\u0026#34; said Indian Hills Principal Gregory Vacca. \u0026#34;Our question was whether we could provide all he would need. Safety was a concern. We already had a relationship with the host parent, Ann Ford, so that helped.  We had to start with a little trust on both sides.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFor Ford, Mert is her eighth exchange student. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Mert had to go to Oregon first for some training,\u0026#34; Ford said. \u0026#34;I made a few adjustments. He didn\u0026#39;t need bedside lamps, they just got in his way. I had to teach him the beeps on the microwave. But now he doesn\u0026#39;t use his cane in the house. He gets around on his own.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMert\u0026#39;s English was good when he arrived, Ford said, however, she said he became more fluent and acquired something of a North Jersey accent as the year went on.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73920288007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;He came out the first day after class with two students who had volunteered to make sure he found me,\u0026#34; Ford said.  \u0026#34;He did great.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt was a mutual learning experience for Mert and the faculty, according to Vacca. Mert had to demonstrate his keyboarding and computer skills using programs for the blind so teachers could understand how he could function in a mainstream classroom.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Our students have MacBooks, and he had his own PC,\u0026#34; said Guidance Counselor Susan Wiener. \u0026#34;He has an electronic device attached to his laptop that displays Braille. His biggest concern was that the constant presence of an aide made it difficult for him to interact with other students. It took awhile, but we figured it out. We even had to move him to a more challenging English class.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73894923007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe teachers also improvised. Physics teacher Timothy Walkowich devised a tactile graph-drawing system using foam rubber sheets in various shapes so Mert could conceptualize how to chart results.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Our physical education teachers had to create ways for Mert to participate in class, and the students were good about making sure he was included,\u0026#34; Vacca said. \u0026#34;Everyone went above and beyond to find ways to help. The full community came together.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMert\u0026#39;s musical gifts provided another way for him to interact with his fellow students. Self-taught on the piano, Mert picked up the guitar in New Jersey, although he concedes he still needs help \u0026#34;where to put my fingers.\u0026#34; His voice got him a lead role in the school\u0026#39;s fall \u0026#34;Four Seasons\u0026#34; production, and the part of the Electric Skate in their spring musical \u0026#34;SpongeBob SquarePants.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I had to dance, and didn\u0026#39;t know if I could,\u0026#34; Mert said. \u0026#34;Victoria Fox was our choreographer, and she was really helpful. I even had to learn how to bow.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73920033007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHis efforts earned him several awards at the year-end ceremonies on Wednesday.  He was awarded The Instrumentalist Magazine Musicianship Award in band, the Chamber Choir Gold Pin in choir, the Musicianship Certificate for \u0026#34;Outstanding Soloist\u0026#34; and the Merit Certificate for Tenor in the school\u0026#39;s Chamber Choir.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFord said Mert has enjoyed a full year of music and travel, venturing into New York City with friends and attending several concerts including singers Andrea Bocelli, Billy Joel and Barry Manilow.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;We were up in the rafters at one concert, and the staff quietly came and invited us to take open orchestra seats because they could see he was blind,\u0026#34; Ford said.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73920256007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAmong Mert\u0026#39;s travels was a trip to Boston where he fell in love with its accessibility, its signaled traffic lights, and consequently its Berklee College of Music, which he hopes to attend after graduation in Turkey.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eJust before a trip to prom with former exchange student Yazgi Akata, Mert presented the school with a \u0026#34;Medallion Member Recognition\u0026#34; certificate for providing him with a supportive educational community during his visit.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;What I learned was don\u0026#39;t hesitate to ask for help,\u0026#34; Mert said. \u0026#34;Direct communication is the most important. Don\u0026#39;t assume earlier than you have to.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn that regard, Mert said for all his exposure to an American teen diet of hamburgers and pizza, there was something he was looking forward to back home.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;My mother is the best cook,\u0026#34; Mert said. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

