    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73174220007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBig protests from Englewood to LA \u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCities around New Jersey and the U.S. − from Englewood, Paterson and Fort Lee to Chicago, New York and Los Angeles − have faced similar challenges\u003cstrong\u003e,\u003c/strong\u003e amid widespread protest over the death toll in Gaza. In recent months, activists have blocked highways, airports, and bridges to make their points.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEnglewood\u0026#39;s $32,000 overtime bill since Oct. 7 has mostly been spent on additional police at council meetings and protests, according to City Manager Robert Hoffmann. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn New York, protestors have targeted some of the city\u0026#39;s most iconic events, including the Macy\u0026#39;s Thanksgiving Day Parade, the annual Christmas tree-lighting at Rockefeller Center and the Met Gala, leading to the $53 million OT tab, an NYPD spokesperson said.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHamas\u0026#39; Oct. 7 attack killed 1,200 people in Israel; another 240 were taken hostage. It also sparked an Israeli offensive in Gaza in which some 33,000 people have been killed, according to the Hamas-run Gaza health ministry.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Record and NorthJersey.com sought comment from groups that have organized Teaneck demonstrations, including Wheels for Palestine, American Muslims for Palestine and the Council on American-Islamic Relations\u0026#39; New Jersey chapter. But calls and emails were not returned. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn a post on Instagram, Wheels for Palestine, which has organized weekly car caravans through town, wrote, \u0026#34;If you don\u0026#39;t want these car rallies to go through your town, do not pass resolutions supporting\u0026#34; Israel or its campaign in Gaza.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMike Kelly:  \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/columnists/mike-kelly/2023/12/13/israel-hamas-war-teaneck-nj-rift-mike-kelly-protest/71830560007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eThe Israel-Hamas war tears at Teaneck\u0026#39;s inclusive tradition. Can it be fixed?\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe account says the group \u0026#34;is dedicated to standing for the people of Palestine,\u0026#34; and since October, it has rallied \u0026#34;with our vehicles to expose Zionism\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;raise funds for Gaza.\u0026#34;  It also urges its followers to attend council meetings and offers talking points to express pro-Palestinian positions.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eHow Teaneck police try to keep the peace\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn Teaneck, police officers have been trained in \u0026#34;crowd management and de-escalation techniques\u0026#34; and are prepared to handle the rigors of the current climate, Kriegel said. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003ePolice have implemented measures including designated protest areas, and they work to ensure clear communication with protest leaders, he said. Officers also wear body cameras to ensure transparency and accountability, the deputy chief added.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;We\u0026#39;re also monitoring social media for any signs of planned violence or disruption,\u0026#34; he said. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSome residents fear services will suffer because of all of the attention being devoted to the demonstrations. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAt a recent council meeting, resident Aviva Angel said she was distraught that protestors \u0026#34;came from outside our community\u0026#34;and \u0026#34;placed a financial burden on our town.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73174216007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAngel said that the funds spent on police overtime \u0026#34;could have been better used to enrich our community\u0026#34; by boosting playgrounds or children\u0026#39;s programs. \u0026#34;Our resources are being strained by a group that wants to spread discord.\u0026#34; She suggested that the participants \u0026#34;should be billed for the expense.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eKriegel said that ultimately, people have the right to protest or to drive through the town in car rallies.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;We don\u0026#39;t have the legal authority to stop them. Everyone has the First Amendment right to protest peacefully,\u0026#34;  he said. \u0026#34;Anyone peacefully protesting will be protected. However, we have previously and will continue to enforce violations of the law when we observe them.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Our goal is to keep the peace and keep everyone safe,\u0026#34; he said.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cem\u003eDeena Yellin covers religion for NorthJersey.com. For unlimited access to her work covering how the spiritual intersects with our daily lives, \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://cm.dailyrecord.com/specialoffer/?gps-source\u003dCPNAVBARBBB\u0026utm_medium\u003dONSITE\u0026utm_campaign\u003d2019SLJP10\u0026utm_content\u003dCPNAVBARBBB\u0026utm_source\u003dCPNAVBARBBB\u0026onSuccessRedirectURL\u003dhttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.dailyrecord.com%2F\"\u003e\u003cem\u003eplease subscribe or activate your digital account today\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eEmail: \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"mailto:yellin@northjersey.com\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003eyellin@northjersey.com\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

contentBody:
{
  "contentBody": [{
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "71232305007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Teaneck Police Department has racked up nearly $130,000 in overtime pay as a result of demonstrations and other events related to the Gaza conflict since the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/2024/05/24/new-york-play-exhibit-spotlight-oct-7-attack-trauma/73776547007/\"\u003eOct. 7 Hamas attack\u003c/a\u003e on Israel, according to township officials. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt\u0026#39;s not alone. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/2023/10/25/israel-hamas-war-protests-arrests-north-jersey-nj/71255351007/\"\u003eEnglewood \u003c/a\u003epolice have spent more than $32,000 in that time. In New York, the NYPD says it\u0026#39;s amassed almost $53 million in OT costs − just one tally of the intensity the war has generated the last eight months.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn Teaneck, whose large Jewish and Muslim populations have made it an epicenter for activism over the conflict, police overtime is up roughly 27% through May, compared with the same period last year. The expenditure has covered several large protests, weekly car rallies and extra staffing at council meetings, which have \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/bergen/teaneck/2023/10/18/emotions-from-israel-hamas-war-boil-over-in-teaneck-nj-protests/71222152007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003egrown volatile\u003c/a\u003e in recent months. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "72899959007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eLocal police have also provided extra staffing at a prayer vigil and at an annual event celebrating Israel\u0026#39;s Independence Day because of concerns of possible protests, said Deputy Police Chief Seth Kriegel.  \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe 93-person Teaneck force \u0026#34;has been strained because this causes our officers to work more hours,\u0026#34; Kriegel said. \u0026#34;These events have been challenging for our department, but it\u0026#39;s part of the job.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eNo Teaneck officers have been injured during the events, he added. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eProtest at Teaneck synagogue drew hundreds\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAmong the biggest expenses for the town was policing a March 10 demonstration outside the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/bergen/teaneck/2024/03/10/teaneck-protest-targets-sale-of-homes-in-west-bank-settlements/72864693007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eCongregation Keter Torah synagogue\u003c/a\u003e, where protesters objected to a real estate event involving properties in both Israel and the occupied West Bank. The event drew hundreds of pro-Palestinian demonstrators, including some who arrived by bus from outside of town, as well as a smaller group of counter-protesters waving Israeli flags. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhile the day was largely non-violent, there were some skirmishes, including demonstrators who tossed bottles at cars exiting the synagogue. Teaneck police arrested two people on charges of bias intimidation, assault and harassment after they were observed spraying liquids at vehicles.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThere have been other flareups as well. At dueling pro-Israel and Palestinian events that drew more than 1,000 people on April 1, one man was arrested for \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/bergen/teaneck/2024/04/01/demonstrations-outside-teaneck-nj-synagogue-over-israel-gaza-war/73173689007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003espitting in the face\u003c/a\u003e of another person. In May, a Queens man was arrested for allegedly harassing a pro-Palestinian demonstrator and \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/bergen/teaneck/2024/05/03/ny-man-charged-knife-teaneck-nj-pro-palestine-protest/73559476007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003ethreatening her with a knife\u003c/a\u003e. That same month, a Teaneck woman was arrested for allegedly \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/bergen/teaneck/2024/05/08/gaza-protester-arrested-teaneck-nj-council-meeting-police/73613402007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003edisrupting a town council meeting\u003c/a\u003e as she railed against the military campaign in Gaza. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73174179007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe proposed 2024 police budget, which has not yet been approved, is $14 million. That includes $600,000 for overtime. As of May 31, Teaneck was already more than halfway through its police OT budget, having spent $386,000. Israel and Gaza-related events have accounted for almost a third of that, according to Kriegel. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Despite the challenges we have faced with providing police services for these events, we have taken steps to mitigate the overtime expenditures, most notably by reassigning detectives and officers from specialty bureaus, when possible, to cover these events and shortages in the patrol division,\u0026#34; he said.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;It could turn into a budget crisis\u0026#39;\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eTeaneck will have to absorb the additional costs and pull from other parts of the budget to cover them, said Township Manager Dean Kazinci. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;There is an extraordinary cost for security when we have to call in other towns and agencies,\u0026#34; he said. Teaneck had to do that for the Keter Torah event, which required 160 officers at a total expense of more than $200,000. That included the cost for both Teaneck police and officers who assisted from neighboring towns and county agencies.  \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;People were called into work and ran on overtime because it was an 8-hour event,\u0026#34; Kazinci said. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;We budgeted $600,000 for police overtime, but salaries go up and these unplanned events are taking a big percentage of our overtime,\u0026#34; he continued. \u0026#34;When we exceed the number of overtime hours we will have to find that money somewhere and transfer from other areas to compensate. This could become problematic if there are many more of these protests, and it could turn into a budget crisis for us.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73174220007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBig protests from Englewood to LA \u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eCities around New Jersey and the U.S. − from Englewood, Paterson and Fort Lee to Chicago, New York and Los Angeles − have faced similar challenges\u003cstrong\u003e,\u003c/strong\u003e amid widespread protest over the death toll in Gaza. In recent months, activists have blocked highways, airports, and bridges to make their points.  \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eEnglewood\u0026#39;s $32,000 overtime bill since Oct. 7 has mostly been spent on additional police at council meetings and protests, according to City Manager Robert Hoffmann. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn New York, protestors have targeted some of the city\u0026#39;s most iconic events, including the Macy\u0026#39;s Thanksgiving Day Parade, the annual Christmas tree-lighting at Rockefeller Center and the Met Gala, leading to the $53 million OT tab, an NYPD spokesperson said.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eHamas\u0026#39; Oct. 7 attack killed 1,200 people in Israel; another 240 were taken hostage. It also sparked an Israeli offensive in Gaza in which some 33,000 people have been killed, according to the Hamas-run Gaza health ministry.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Record and NorthJersey.com sought comment from groups that have organized Teaneck demonstrations, including Wheels for Palestine, American Muslims for Palestine and the Council on American-Islamic Relations\u0026#39; New Jersey chapter. But calls and emails were not returned. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn a post on Instagram, Wheels for Palestine, which has organized weekly car caravans through town, wrote, \u0026#34;If you don\u0026#39;t want these car rallies to go through your town, do not pass resolutions supporting\u0026#34; Israel or its campaign in Gaza.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMike Kelly:  \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/columnists/mike-kelly/2023/12/13/israel-hamas-war-teaneck-nj-rift-mike-kelly-protest/71830560007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eThe Israel-Hamas war tears at Teaneck\u0026#39;s inclusive tradition. Can it be fixed?\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe account says the group \u0026#34;is dedicated to standing for the people of Palestine,\u0026#34; and since October, it has rallied \u0026#34;with our vehicles to expose Zionism\u0026#34; and \u0026#34;raise funds for Gaza.\u0026#34;  It also urges its followers to attend council meetings and offers talking points to express pro-Palestinian positions.  \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eHow Teaneck police try to keep the peace\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn Teaneck, police officers have been trained in \u0026#34;crowd management and de-escalation techniques\u0026#34; and are prepared to handle the rigors of the current climate, Kriegel said. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003ePolice have implemented measures including designated protest areas, and they work to ensure clear communication with protest leaders, he said. Officers also wear body cameras to ensure transparency and accountability, the deputy chief added.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;We\u0026#39;re also monitoring social media for any signs of planned violence or disruption,\u0026#34; he said. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eSome residents fear services will suffer because of all of the attention being devoted to the demonstrations. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAt a recent council meeting, resident Aviva Angel said she was distraught that protestors \u0026#34;came from outside our community\u0026#34;and \u0026#34;placed a financial burden on our town.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "73174216007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAngel said that the funds spent on police overtime \u0026#34;could have been better used to enrich our community\u0026#34; by boosting playgrounds or children\u0026#39;s programs. \u0026#34;Our resources are being strained by a group that wants to spread discord.\u0026#34; She suggested that the participants \u0026#34;should be billed for the expense.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eKriegel said that ultimately, people have the right to protest or to drive through the town in car rallies.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;We don\u0026#39;t have the legal authority to stop them. Everyone has the First Amendment right to protest peacefully,\u0026#34;  he said. \u0026#34;Anyone peacefully protesting will be protected. However, we have previously and will continue to enforce violations of the law when we observe them.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Our goal is to keep the peace and keep everyone safe,\u0026#34; he said.  \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cem\u003eDeena Yellin covers religion for NorthJersey.com. For unlimited access to her work covering how the spiritual intersects with our daily lives, \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://cm.dailyrecord.com/specialoffer/?gps-source\u003dCPNAVBARBBB\u0026utm_medium\u003dONSITE\u0026utm_campaign\u003d2019SLJP10\u0026utm_content\u003dCPNAVBARBBB\u0026utm_source\u003dCPNAVBARBBB\u0026onSuccessRedirectURL\u003dhttps%3A%2F%2Fwww.dailyrecord.com%2F\"\u003e\u003cem\u003eplease subscribe or activate your digital account today\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eEmail: \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"mailto:yellin@northjersey.com\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003eyellin@northjersey.com\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

