  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eMadigan was at the May 30 board meeting to praise the trustees for their unanimous vote on the newly hired Superintendent Ronnie Tarchichi. He has declared himself a \u0026#34;believer in family values\u0026#34; in this year\u0026#39;s election. Bogdansky is a founder of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://wsnj.org/\"\u003eWomen United for a Stronger New Jersey\u003c/a\u003e encouraging \u0026#34;moderate Republican and Independent women\u0026#34; to run for office,  and sponsoring a mix of Republican and nonpartisan board candidates together at meet-and-greets during election season.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eLane, a resident since 1991, previously served on the New Milford Borough Council from 1980 to 1982 and 1985 to 1986 and as mayor from 1987 to 1989. He served on the Ramapo Indian Hills Board of Education from 1999 to 2002. He has most recently served on the township\u0026#39;s Environmental Committee.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72338339007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eProvident Bank plans to close a branch in Bloomfield later this summer, as the financial giant carries out a controversial $1.3 billion merger with Lakeland Bank. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;As part of the merger with Lakeland Bank, a careful review of our combined branch office network was undertaken, and we have decided to consolidate certain nearby branch offices into single locations that can effectively serve our customers and local communities,\u0026#34; a spokesperson said in an email.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Provident branch at 1260 Broad Street in Bloomfield was one of those locations and will close at 3 p.m. on Friday, Aug. 30, the spokesperson said. All operations at that branch will be transferred to a neighboring Bloomfield branch at 11 Broad Street. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;For our customers who bank at the branches that are being consolidated, we have provided this notification well in advance of these closures and we will be communicating directly with them and commit to a smooth transition,\u0026#34; the spokesperson continued. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe closure was first reported by \u003ca href\u003d\"https://patch.com/new-jersey/bloomfield/provident-bank-will-close-bloomfield-branch-due-lakeland-merger\"\u003ePatch.com\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73327756007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eProvident’s merger with Lakeland comes more than a year and a half after the September 2022 announcement about the creation of the new entity, which has been dubbed a “super community bank” for the Garden State and will operate under the banner of Provident Bank. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eNewark city officials and activists from New Jersey Citizen Action called for tougher community banking standards to be included in the merger agreement — but an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.federalreserve.gov/newsevents/pressreleases/files/orders20240411a1.pdf\"\u003eApril announcement\u003c/a\u003e on federal approval of the merger includes no such requirements. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“It does present an issue around equality in terms of accessing basic financial services,” said Leila Amirhamzeh, director of development at the progressive advocacy group New Jersey Citizen Action. ”A lot of individuals really only access financial services through their local bank branches.” \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“Any branch closure is going to impact the community,” she said. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe two banks finalized the merger last month, according to a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.provident.bank/press-releases/provident-financial-services-inc-completes-merger-with-lakeland-bancorp-inc\"\u003eMay 16 press release\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eActivists — groups such as New Jersey Citizen Action — and federal lawmakers warned that banking mergers could lead to fewer branches serving the most at-risk residents, including minorities, the elderly and those with lower incomes, essentially \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/money/business/consumer/2023/03/01/south-jersey-bank-branch-closures-banking-deserts-growing-rapidly/69953776007/\"\u003ecreating “banking deserts.”\u003c/a\u003e \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eKeith Buscio, a spokesperson for Provident Bank, previously assured that the financial institution \u0026#34;has and will continue to meet the banking and financial services needs of every member of the communities we serve.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe push for tougher standards came after U.S Justice Department officials levied a $13 million settlement in 2022 against Lakeland Bank over alleged redlining of Black and Hispanic customers. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFederal authorities said Lakeland Bank deliberately avoided selling mortgages to otherwise eligible Black and Hispanic customers in and around Newark — a form of racial discrimination known as redlining. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eNone of Lakeland’s branches were in Newark. Lakeland did not admit any guilt in its federal settlement. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eMust open two branches in underserved areas\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eProvident would effectively take ownership of the settlement and the mandate to open two branches in underserved areas of New Jersey. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eNewark Mayor Ras Baraka wanted one of them to be in his city, and the Greater Toms River Chamber of Commerce \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/money/business/main-street/2023/01/30/what-nj-bank-branch-closures-mean-for-customers-why-it-happened/69832237007/\"\u003ewanted a branch in its area\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The fewer banks there are, the less products there are, the less service, the less investment,\u0026#34; Phyllis Salowe-Kaye, former president of New Jersey Citizen Action, said in an \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/money/business/main-street/2023/01/30/what-nj-bank-branch-closures-mean-for-customers-why-it-happened/69832237007/\"\u003einterview with the Asbury Park Press\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe number of bank branches fell from 3,277 in 2012 to 2,478 in 2022 — a 24% drop — according to the FDIC. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhile banks have adopted technology such as mobile banking, the Federal Reserve Bank of Philadelphia — which covers large portions of South Jersey — warned in a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.philadelphiafed.org/-/media/frbp/assets/community-development/reports/230216-banking-deserts-report.pdf\"\u003erecent report\u003c/a\u003e that “low- and moderate-income individuals and businesses in banking deserts may face increased challenges in accessing retail products and services, limiting their opportunity to improve their financial health and accumulate wealth.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eDaniel Munoz covers business, consumer affairs, labor and the economy for NorthJersey.com and The Record. \u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eEmail: \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"mailto:munozd@northjersey.com\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003emunozd@northjersey.com\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e; Twitter:\u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://twitter.com/DanielMunoz100\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003e@danielmunoz100\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e \u003cem\u003eand \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.facebook.com/people/Daniel-Munoz-Journalist/61559022552294/\"\u003eFacebook\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
