body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73806682007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Red Lobster on Route 17 southbound in Paramus is in danger of closing as the casual dining chain files for bankruptcy, according to bankruptcy documents. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe company listed 228 rejected leases it says will keep losing money if they continue operating as they currently are. The list includes at least some locations it has already closed, according to Restaurant Business.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eRed Lobster’s bankruptcy filing in the Middle District of Florida details how \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/nation/2024/05/22/longtime-diners-hope-red-lobsters-demise-is-not-on-the-menu/73791962007/\"\u003ethe restaurant chain has struggled in various ways\u003c/a\u003e, including a 30% drop in guests since 2019.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74005506007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe company — which has about 36,000 workers — also wants to abandon personal property at its closed restaurants, including furniture and fixtures. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Recently, the debtors have faced a number of financial and operational challenges, including a difficult macroeconomic environment, a bloated and underperforming restaurant footprint, failed or ill-advised strategic initiatives, and increased competition within the restaurant industry,\u0026#34; Red Lobster CEO Jonathan Tibus said in bankruptcy documents obtained by NorthJersey.com partner USA TODAY.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eUnder its bankruptcy filing, Red Lobster and its subsidiaries have an agreement to sell the company to their largest creditors.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eA court ruling is pending on the chain’s request to close the restaurants. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhere are the other locations? \u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAccording to court documents, two of the other New Jersey locations at risk are in Delran and Mays Landing, both in South Jersey. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/business/2024/05/20/red-lobster-chapter-11-bankruptcy-16-nj-sites/73772810007/\"\u003eFour other New Jersey locations have already closed\u003c/a\u003e — in Bridgewater, East Brunswick, Lawrenceville and Ledgewood. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFormer workers at the Ledgewood location are \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/business/2024/05/21/red-lobster-closing-leads-to-lawsuit-in-new-jersey/73785485007/\"\u003esuing Red Lobster\u003c/a\u003e, alleging that they were not given sufficient notice that their jobs were being terminated. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe suit said more than 50 people had their jobs terminated just a month after the news that Red Lobster was considering filing for Chapter 11 and failed to provide the required 90-day notice under New Jersey law.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThat suit is seeking judgment against Red Lobster to give workers an amount equal to the sum of their unpaid wages, salary, commissions, bonuses, accrued holiday pay, accrued vacation pay, pension and 401K contributions and other benefits for 90 days.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eProblems with all-you-can-eat shrimp\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eTibus, the Red Lobster CEO, noted that the May 2023 all-you-can eat shrimp as a $20 menu item cost the chain $11 million, and saddled it with supply chain problems. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAccording to a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.nbcnews.com/business/consumer/private-equity-rolled-red-lobster-rcna153397\"\u003ereport by NBC News\u003c/a\u003e, Red Lobster was bought out by a private equity firm which embarked on a process known as “asset-stripping.” \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe land on which Red Lobster’s restaurants sat was sold off by the firm, Golden Gate Capital. Red Lobster then had to pay rent on stores it previously owned, costing $200 million in additional expenses, according to NBC.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAmerican Realty Capital Partners bought the properties, NBC reported. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eA spokesperson for Golden Gate declined to comment for this story. Golden Gate sold its stake in Red Lobster in 2020. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eThis article contains information from USA TODAY. \u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cem\u003eDaniel Munoz covers business, consumer affairs, labor and the economy for NorthJersey.com and The Record. \u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eEmail: \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"mailto:munozd@northjersey.com\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003emunozd@northjersey.com\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e; Twitter:\u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://twitter.com/DanielMunoz100\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003e@danielmunoz100\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e \u003cem\u003eand \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.facebook.com/people/Daniel-Munoz-Journalist/61559022552294/\"\u003eFacebook\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73806682007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Red Lobster on Route 17 southbound in Paramus is in danger of closing as the casual dining chain files for bankruptcy, according to bankruptcy documents. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe company listed 228 rejected leases it says will keep losing money if they continue operating as they currently are. The list includes at least some locations it has already closed, according to Restaurant Business.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eRed Lobster’s bankruptcy filing in the Middle District of Florida details how \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.usatoday.com/story/news/nation/2024/05/22/longtime-diners-hope-red-lobsters-demise-is-not-on-the-menu/73791962007/\"\u003ethe restaurant chain has struggled in various ways\u003c/a\u003e, including a 30% drop in guests since 2019.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74005506007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe company — which has about 36,000 workers — also wants to abandon personal property at its closed restaurants, including furniture and fixtures. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Recently, the debtors have faced a number of financial and operational challenges, including a difficult macroeconomic environment, a bloated and underperforming restaurant footprint, failed or ill-advised strategic initiatives, and increased competition within the restaurant industry,\u0026#34; Red Lobster CEO Jonathan Tibus said in bankruptcy documents obtained by NorthJersey.com partner USA TODAY.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eUnder its bankruptcy filing, Red Lobster and its subsidiaries have an agreement to sell the company to their largest creditors.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eA court ruling is pending on the chain’s request to close the restaurants. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhere are the other locations? \u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAccording to court documents, two of the other New Jersey locations at risk are in Delran and Mays Landing, both in South Jersey. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/business/2024/05/20/red-lobster-chapter-11-bankruptcy-16-nj-sites/73772810007/\"\u003eFour other New Jersey locations have already closed\u003c/a\u003e — in Bridgewater, East Brunswick, Lawrenceville and Ledgewood. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFormer workers at the Ledgewood location are \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/business/2024/05/21/red-lobster-closing-leads-to-lawsuit-in-new-jersey/73785485007/\"\u003esuing Red Lobster\u003c/a\u003e, alleging that they were not given sufficient notice that their jobs were being terminated. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe suit said more than 50 people had their jobs terminated just a month after the news that Red Lobster was considering filing for Chapter 11 and failed to provide the required 90-day notice under New Jersey law.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThat suit is seeking judgment against Red Lobster to give workers an amount equal to the sum of their unpaid wages, salary, commissions, bonuses, accrued holiday pay, accrued vacation pay, pension and 401K contributions and other benefits for 90 days.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eProblems with all-you-can-eat shrimp\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eTibus, the Red Lobster CEO, noted that the May 2023 all-you-can eat shrimp as a $20 menu item cost the chain $11 million, and saddled it with supply chain problems. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAccording to a \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.nbcnews.com/business/consumer/private-equity-rolled-red-lobster-rcna153397\"\u003ereport by NBC News\u003c/a\u003e, Red Lobster was bought out by a private equity firm which embarked on a process known as “asset-stripping.” \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe land on which Red Lobster’s restaurants sat was sold off by the firm, Golden Gate Capital. Red Lobster then had to pay rent on stores it previously owned, costing $200 million in additional expenses, according to NBC.  \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAmerican Realty Capital Partners bought the properties, NBC reported. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eA spokesperson for Golden Gate declined to comment for this story. Golden Gate sold its stake in Red Lobster in 2020. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eThis article contains information from USA TODAY. \u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cem\u003eDaniel Munoz covers business, consumer affairs, labor and the economy for NorthJersey.com and The Record. \u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eEmail: \u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"mailto:munozd@northjersey.com\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003emunozd@northjersey.com\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e\u003cem\u003e; Twitter:\u003c/em\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://twitter.com/DanielMunoz100\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003e\u003cem\u003e@danielmunoz100\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/a\u003e \u003cem\u003eand \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.facebook.com/people/Daniel-Munoz-Journalist/61559022552294/\"\u003eFacebook\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

