      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThere are only a handful of contested primaries in Essex County municipalities this year and on the county level.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOne of the major races is in the Essex County sheriff primary, where two Democrats and two Republicans are vying for their party\u0026#39;s nomination to replace retiring Armando B. Fontoura. The longest serving sheriff in New Jersey history, Fontoura at age 81 announced in March that he will not seek a 13th term.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe other hotly-contested race is the Democratic primary for the Bloomfield mayoral race. \u003c/p\u003e"
