body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "1685273001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe body of an elderly Roxbury resident was recovered from Lake Hopatcong Monday morning, ending a multi-agency search that began Saturday night.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Morris County Prosecutor\u0026#39;s Office confirmed William Ryan, a 79-year-old resident of the Landing section, was found deceased at the southern end of the lake. He was last seen entering the lake at 7:30 p.m. Saturday \u0026#34;and did not return.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eA search launched by the Roxbury Township Police Department, Morris County Sheriff’s Office, Morris County Prosecutor’s Office and New Jersey State Police Marine Unit was suspended Saturday night and resumed on Sunday morning. The Roxbury Fire Department also joined the search.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWater conditions and visibility hindered recovery efforts before the search was suspended again on Sunday night, a Morris County Prosecutor\u0026#39;s Office spokesperson said. Search efforts included the use of a county submersible device, State Police divers, sonar and aviation.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe investigation continues but the circumstances of the incident are not considered suspicious, the prosecutor\u0026#39;s office spokesperson said.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "1685273001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe body of an elderly Roxbury resident was recovered from Lake Hopatcong Monday morning, ending a multi-agency search that began Saturday night.\u003c/p\u003e"
