body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "10392426002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter declaring a state of emergency in Jefferson over the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/transportation/2024/06/05/route-15-closed-nj-when-reopen-expected-delays-morris-sussex/73984900007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eclosure of Route 15\u003c/a\u003e South, Mayor Eric Wilsusen said that one lane of the highway has been reopened for residents to access some local homes and businesses.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe state Department of Transportation agreed to the partial reopening on Thursday but only for local traffic, Wilsusen told the Daily Record.  He added on his \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.facebook.com/mayorjeffersontownship\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eFacebook page\u003c/a\u003e that only the \u0026#34;top portion\u0026#34; of the area affected by the shutdown would now be accessible, though efforts were underway to expand that by Friday. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe state abruptly closed the road on Tuesday after a bridge over the Rockaway River near Berkshire Valley Road failed a safety inspection. That has led to massive delays for the thousands of travelers in Morris and Sussex counties who use the highway every day, and problems for local businesses and residents dealing with the traffic detoured through their streets. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73991805007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eRoute 15 northbound through the township remains open. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhile Wilsusen had no word on a long-term solution, he told the Daily Record that  the DOT would hold a conference call at 9 a.m. Friday with local officials to offer an update on the state\u0026#39;s plan. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eJefferson declares state of emergency\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I have been emphasizing that there is no other option than creating a temporary structure, detours on my local roads cannot be a sustainable option.\u0026#34; the mayor added. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn Wednesday, Wilsusen said he had declared a local state of emergency, which he said would increase the town\u0026#39;s ability to regulate traffic and deal with expenses created by the shutdown. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;It does not give us a lot of authority, but we are incurring expenses due to this closure,\u0026#34; Wilsusen said in another update on Facebook. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eDOT plans website for Route 15 commuters\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe DOT is promising to release more information to help travelers, state Senator Parker Space said on his \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.facebook.com/NJ24th\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eFacebook page\u003c/a\u003e with fellow 24th District legislators Dawn Fantasia and Michael Inganamort. The district includes parts of Morris County and all of Sussex. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The DOT is establishing a website where commuters and residents can find daily project updates and other pertinent information,\u0026#34; they wrote, promising to notify the public as soon as the website is up and running.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe legislators said they held an online meeting with state officials and local leaders to press for a solution. \u0026#34;Knowing that upwards of 60 percent of Sussex County residents commute out of the county for work, they stressed the severity of the situation for our commuters and advocated for an opening as quickly as possible,\u0026#34; according to their statement. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore:  \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/transportation/2024/06/05/route-15-closed-nj-when-reopen-expected-delays-morris-sussex/73984900007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003eWhen will Route 15 reopen? Here\u0026#39;s the latest as Morris, Sussex drivers battle huge delays\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eLocal residents \u0026#39;terrified\u0026#39; by speeding traffic \u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMeanwhile, commuters and residents are frustrated. The detours are causing speeding and reckless driving around local roads.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The worst part is the angry drivers absolutely flying up the side streets, thinking they\u0026#39;ve found some kind of shortcut, only to be met with even more traffic as they stand on their horn,\u0026#34; one Facebook user wrote under Mayor Wilsusen\u0026#39;s post. \u0026#34;I don\u0026#39;t even have kids but I\u0026#39;m terrified for my neighbors kids.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe state had planned to reduce Route 15 Southbound to one lane this week as part of an $11.6 million replacement of the bridge. But the entire roadway was shut down on Tuesday afternoon after the failed inspection.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe DOT hasn\u0026#39;t yet given a timetable for the emergency repairs.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Work continues on the project to replace the 124-year-old Route 15 southbound bridge over the Rockaway River, which began last summer,\u0026#34; the department said in a statement Wednesday. \u0026#34;Engineers are conducting a structural evaluation. The bridge will remain closed and detoured at this time.\u0026#34;\u003cem\u003eEmail: NFlanagan@gannett.com\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "10392426002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter declaring a state of emergency in Jefferson over the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/transportation/2024/06/05/route-15-closed-nj-when-reopen-expected-delays-morris-sussex/73984900007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eclosure of Route 15\u003c/a\u003e South, Mayor Eric Wilsusen said that one lane of the highway has been reopened for residents to access some local homes and businesses.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
