body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "11610720002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eDENVILLE -- A fourth North Non-Public B title for Morris Catholic was sealed on a four bagger.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eKate Heslin’s walk-off grand slam was the coup de grace as Morris Catholic took down St. Mary 14-4 in six innings Monday afternoon to earn another sectional crown.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“If we’re going to have anybody with a chance to finish the game, you couldn’t design it any better than Kate Heslin, there is not a better hitter in New Jersey,” said Crusaders coach Nick DeGennaro. “We’ve had a lot of ups and downs, and we’re playing a lot of young kids that don’t know what this grind is. I am really proud of them. There’s a lot of character on this team.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHeslin finished the day 2-4 with two runs scored. Sophomore pitcher Sofia Reisinger was 2-2 with two RBIs and also took control in the last two innings in the circle.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“We had one bad inning and that’s what we were trying to work on all year, limiting the walks and the errors,” said St. Mary coach Sarah Piening. “They were the better team today.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73965370007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eWhat It Means\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Crusaders (19-8) won the Non-Public B title in 2021 and 2022, but lost to St. Joe’s of Hammonton 7-1 in the final in 2023. They’ll face the Wildcats again for the state title Thursday at Kean.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSt. Joe’s of Hammonton features East Carolina commitment Ava Fisher in the circle.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“I think this team, the challenge, every time you throw a challenge in front of them, they’ve stepped up every time,” said DeGennaro. “I think facing St. Joe’s will bring out the best in us. It’s going to be a challenge. I will think about them tomorrow.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSt. Mary became a contender again in North Jersey with the school absorbing the bulk of the talented Immaculate Conception team when that school closed.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“It was a great season overall, I think our program is headed in a great direction,” said Piening. “I am very proud of our team. We had a senior transfer and a junior transfer who did a lot for us this year. I am looking forward to the direction that the program is heading in.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eTwo Outs In the Fifth\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe teams traded punches in the early innings. Morris Catholic took a 2-0 lead in the second inning, only to see St. Mary rally back for two in the top of the third. Morris Catholic answered with two in their half of the third.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIt was 4-3 Morris Catholic with two outs in the bottom of the fifth when the game swung for Morris Catholic. Reisinger started things off with a double, then Natalie Carovillano followed with an RBI double. An error, a misplay and a couple of walks kept the inning going and St. Mary brought in a new pitcher.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMarielle Balonze laced a two-run single down the right field line to make it 10-3 and take all the wind out of St Mary’s sails.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“I knew they would come to play,” said DeGennaro. “The graduating seniors were kids that gave us a dogfight two years ago from IC. They have a lot of energy. I fully expected that this was going to be a dogfight, but I thought when they made a pitching change and we started getting on base, we played against her last year and we felt good about hitting against her.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThey Said It\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“I think we figured out a lot of things about ourselves,” said DeGennaro. “I think the Mount game, a 2-1 loss, was one of our best games we played all year. We made some great plays in the outfield that game, but I think that it was knowing that who we see, they’re not better than we’ve already seen.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
