body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72848596007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe trendy Stanley tumbler has made its way into the kid\u0026#39;s cup section of Target and parents on TikTok are loving it. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEarlier this month, lifestyle vlogger Madilynn Cameron, @themadivlog on TikTok, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.tiktok.com/@themadivlog/video/7380156864799018283?is_from_webapp\u003d1\u0026sender_device\u003dpc\u0026web_id\u003d7330337368018421294\"\u003eposted a video to her page\u003c/a\u003e that said, \u0026#34;This is not a drill. Baby Stanleys for toddlers at Target,\u0026#34; with the caption, \u0026#34;Ur coming home with me, Target I\u0026#39;m screaming.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn the video, she highlights small Stanley tumblers that she found on the kid\u0026#39;s cup shelves at her local Target. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;They make kids\u0026#39; Stanleys now,\u0026#34; she says in the video while picking up the cup in four different colors. \u0026#34;This is the cutest thing ever.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis video, which was posted on June 13, now has over 33,000 likes, 475 comments, and 570,000 views. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore trending:  \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.poconorecord.com/story/news/2024/06/24/paul-mary-thorley-baby-on-beach-lake-george-mount-pocono/74190351007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ePocono pair left baby on Lake George Beach. What we know\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe cups shown in the video are in fact the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.stanley1913.com/products/adventure-quencher-travel-tumbler-14-oz\"\u003e14-ounce version of the Quencher H2.0 Flowstate Tumbler\u003c/a\u003e, the same \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/01/09/stanley-cups-trend-new-limited-edition-release-drop-tuesday/72121474007/\"\u003ecup that has caused a craze\u003c/a\u003e over the last year, rising to the top of the reusable water bottle game. These tumblers have sold out immediately upon dropping online and in stores with some collections being resold for way more than the original price. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Quencher comes in five sizes including 14, 20, 30, 40 and 64 ounces. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Compact without compromise, our smallest and lightest Quencher H2.0 is a great choice for quick and easy sipping, wherever the day takes you,\u0026#34; says the 14 ounce Quencher\u0026#39;s description. \u0026#34;The 14oz size is also perfect for kids, encouraging them to stay hydrated at home, school or the playground.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhile these, Stanley\u0026#39;s smallest tumblers, have been around for a while, the cups shown in the video appear to be part of the company\u0026#39;s brand-new \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.stanley1913.com/products/the-heatwave-quencher-h2-o-flowstate%E2%84%A2-tumbler-14-oz?_pos\u003d8\u0026_sid\u003d9a5fcada6\u0026_ss\u003dr?variant\u003d44560036528255\"\u003eHeat Wave Collection\u003c/a\u003e which dropped on June 11. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe 14 ounce Quenchers sold under the Heat Wave Collection can be purchased in four colors including Vivid Violet, Bright Lime, Tropical Teal and Passion Pink. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe 14 ounce Tumbler retails for $20 online and in stores. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "72848596007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe trendy Stanley tumbler has made its way into the kid\u0026#39;s cup section of Target and parents on TikTok are loving it. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEarlier this month, lifestyle vlogger Madilynn Cameron, @themadivlog on TikTok, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.tiktok.com/@themadivlog/video/7380156864799018283?is_from_webapp\u003d1\u0026sender_device\u003dpc\u0026web_id\u003d7330337368018421294\"\u003eposted a video to her page\u003c/a\u003e that said, \u0026#34;This is not a drill. Baby Stanleys for toddlers at Target,\u0026#34; with the caption, \u0026#34;Ur coming home with me, Target I\u0026#39;m screaming.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn the video, she highlights small Stanley tumblers that she found on the kid\u0026#39;s cup shelves at her local Target. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;They make kids\u0026#39; Stanleys now,\u0026#34; she says in the video while picking up the cup in four different colors. \u0026#34;This is the cutest thing ever.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis video, which was posted on June 13, now has over 33,000 likes, 475 comments, and 570,000 views. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore trending:  \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.poconorecord.com/story/news/2024/06/24/paul-mary-thorley-baby-on-beach-lake-george-mount-pocono/74190351007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ePocono pair left baby on Lake George Beach. What we know\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe cups shown in the video are in fact the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.stanley1913.com/products/adventure-quencher-travel-tumbler-14-oz\"\u003e14-ounce version of the Quencher H2.0 Flowstate Tumbler\u003c/a\u003e, the same \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/01/09/stanley-cups-trend-new-limited-edition-release-drop-tuesday/72121474007/\"\u003ecup that has caused a craze\u003c/a\u003e over the last year, rising to the top of the reusable water bottle game. These tumblers have sold out immediately upon dropping online and in stores with some collections being resold for way more than the original price. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Quencher comes in five sizes including 14, 20, 30, 40 and 64 ounces. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Compact without compromise, our smallest and lightest Quencher H2.0 is a great choice for quick and easy sipping, wherever the day takes you,\u0026#34; says the 14 ounce Quencher\u0026#39;s description. \u0026#34;The 14oz size is also perfect for kids, encouraging them to stay hydrated at home, school or the playground.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhile these, Stanley\u0026#39;s smallest tumblers, have been around for a while, the cups shown in the video appear to be part of the company\u0026#39;s brand-new \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.stanley1913.com/products/the-heatwave-quencher-h2-o-flowstate%E2%84%A2-tumbler-14-oz?_pos\u003d8\u0026_sid\u003d9a5fcada6\u0026_ss\u003dr?variant\u003d44560036528255\"\u003eHeat Wave Collection\u003c/a\u003e which dropped on June 11. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe 14 ounce Quenchers sold under the Heat Wave Collection can be purchased in four colors including Vivid Violet, Bright Lime, Tropical Teal and Passion Pink. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe 14 ounce Tumbler retails for $20 online and in stores. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

contentBody:
{
  "contentBody": [{
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "72848596007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe trendy Stanley tumbler has made its way into the kid\u0026#39;s cup section of Target and parents on TikTok are loving it. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eEarlier this month, lifestyle vlogger Madilynn Cameron, @themadivlog on TikTok, \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.tiktok.com/@themadivlog/video/7380156864799018283?is_from_webapp\u003d1\u0026sender_device\u003dpc\u0026web_id\u003d7330337368018421294\"\u003eposted a video to her page\u003c/a\u003e that said, \u0026#34;This is not a drill. Baby Stanleys for toddlers at Target,\u0026#34; with the caption, \u0026#34;Ur coming home with me, Target I\u0026#39;m screaming.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eIn the video, she highlights small Stanley tumblers that she found on the kid\u0026#39;s cup shelves at her local Target. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;They make kids\u0026#39; Stanleys now,\u0026#34; she says in the video while picking up the cup in four different colors. \u0026#34;This is the cutest thing ever.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis video, which was posted on June 13, now has over 33,000 likes, 475 comments, and 570,000 views. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cspan class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong style\u003d\"margin-right:3px;\"\u003eMore trending:  \u003c/strong\u003e\u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.poconorecord.com/story/news/2024/06/24/paul-mary-thorley-baby-on-beach-lake-george-mount-pocono/74190351007/\" target\u003d\"_blank\"\u003ePocono pair left baby on Lake George Beach. What we know\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/span\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe cups shown in the video are in fact the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.stanley1913.com/products/adventure-quencher-travel-tumbler-14-oz\"\u003e14-ounce version of the Quencher H2.0 Flowstate Tumbler\u003c/a\u003e, the same \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/entertainment/2024/01/09/stanley-cups-trend-new-limited-edition-release-drop-tuesday/72121474007/\"\u003ecup that has caused a craze\u003c/a\u003e over the last year, rising to the top of the reusable water bottle game. These tumblers have sold out immediately upon dropping online and in stores with some collections being resold for way more than the original price. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Quencher comes in five sizes including 14, 20, 30, 40 and 64 ounces. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;Compact without compromise, our smallest and lightest Quencher H2.0 is a great choice for quick and easy sipping, wherever the day takes you,\u0026#34; says the 14 ounce Quencher\u0026#39;s description. \u0026#34;The 14oz size is also perfect for kids, encouraging them to stay hydrated at home, school or the playground.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhile these, Stanley\u0026#39;s smallest tumblers, have been around for a while, the cups shown in the video appear to be part of the company\u0026#39;s brand-new \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.stanley1913.com/products/the-heatwave-quencher-h2-o-flowstate%E2%84%A2-tumbler-14-oz?_pos\u003d8\u0026_sid\u003d9a5fcada6\u0026_ss\u003dr?variant\u003d44560036528255\"\u003eHeat Wave Collection\u003c/a\u003e which dropped on June 11. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe 14 ounce Quenchers sold under the Heat Wave Collection can be purchased in four colors including Vivid Violet, Bright Lime, Tropical Teal and Passion Pink. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe 14 ounce Tumbler retails for $20 online and in stores. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73122483007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAttention North Jersey! Over the last week we have been asking you to submit your \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/food/2024/06/11/best-fries-north-jersey-nominate/74016306007/\"\u003esuggestions for the best french fries in Northern New Jersey\u003c/a\u003e. Now, after receiving a ton of responses, we have narrowed down the list to 21 restaurants — and we need your help to decide which one makes the region\u0026#39;s number one fry. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eIs it Rutt\u0026#39;s Hutt in Clifton, where you can indulge in fries smothered in gravy alongside one of its famous rippers? \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eMaybe it is Davey\u0026#39;s Irish Pub and Restaurant in Montvale, where you can choose among shoestring, seasoned waffle, steak, beer battered, or sweet potato fries. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eYou can go for a classic, crinkle-cut fry, seasoned to perfection at Ted\u0026#39;s North Delicatessen in Paramus, or check out Fire and Oak in Montvale where you can order truffle fries topped with a fluffy pile of parmesan cheese. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWhether you like your fries simple and crispy, smothered in toppings, or dipped in a delicious sauce, there are so many options in North Jersey to choose from. Let\u0026#39;s crown a winner!\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eCast your vote for the best french fries in North Jersey \u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThank you for voting for the best french fries in North Jersey. The deadline to vote was Friday, June 21, at noon so the poll is now closed. The winner will be announced July 8. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73122483007"
    }, {
