      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The war birds are always a favorite,\u0026#34; Wagner said. \u0026#34;We have people that leave saying that\u0026#39;s the best pyrotechnics they\u0026#39;ve ever seen.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eGreenwood Lake Airshow schedule, tickets\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGates open at 4 p.m. Friday with the show beginning at 7 p.m. Gates open at 2 p.m. Saturday and Sunday with performances starting at 5:30 p.m. All shows are expected to end around 9:30 p.m. \u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003eGeneral admission tickets are $35 per adult, $25 for senior citizens and veterans and $15 per child when purchased online, $5 more at the gate. A family package is $90, granting admission for two adults and up to four children. Other options include the front-line seating package and V.I.P pavilion performer package. \u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eTickets are available at \u003ca href\u003d\"https://greenwoodlakeairshow.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003enjairshow.com\u003c/a\u003e.According to the show\u0026#39;s latest news release, this year\u0026#39;s headline acts will include: \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSpotlight on the Titan Aerobatic Team: \u003c/strong\u003eThe most sought-after civilian aerial act in the industry, these four pilots perform awe-inspiring maneuvers in their World War II T-6 Texans.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNathan Hammond \u0026#34;Ghost Writer\u0026#34;:\u003c/strong\u003e After dark, watch as Hammond lights up the sky with 200 pounds of pyrotechnics and 4,000 brilliant LED lights in a graceful ballet among the stars. \u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBuck Roetman\u0026#39;s High-Energy Aerobatics:\u003c/strong\u003e Experience the electrifying aerobatics of Buck Roetman, known for his powerful performances with a 375+ horsepower Lycoming engine that fills the sky with roaring sounds and dramatic smoke trails. \u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRob Holland, Premier Aerobatic Pilot\u003c/strong\u003e: Witness Rob Holland, a premier freestyle aerobatic pilot, as he blends precision, artistry, and adrenaline into each routine, captivating spectators with his flawless execution of complex maneuvers.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eJerry McCart \u0026#34;The Homewrecker\u0026#34;:\u003c/strong\u003e Be amazed as McCart\u0026#39;s 375 mph triple engine jet-powered semi-truck roars down the runway with over 36,000 horsepower.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBob Carlton Makes Debut with Unique Fox Jet Sailplane: \u003c/strong\u003eExperience Bob Carlton\u0026#39;s thrilling debut, where he pilots the unique Fox Jet sailplane, the only two-seater designed for low-level, jet-powered performances, equipped with two PBS TJ-100 jet engines.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAirythmia: A Spectacle of Freedom and Fire:\u003c/strong\u003e Join Airythmia at the Day and Night Show to experience the \u0026#34;irregular\u0026#34; side of aviation with paramotors, featuring a dazzling pyrotechnic display that adds fiery excitement to their celebration of aerial freedom.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eExperience the Thrill of History: \u003c/strong\u003eWitness the iconic P-40 Warhawk and P-51 Mustang as they dominate the skies in a breathtaking display of World War II aviation prowess.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

contentBody:
{
  "contentBody": [{
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "12079084002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe annual \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.northjersey.com/story/news/passaic/west-milford/2022/06/07/greenwood-lake-air-show-skytypers-new-acts-west-milford-nj/7487264001/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003eGreenwood Lake Airshow \u003c/a\u003eis back and expected to be bigger than ever, with an expanded lineup of aerial acrobatics for its nighttime show. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe event takes place this Father\u0026#39;s Day weekend, June 14-16, with three day-into-night performances at the airport in West Milford.  \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The top performers of the nation are coming here,\u0026#34; said Tim Wagner, the air show\u0026#39;s chairman. \u0026#34;We are expecting up to 50,000 people.\u0026#34;  \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "12079009002"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe event turns 15 this year, with three golds in the International Council of Airshows Pinnacle Awards under its belt. North Jersey\u0026#39;s only air show, will feature eight headliners doing stunts involving pyrotechnics and skywriting. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eWhat\u0026#39;s new for 2024?\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;We started a few years back trying different things out,\u0026#34; Wagner said. \u0026#34;Now we have a laser show, an expanded night show and more performers.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFriday\u0026#39;s show will honor all of the armed forces in celebration of Flag Day. Four performances will \u003ca href\u003d\"https://greenwoodlakeairshow.com/pages/performers\"\u003efeature retired U.S. military aircrafts\u003c/a\u003e, or \u0026#34;war birds.\u0026#34; Visitors are encouraged to wear red, white, and blue. Sunday\u0026#39;s show will feature a \u0026#34;special skywriting surprise for Father\u0026#39;s Day\u0026#34; Wagner told NorthJersey.com. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe event will offer a variety of \u003ca href\u003d\"https://greenwoodlakeairshow.com/pages/press\"\u003efood options, vendors, and \u0026#34;upgradeable viewing experiences,\u0026#34;\u003c/a\u003e according to its website. Organizers also recommend general admission visitors bring folding chairs or blankets. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The war birds are always a favorite,\u0026#34; Wagner said. \u0026#34;We have people that leave saying that\u0026#39;s the best pyrotechnics they\u0026#39;ve ever seen.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eGreenwood Lake Airshow schedule, tickets\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003eGates open at 4 p.m. Friday with the show beginning at 7 p.m. Gates open at 2 p.m. Saturday and Sunday with performances starting at 5:30 p.m. All shows are expected to end around 9:30 p.m. \u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003eGeneral admission tickets are $35 per adult, $25 for senior citizens and veterans and $15 per child when purchased online, $5 more at the gate. A family package is $90, granting admission for two adults and up to four children. Other options include the front-line seating package and V.I.P pavilion performer package. \u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eTickets are available at \u003ca href\u003d\"https://greenwoodlakeairshow.com/\" target\u003d\"_blank\" rel\u003d\"noreferrer noopener\"\u003enjairshow.com\u003c/a\u003e.According to the show\u0026#39;s latest news release, this year\u0026#39;s headline acts will include: \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSpotlight on the Titan Aerobatic Team: \u003c/strong\u003eThe most sought-after civilian aerial act in the industry, these four pilots perform awe-inspiring maneuvers in their World War II T-6 Texans.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eNathan Hammond \u0026#34;Ghost Writer\u0026#34;:\u003c/strong\u003e After dark, watch as Hammond lights up the sky with 200 pounds of pyrotechnics and 4,000 brilliant LED lights in a graceful ballet among the stars. \u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBuck Roetman\u0026#39;s High-Energy Aerobatics:\u003c/strong\u003e Experience the electrifying aerobatics of Buck Roetman, known for his powerful performances with a 375+ horsepower Lycoming engine that fills the sky with roaring sounds and dramatic smoke trails. \u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eRob Holland, Premier Aerobatic Pilot\u003c/strong\u003e: Witness Rob Holland, a premier freestyle aerobatic pilot, as he blends precision, artistry, and adrenaline into each routine, captivating spectators with his flawless execution of complex maneuvers.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eJerry McCart \u0026#34;The Homewrecker\u0026#34;:\u003c/strong\u003e Be amazed as McCart\u0026#39;s 375 mph triple engine jet-powered semi-truck roars down the runway with over 36,000 horsepower.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eBob Carlton Makes Debut with Unique Fox Jet Sailplane: \u003c/strong\u003eExperience Bob Carlton\u0026#39;s thrilling debut, where he pilots the unique Fox Jet sailplane, the only two-seater designed for low-level, jet-powered performances, equipped with two PBS TJ-100 jet engines.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eAirythmia: A Spectacle of Freedom and Fire:\u003c/strong\u003e Join Airythmia at the Day and Night Show to experience the \u0026#34;irregular\u0026#34; side of aviation with paramotors, featuring a dazzling pyrotechnic display that adds fiery excitement to their celebration of aerial freedom.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eExperience the Thrill of History: \u003c/strong\u003eWitness the iconic P-40 Warhawk and P-51 Mustang as they dominate the skies in a breathtaking display of World War II aviation prowess.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e"
  }]
}

