body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74205310007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Shore isn\u0026#39;t the only place for summer fun in New Jersey (especially if it rains!). Below are a dozen things to do right here in North Jersey.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThere\u0026#39;s never a shortage of music in the area and this weekend\u0026#39;s offerings include the Pop 2000 Tour in Paramus, Deni Bonet and Chris Flynn in Bloomfield, Stop the Presses in Teaneck, and a gospel festival in Orange.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSoccer fans can catch the Uruguay vs. Bolivia CONMEBOL match at MetLife Stadium. Those who want to get into the sports action can run a race in Bloomfield.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCannabis enthusiasts can visit the grand opening of a new dispensary in Bloomfield, the fashion-conscious have the option of three days of Fashion Week events in Newark and East Rutherford, wine lovers can enjoy trivia and live music at a Chester winery, fans of author duo Liv Constantine can attend a signing in Northvale, theater buffs can see Montclair\u0026#39;s production of \u0026#34;Pippin,\u0026#34; and art lovers can check out two exhibits in Montclair. And for the kids, Blippi is coming to BergenPAC.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eScroll down for details and for the weather, too! Have fun!\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBeautiful Thursday, Friday then possibly rainy weekend\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAccording to the National Weather Service:\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThursday night:\u003c/strong\u003e Mostly clear, with a low approaching 60.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFriday\u003c/strong\u003e: Sunny, with a high in the low 80s, with increasing clouds in the evening and a low in the mid-60s.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSaturday\u003c/strong\u003e: Mostly cloudy with a 50 percent chance of showers and a high in the low 80s. Showers are likely and  a thunderstorm is possible in the evening, and a low around 75.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSunday:\u003c/strong\u003e Partly sunny with a high near 90, but showers are likely with a possible thunderstorms in the afternoon and evening. The nighttime low will be around 65.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eDisabled vet opens speakeasy-themed dispensary in Bloomfield\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Emerald Tea Supply Co. will open its doors to recreational cannabis users on Thursday. Co-owner Jason Leisey became interested in cannabis after he was severely injured by a car bomb while serving in Iraq in 2005, leaving him searching for an effective and natural solution to treat pain and trauma. Leisey and co-owner Amy Paterno have joined forces to upgrade the recreational dispensary experience. The store is an immersive experience, inviting patrons to step through a bookcase and into a 1920s speakeasy. With refurbished original tin ceilings, experienced bud tenders, vintage smoking pipes and product that is delivered from the vault via a working dumbwaiter, Leisey and Paterno offer a destination that encourages customers to connect with each other, share their appreciation for cannabis and engage in locally focused charitable give-back.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Grand opening of Emerald Tea Supply Co., 368B Broad St., Bloomfield. 11 a.m. Thursday. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://etsc.store/\"\u003eetsc.store\u003c/a\u003e, info@etsc.store\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Text\u0026#39; exhibit at Studio Montclair\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74205959007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eStudio Montclair Inc. presents its first exhibit of artwork using the written word as a source of inspiration. The final three days are Thursday, Friday and Saturday at the Studio Montclair Gallery. “Text” demonstrates the ability for words to be translated into art using an abundance of materials and mediums to create imagery. The use of typography and text in art dates from the late 19th century when advertising — posters created by such artists as Toulouse-Lautrec and Alphonse Mucha — emerged as an art form, followed by its use in Cubism by Picasso, Braque and Gris. More recently, typography and text has been used by artists such as Jenny Holzer, Shepard Fairy, Ed Ruscha and Barbara Kruger to make political statements.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eUsing these artists as inspiration and stepping-stones — either consciously or unconsciously — the 42 contributors to “Text” provide artwork based on the written word. According to juror Teddi Dolph, \u0026#34;From the use of actual documents as the main focus of a work to a cut piece of a document collaged onto another image, from neon signs to graffiti markings, from full sentences to a handful of words to a jumble of letters, artists use text as inspiration, as focal point, as accessory.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWith a BFA from Rutgers and post graduate work at both FIT and Parsons, Ms. Dolph founded Teddi Dolph Designs, specializing in packaging and graphic design. She serves on the Montclair State University Board of the College of the Arts.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e\u0026#34;Text\u0026#34; at Studio Montclair Gallery, 127 Bloomfield Ave. Gallery hours are 1 to 5 p.m. Thursday, Friday and Saturday, based on staffing availability or by appointment. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://studiomontclair.org/text/\"\u003estudiomontclair.org\u003c/a\u003e, smi@studiomontclair.org, 862-500-1447. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNewark Fashion Week Festival\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis three-day event is a fashion-forward celebration featuring runway shows, retail events, networking opportunities, industry parties and design and modeling competitions.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThursday is Dinner \u0026amp; Designs in Newark, where you can elevate your fashion experience and indulge in a meal. The event has add-on bar availability and will end with networking and positive vibes. In addition to dinner from a Newark restaurant, there will be a designer showcase, model and best-dressed competitions, a small business market, special guests, content creation and more. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFriday in Newark and Saturday at American Dream, runway events will showcase designs from streetwear designers and one-of-a-kind creations from couture designers of the world. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eNewark Fashion Week Festival - Dinner \u0026amp; Designs, 5 to 10 p.m. Thursday at Loft Life Venue, 47 Edison Place, Newark, $64 to $69.25; Runway I, 6 to 10 p.m. Friday at Crafty Studios, 640 N. Third St., Newark, $22 to $32.50; and Runway II, 6 to 10 p.m. Saturday at American Dream\u0026#39;s Dream Live, East Rutherford, $64 to $74.50. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.newarkfashionweekfestival.com/\"\u003enewarkfashionweekfestival.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eTrivia and music nights at Rebel Sheep winery\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThursday is trivia night at Rebel Sheep Wine at Stony Hill Farm in Chester. Have fun with your friends and make new ones, too.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFriday and Saturday are Summer Wine and Music Nights with live music and other activities for all ages. The farm and playgrounds will be open. Wine and small bites will be available for purchase. You are welcome to bring your own dinner, but no outside alcohol is permitted. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Trivia Night and Summer Wine and Music Nights at Rebel Sheep Wine, Stony Hill Farm, 15 North Road, Chester.  Trivia is 6 to 8 p.m. Thursday, no cover charge. Music is 5 to 7:30 p.m. Friday and Saturday.  Reservations are recommended. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://stonyhillfarms.com/rebel-sheep-wine/\"\u003estonyhillfarms.com/rebel-sheep-wine\u003c/a\u003e for information and reservations. Tasting room hours are noon to 5 p.m.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eLiv Constantine book signing at Books \u0026amp; Greetings\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The Next Mrs. Parrish\u0026#34; is the new book by Liv Constantine (sisters Lynne and Valerie Constantine), who will be at Books \u0026amp; Greetings in Northvale for a meet-and-greet on Thursday. Each attendee must purchase a book/ticket. A number system is used, based on how early the book was ordered. It is not first come first serve. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Liv Constantine at Books \u0026amp; Greetings, 271 Livingston St., Northvale. 6 p.m. Thursday. For information, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.booksandgreetings.com/\"\u003ebooksandgreetings.com\u003c/a\u003e. Order a book and ticket through \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/the-last-mrs-parrish-authors-liv-constantine-627-6pm-tickets-877508811477\"\u003eeventbrite.com\u003c/a\u003e, call 201-784-2665 or stop by the store. $30 for a book and ticket; $47 for a book to be shipped. Prices do not include applicable taxes and fees.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSunset Classic road race in Bloomfield\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe 36th running of the Tom Fleming Sunset Classic sponsored by Brookdale Shop Rite takes place on Thursday in Bloomfield. The event benefits the Bloomfield Educational Foundation and the Vocational Educational Special Training (V.E.S.T) program. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eTake on the challenge of the five-mile race through the township or the Rick Peterson Mile race, both of which finish on the track at Foley Field; or come out to cheer the runners and enjoy hot dogs, beverages, ice cream and beer. All runners will be entered in a bonus cash prize drawing. There will also be Kids Sprints on the field for ages 2 to 12 on the field. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Sunset Classic in Bloomfield, starting on Broad and Baldwin streets, ending at Foley Field. Registration begins at 5 p.m., Kids Sprints at 6, mile race at 7, five-mile race at 7:30. $12 to $50. All registrations will be online only, so bring your smart phone. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://runsignup.com/Race/Events/NJ/Bloomfield/TheVirtualTomFlemingSunsetClassic\"\u003erunsignup.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Pippin\u0026#39; at Vanguard Theater in Montclair\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eImmerse yourself in this tale - book by Roger O. Hirson, and music and lyrics by Stephen Schwartz - where fantasy and reality collide in a whirlwind of adventure and intrigue. Follow our enigmatic hero as he seeks purpose and fulfillment in a world full of possibilities and pitfalls. As Pippin navigates the trials and tribulations of life, love and the pursuit of happiness, you are invited to journey beyond the ordinary and discover the extraordinary. ​\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHeir to the Frankish throne, the young prince Pippin is in search of the secret to true happiness and fulfillment. He seeks it in the glories of the battlefield, the temptations of the flesh and the intrigues of political power (after disposing of his father, King Charlemagne the Great). In the end, though, Pippin finds that happiness lies not in extraordinary endeavors, but rather in the unextraordinary moments that happen every day.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003ePlus, Friday is NJ LGBTQ Community Night, so you can celebrate with NJ LGBTQ organizations in a night of inclusivity and pride; and Sunday is Howe House Night to honor community heritage before and after the matinee.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eContent warning: This production features scenes depicting the violence of war, the dangers of occult activities, and the dark side of group sexual activities and recreational drug use. During this performance, pyrotechnics, including small explosions, bomb and gun sound effects will be used, as well as strobe lights, fog, haze, smoke and fake weaponry. Viewer discretion is advised.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026#34;Pippin\u0026#34; at Vanguard Theater, 180 Bloomfield Ave., Montclair. 8 p.m. Thursday and Friday, 3 and 8 p.m. Saturday, and 2 and 7 p.m. Sunday. $25 to $50. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.vanguardtheatercompany.org/season/pippin-2024\"\u003evanguardtheatercompany.org\u003c/a\u003e, info@dreamvtc.org, 862-205-3525.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eCONMEBOL Copa America at MetLife Stadium\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Confederación Sudamericana de Fútbol Copa America 2024 soccer matches are taking place through July 14 in 14 cities in the U.S. The Group C match - Uruguay vs. Bolivia is the second of three that MetLife Stadium is hosting. The first was Group A - Chile vs. Argentina - on June 25, and the third is the semi-final on July 9.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Copa America at MetLife Stadium in East Rutherford, 9 p.m. Thursday. Parking lots open at 4, gates open at 7. $86 to $425 for tickets. $40 to $160 for parking. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.metlifestadium.com/event/2024/06/28/metlife-stadium/conmebol-copa-america---june-27\"\u003emetlifestadium.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;The Art of Hope for the Flowers\u0026#39; exhibit at Montclair Public Library\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "3338251001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis exhibit brings the art of Montclair’s “Butterfly Lady” - author and 93-year-old environmental warrior Trina Paulus  - through Saturday. A special author visit will be held on Saturday, with a tour of the exhibit followed by an auditorium presentation which will include a storytime for children of all ages, a time for people to share stories of hope, author/illustrator Q-and-A, and a reading of the book, \u0026#34;Hope For The Flowers,\u0026#34; in several languages.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eExhibited art will be sold with a portion of proceeds going to the Montclair Public Library. During the exhibit, signed copies of “Hope for the Flowers” will be available for purchase online using a QR code. The author will also have physical copies available for purchase on Saturday.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003ePaulus\u0026#39; book honors the journey to personal purpose and transformation. This parable is celebrating its second half century, with more than four million copies sold in English and translated into 15 languages across the globe. Her art and the story of Yellow and Stripe invite viewers to contemplate the struggle, sacrifice and strength it takes to become one’s true self.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe author will provide reading copies at the front desk to borrow, for visitors who wish to fully immerse themselves in not just the art, but the written story of hope.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003ePaulus is on the board of the Northeast Earth Coalition and is vice president of Cornucopia and the Central Rocky Mountain Permaculture Institute.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo\u003c/strong\u003e: \u0026#34;The Art of Hope for the Flowers\u0026#34; at Montclair Public Library, 50 S. Fullerton Ave. The exhibit is open during library hours (10 a.m. to 8 p.m. Thursday, 10 a.m. to 6 p.m. Friday and Saturday, 1 to 6 p.m. Sunday). The author visit begins at noon Saturday with a tour and continues with a presentation from 1 to 5 p.m. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://exhibit.hopefortheflowers.com/\"\u003eexhibit.hopefortheflowers.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003ePop 2000 Tour at Garden State Plaza\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWestfield Garden State Plaza will host a free throwback party and outdoor concert, when the Pop 2000 Tour - featuring Chris Kirkpatrick of *NSync, Jeff Timmons, O-Town, BBMAK, Ryan Cabrera and LFO - touches down in Paramus on Saturday. Hosted by Kirkpatrick, the tour promises an afternoon of nostalgia celebrating the hits from the turn of the millennium. Fans can anticipate a journey through the sounds of the early 2000s, such as “Tearing Up My Heart,” “All or Nothing,” and “Summer Girls.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003ePre-concert activities include beats from DJ Xcel at the concert stage, offerings at the Food Village from select cafes and restaurants, and shopping at retailer pop-ups. Then, dance to DJ Skribble who has worked with the likes of Taio Cruz, Britney Spears. and Wyclef Jean. The Pop 2000 concert takes place in the late afternoon, and the tour’s pop-up shop will be available for exclusive tour merchandise and memorabilia. After the show, meet and greet with the performers. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003ePop 2000 Tour at Westfield Garden State Plaza in Paramus. 1 to 6 p.m. Saturday. The event is free, but RSVP is requested. For details and to RSVP, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.westfield.com/united-states/gardenstateplaza/events-detail/pop-2000s-tour\"\u003ewestfield.com/united-states/gardenstateplaza\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eDeni Bonet \u0026amp; Chris Flynn - free concert in Bloomfield\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSinger/songwriter/violinist Deni Bonet and guitarist Chris Flynn play quirky, melodic and fun folk rock for all ages. They will perform a free concert at Bloomfield Public Library on Saturday.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Deni Bonet \u0026amp; Chris Flynn at Bloomfield Public Library, 90 Broad St. 2 p.m. Saturday. Free. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.bplnj.org/\"\u003ebplnj.com\u003c/a\u003e, 973-566-6200.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eStop the Presses at Debonair Music Hall\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBrooklyn-based Stop the Presses delivers a mix of traditional ska and reggae with pop, new wave and punk rock, and a splash of British two-tone. The show will also feature K-Mann \u0026amp; The 45\u0026#39;s, Backyard Superheros and more.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eStep the Presses at Debonair Music Hall, 1409 Queen Anne Road, Teaneck. 7 p.m. Saturday. Doors open at 6. General admission. $15 in advance; $20 day of show. debonairmusichall.com, 201-833-0011.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eGospel festival in Orange\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEssex County Executive Joseph N. DiVincenzo Jr., the Board of County Commissioners, and the Department of Parks, Recreation \u0026amp; Cultural Affairs present a gospel festival on Saturday at Monte Irvin Orange Park. This free live concert will go on all afternoon and will feature the Sensational Mighty Stars, McKevia Scott, St. Matthews AME Choir, Bethel Baptist Church Choir, Cross and Crown Christian Church Choir, Mr. Charles Barner Gospel Singers, Jesus Church of Deliverance Ministries Artist and more.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Gospel festival at Monte Irvin Orange Park, Center and S. Harrison streets, Orange. Noon to 6 p.m. Saturday. Free. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://orangenj.gov/CivicAlerts.aspx?AID\u003d287\"\u003eorangenj.gov\u003c/a\u003e. The rain date is Sunday.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBlippi at BergenPAC\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBlippi is coming to Englewood on Saturday for a curiosity adventure in \u0026#34;Blippi: The Wonderful World Tour!\u0026#34; Dance, sing and learn with Blippi and special guest Meekah as they discover what makes different cities unique and special. Will there be monster trucks, excavators and garbage trucks galore? You bet! Get ready to shake those wiggles out and OJ Twist your way through this brand-new musical party.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eBlippi: The Wonderful World Tour! at BergenPAC, 30 N. Van Brunt St., Englewood. 1 and 5 p.m. Saturday. $29 to $69. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.bergenpac.org/events/detail/blippi-the-wonderful-world-tour-1\"\u003ebergenpac.org\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eHave an event coming up? Tell us about it. Write to Daniel Galioto at galiotod@northjersey.com.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74205310007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Shore isn\u0026#39;t the only place for summer fun in New Jersey (especially if it rains!). Below are a dozen things to do right here in North Jersey.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThere\u0026#39;s never a shortage of music in the area and this weekend\u0026#39;s offerings include the Pop 2000 Tour in Paramus, Deni Bonet and Chris Flynn in Bloomfield, Stop the Presses in Teaneck, and a gospel festival in Orange.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSoccer fans can catch the Uruguay vs. Bolivia CONMEBOL match at MetLife Stadium. Those who want to get into the sports action can run a race in Bloomfield.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCannabis enthusiasts can visit the grand opening of a new dispensary in Bloomfield, the fashion-conscious have the option of three days of Fashion Week events in Newark and East Rutherford, wine lovers can enjoy trivia and live music at a Chester winery, fans of author duo Liv Constantine can attend a signing in Northvale, theater buffs can see Montclair\u0026#39;s production of \u0026#34;Pippin,\u0026#34; and art lovers can check out two exhibits in Montclair. And for the kids, Blippi is coming to BergenPAC.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eScroll down for details and for the weather, too! Have fun!\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBeautiful Thursday, Friday then possibly rainy weekend\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAccording to the National Weather Service:\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThursday night:\u003c/strong\u003e Mostly clear, with a low approaching 60.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFriday\u003c/strong\u003e: Sunny, with a high in the low 80s, with increasing clouds in the evening and a low in the mid-60s.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSaturday\u003c/strong\u003e: Mostly cloudy with a 50 percent chance of showers and a high in the low 80s. Showers are likely and  a thunderstorm is possible in the evening, and a low around 75.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSunday:\u003c/strong\u003e Partly sunny with a high near 90, but showers are likely with a possible thunderstorms in the afternoon and evening. The nighttime low will be around 65.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eDisabled vet opens speakeasy-themed dispensary in Bloomfield\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Emerald Tea Supply Co. will open its doors to recreational cannabis users on Thursday. Co-owner Jason Leisey became interested in cannabis after he was severely injured by a car bomb while serving in Iraq in 2005, leaving him searching for an effective and natural solution to treat pain and trauma. Leisey and co-owner Amy Paterno have joined forces to upgrade the recreational dispensary experience. The store is an immersive experience, inviting patrons to step through a bookcase and into a 1920s speakeasy. With refurbished original tin ceilings, experienced bud tenders, vintage smoking pipes and product that is delivered from the vault via a working dumbwaiter, Leisey and Paterno offer a destination that encourages customers to connect with each other, share their appreciation for cannabis and engage in locally focused charitable give-back.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Grand opening of Emerald Tea Supply Co., 368B Broad St., Bloomfield. 11 a.m. Thursday. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://etsc.store/\"\u003eetsc.store\u003c/a\u003e, info@etsc.store\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Text\u0026#39; exhibit at Studio Montclair\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74205959007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eStudio Montclair Inc. presents its first exhibit of artwork using the written word as a source of inspiration. The final three days are Thursday, Friday and Saturday at the Studio Montclair Gallery. “Text” demonstrates the ability for words to be translated into art using an abundance of materials and mediums to create imagery. The use of typography and text in art dates from the late 19th century when advertising — posters created by such artists as Toulouse-Lautrec and Alphonse Mucha — emerged as an art form, followed by its use in Cubism by Picasso, Braque and Gris. More recently, typography and text has been used by artists such as Jenny Holzer, Shepard Fairy, Ed Ruscha and Barbara Kruger to make political statements.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eUsing these artists as inspiration and stepping-stones — either consciously or unconsciously — the 42 contributors to “Text” provide artwork based on the written word. According to juror Teddi Dolph, \u0026#34;From the use of actual documents as the main focus of a work to a cut piece of a document collaged onto another image, from neon signs to graffiti markings, from full sentences to a handful of words to a jumble of letters, artists use text as inspiration, as focal point, as accessory.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWith a BFA from Rutgers and post graduate work at both FIT and Parsons, Ms. Dolph founded Teddi Dolph Designs, specializing in packaging and graphic design. She serves on the Montclair State University Board of the College of the Arts.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e\u0026#34;Text\u0026#34; at Studio Montclair Gallery, 127 Bloomfield Ave. Gallery hours are 1 to 5 p.m. Thursday, Friday and Saturday, based on staffing availability or by appointment. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://studiomontclair.org/text/\"\u003estudiomontclair.org\u003c/a\u003e, smi@studiomontclair.org, 862-500-1447. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNewark Fashion Week Festival\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis three-day event is a fashion-forward celebration featuring runway shows, retail events, networking opportunities, industry parties and design and modeling competitions.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThursday is Dinner \u0026amp; Designs in Newark, where you can elevate your fashion experience and indulge in a meal. The event has add-on bar availability and will end with networking and positive vibes. In addition to dinner from a Newark restaurant, there will be a designer showcase, model and best-dressed competitions, a small business market, special guests, content creation and more. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFriday in Newark and Saturday at American Dream, runway events will showcase designs from streetwear designers and one-of-a-kind creations from couture designers of the world. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eNewark Fashion Week Festival - Dinner \u0026amp; Designs, 5 to 10 p.m. Thursday at Loft Life Venue, 47 Edison Place, Newark, $64 to $69.25; Runway I, 6 to 10 p.m. Friday at Crafty Studios, 640 N. Third St., Newark, $22 to $32.50; and Runway II, 6 to 10 p.m. Saturday at American Dream\u0026#39;s Dream Live, East Rutherford, $64 to $74.50. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.newarkfashionweekfestival.com/\"\u003enewarkfashionweekfestival.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eTrivia and music nights at Rebel Sheep winery\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThursday is trivia night at Rebel Sheep Wine at Stony Hill Farm in Chester. Have fun with your friends and make new ones, too.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFriday and Saturday are Summer Wine and Music Nights with live music and other activities for all ages. The farm and playgrounds will be open. Wine and small bites will be available for purchase. You are welcome to bring your own dinner, but no outside alcohol is permitted. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Trivia Night and Summer Wine and Music Nights at Rebel Sheep Wine, Stony Hill Farm, 15 North Road, Chester.  Trivia is 6 to 8 p.m. Thursday, no cover charge. Music is 5 to 7:30 p.m. Friday and Saturday.  Reservations are recommended. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://stonyhillfarms.com/rebel-sheep-wine/\"\u003estonyhillfarms.com/rebel-sheep-wine\u003c/a\u003e for information and reservations. Tasting room hours are noon to 5 p.m.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eLiv Constantine book signing at Books \u0026amp; Greetings\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The Next Mrs. Parrish\u0026#34; is the new book by Liv Constantine (sisters Lynne and Valerie Constantine), who will be at Books \u0026amp; Greetings in Northvale for a meet-and-greet on Thursday. Each attendee must purchase a book/ticket. A number system is used, based on how early the book was ordered. It is not first come first serve. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Liv Constantine at Books \u0026amp; Greetings, 271 Livingston St., Northvale. 6 p.m. Thursday. For information, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.booksandgreetings.com/\"\u003ebooksandgreetings.com\u003c/a\u003e. Order a book and ticket through \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/the-last-mrs-parrish-authors-liv-constantine-627-6pm-tickets-877508811477\"\u003eeventbrite.com\u003c/a\u003e, call 201-784-2665 or stop by the store. $30 for a book and ticket; $47 for a book to be shipped. Prices do not include applicable taxes and fees.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSunset Classic road race in Bloomfield\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe 36th running of the Tom Fleming Sunset Classic sponsored by Brookdale Shop Rite takes place on Thursday in Bloomfield. The event benefits the Bloomfield Educational Foundation and the Vocational Educational Special Training (V.E.S.T) program. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eTake on the challenge of the five-mile race through the township or the Rick Peterson Mile race, both of which finish on the track at Foley Field; or come out to cheer the runners and enjoy hot dogs, beverages, ice cream and beer. All runners will be entered in a bonus cash prize drawing. There will also be Kids Sprints on the field for ages 2 to 12 on the field. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Sunset Classic in Bloomfield, starting on Broad and Baldwin streets, ending at Foley Field. Registration begins at 5 p.m., Kids Sprints at 6, mile race at 7, five-mile race at 7:30. $12 to $50. All registrations will be online only, so bring your smart phone. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://runsignup.com/Race/Events/NJ/Bloomfield/TheVirtualTomFlemingSunsetClassic\"\u003erunsignup.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Pippin\u0026#39; at Vanguard Theater in Montclair\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eImmerse yourself in this tale - book by Roger O. Hirson, and music and lyrics by Stephen Schwartz - where fantasy and reality collide in a whirlwind of adventure and intrigue. Follow our enigmatic hero as he seeks purpose and fulfillment in a world full of possibilities and pitfalls. As Pippin navigates the trials and tribulations of life, love and the pursuit of happiness, you are invited to journey beyond the ordinary and discover the extraordinary. ​\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHeir to the Frankish throne, the young prince Pippin is in search of the secret to true happiness and fulfillment. He seeks it in the glories of the battlefield, the temptations of the flesh and the intrigues of political power (after disposing of his father, King Charlemagne the Great). In the end, though, Pippin finds that happiness lies not in extraordinary endeavors, but rather in the unextraordinary moments that happen every day.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003ePlus, Friday is NJ LGBTQ Community Night, so you can celebrate with NJ LGBTQ organizations in a night of inclusivity and pride; and Sunday is Howe House Night to honor community heritage before and after the matinee.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eContent warning: This production features scenes depicting the violence of war, the dangers of occult activities, and the dark side of group sexual activities and recreational drug use. During this performance, pyrotechnics, including small explosions, bomb and gun sound effects will be used, as well as strobe lights, fog, haze, smoke and fake weaponry. Viewer discretion is advised.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026#34;Pippin\u0026#34; at Vanguard Theater, 180 Bloomfield Ave., Montclair. 8 p.m. Thursday and Friday, 3 and 8 p.m. Saturday, and 2 and 7 p.m. Sunday. $25 to $50. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.vanguardtheatercompany.org/season/pippin-2024\"\u003evanguardtheatercompany.org\u003c/a\u003e, info@dreamvtc.org, 862-205-3525.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eCONMEBOL Copa America at MetLife Stadium\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Confederación Sudamericana de Fútbol Copa America 2024 soccer matches are taking place through July 14 in 14 cities in the U.S. The Group C match - Uruguay vs. Bolivia is the second of three that MetLife Stadium is hosting. The first was Group A - Chile vs. Argentina - on June 25, and the third is the semi-final on July 9.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Copa America at MetLife Stadium in East Rutherford, 9 p.m. Thursday. Parking lots open at 4, gates open at 7. $86 to $425 for tickets. $40 to $160 for parking. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.metlifestadium.com/event/2024/06/28/metlife-stadium/conmebol-copa-america---june-27\"\u003emetlifestadium.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;The Art of Hope for the Flowers\u0026#39; exhibit at Montclair Public Library\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "3338251001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis exhibit brings the art of Montclair’s “Butterfly Lady” - author and 93-year-old environmental warrior Trina Paulus  - through Saturday. A special author visit will be held on Saturday, with a tour of the exhibit followed by an auditorium presentation which will include a storytime for children of all ages, a time for people to share stories of hope, author/illustrator Q-and-A, and a reading of the book, \u0026#34;Hope For The Flowers,\u0026#34; in several languages.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eExhibited art will be sold with a portion of proceeds going to the Montclair Public Library. During the exhibit, signed copies of “Hope for the Flowers” will be available for purchase online using a QR code. The author will also have physical copies available for purchase on Saturday.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003ePaulus\u0026#39; book honors the journey to personal purpose and transformation. This parable is celebrating its second half century, with more than four million copies sold in English and translated into 15 languages across the globe. Her art and the story of Yellow and Stripe invite viewers to contemplate the struggle, sacrifice and strength it takes to become one’s true self.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe author will provide reading copies at the front desk to borrow, for visitors who wish to fully immerse themselves in not just the art, but the written story of hope.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003ePaulus is on the board of the Northeast Earth Coalition and is vice president of Cornucopia and the Central Rocky Mountain Permaculture Institute.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo\u003c/strong\u003e: \u0026#34;The Art of Hope for the Flowers\u0026#34; at Montclair Public Library, 50 S. Fullerton Ave. The exhibit is open during library hours (10 a.m. to 8 p.m. Thursday, 10 a.m. to 6 p.m. Friday and Saturday, 1 to 6 p.m. Sunday). The author visit begins at noon Saturday with a tour and continues with a presentation from 1 to 5 p.m. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://exhibit.hopefortheflowers.com/\"\u003eexhibit.hopefortheflowers.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003ePop 2000 Tour at Garden State Plaza\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWestfield Garden State Plaza will host a free throwback party and outdoor concert, when the Pop 2000 Tour - featuring Chris Kirkpatrick of *NSync, Jeff Timmons, O-Town, BBMAK, Ryan Cabrera and LFO - touches down in Paramus on Saturday. Hosted by Kirkpatrick, the tour promises an afternoon of nostalgia celebrating the hits from the turn of the millennium. Fans can anticipate a journey through the sounds of the early 2000s, such as “Tearing Up My Heart,” “All or Nothing,” and “Summer Girls.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003ePre-concert activities include beats from DJ Xcel at the concert stage, offerings at the Food Village from select cafes and restaurants, and shopping at retailer pop-ups. Then, dance to DJ Skribble who has worked with the likes of Taio Cruz, Britney Spears. and Wyclef Jean. The Pop 2000 concert takes place in the late afternoon, and the tour’s pop-up shop will be available for exclusive tour merchandise and memorabilia. After the show, meet and greet with the performers. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003ePop 2000 Tour at Westfield Garden State Plaza in Paramus. 1 to 6 p.m. Saturday. The event is free, but RSVP is requested. For details and to RSVP, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.westfield.com/united-states/gardenstateplaza/events-detail/pop-2000s-tour\"\u003ewestfield.com/united-states/gardenstateplaza\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eDeni Bonet \u0026amp; Chris Flynn - free concert in Bloomfield\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eSinger/songwriter/violinist Deni Bonet and guitarist Chris Flynn play quirky, melodic and fun folk rock for all ages. They will perform a free concert at Bloomfield Public Library on Saturday.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Deni Bonet \u0026amp; Chris Flynn at Bloomfield Public Library, 90 Broad St. 2 p.m. Saturday. Free. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.bplnj.org/\"\u003ebplnj.com\u003c/a\u003e, 973-566-6200.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eStop the Presses at Debonair Music Hall\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBrooklyn-based Stop the Presses delivers a mix of traditional ska and reggae with pop, new wave and punk rock, and a splash of British two-tone. The show will also feature K-Mann \u0026amp; The 45\u0026#39;s, Backyard Superheros and more.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eStep the Presses at Debonair Music Hall, 1409 Queen Anne Road, Teaneck. 7 p.m. Saturday. Doors open at 6. General admission. $15 in advance; $20 day of show. debonairmusichall.com, 201-833-0011.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eGospel festival in Orange\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eEssex County Executive Joseph N. DiVincenzo Jr., the Board of County Commissioners, and the Department of Parks, Recreation \u0026amp; Cultural Affairs present a gospel festival on Saturday at Monte Irvin Orange Park. This free live concert will go on all afternoon and will feature the Sensational Mighty Stars, McKevia Scott, St. Matthews AME Choir, Bethel Baptist Church Choir, Cross and Crown Christian Church Choir, Mr. Charles Barner Gospel Singers, Jesus Church of Deliverance Ministries Artist and more.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Gospel festival at Monte Irvin Orange Park, Center and S. Harrison streets, Orange. Noon to 6 p.m. Saturday. Free. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://orangenj.gov/CivicAlerts.aspx?AID\u003d287\"\u003eorangenj.gov\u003c/a\u003e. The rain date is Sunday.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBlippi at BergenPAC\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBlippi is coming to Englewood on Saturday for a curiosity adventure in \u0026#34;Blippi: The Wonderful World Tour!\u0026#34; Dance, sing and learn with Blippi and special guest Meekah as they discover what makes different cities unique and special. Will there be monster trucks, excavators and garbage trucks galore? You bet! Get ready to shake those wiggles out and OJ Twist your way through this brand-new musical party.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eBlippi: The Wonderful World Tour! at BergenPAC, 30 N. Van Brunt St., Englewood. 1 and 5 p.m. Saturday. $29 to $69. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.bergenpac.org/events/detail/blippi-the-wonderful-world-tour-1\"\u003ebergenpac.org\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eHave an event coming up? Tell us about it. Write to Daniel Galioto at galiotod@northjersey.com.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

contentBody:
{
  "contentBody": [{
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74205310007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Shore isn\u0026#39;t the only place for summer fun in New Jersey (especially if it rains!). Below are a dozen things to do right here in North Jersey.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThere\u0026#39;s never a shortage of music in the area and this weekend\u0026#39;s offerings include the Pop 2000 Tour in Paramus, Deni Bonet and Chris Flynn in Bloomfield, Stop the Presses in Teaneck, and a gospel festival in Orange.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eSoccer fans can catch the Uruguay vs. Bolivia CONMEBOL match at MetLife Stadium. Those who want to get into the sports action can run a race in Bloomfield.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eCannabis enthusiasts can visit the grand opening of a new dispensary in Bloomfield, the fashion-conscious have the option of three days of Fashion Week events in Newark and East Rutherford, wine lovers can enjoy trivia and live music at a Chester winery, fans of author duo Liv Constantine can attend a signing in Northvale, theater buffs can see Montclair\u0026#39;s production of \u0026#34;Pippin,\u0026#34; and art lovers can check out two exhibits in Montclair. And for the kids, Blippi is coming to BergenPAC.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eScroll down for details and for the weather, too! Have fun!\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBeautiful Thursday, Friday then possibly rainy weekend\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAccording to the National Weather Service:\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cul\u003e\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eThursday night:\u003c/strong\u003e Mostly clear, with a low approaching 60.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eFriday\u003c/strong\u003e: Sunny, with a high in the low 80s, with increasing clouds in the evening and a low in the mid-60s.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSaturday\u003c/strong\u003e: Mostly cloudy with a 50 percent chance of showers and a high in the low 80s. Showers are likely and  a thunderstorm is possible in the evening, and a low around 75.\u003c/li\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cli\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eSunday:\u003c/strong\u003e Partly sunny with a high near 90, but showers are likely with a possible thunderstorms in the afternoon and evening. The nighttime low will be around 65.\u003c/li\u003e\n\u003c/ul\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eDisabled vet opens speakeasy-themed dispensary in Bloomfield\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Emerald Tea Supply Co. will open its doors to recreational cannabis users on Thursday. Co-owner Jason Leisey became interested in cannabis after he was severely injured by a car bomb while serving in Iraq in 2005, leaving him searching for an effective and natural solution to treat pain and trauma. Leisey and co-owner Amy Paterno have joined forces to upgrade the recreational dispensary experience. The store is an immersive experience, inviting patrons to step through a bookcase and into a 1920s speakeasy. With refurbished original tin ceilings, experienced bud tenders, vintage smoking pipes and product that is delivered from the vault via a working dumbwaiter, Leisey and Paterno offer a destination that encourages customers to connect with each other, share their appreciation for cannabis and engage in locally focused charitable give-back.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Grand opening of Emerald Tea Supply Co., 368B Broad St., Bloomfield. 11 a.m. Thursday. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://etsc.store/\"\u003eetsc.store\u003c/a\u003e, info@etsc.store\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Text\u0026#39; exhibit at Studio Montclair\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74205959007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eStudio Montclair Inc. presents its first exhibit of artwork using the written word as a source of inspiration. The final three days are Thursday, Friday and Saturday at the Studio Montclair Gallery. “Text” demonstrates the ability for words to be translated into art using an abundance of materials and mediums to create imagery. The use of typography and text in art dates from the late 19th century when advertising — posters created by such artists as Toulouse-Lautrec and Alphonse Mucha — emerged as an art form, followed by its use in Cubism by Picasso, Braque and Gris. More recently, typography and text has been used by artists such as Jenny Holzer, Shepard Fairy, Ed Ruscha and Barbara Kruger to make political statements.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eUsing these artists as inspiration and stepping-stones — either consciously or unconsciously — the 42 contributors to “Text” provide artwork based on the written word. According to juror Teddi Dolph, \u0026#34;From the use of actual documents as the main focus of a work to a cut piece of a document collaged onto another image, from neon signs to graffiti markings, from full sentences to a handful of words to a jumble of letters, artists use text as inspiration, as focal point, as accessory.”\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWith a BFA from Rutgers and post graduate work at both FIT and Parsons, Ms. Dolph founded Teddi Dolph Designs, specializing in packaging and graphic design. She serves on the Montclair State University Board of the College of the Arts.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003e\u0026#34;Text\u0026#34; at Studio Montclair Gallery, 127 Bloomfield Ave. Gallery hours are 1 to 5 p.m. Thursday, Friday and Saturday, based on staffing availability or by appointment. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://studiomontclair.org/text/\"\u003estudiomontclair.org\u003c/a\u003e, smi@studiomontclair.org, 862-500-1447. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eNewark Fashion Week Festival\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis three-day event is a fashion-forward celebration featuring runway shows, retail events, networking opportunities, industry parties and design and modeling competitions.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThursday is Dinner \u0026amp; Designs in Newark, where you can elevate your fashion experience and indulge in a meal. The event has add-on bar availability and will end with networking and positive vibes. In addition to dinner from a Newark restaurant, there will be a designer showcase, model and best-dressed competitions, a small business market, special guests, content creation and more. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFriday in Newark and Saturday at American Dream, runway events will showcase designs from streetwear designers and one-of-a-kind creations from couture designers of the world. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eNewark Fashion Week Festival - Dinner \u0026amp; Designs, 5 to 10 p.m. Thursday at Loft Life Venue, 47 Edison Place, Newark, $64 to $69.25; Runway I, 6 to 10 p.m. Friday at Crafty Studios, 640 N. Third St., Newark, $22 to $32.50; and Runway II, 6 to 10 p.m. Saturday at American Dream\u0026#39;s Dream Live, East Rutherford, $64 to $74.50. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.newarkfashionweekfestival.com/\"\u003enewarkfashionweekfestival.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eTrivia and music nights at Rebel Sheep winery\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThursday is trivia night at Rebel Sheep Wine at Stony Hill Farm in Chester. Have fun with your friends and make new ones, too.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFriday and Saturday are Summer Wine and Music Nights with live music and other activities for all ages. The farm and playgrounds will be open. Wine and small bites will be available for purchase. You are welcome to bring your own dinner, but no outside alcohol is permitted. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Trivia Night and Summer Wine and Music Nights at Rebel Sheep Wine, Stony Hill Farm, 15 North Road, Chester.  Trivia is 6 to 8 p.m. Thursday, no cover charge. Music is 5 to 7:30 p.m. Friday and Saturday.  Reservations are recommended. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://stonyhillfarms.com/rebel-sheep-wine/\"\u003estonyhillfarms.com/rebel-sheep-wine\u003c/a\u003e for information and reservations. Tasting room hours are noon to 5 p.m.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eLiv Constantine book signing at Books \u0026amp; Greetings\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;The Next Mrs. Parrish\u0026#34; is the new book by Liv Constantine (sisters Lynne and Valerie Constantine), who will be at Books \u0026amp; Greetings in Northvale for a meet-and-greet on Thursday. Each attendee must purchase a book/ticket. A number system is used, based on how early the book was ordered. It is not first come first serve. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Liv Constantine at Books \u0026amp; Greetings, 271 Livingston St., Northvale. 6 p.m. Thursday. For information, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.booksandgreetings.com/\"\u003ebooksandgreetings.com\u003c/a\u003e. Order a book and ticket through \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.eventbrite.com/e/the-last-mrs-parrish-authors-liv-constantine-627-6pm-tickets-877508811477\"\u003eeventbrite.com\u003c/a\u003e, call 201-784-2665 or stop by the store. $30 for a book and ticket; $47 for a book to be shipped. Prices do not include applicable taxes and fees.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eSunset Classic road race in Bloomfield\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe 36th running of the Tom Fleming Sunset Classic sponsored by Brookdale Shop Rite takes place on Thursday in Bloomfield. The event benefits the Bloomfield Educational Foundation and the Vocational Educational Special Training (V.E.S.T) program. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eTake on the challenge of the five-mile race through the township or the Rick Peterson Mile race, both of which finish on the track at Foley Field; or come out to cheer the runners and enjoy hot dogs, beverages, ice cream and beer. All runners will be entered in a bonus cash prize drawing. There will also be Kids Sprints on the field for ages 2 to 12 on the field. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Sunset Classic in Bloomfield, starting on Broad and Baldwin streets, ending at Foley Field. Registration begins at 5 p.m., Kids Sprints at 6, mile race at 7, five-mile race at 7:30. $12 to $50. All registrations will be online only, so bring your smart phone. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://runsignup.com/Race/Events/NJ/Bloomfield/TheVirtualTomFlemingSunsetClassic\"\u003erunsignup.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;Pippin\u0026#39; at Vanguard Theater in Montclair\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eImmerse yourself in this tale - book by Roger O. Hirson, and music and lyrics by Stephen Schwartz - where fantasy and reality collide in a whirlwind of adventure and intrigue. Follow our enigmatic hero as he seeks purpose and fulfillment in a world full of possibilities and pitfalls. As Pippin navigates the trials and tribulations of life, love and the pursuit of happiness, you are invited to journey beyond the ordinary and discover the extraordinary. ​\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eHeir to the Frankish throne, the young prince Pippin is in search of the secret to true happiness and fulfillment. He seeks it in the glories of the battlefield, the temptations of the flesh and the intrigues of political power (after disposing of his father, King Charlemagne the Great). In the end, though, Pippin finds that happiness lies not in extraordinary endeavors, but rather in the unextraordinary moments that happen every day.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003ePlus, Friday is NJ LGBTQ Community Night, so you can celebrate with NJ LGBTQ organizations in a night of inclusivity and pride; and Sunday is Howe House Night to honor community heritage before and after the matinee.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eContent warning: This production features scenes depicting the violence of war, the dangers of occult activities, and the dark side of group sexual activities and recreational drug use. During this performance, pyrotechnics, including small explosions, bomb and gun sound effects will be used, as well as strobe lights, fog, haze, smoke and fake weaponry. Viewer discretion is advised.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e \u0026#34;Pippin\u0026#34; at Vanguard Theater, 180 Bloomfield Ave., Montclair. 8 p.m. Thursday and Friday, 3 and 8 p.m. Saturday, and 2 and 7 p.m. Sunday. $25 to $50. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.vanguardtheatercompany.org/season/pippin-2024\"\u003evanguardtheatercompany.org\u003c/a\u003e, info@dreamvtc.org, 862-205-3525.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eCONMEBOL Copa America at MetLife Stadium\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Confederación Sudamericana de Fútbol Copa America 2024 soccer matches are taking place through July 14 in 14 cities in the U.S. The Group C match - Uruguay vs. Bolivia is the second of three that MetLife Stadium is hosting. The first was Group A - Chile vs. Argentina - on June 25, and the third is the semi-final on July 9.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Copa America at MetLife Stadium in East Rutherford, 9 p.m. Thursday. Parking lots open at 4, gates open at 7. $86 to $425 for tickets. $40 to $160 for parking. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.metlifestadium.com/event/2024/06/28/metlife-stadium/conmebol-copa-america---june-27\"\u003emetlifestadium.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003e\u0026#39;The Art of Hope for the Flowers\u0026#39; exhibit at Montclair Public Library\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "3338251001"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThis exhibit brings the art of Montclair’s “Butterfly Lady” - author and 93-year-old environmental warrior Trina Paulus  - through Saturday. A special author visit will be held on Saturday, with a tour of the exhibit followed by an auditorium presentation which will include a storytime for children of all ages, a time for people to share stories of hope, author/illustrator Q-and-A, and a reading of the book, \u0026#34;Hope For The Flowers,\u0026#34; in several languages.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eExhibited art will be sold with a portion of proceeds going to the Montclair Public Library. During the exhibit, signed copies of “Hope for the Flowers” will be available for purchase online using a QR code. The author will also have physical copies available for purchase on Saturday.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003ePaulus\u0026#39; book honors the journey to personal purpose and transformation. This parable is celebrating its second half century, with more than four million copies sold in English and translated into 15 languages across the globe. Her art and the story of Yellow and Stripe invite viewers to contemplate the struggle, sacrifice and strength it takes to become one’s true self.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe author will provide reading copies at the front desk to borrow, for visitors who wish to fully immerse themselves in not just the art, but the written story of hope.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003ePaulus is on the board of the Northeast Earth Coalition and is vice president of Cornucopia and the Central Rocky Mountain Permaculture Institute.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo\u003c/strong\u003e: \u0026#34;The Art of Hope for the Flowers\u0026#34; at Montclair Public Library, 50 S. Fullerton Ave. The exhibit is open during library hours (10 a.m. to 8 p.m. Thursday, 10 a.m. to 6 p.m. Friday and Saturday, 1 to 6 p.m. Sunday). The author visit begins at noon Saturday with a tour and continues with a presentation from 1 to 5 p.m. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://exhibit.hopefortheflowers.com/\"\u003eexhibit.hopefortheflowers.com\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003ePop 2000 Tour at Garden State Plaza\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eWestfield Garden State Plaza will host a free throwback party and outdoor concert, when the Pop 2000 Tour - featuring Chris Kirkpatrick of *NSync, Jeff Timmons, O-Town, BBMAK, Ryan Cabrera and LFO - touches down in Paramus on Saturday. Hosted by Kirkpatrick, the tour promises an afternoon of nostalgia celebrating the hits from the turn of the millennium. Fans can anticipate a journey through the sounds of the early 2000s, such as “Tearing Up My Heart,” “All or Nothing,” and “Summer Girls.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003ePre-concert activities include beats from DJ Xcel at the concert stage, offerings at the Food Village from select cafes and restaurants, and shopping at retailer pop-ups. Then, dance to DJ Skribble who has worked with the likes of Taio Cruz, Britney Spears. and Wyclef Jean. The Pop 2000 concert takes place in the late afternoon, and the tour’s pop-up shop will be available for exclusive tour merchandise and memorabilia. After the show, meet and greet with the performers. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003ePop 2000 Tour at Westfield Garden State Plaza in Paramus. 1 to 6 p.m. Saturday. The event is free, but RSVP is requested. For details and to RSVP, visit \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.westfield.com/united-states/gardenstateplaza/events-detail/pop-2000s-tour\"\u003ewestfield.com/united-states/gardenstateplaza\u003c/a\u003e. \u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eDeni Bonet \u0026amp; Chris Flynn - free concert in Bloomfield\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eSinger/songwriter/violinist Deni Bonet and guitarist Chris Flynn play quirky, melodic and fun folk rock for all ages. They will perform a free concert at Bloomfield Public Library on Saturday.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Deni Bonet \u0026amp; Chris Flynn at Bloomfield Public Library, 90 Broad St. 2 p.m. Saturday. Free. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.bplnj.org/\"\u003ebplnj.com\u003c/a\u003e, 973-566-6200.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eStop the Presses at Debonair Music Hall\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBrooklyn-based Stop the Presses delivers a mix of traditional ska and reggae with pop, new wave and punk rock, and a splash of British two-tone. The show will also feature K-Mann \u0026amp; The 45\u0026#39;s, Backyard Superheros and more.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eStep the Presses at Debonair Music Hall, 1409 Queen Anne Road, Teaneck. 7 p.m. Saturday. Doors open at 6. General admission. $15 in advance; $20 day of show. debonairmusichall.com, 201-833-0011.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eGospel festival in Orange\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eEssex County Executive Joseph N. DiVincenzo Jr., the Board of County Commissioners, and the Department of Parks, Recreation \u0026amp; Cultural Affairs present a gospel festival on Saturday at Monte Irvin Orange Park. This free live concert will go on all afternoon and will feature the Sensational Mighty Stars, McKevia Scott, St. Matthews AME Choir, Bethel Baptist Church Choir, Cross and Crown Christian Church Choir, Mr. Charles Barner Gospel Singers, Jesus Church of Deliverance Ministries Artist and more.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo:\u003c/strong\u003e Gospel festival at Monte Irvin Orange Park, Center and S. Harrison streets, Orange. Noon to 6 p.m. Saturday. Free. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://orangenj.gov/CivicAlerts.aspx?AID\u003d287\"\u003eorangenj.gov\u003c/a\u003e. The rain date is Sunday.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBlippi at BergenPAC\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eBlippi is coming to Englewood on Saturday for a curiosity adventure in \u0026#34;Blippi: The Wonderful World Tour!\u0026#34; Dance, sing and learn with Blippi and special guest Meekah as they discover what makes different cities unique and special. Will there be monster trucks, excavators and garbage trucks galore? You bet! Get ready to shake those wiggles out and OJ Twist your way through this brand-new musical party.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cstrong\u003eGo: \u003c/strong\u003eBlippi: The Wonderful World Tour! at BergenPAC, 30 N. Van Brunt St., Englewood. 1 and 5 p.m. Saturday. $29 to $69. \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.bergenpac.org/events/detail/blippi-the-wonderful-world-tour-1\"\u003ebergenpac.org\u003c/a\u003e.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u003cem\u003eHave an event coming up? Tell us about it. Write to Daniel Galioto at galiotod@northjersey.com.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

