body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74071329007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eElmwood Park resident Alessandra Curcio has competed on both “Wheel of Fortune” and “The Price is Right,” and she hopes to conquer other game shows soon.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCurcio was on “Wheel of Fortune” in 2019, and was invited to “The Price is Right” in Television City, California as part of an alumni reunion.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCurcio said that it was “pure luck” that she got selected as a contestant for the June 3 episode, when she was originally just an audience member. Once on the show, Curcio managed to “win the wheel, and the entire showcase.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74097207007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn “Wheel of Fortune,” Curcio won $1,000 dollars in 2019. On \u0026#34;The Price is Right,\u0026#34; she won over $65,000 in prizes and money. Some of the prizes include a paddleboard, jumper cables, a car, a vanity set, a jukebox, a barbecue island, a Margaritaville cruise with a four night stay in the Bahamas, and a trip to the Cook Islands in New Zealand.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCurcio explained her time on the show as a “heart-racing” experience.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“I love being on TV, and being on stage,” Curcio said. “So that was definitely my favorite part. I\u0026#39;d say my least favorite part was being so thirsty. Because you\u0026#39;re outside standing in the sun, it was probably like 95 degrees that day in California.\u0026#34;\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCurcio even kept her involvement on the show a secret from many people in her life.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I was just excited for them [the viewers] to experience it with me for the first time because I had gameshow blackout,\u0026#34; Curcio said. \u0026#34;So I was there, but I don\u0026#39;t remember a lot of things. So I was excited to experience it with them [the viewers].”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eCurcio has been watching “The Price is Right” since she was little, and stresses the importance to keep trying.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“Like if you want something and you never try, you\u0026#39;re never going to get it,” Curcio said. “Things don\u0026#39;t just come to you.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
