    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eTo participate in Krispy Kreme\u0026#39;s July giveaway, customers must be part of the chain\u0026#39;s rewards program. Signing up is simple: download the Krispy Kreme app or create an account on the company’s website. Once a member, any purchase made on Tuesdays or Fridays qualifies for the respective freebie.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFollowing the holiday-themed doughnut giveaway, Tuesday, July 9, brings the return of the Kit Kat Collection. Rewards members can select their free doughnut from options like the Kit Kat Crunch Doughnut, Kit Kat Cookie Dream Doughnut, and the Kit Kat Salted Caramel Brownie Doughnut. These Kit Kat doughnuts, which were first introduced in April, will be available only during the week of July 8.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eKrispy Kreme will announce the free doughnut options for subsequent Tuesdays later in the month on its social media accounts and website.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, any customer wearing red, white, and blue on July 4 can receive a free Original Glazed doughnut at participating Krispy Kreme locations.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eFor more details, visit Krispy Kreme\u0026#39;s \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.krispykreme.com/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.krispykreme.com/\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e or follow their social media channels.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }]
  }
}

contentBody:
{
  "contentBody": [{
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "2854690001"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eKrispy Kreme is sweetening July with free doughnuts and iced coffee for its loyal customers.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe popular bakery chain, known for its iconic glazed doughnuts, is extending its Fourth of July giveaway throughout the month. Members of the \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.krispykreme.com/rewards\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.krispykreme.com/rewards\"\u003eKrispy Kreme Rewards\u003c/a\u003e program can indulge in a free doughnut every Tuesday and a free iced coffee every Friday with any purchase, the company announced.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eFree doughnuts at Krispy Kreme\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eOn the first giveaway date, Tuesday, July 2, rewards members can choose a free doughnut from Krispy Kreme\u0026#39;s special Star Spangled Sweetness Collection. This collection features festive options including the Firework Cookies \u0026amp; Kreme Filled Doughnut, Cotton Candy Sparkler Doughnut, and Freedom Flag Doughnuts.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe Friday freebies begin on July 5, offering rewards members a free iced coffee of any size with a purchase. This promotion will continue every Friday in July.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "asset",
    "value": "74247529007"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eHow to get free iced coffee and donuts in July?\u003c/h2\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eTo participate in Krispy Kreme\u0026#39;s July giveaway, customers must be part of the chain\u0026#39;s rewards program. Signing up is simple: download the Krispy Kreme app or create an account on the company’s website. Once a member, any purchase made on Tuesdays or Fridays qualifies for the respective freebie.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFollowing the holiday-themed doughnut giveaway, Tuesday, July 9, brings the return of the Kit Kat Collection. Rewards members can select their free doughnut from options like the Kit Kat Crunch Doughnut, Kit Kat Cookie Dream Doughnut, and the Kit Kat Salted Caramel Brownie Doughnut. These Kit Kat doughnuts, which were first introduced in April, will be available only during the week of July 8.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eKrispy Kreme will announce the free doughnut options for subsequent Tuesdays later in the month on its social media accounts and website.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eAdditionally, any customer wearing red, white, and blue on July 4 can receive a free Original Glazed doughnut at participating Krispy Kreme locations.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }, {
    "type": "text",
    "value": "\u003cp\u003eFor more details, visit Krispy Kreme\u0026#39;s \u003ca href\u003d\"https://www.krispykreme.com/\" data-type\u003d\"link\" data-id\u003d\"https://www.krispykreme.com/\"\u003ewebsite\u003c/a\u003e or follow their social media channels.\u003c/p\u003e"
  }]
}

body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73600883007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHere\u0026#39;s what Donna Liotto-Scocozza’s grandfather always told her when she watched him cook: \u0026#34;First, bambina, a little olive oil in the pan.\u0026#34; \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eLiotto-Scocozza would sit by her Italian grandfather’s side while he cooked, discussing olive oils and food. Now, Liotto-Scocozza, a Montclair resident, is a registered olive oil sommelier and helps consumers find the perfect one  for their needs and tastes.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eLiotto-Scocozza launched Firenze International Olive Oils in 2015, she said, to “provide customers with the highest quality, best-in-class, extra virgin olive oils, vinegars and condiments from across the globe.” \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp class\u003d\"exclude-from-newsgate\"\u003e\u003cstrong\u003e\u003cem\u003eStory continues below photo gallery\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "2441906001"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter she graduated from Montclair State University with a degree in food and nutrition, Liotto-Scocozza worked in New York City as a food editor for women\u0026#39;s magazines, including Woman\u0026#39;s Day and Weightwatchers.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter earning a culinary degree from Johnson \u0026amp; Wales University in Providence, Rhode Island, Liotto-Scocozza worked in test kitchens for appliance companies before she landed a job with Shark Kitchen in Boston, and expected to retire shortly after.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eBut she was devastated when she was laid off from the job a year after she was hired. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74063424007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eShortly after, she traveled to Italy with her husband, Victor Scocozza, a trip they took every other year. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eHe had been a commercial food photographer for advertising and editorial until he retired in 1996. They had met when she was working in the test kitchen at Woman\u0026#39;s Day magazine.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAfter traveling around tasting different olive oils and wines, Victor asked Donna what she was going to do for work. She had no idea. He suggested she could work with olive oil. With her culinary knowledge, Liotto-Scocozza took the idea and never looked back. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003ch2 class\u003d\"presto-h2 wp-block-heading\"\u003eBecoming an olive oil sommelier\u003c/h2\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAround a year ago, right after Victor died, Liotto-Scocozza attended the Olive Oil Times Education Lab sommelier program in New York, which costs $2,800, where she took sessions to help her become an olive oil educator. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs part of the program, she passed the test to become a sommelier, where she had to describe whether olive oil samples were extra virgin, based on taste and smell.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74122924007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eShe had actually signed up for the sommelier program in 2019, but wasn\u0026#39;t able to travel for the course. Then she signed up again in 2020, but it was canceled due to the COVID-19 pandemic. Last year was the first time it was offered again in New York.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e She had told so many customers that she was taking the course and once she passed, Liotto-Scocozza reprinted her business cards to add the sommelier title, and started talking to customers about what she learned. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eA lot of the information from the program \u0026#34;was info I had picked up from farmers and producers and importers I had met through the years of buying and selling and traveling,\u0026#34; she said. \u0026#34;But once I passed the test I felt even more comfortable talking about olive oil production in various countries, the healthful aspects of olive oil,\u0026#34; and other details.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eToday\u003cstrong\u003e,\u003c/strong\u003e Liotto-Scocozza buys dozens of different olive oils as a sommelier, and when she tastes them, she can pinpoint the type of olives used and the region they came from.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "74073824007"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eLiotto-Scocozza finds and sells olive oils from Italy, France, Spain, Greece, Portugal, Israel, South Africa, Australia, and California. “There are not many people in the industry that are basic retailers,\u0026#34; she said. \u0026#34;I talk about the healthful aspects and let people taste the olive oil.”\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eWorking in Montclair, she uses her knowledge of olive oil to help consumers find the right one for their cooking needs. “I offer the opportunity to taste something and to find out about something that is healthful,\u0026#34; she said.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e\u0026#34;I enjoy talking to people about olive oil and deflating the misconceptions out there,” Liotto-Scocozza. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eOne of those misconceptions among consumers include people saying olive oil is becoming diluted. Liotto-Scocozza also believes consumers are not getting proper olive oils from supermarkets, so she sells her product at farmers\u0026#39; markets.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003e“Enlightening people and making sure consumers get what they are paying for and know what they are getting from a supermarket… that’s the consumer aspect I bring to the community,” she said.\u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "73600883007"
