body:
{
  "body": {
    "desktop": [{
      "type": "asset",
      "value": "7841699002"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eA large brush fire is burning in the Meadowlands marsh near the New Jersey Turnpike between exits 15X and 16E according the Secaucus Police Department. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003ePolice officers said there is no current threat to Secaucus structures. Officials warn of ash and smoke conditions filling the surrounding proximity. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eThe fire started at approximately 2:30 p.m. on Thursday, said a Secaucus police officer. The cause of the fire is still unknown. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eNJ Transit rail service into and out of New York Penn Station has been suspended due to Amtrak overhead wire issues, and the fire was affecting wire repair efforts, NJ Transit said. Midtown Direct trains are being diverted to Hoboken. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }, {
      "type": "text",
      "value": "\u003cp\u003eAs of 4 p.m. firefighters were still working to extinguish the blaze. \u003c/p\u003e"
    }],
    "mobile": [{
      "type": "asset",
